PVD("philippines_ndp_2023-2028",{"docs":["","PDP 2023 2028"],"s":{"1":[[1,"332","4","National Cybersecurity Plan and Cybersecurity Response Center Activation","formulation of the National Cybersecurity plan and activation of the National Computer Emergency Response Team and the National Cybersecurity Operations Center",""],[1,"337","5","Cybersecurity Protection for Critical Information Infrastructure","To strengthen security against cyberattacks on critical information infrastructure (CII),",""],[1,"337","6","CII Sectoral Cybersecurity Emergency Response Teams","the government will: (a) capacitate CII sectoral cybersecurity emergency response teams",""],[1,"337","6","Cybersecurity Operations Manual and Standard Protocols","develop a manual of operations and standard protocols on cybersecurity for public and private institutions",""],[1,"337","6","Interoperable Cybercrime Intelligence Fusion System","ensure interoperability and intelligence fusion of security and law enforcement agencies in tracking and monitoring online transactions of criminal elements, terrorist groups, and illegal drug traders",""],[1,"337","6","Cybersecurity Capacity and Skills Upgrading for Strategic Agencies","strengthen capacity and upgrade technical skills of strategic agencies on cybersecurity",""],[1,"337","6","AFP Cyber Defense Modernization Component","strengthen cyber defense component in the modernization of the AFP",""],[1,"337","6","Cybersecurity Partnership Strengthening Initiative","forge stronger collaboration with local and international partners",""],[1,"337","6","Minimum Cybersecurity Standards for CII and Government","institute minimum information security and cybersecurity standards for CII and government agencies",""],[1,"337","6","Cybersecurity Curriculum Development in Education Institutions","develop cybersecurity curriculum in academic and technical education institutions",""],[1,"337","6","National Cybersecurity Policy Framework","institute a national policy framework on cybersecurity",""],[1,"339","17","Critical Information Infrastructure Compliance Standards","This aims to protect critical information infrastructure (CIIs) by prescribing minimum standards for compliance by government agencies.",""],[1,"339","18","Cybersecurity Workforce and DICT Regulatory Capacity Strengthening","This aims to strengthen the cybersecurity workforce in the country and strengthen capabilities of the Department of Information and Communications Technology (DICT] by providing it with regulatory authority over CIIs and the cybersecurity industry.","Department of Information and Communications Technology (DICT)"]],"2":[[1,"57","23","Interoperable Health Information Systems","Accelerate interoperable health information systems",""],[1,"62","1","Philippine eHealth Strategic Framework and Plan Implementation","An enabling environment for sector-wide application of digital technologies for health will be fostered through implementation of the components of the Philippine eHealth Strategic Framework and Plan.",""],[1,"62","1","Health Information Exchange Technology Investment","Multisectoral engagements will be maximized for investments in physical technology and software platforms, services, and applications to support health information exchange.",""],[1,"62","1","National Health Insurance Program Information Systems Upgrade","Other priority areas include improving the National Health Insurance Program information systems, to manage enrollment, collection, and claims processing, and streamlining licensing and permit processes with the Department of Health (DOH), PhilHealth, Food and Drug Administration, and other government institutions, to address some barriers to health facility and technology access.","Department of Health (DOH) | PhilHealth | Food and Drug Administration"]],"3":[[1,"30","7","PhilSys Digital Identification and Financial Inclusion Acceleration","The government has already taken initial steps toward digitalization and financial inclusion through the Philippine Identification System or PhilSys Act (RA 11055). However, PhilSys processes need to be expedited.",""],[1,"36","8","Targeted Social Protection through PhilSys","Digitalization can also help the government build better data systems that will create better programs, such as more targeted social protection enabled by the national ID through PhilSys;",""],[1,"113","34","Social Registry Establishment and Updating","Ensure the establishment and updating of social registries",""],[1,"113","38","Digital Payment Services for Cash Transfers","Strengthen services and facilities for digital payments of cash transfers",""],[1,"113","39","Social Protection Statistics Enhancement","Enhance SP statistics guided by the approved framework",""],[1,"115","2","Social Registry Harmonization and Integration Initiative","Concerned agencies shall establish and update social registries for vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"116","2","Digital Payments for Cash Transfers","Strengthen services and facilities for digital payments of cash transfers",""],[1,"116","3","Expansion of Digital Payment Platforms for Cash Transfers","digital payment platforms will be increasingly used for cash transfers.",""],[1,"116","3","Shared Social Protection Digital Platform Integration","SP programs that share their digital platforms will result in greater efficiency and wider options for their beneficiaries.",""],[1,"116","4","Social Protection Statistics Enhancement","Enhance social protection statistics guided by the approved framework",""]],"4":[[1,"181","19","E-Commerce Regulatory Policy Framework","The bill seeks to establish an effective regulatory policy for commercial activities conducted through the internet or electronic means.",""],[1,"251","1","Emerging Technologies, Markets, and Business Models Monitoring and Analysis","Enhance monitoring and understanding of emerging technologies, markets, and business models",""],[1,"251","3","Competition Authority Digital Economy Regulatory Capacity Building","The PCC and sector regulators will keep abreast of emerging technologies and understand how these can alter markets and business models, develop capacity and expertise to use data science and analytics, and learn from the experience of other countries to enhance their enforcement capability and develop regulatory foresight.",""],[1,"251","3","Ex Ante Competition Regulation Review","The PCC will explore the opportunities and risks in adopting ex ante regulation, while continuing to build upon its existing ex post enforcement approach to address competition issues in the digital economy.",""],[1,"251","4","Regulatory Sandbox Framework Consideration","The agencies will also consider regulatory sandboxes (See Chapter 8), similar to the Regulatory Sandbox Framework of the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas.",""],[1,"253","12","Consumer Act Amendment for Fraud Protection","Considering the growth of e-commerce, the amendment of the Consumer Act of the Philippines, including the imposition of stiffer fines will ensure protection of consumers and firms against fraudulent schemes, including protection against deceptive, unfair, and unconscionable sales acts and practices, and observance of truth and accuracy in advertising.",""],[1,"253","12","Internet Transactions Act for E-commerce Regulation","The Internet Transactions Act will protect consumers and firms engaged in electronic or digital transactions by improving the regulatory environment for e-commerce (See Chapters 6 and 7).",""],[1,"262","8","Cybersecurity and Digital Payments Regulatory Improvement","The BSP has been proactive in issuing policies concerning cybersecurity, consumer protection, data integrity, and adoption of global standards and best practices, among other key regulations, as well as in continuously collaborating with the payment industry and other government bodies to improve the facilities continuously and offer innovative options for digital payments.",""],[1,"271","6","E-Commerce Transaction Regulation Act","This act will regulate all Business-to-Business and Business-to-Customer commercial transactions over the internet, including those related to internet retail, online travel services, digital media providers, ride hailing services, and digital financial services",""]],"5":[[1,"242","2","ICT Sector Regulatory Reform Package","Public clamor ushered the approval of some long overdue reforms intended to increase competition and improve regulatory efficiency in the ICT sector, including the streamlining of permits to speed up telecommunications infrastructure rollout, liberalizing satellite access to non-telecommunications, and opening telecommunications to full foreign ownership.",""],[1,"245","4","Fair Access to Essential Telecommunications Facilities","the PCC and the National Telecommunications Commission (NTC) will ensure fair, reasonable, and non-discriminatory access to essential facilities and resources controlled by incumbents to improve the digital infrastructure (See Chapter 12) and expand access to fast and affordable internet services (See Chapter 8).","National Telecommunications Commission (NTC)"],[1,"246","6","Open Access in Data Transmission Bill","The government will pursue the enactment of the Open Access in Data Transmission Bill to liberalize the telecommunications and broadband sectors further by removing the legislative franchise requirement for players to build their own network and gain access to the country's spectrum resources.",""],[1,"246","8","ICT Infrastructure Sharing Policy","The DICT and NTC will promote infrastructure sharing, including of government assets, by working with private owners of essential facilities.","DICT | NTC"],[1,"246","8","Fair Access Policy for Essential ICT Facilities","They will issue policies to ensure that all players in the ICT sector are assured of fair, reasonable, and non-discriminatory terms to access essential facilities.","DICT | NTC"],[1,"247","5","Open Access Regulation for Essential and Bottleneck Facilities","the government shall work with the private sector to ensure open access at fair and reasonable prices to essential or bottleneck facilities",""],[1,"317","21","National Broadband Program Institutionalization","The bill proposes to institutionalize the National Broadband Program, public safety and emergency communications, and policies for the use of other passive infrastructures- poles, ducts, and dark fiber.",""],[1,"317","24","Minimum Telecommunications Facilities in Buildings Requirement","This seeks to ensure that buildings are capacitated toward achieving universal access to quality, reliable, and secure ICT services by incorporating minimum electronic requirements, i.e., telecommunications facilities, in multi-dwelling buildings, commercial, buildings, government buildings, office buildings, schools, and hospitals, among others.",""]],"6":[[1,"38","3","LGU Capacity-Building and Mentoring Program","Over the medium term, there will be close coordination through capacity- building programs and mentoring for LGUs, especially in areas where national government support will be needed.",""],[1,"38","4","Devolution Transition Plan Fast-Tracking and Operationalization","the completion of Devolution Transition Plans (DTP) will be fast-tracked and operationalized to improve each LGU's capacity for delivering public services and raising local revenues.",""],[1,"274","1","Local Government Capacity Development and Devolution Support Program","A smooth transition to full devolution, therefore, requires an extensive capacity development program and assistance for LGUs with limited local resources.",""],[1,"274","25","Local Government Revenue and Devolved Functions Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the capacity of LGUs to raise more revenues and implement devolved functions",""],[1,"274","25","Equitable and Efficient National Tax Allotment Reform","Pursue an equitable and efficient National Tax Allotment",""],[1,"279","4","Local Government Revenue Capacity Support","The government will support the capacity of local governments in resource generation.",""],[1,"279","4","Real Property Valuation and Assessment Reform Bill","A Real Property Valuation and Assessment Reform Bill has been proposed to strengthen tax collection through the regular valuation of real properties using improved valuation standards.",""],[1,"279","4","Local Tax Structure Simplification and Modernization","The local tax structure, which was formulated in 1991, will be revisited to make it simpler, more efficient, and responsive to the current economic environment.",""],[1,"279","4","Peer Mentoring for Fiscal Management Replication","These practices will be replicated and scaled up through peer mentoring, to be spearheaded by the Bureau of Local Government Finance, in partnership with the Philippine Tax Academy-Local Government Finance Institute.",""],[1,"279","6","Devolution Transition Plan Implementation and LGU Capacity Support","will ensure that the increased resources of LGUs will result in the implementation of Devolution Transition Plans and the efficient delivery of public services.","Department of Budget and Management | Department of the Interior and Local Government"],[1,"279","7","National Tax Allotment Formula Reform","The potential of the National Tax Allotment (NTA) to lessen regional disparities will be explored.",""],[1,"281","14","Real Property Valuation and Assessment Reform Bill","Real Property Valuation and Assessment Reform Bill to rationalize and support the regular valuation of real properties, in accordance with internationally-accepted valuation standards.",""],[1,"281","14","Amendment of the National Tax Allotment Formula","Amendment of the National Tax Allotment (NTA) formula: Intends to address equity issues, and vertical and horizontal fiscal imbalances between local government units (LGU].",""],[1,"281","14","LGU Income Classification Reform","LGU Income Classification Bill: Seeks to authorize the Secretary of Finance to set the income ranges and undertake the regular income reclassification of all provinces, cities, and municipalities once every three fiscal years.",""],[1,"281","14","LGU Property Insurance Mandate","LGU Property Insurance: Proposes to mandate all provinces, cities, and municipalities to insure all government properties with the Government Insurance Fund.",""]],"7":[[1,"79","5","Civil Society Representation and Participation Mechanisms in Local Governance","Civil society representation in local special bodies needs to be improved.",""],[1,"83","4","Community CSO Empowerment and Accreditation Desks","Communities shall be empowered to create or join CSOs.",""],[1,"359","5","Fiscal Openness Program","Higher rates of civil society organizations (CSO) participation were facilitated by the Fiscal Openness Program of the Department of Budget and Management (DBM)","Department of Budget and Management (DBM)"],[1,"359","5","Support for Local Governance Program","the Support for Local Governance Program of the Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG)","Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG)"],[1,"359","5","Philippine Open Government Partnership Commitments","the commitments made under the Philippine Open Government Partnership (PH-OGP)",""],[1,"359","5","Citizens Participatory Audit Program","the Citizens Participatory Audit (CPA) program of the Commission on Audit (COA) improved citizen participation in the public audit process","Commission on Audit (COA)"],[1,"361","3","Measures to Address Inclusion Barriers and Strengthen Participatory Governance","Finally, socio-political barriers to inclusion and the meaningful participation of marginalized sectors must be strategically addressed, particularly, the gaps in implementing the Magna Carta for Women (RA 9710), the Indigenous People's Rights Act (RA 8371), the mandatory representation of the 14 basic sectors, and inclusionary policies espousing government support of CSO participation at all levels of governance.",""],[1,"362","3","Functional Participatory Platforms for Public Decision-Making","Deepening participatory governance not only means establishing functional participatory platforms that inform or consult citizens, but also ensuring that citizens and CSOs have concrete roles and significant influence in all stages of public decision-making.",""],[1,"362","4","Expansion of Protected Participatory Spaces","the government will increase the availability and accessibility of protected spaces for various sectors and concerns, while functionality will be secured through platforms that are established and",""],[1,"362","5","Civil Society Participation in Budget Preparation","the DBM will intensify CSOs' participation in the national budget preparation process.","DBM"],[1,"362","5","Inclusive CSO Accreditation and Local Networking Guidelines","enhance policy guidelines to make CSO accreditation and local networking more inclusive.",""],[1,"362","5","Sectorally Representative Decision-Making Bodies","Agencies will ensure that their decision-making bodies with sufficient sectoral representation, particularly from marginalized sectors, are created, reviewed for functionality and effectiveness, and enhanced accordingly.","Agencies"],[1,"363","2","Participatory Governance Metrics Mainstreaming","To improve the quality of participation, the DBM and DILG, with PH-OGP partner agencies, will mainstream the implementation of Participatory Governance Metrics20 for assessing the quality of participation in LSBs and national programs.","DBM | DILG | PH-OGP partner agencies"],[1,"363","3","Capacity Development for CSO Members of Local School Boards","intensify capacity development interventions for CSO members of LSBs.",""],[1,"363","3","PH-OGP Collaborative CSO Engagement Mechanism","The PH-OGP will continue to implement collaborative practices with CSOs in developing, implementing, and monitoring government programs; and will strengthen the capacity of national and local CSOs to engage the government effectively.",""],[1,"363","6","Citizen Feedback Helpline and Hotline Strengthening","To operationalize this strategy, the government will ensure the functionality, efficiency, and effectiveness of helplines, hotlines, and",""],[1,"364","1","National Citizen Feedback and Complaint Resolution Mechanisms","At the national level, the monitoring and resolution of citizen reports will be improved through the EODB and EGSD Acts, the Anti-Red Tape Authority's (ARTA) Harmonized Client Satisfaction Measurement, the Civil Service Commission's (CSC) Contact Center ng Bayan, and people's feedback mechanisms required in national agency websites.","Anti-Red Tape Authority | Civil Service Commission"],[1,"364","1","CSO Budget Concern Desk","The DBM will also institute a CSO desk to receive and respond to CSOs' budget-related concerns.","DBM"],[1,"364","1","Local Feedback Mechanism Monitoring and Third-Party Project Oversight","At the local level, the DILG will monitor the functionality and responsiveness of feedback mechanisms, including the CSO desks and Barangay Violence Against Women helpdesks; improve the Citizen Satisfaction Index System implementation with CSOs; and pursue third-party monitoring of state-funded projects.","DILG"],[1,"364","1","Digital Enhancement of Feedback and Monitoring Systems","Moreover, digital technologies will be used to augment the implementation of these mechanisms with due emphasis on access, inclusion, context-sensitivity, and empowerment of marginalized sectors.",""],[1,"368","8","Public Participation in Local Budgeting","It will also promote public participation in the local budgeting process for shared",""],[1,"368","15","Recognition of IP Mandatory Representatives in Local Legislative Bodies","This will ensure that IP Mandatory Representatives are recognized in local legislative bodies and their capabilities for local legislation are harnessed for more effective representation and promotion of IP rights through policymaking.",""]],"8":[[1,"332","1","Operationalization of BARMM Intergovernmental Relations Mechanisms","In BARMM, all other intergovernmental relations mechanisms still need to be operationalized, such as the newly created Bangsamoro Sustainable Development Board and other intergovernmental arrangements between BARMM, the national government, and relevant LGUs.",""],[1,"332","1","Healing, Reconciliation, and Gender Mainstreaming Enhancement in GICA Communities","and in the necessary enhancements in the healing, reconciliation, and gender mainstreaming components in GICA communities.",""],[1,"333","14","Full Transition of the BARMM Government","Ensure the full transition of the BARMM government",""],[1,"334","2","Full Transition of the BARMM Government","Ensure full transition of the BARMM Government",""],[1,"334","3","Bangsamoro Transition Authority Capacity and Institution Building Support","Support will be extended to the Bangsamoro Transition Authority in institution building, personnel development, and economic management toward an inclusive BARMM government.",""],[1,"334","3","BARMM Election Preparation Measures","Necessary policy and processes will be implemented to ensure a smooth BARMM elections in 2025.",""],[1,"334","3","Intergovernmental Relations Mechanism Operationalization and Strengthening","All intergovernmental relations mechanisms will be operationalized and strengthened to resolve remaining and potential issues between the national and the Bangsamoro governments.",""],[1,"339","20","Operational Basis for Cordillera Autonomy Convergence Efforts","This will provide an operational basis for future convergence efforts between local government units, national government agencies, and stakeholders in the organization of the Cordillera as an autonomous region.",""]],"9":[[1,"363","4","Election Resilience and Reform Package","the Commission on Elections will expand the use of satellite and special registrations, innovate voting modalities, intensify voters' education and information campaigns outside of the election period, and strengthen election laws and procedures to build resilience against health and natural hazards.","Commission on Elections"],[1,"363","4","Political Party and Electoral Competition Reform","policies on strengthening political parties, regulating political dynasties, and enhancing competition in the political sphere will be jointly pursued by the relevant agencies and Congress.","relevant agencies | Congress"]],"10":[[1,"194","4","Business Registration, Licensing, and Social Protection Support for Enterprises and Gig Workers","Facilitate business name registration, licensing, and social protection of enterprises and gig workers (freelancers, contractors, independent professionals), and enable",""],[1,"243","12","Business Registration Process Automation and Streamlining","Expedite efforts to automate and streamline processes for business registration, renewal, closure, and pivot",""],[1,"243","14","Regulatory Rationalization and Streamlining","Eliminate redundant, duplicative and overlapping regulations",""],[1,"243","17","Philippine Ease of Doing Business Reporting System","Establish the Philippine Ease of Doing Business Reporting System",""],[1,"243","18","National Regulatory Management System Policy Implementation","Implement the National Policy on Regulatory Management System",""],[1,"247","6","Business Registration and Lifecycle Process Automation","Expedite efforts to automate and streamline processes for business registration, renewal, closure, and pivots",""],[1,"247","7","Automation and Streamlining of Government Services","National government agencies (NGA) and LGUs will fully implement existing government programs on the automation and streamlining of government services.",""],[1,"247","8","Philippine Business Hub for Business Registration and Licensing Simplification","The Philippine Business Hub will facilitate ease of compliance with the regulatory and licensing requirements covering the full life cycle of a business from initial registration to closure, as well as in facilitating necessary changes to business purpose, or pivoting of operations to respond to opportunities or challenges in the market environment and to encourage and facilitate the entry and re-entry of MSMEs, especially as the economy recovers and moves forward from the pandemic.",""],[1,"248","1","Regulatory Rationalization Reform","Eliminate redundant, duplicative, and overlapping regulations",""],[1,"248","2","Permit and Licensing Streamlining and Paperless Transaction Reform","NGAs and LGUs, with the guidance of the ARTA and DICT, will expedite the elimination of redundant and superfluous permits and licensing steps, automate procedures, promote paperless transactions, and ensure that regulatory fees are transparent, just, reasonable, and based only on the actual cost incurred by the government in providing the service.","ARTA | DICT | NGAs | LGUs"],[1,"248","2","Whole-of-Government Regulatory Simplification Approach","ARTA will continue to take a whole-of-government approach to minimize as well as eliminate redundant, duplicative, and overlapping regulations.","ARTA"],[1,"248","2","Program NEHEMIA for Priority Sectors","It will continue Program NEHEMIA for priority sectors, including transportation, telecommunications infrastructure, and financial technology.",""],[1,"248","2","Modernizing Government Regulations Program","The Development Academy of the Philippines (DAP), NEDA, and DBM will continue to implement the Modernizing Government Regulations Program, which examines regulations with the goal of streamlining unnecessary rules, reducing compliance costs, and constantly improving good regulatory practices across NGAs and LGUs.","Development Academy of the Philippines (DAP) | NEDA | DBM"],[1,"248","3","Philippine EODB Reporting System","The government will establish and fully implement the Philippine EODB Reporting System.",""],[1,"248","4","National Regulatory Management System Policy Implementation","Implement the National Policy on Regulatory Management System",""],[1,"248","5","National Policy on Regulatory Management System Capacity Building","Toward this, the government will build its capacity to implement the NPRMS.",""],[1,"248","5","Philippine Business Regulations Information System Rollout","The Philippine Business Regulations Information System, a web-based platform that ensures the dissemination of and access to information on regulatory management system and changes in laws and regulations relevant to the public, will also be rolled out and implemented.",""],[1,"249","2","Whole-of-Nation Red Tape Elimination Initiative","The government shall continue to work with the private sector and the academe to adopt a whole-of-nation approach to eliminate red tape in the government as well as in private",""],[1,"249","3","Private Sector Champions and Volunteer Complaint Reception Network","ARTA shall expand its roster of private sector champions and volunteers, who are authorized to receive complaints in relation to EODB-EGSD and help promote and raise awareness on ARTA initiatives.",""],[1,"249","3","Academic Partnership for Ease of Doing Business Outreach","It shall also partner with academic institutions to augment the agency's reach in promoting ease of doing business and anti-red tape practices in the country.",""],[1,"261","1","Business Environment Improvement Strategy","In order to push for economic transformation in a post-pandemic context, a favorable business environment is required.",""],[1,"306","10","Administrative Process Streamlining and Licensing Reform","Streamline bureaucratic processes and relax the administrative procedures and licensing requirements to ease market entry.",""],[1,"371","12","Philippine Business Hub Central Business Portal","The Philippine Business Hub - Central Business Portal (https://business.gov.ph/home) serves as a central system to receive applications and capture application data involving business-related transactions.",""],[1,"431","13","Regulatory Governance Reform Initiative","A regulatory reform initiative that aims to make broad-based improvements in national productivity and competitiveness by examining regulations and identifying possible regulatory governance reforms.",""],[1,"432","4","Sectoral Streamlining and Anti-Red Tape Reform","A sectoral-based streamlining effort which targets to reduce the time, cost, requirements, and procedures in sectors of economic and social significance by 52 percent within 52 weeks.",""],[1,"432","16","Standardization, Accreditation, Testing, Certification, and Measurement Framework","Refers to policy, legal, regulatory, and administrative frameworks, and the institutional arrangements, public and private, to implement standardization, accreditation, and totality of the testing, certification, and measurement necessary to provide acceptable evidence that products and services meet the defined government and market standards.",""],[1,"432","19","Single-Window Customs Cargo Release System","A system that enables a single submission of data and information that is synchronously processed, resulting in a single point of decision for the release of cargoes by Customs, based on decisions made by other Departments and Agencies of government and communicated in a timely manner to Customs.",""]],"11":[[1,"343","13","Penal Facilities Construction and Repair Programme","Undertake construction and repair of penal facilities",""],[1,"343","16","Unified Penology and Corrections System","Establish a unified penology and corrections system",""],[1,"343","18","Justice Sector Human Resource Allocation Improvement","Improve human resource allocation in the justice sector",""],[1,"343","20","Operationalize the National Preventive Mechanism","Operationalize the National Preventive Mechanism",""],[1,"349","1","Penal Facilities Construction and Repair Programme","Undertake construction and repair of penal facilities",""],[1,"349","2","Penal Facilities Expansion and Construction Programme","The government will expand existing penal facilities and establish new ones to house the inmate population adequately.",""],[1,"349","2","Standards-Based Penal Facility Construction and Repair","Construction and repair of penal facilities will adhere to international standards56 to guarantee dignity and health of detainees, as well as support effective rehabilitation and social re-integration of PDL.",""],[1,"349","2","Digitalization of Jail Records","Likewise, concerned agencies will adopt digitalization of jail records.",""],[1,"349","2","Interagency Budget Support for Penal Facility Implementation","the DOJ, the DILG, and the LGUs will also secure the required annual budgetary allocation and seek the assistance of the Department of Public Works and Highways and the DICT to ensure uninterrupted project implementation.","DOJ | DILG | LGUs | Department of Public Works and Highways | DICT"],[1,"349","3","Unified Prison and Rehabilitation Agency","A single agency will be created to manage all seven national prisons and 926 city, district, municipal, and provincial jails, as well as administer rehabilitation programs for convicted offenders.",""],[1,"349","3","Court-Prison Information Sharing Mechanism","This new agency and the courts will work together through information sharing to guarantee the timely release of detainees or convicted offenders.",""],[1,"349","4","National Preventive Mechanism Operationalization","Operationalize the National Preventive Mechanism",""],[1,"349","5","Anti-Torture Compliance Legislation","Champions in Congress will be tapped to enact a law that will comply with the UN Convention Against Torture and Other Cruel, Inhuman, or Degrading Treatment or Punishment (UN CAT) and its Optional Protocol (OPCAT).",""]],"12":[[1,"216","6","Virology and Vaccine Institute Establishment","Establishing the Virology and Vaccine Institute of the Philippines [VIP]",""],[1,"216","7","Virology Innovation Program","The creation of the VIP will make the Philippines become globally competitive in the field of Science and Technology, particularly in virology, when it comes to detecting, identifying, and responding to viruses that affect our people and our resources.",""]],"13":[[1,"314","5","Equitable Health and Educational Infrastructure Access Initiative","Ensure equitable access to health and educational infrastructure, in partnership with the private sector",""],[1,"314","6","Health Care Provider Network Establishment","In line with the Universal Health Care Act, a health care provider network will be established in every province or highly urbanized city to ensure comprehensive and",""],[1,"314","7","Primary Care Network and Health Facility Coordination","LGUs and private providers will work with the national government to ensure that the primary care network (barangay health stations and primary health care facilities), hospitals, standalone or specialized facilities, and other ancillary facilities (i.e., private medical outpatient clinics, infirmaries, birthing homes, dental clinics), whether publicly or privately",""],[1,"315","2","Regular Needs Assessment for Health Facilities","A comprehensive needs assessment of critical health facilities involved in service delivery networks will be regularly conducted.",""],[1,"315","2","Health Facilities Enhancement Program","The assessment results will form part of the basis for determining which facilities will be constructed upgraded, or expanded under the Health Facilities Enhancement Program (HFEP).",""],[1,"315","2","National Allocation Framework for Health Infrastructure Support","National government support for health infrastructure will be guided by the National Allocation Framework, which gives priority to low-capacity and high-gap areas.",""],[1,"315","3","Telemedicine and Remote Health Care Expansion","Multisectoral partnerships will also be pursued to deliver telemedicine, remote health care services, emergency medical service through ambulance and patient transport services, and other innovations for health.",""],[1,"315","3","Health Financing Guidance for Underserved Areas","The national government will issue guidance regarding appropriate financing for such services to reach more underserved and unserved areas with timely healthcare.",""],[1,"424","6","Public Health Event Surveillance and Rapid Information Capture System","Organized and rapid capture of information about events that are a potential risk to public health; can be rumours and other ad-hoc reports transmitted through formal channels (i.e. established routine reporting systems) and informal channels (i.e. media, health workers and nongovernmental organizations reports), including events related to the occurrence of disease in humans, and events related to potential exposure for humans.",""],[1,"427","5","Philippine Health Facility Development Plan","A priority program of the DOH, attempting to address perennial shortages in health facilities by augmenting capital investments in the national and LGU health facilities.","DOH"],[1,"433","13","Fee-Free Basic and Ward Accommodation Policy","No other fees or expenses, including professional fees, shall be charged to all members admitted in any basic or ward accommodations.",""],[1,"436","11","Integrated Local Health Systems","The private sector shall be encouraged to participate in the integrated local health system through a contractual arrangement with the P/CWHS.",""]],"14":[[1,"19","5","Agricultural Sector Modernization","The PDP identifies the policies, programs, and legislative priorities required to modernize the agricultural sector (Chapter 5),",""],[1,"40","10","Agriculture and Agribusiness Modernization Programme","Agriculture and agribusiness will be modernized (Chapter 5).",""],[1,"40","10","Innovation Hubs and Farm Demonstration Sites Expansion","More innovation hubs and farm demonstration sites will be established and the Province-led Agriculture and Fisheries Extension System will be strengthened.",""],[1,"40","10","Province-led Agriculture and Fisheries Extension System Strengthening","More innovation hubs and farm demonstration sites will be established and the Province-led Agriculture and Fisheries Extension System will be strengthened.",""],[1,"40","10","Blue Economy Development and Fisheries Management Implementation","The blue economy will be developed with the full implementation of the Fisheries Management Act plans, and the upgrading of Technology Outreach Stations, and National Technology Centers, among others.",""],[1,"40","10","Technology Outreach Stations and National Technology Centers Upgrading","The blue economy will be developed with the full implementation of the Fisheries Management Act plans, and the upgrading of Technology Outreach Stations, and National Technology Centers, among others.",""],[1,"40","10","Primary Producer Value-Addition and Market Linkage Support","Opportunities for greater value-adding will be created by expanding business partnerships between primary producers and other entrepreneurs, and by strengthening the capacity of primary producers to process raw materials, understand markets, and ensure that food safety and quality standards are met.",""],[1,"41","1","Mobile Platform Support for Marketing, Payment, and Delivery","Use of mobile platforms and channels will be encouraged for marketing, payment, and product delivery.",""],[1,"41","1","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Planning, R&D, Extension, Monitoring, and Regulation","Institutional capacity to formulate plans, conduct R&D, provide extension services, and undertake monitoring and regulation will be enhanced with the use of modern technology and better information systems.",""],[1,"102","27","Agriculture and Fisheries Productivity and Resilience Interventions","The interventions to be pursued include the (a) diversification of",""],[1,"102","28","Farm Consolidation and Agricultural Modernization Measures","consolidation and clustering of farms to take advantage of economies of scale; and (c) adoption of improved technologies to modernize the sector.",""],[1,"102","28","Agricultural Input Access and Land Titling Improvement","Access of primary producers to production inputs shall also be improved, in conjunction with efforts to hasten land titling, improve water management, utilize farm and non-farm wastes and biological",""],[1,"103","1","Blue Economy Development Prioritization","The development of the blue economy, which is a critical source of fisheries and aquaculture products, shall also be prioritized.",""],[1,"103","2","Climate- and Disaster-Resilient Technology Expansion","the creation and adoption of climate- and disaster-resilient technologies shall be expanded to improve the resiliency of the agriculture and fisheries sector",""],[1,"103","2","Early Warning Systems and Anticipatory Mechanisms Development","This will be accompanied by the development and mainstreaming of early warning systems and anticipatory mechanisms",""],[1,"103","5","Promotion of Non-Agricultural Urban Food Production","Production in non-agricultural areas, such as urban farming, vertical or rooftop gardening, and school and community gardening, shall be further promoted for subsistence supply",""],[1,"103","6","Household and Community Urban Food Production Support","Households and communities will likewise be encouraged to till idle or vacant lots for food.",""],[1,"103","6","Starter Kits and Skills Training for Food Production","In this endeavor, the government shall provide production inputs, such as seeds or seedlings, soil, compost, and initial stock (e.g., small ruminants, chicken, and ducks) as starter kits, complemented with skills training (e.g., sowing of seeds and proper management, composting, and pest disease management).",""],[1,"108","7","Urban Agriculture Law Enactment","Enactment of Urban Agriculture Law",""],[1,"108","8","Urban Agriculture and Vertical Farming Promotion Law","The proposed law aims to promote urban agriculture and vertical farming in the country's metropolitan areas as an instrument to contribute to attaining food security.",""],[1,"122","10","Fuel Discount for Farmers and Fisherfolk Program","Includes (a) DA's Fuel Discount for Farmers and Fisherfolk Program","DA"],[1,"147","2","Holistic Agri-Food System Development Measures","In the next six years, sound agricultural development through holistic agri-food system measures espoused in the National Agriculture and Fisheries Modernization and Industrialization Plan (NAFMIP) 2021-2030 will be pursued, with the ultimate objective of raising the level of income of primary producers (i.e., farmers and fisherfolk) beyond the poverty threshold.",""],[1,"150","4","Holistic Agriculture, Fisheries, and Forestry Development Planning","Moving forward, the DA's programs and projects will build on the holistic approach to AFF development as embodied in the NAFMIP and other road maps for the major AFF sectors (e.g., National Irrigation Master Plan).",""],[1,"151","1","Whole-of-Society Agricultural Modernization and Agribusiness Development","The Plan pursues a whole-of-society approach in modernizing agriculture and agribusiness, emphasizing the crucial role of both the government and private sector in enhancing the efficiency of AFF production, expanding access to markets and AFF-based",""],[1,"151","2","Agricultural Institutions Strengthening and Agribusiness Modernization Strategy","This will be complemented with strategies to strengthen agricultural institutions that will enable the modernization of the country's agriculture and agribusiness.",""],[1,"152","1","Integrated Farming Systems and Commodity System Planning","This entails the (a) operationalization of various integrated farming systems and commodity system-based planning approach in the production of food and non-food commodities, value-adding, and other segments of the value chain; (b) cascading AFF planning tools at the regional and provincial levels; and (c) scaling-up value chain analyses to guide and ensure strategic interventions.",""],[1,"167","28","Agribusiness Roadmap Update","Update agribusiness roadmaps",""]],"15":[[1,"151","10","Primary Producer Participation in Value Addition for AFF Products","Create opportunities for the participation of primary producers in value adding of AFF products",""],[1,"151","25","Agricultural Income Diversification and Farm Consolidation Programme","Diversification of income sources will be intensified, economies of scale through farm consolidation and clustering will be pursued, and innovative technologies will be adopted to enhance efficiency of resource use and improve the sector's productivity.",""],[1,"152","2","Farm and Fisheries Consolidation and Clustering","the government will: (a) strengthen support for bridging institutions, such as cooperatives and farmers associations, as channels for technology diffusion; and (b) institutionalize at the level of smallholder primary producers the implementation of farm and fisheries consolidation and clustering in the programs and projects of rural development agencies.",""],[1,"152","2","Private Sector Engagement with Smallholder Producers","The DA and DAR will also continue to promote private sector engagement with smallholder primary producers through agribusiness venture agreements and sugar block farms, among other modalities.","DA | DAR"],[1,"153","4","Primary Producer Participation in Value-Adding for Agricultural Products","Create opportunities for the participation of primary producers in value-adding of AFF products",""],[1,"153","5","Primary Producer Value-Addition Support Programme","To this end, value-adding activities of primary producers will be intensified by (a) piloting toll-based processing facilities and investing in these through build-operate-transfer schemes; (b) developing domestic industries to use local materials for packaging (e.g., bamboo, seaweeds) and to fabricate farm and processing machinery and equipment; (c) expanding business partnerships between the private sector and primary producers (e.g., small brother-big brother arrangements, block farms, private sector-led contract",""],[1,"153","6","Smallholder Primary Producer Capacity Building","strengthening the capacity of smallholder primary producers to process raw materials, understand markets, and ensure that food safety and quality standards are met.",""],[1,"153","6","Inclusive Value Chain Livelihood and Entrepreneurship Support","These activities will also expand livelihood and entrepreneurial opportunities that can be made available and accessible for vulnerable groups-particularly women, IPs, and the youth-and increase their participation along the value chains.",""],[1,"158","30","Youth Agricultural Engagement and Agribusiness Support Programme","This aims to [a] encourage the youth to pursue a career or engage in activities related to agriculture; [b] ensure participation of young farmers and fisherfolk in policy formulation and program implementation relative to the agriculture sector; and [c] provide institutional support for agribusiness and agri- entrepreneurship initiatives of the youth to realize fully their role as agents and partners for development.",""]],"16":[[1,"151","14","Improved Technology Adoption Facilitation","Create and facilitate adoption of improved technology",""],[1,"151","24","Agricultural Education and Job-Skills Matching Support","Enhance support to agricultural education and job-skills matching",""],[1,"152","3","Scale Up Modern Production Technologies for Primary Producers","The adoption of modern production technologies responsive to the needs of primary producers shall be scaled up (See Chapter 8) to reduce the threat of diseases, increase sustainability and yield, and reduce the overall cost of operation.",""],[1,"152","3","Deepen Public-Private Partnerships for Agricultural Technology Delivery","Thus, public-private partnerships will be deepened to address the weak spot- the \"last mile\" of technology delivery-by increasing investments in RDE for biological, physical, and digital technologies, establishing more innovation hubs and demonstration sites, and strengthening the Province-led Agriculture and Fisheries Extension System (PAFES).",""],[1,"157","3","Agricultural Cooperative Coordination and Extension Strengthening","Agricultural cooperatives will also be strengthened by enhancing the coordination mechanisms between the DA and Cooperative Development Authority, with the DA assuming a greater role in steering the needed development interventions to organize smallholder farmers and link them with investors.","DA | Cooperative Development Authority"],[1,"157","3","Devolved Agricultural Extension Service Delivery","This strategy also ensures horizontal and vertical coordination and multi-sectoral approach in the delivery of devolved extension services, given the Supreme Court ruling on the Mandanas-Garcia case.",""],[1,"157","3","Agricultural Extension Worker Capacity and Training Programme","This covers capacity and competency-enhancing interventions for the national and local agriculture extension workers and collaborative training engagements with other stakeholders (e.g., private sector and academe).",""],[1,"157","4","Skills Needs Assessment for Primary Producers","Education and Skills Development Authority's (TESDA) skills needs assessment to guide training and other capacity building activities for primary producers.",""],[1,"157","6","Industry-Responsive Agri-Fishery Skills Matching and Curriculum Reform","improving the responsiveness of job and skills matching programs through the participation of industry in formulating curricula in agri-fishery schools",""],[1,"157","6","Needs-Based Capacity Development for Farmers, Fisherfolk, and MSMEs","redeveloping education and training services by adopting needs-based capacity development programs for small farmers and fisherfolk and micro, small, and medium enterprises",""],[1,"157","6","Modern Agri-Fishery School Capacity Upgrading","capacitating schools for teaching modern agri-fishery in the context of agri-food systems, with focus on innovations for best and modern techniques and applications as well as commercialization of modern farming and fishing technologies",""],[1,"158","18","Provincial Agriculture and Fisheries Extension System Funding Support","This aims to provide additional funding for provincial LGUs to incentivize them in investing in and/or improving the provincial agri-fishery extension system.",""],[1,"158","18","Province-led Agriculture and Fisheries Extension Systems Institutionalization","This builds on the draft Executive Order institutionalizing the Province-led Agriculture and Fisheries Extension Systems and mandating its implementation across all provinces.",""]],"17":[[1,"113","23","Free Agricultural Insurance Expansion","Expand coverage of free agricultural insurance for qualified farmers and fisherfolk",""],[1,"118","4","Free Agricultural Insurance Coverage Expansion","Expand coverage of free agricultural insurance for qualified farmers and fisherfolk",""],[1,"118","5","Registry System Update for Agricultural Insurance Beneficiaries","The government, through the DA, is reviewing and updating the Registry System for Basic Sectors in Agriculture to come up with a clean list of beneficiaries for free insurance to be delivered by the Philippine Crop Insurance Corporation.","DA"],[1,"118","5","Agricultural Insurance Coverage Expansion and Product Enhancement","Expansion of coverage shall also be facilitated through an updated list and agricultural insurance products shall be enhanced.",""],[1,"150","4","Digital Access to Agricultural Finance and Markets","This plan will build on these positive developments to formulate strategies to address the dysfunctionalities of the existing agri-food system.",""],[1,"151","15","Primary Producers Access to Production Inputs Support","Improve access of primary producers to production requirements (e.g., land, water, renewable energy, and credit)",""],[1,"151","21","Innovative Insurance Schemes Development","Develop innovative insurance schemes",""],[1,"153","2","Capital Access Expansion Measures for the Sector","Moreover, the sector's access to capital will be further increased by (a) expanding the",""],[1,"153","3","Innovative Financing Schemes for Smallholder Producers","coverage of innovative financing schemes and processes for smallholder primary producers (e.g., crowdsourcing, digital banking, and DA-Agricultural Credit Policy Council's credit programs);",""],[1,"153","3","Expansion of Rural Banking Network","increasing the physical network of banks and financial institutions in rural areas;",""],[1,"153","3","Bank Data Sharing for Agricultural Finance","facilitating data sharing among banks and formal financial institutions to gain granular knowledge of the financial services needs of the sector;",""],[1,"153","3","Agricultural Guarantee Services and Credit Surety Funds","intensifying agricultural guarantee services and establishing more credit surety funds to mitigate risks faced by financial institutions in extending unsecured loans to farmers and fisherfolk.",""],[1,"156","3","Index- and Weather-Based Crop Insurance Schemes","the Philippine Crop Insurance Corporation (PCIC) will implement index- and weather-based insurance schemes to provide adequate and timely compensation to primary producers.",""],[1,"156","3","Digitalization of Insurance Programs","Greater digitalization of insurance programs will also be pursued for faster transactions and provision of indemnity payments.",""],[1,"158","20","Increase Authorized Capital of the Land Bank of the Philippines","This aims to increase the authorized capital of the bank for better funding assistance in government programs for primary producers.",""],[1,"158","20","Expand Land Bank of the Philippines as a Government Financial Institution for Agricultural and Rural Development","This will also enable LBP to operate as a government financial institution responsible for broad-based agricultural and rural development as well as financial inclusion.",""],[1,"158","28","Agricultural Insurance Expansion by PCIC","This aims to strengthen and expand the agricultural insurance provision by the PCIC to protect farmers and fisherfolk from losses and damage brought about by natural calamities.",""],[1,"160","10","Agricultural Loan Access Programs","Production Loan Easy Access, Survival and Recovery Loan, Kapital Access for Young Agripreneurs, and Agri-Negosyo Loan Program, among others.",""]],"18":[[1,"102","24","Food Labeling and Food Safety Promotion Measures","Intensify promotion of food labeling and food safety measures",""],[1,"103","7","Risk-Based Inspection System for Imported Agri-Food Commodities","This strategy includes the government's full adoption of a risk-based inspection system in lieu of a 100 percent physical inspection.",""],[1,"106","2","Food Labeling and Food Safety Promotion","Intensify promotion of food labeling and food safety measures",""],[1,"106","3","Strengthen Implementation of Existing Measures","The government shall strengthen the implementation of measures and other existing",""],[1,"106","4","Food Safety and Quality Regulatory Strengthening","This will cover measures on the traceability of products to support the targeting of regulations and regulatory actions to specific sources of risks.",""],[1,"106","4","Regulatory Service Harmonization and Standards Development","There is also a need to strengthen, harmonize, and streamline regulatory services and develop standards to ensure safe and quality products, facilitate trade, and promote ease of doing business.",""],[1,"106","4","Institutional and Human Capacity Enhancement for Food Regulation","Institutional and human capacities of key agencies (e.g., Department of Health [DOH],19 DA,20 and DTI21) to enforce regulations and enhance consumer awareness on the safety and quality of food products shall be enhanced.","Department of Health [DOH] | DA | DTI"],[1,"122","19","Food, Drug, and Cosmetics Standards Setting","The DOH, through the Food and Drug Administration (FDA), establishes standards for processed food, drugs, and cosmetics.","DOH | Food and Drug Administration (FDA)"],[1,"122","20","Agriculture and Food Safety Standards Development and Enforcement","The DA's Bureau of Agriculture and Fisheries Standards develops standards for agriculture and agriculture-related products including fruits and vegetables and grains.",""],[1,"122","20","Food Safety Standards Enforcement for Animal, Fish, and Plant Foods","The Bureau of Animal Industry, National Dairy Authority, National Meat Inspection Service, Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources, and Bureau of Plant Industry enforce food safety standards and regulations on food derived from animals, fresh fish and seafood, and plant foods.",""],[1,"122","21","National Standardization Activities","The DTI's Bureau of Philippine Standards formulates standards for food and other categories (e.g., building, construction, and transport products).","DTI's Bureau of Philippine Standards | DOH | DA"],[1,"154","4","Agri-Food Regulatory Modernization and Standards Adoption","A regulatory system necessary to modernize the agri-food system should put in place enabling policies and institutions conducive for private sector investments",""],[1,"155","1","Ease of Doing Business and Efficient Government Service Delivery Act Implementation","Supporting these interventions is the strengthened implementation of Ease of Doing Business and Efficient Government Service Delivery Act (RA 11032)",""],[1,"155","2","Protection of Local Agricultural Production from Unfair Competition and Price Manipulation","Protect local AFF against unfair competition and supply/price manipulation",""],[1,"155","3","Enforcement Against Unfair Agricultural Market Practices","The government will strictly enforce measures intended to minimize or stop illegal and unfair practices that disincentivize local farmers and investors such as smuggling, hoarding, dumping, and other forms of unfair practices",""],[1,"158","22","Livestock and Poultry Development Law","The proposed law aims to [a] improve the availability and affordability of nutritious and safe LPD products; [b] pursue better government response to pests and diseases; and [c] increase the incomes of LPD and corn farmers.",""],[1,"158","26","Fishery Products Trade Law","The proposed law aims to improve efficiency and transparency in the trade of fishery products that would reduce trade costs and enable the timely importation of fish to augment domestic production in cases of supply deficiency.",""]],"19":[[1,"28","2","Social Protection Programme Expansion","we need to fast-track investments in ... efficient social protection programs",""],[1,"39","25","Individual and Family Capability Development Programme","Capabilities of individuals and families will be developed to enable them to participate in growth opportunities",""],[1,"39","30","Social Protection System Efficiency and Digitalization Reform","Social protection (SP) systems will be made more efficient with improved targeting and digitalized processes for faster response to the needs of the most vulnerable (Chapter 3).",""],[1,"40","2","Strengthening of Social Protection Systems","Social protection systems will be strengthened (Subchapter 3.2).",""],[1,"40","2","Targeted Vulnerable Group Social Protection Programs","There will be programs to reduce the risks faced by specific vulnerable groups (persons with disability, women, children, indigenous persons, persons in geographically isolated and disadvantaged areas [GIDA], migrant workers, etc.), and to mitigate the impact in case the risk materializes.",""],[1,"40","2","Universal Integrated Social Protection System","A universal, modern, and integrated SP system will be established to improve targeting, rationalize interventions, and facilitate the timely delivery of SP services.",""],[1,"99","1","Transformative Social Protection System","In addition, the country needs a transformative social protection system that empowers every Filipino to prevent, respond to, and recover from possible shocks.",""],[1,"101","1","Financial Assistance for Vulnerable Agricultural Households","Complementary interventions of the DA and DSWD extended financial assistance to vulnerable groups, including farmers and fisherfolk,10 to help them cope with the surge in commodity prices","Department of Agriculture | Department of Social Welfare and Development"],[1,"113","3","Rationalized and Integrated Social Protection System","implementing a rationalized and integrated social protection system will be a key strategy",""],[1,"113","29","Adaptive Shock Responsive Roadmap Implementation","Implement and operationalize the Adaptive Shock Responsive Roadmap",""],[1,"114","1","Universal and Integrated Social Protection System","the government aims to provide a universal and integrated SP system, which can manage various present and future risks and shocks confronting Filipinos and re-engineered to link and enhance existing SP systems.",""],[1,"114","3","Standard Menu of Rationalized Social Protection Floor Programs","Establish a standard menu of rationalized programs for the social protection floor guarantees",""],[1,"114","4","Social Protection Program Review and Rationalization","Current SP programs shall be reviewed for possible overlaps, duplications, gaps, and relevance, given the limited fiscal resources and expanding needs for social protection.",""],[1,"114","4","Social Protection Program Rationalization and Reorganization","For the same reasons, the possibilities for rationalizing, merging, or reorganizing some SP programs shall also be explored.",""],[1,"114","4","SP Floor Guarantee Coordination Package","The proposed package of programs for each SP floor guarantee will improve coordination among agencies and maximize impact for beneficiaries.",""],[1,"114","4","Strengthening of Selected Social Protection Programs","Programs that are selected in the package shall be strengthened at each stage- from targeting, to enrolment, to delivery.",""],[1,"114","4","Mainstreaming of Anticipatory and Adaptive Social Protection Programs","Innovative programs such as anticipatory and adaptive (shock-responsive) programs shall also be encouraged and mainstreamed.",""],[1,"114","4","Institutionalization of Social Protection Monitoring and Evaluation","An important component of this strategy is the institutionalization of monitoring and evaluation of SP programs.",""],[1,"119","5","Adaptive Shock Responsive Roadmap Implementation","Implement and operationalize the Adaptive Shock Responsive Roadmap",""],[1,"119","7","Pilot Testing of Integrated Social Protection Approaches","implement pilot testing of integrated social protection approaches from regular and ancillary programs and services in selected areas around the country.",""],[1,"120","12","Social Protection System Rationalization and Integration Framework","The need for a legal framework that will rationalize SP programs toward an integrated system where there is: · Recognition of SP as a basic right provided by the state; · Institutionalization of SP floor; · Establishment of effective coordination structures; · Establishment and updating of social registries; · Enhancement of digital payment platforms; and · Sustainable financing (See Subchapter 11.1) and partnerships with the private and civil society sectors",""],[1,"122","10","Targeted Cash Transfer Program","DSWD's Targeted Cash Transfer Program","DSWD"],[1,"122","10","Assistance to Individuals in Crisis Situation","and Assistance to Individuals in Crisis Situation","DSWD"],[1,"122","10","Inter-Agency Committee for Targeted Cash Transfer Program Oversight","An Inter-Agency Committee-chaired by the Department of Finance (DOF) and co-chaired by the National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) with the DSWD, Department of Budget and Management (DBM), Bureau of the Treasury (BTr), and Land Bank of the Philippines (LBP) as members- oversees the implementation of the Targeted Cash Transfer Program.","Department of Finance (DOF) | National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) | DSWD | Department of Budget and Management (DBM) | Bureau of the Treasury (BTr) | Land Bank of the Philippines (LBP)"]],"20":[[1,"113","16","Mental Health and Psychosocial Services in Disaster Response Package","Ensure the implementation of mental health and psychosocial services in the disaster response package",""],[1,"113","24","Permanent and Resilient Evacuation Centers","Establish permanent and resilient evacuation centers",""],[1,"118","10","Mental Health and Psychosocial Services in Disaster Response Package","Ensure the implementation of mental health and psychosocial services in the disaster response package",""],[1,"119","1","Gender-Sensitive and Child-Friendly Psychosocial Support for Disaster Victims","the government shall ensure the provision of gender-sensitive and child-friendly mental health and psychosocial services to victims of disasters.",""],[1,"119","2","Construction of Permanent Resilient Evacuation Centers","appropriate facilities shall be built to shelter the affected families.",""],[1,"121","5","Typhoon-Resilient Evacuation Center Construction Programme","This will establish permanent and typhoon-resilient evacuation centers with necessary facilities to avoid the practice of using classrooms during calamities.",""],[1,"121","5","Inclusive Evacuation Center Design Standards","These centers will also take into consideration in their design the welfare of children, women, persons with disability, and the elderly.",""]],"21":[[1,"40","7","Migrant Worker Reintegration Support","Migrant workers will also have access to these opportunities to facilitate their reintegration back into the domestic economy.",""],[1,"73","1","Mutual Recognition Agreement Expansion for Professional Mobility","Additional mutual recognition agreements (MRA) to facilitate the mobility of Filipino professionals within the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) countries and other countries and regions will be initiated.",""]],"22":[[1,"82","10","Basic Services and Social Protection Access Improvement","Improve access to food, health, education, safe drinking water, basic sanitation, social services, social protection, and quality jobs (Ch. 2.1, 2.2, 3.2, 5, 11, 13, 15)",""],[1,"83","2","Basic Human Needs Access Improvement","Access to food, health, education, safe drinking water, basic sanitation, social services, social protection, and quality jobs shall be improved.",""]],"23":[[1,"102","18","Emergency Buffer Stocking of Basic Food Items","Strengthen buffer stocking of rice and other basic food items for emergencies and disasters",""],[1,"103","8","Emergency Buffer Stocking of Basic Food Items","Strengthen buffer stocking of rice and other basic food items for emergencies and disasters",""],[1,"103","9","Rice Buffer Stock Maintenance and Pre-positioning","The National Food Authority (NFA) shall ensure the maintenance of adequate12 rice buffer stock at any given time, as determined by the NFA Council, and strategically pre-position these stocks for easy access during calamities and disasters.",""],[1,"104","1","Emergency Food Pack Distribution","ensure the swift distribution of food packs to distressed families in affected areas.",""],[1,"113","27","Social Protection Program Strengthening and Product Expansion","Strengthen SP programs and introduce relevant products in responding to the pandemic and other health hazards.",""],[1,"113","32","Emergency Financing for Social Protection Programs","Ensure a timely and responsive financing for SP programs in emergencies",""],[1,"114","7","Emergency Social Protection Financing and Response","Ensure a timely response and adequate financing for social protection programs in emergencies",""],[1,"114","8","Social Protection Emergency Financing Mobilization","The government shall mobilize more resources for SP programs through closer coordination with the private and civil society sectors.",""],[1,"114","8","Emergency Social Protection Fund Release Reform","Improvements in the procedures for fund releases during these times shall also be implemented.",""],[1,"119","3","Social Protection Program Strengthening and Product Development","Strengthen social protection programs and introduce relevant products in responding to the pandemic and other health hazards",""],[1,"119","4","Strengthening Social Protection Program Implementation for Health Shocks","the government, in partnership with the private sector, shall strengthen the implementation of SP programs in responding to a health shock or crisis","DOH | DSWD | DTI"],[1,"119","8","Anticipatory Mechanisms and Shock-Responsive Social Protection","Using early warning mechanisms, the government shall implement anticipatory mechanisms and shock-responsive social protection programs to address emergencies.",""]],"24":[[1,"113","17","Anticipatory Shock-Responsive Plans for IDPs and POCs","Prepare anticipatory shook-responsive plans for IDPs and POCs",""],[1,"113","20","Protection Services Implementation Strengthening","Strengthen the implementation of EO 163 (Protection Services for POCs); and RA 11188 (Special Protection of Children in Situations of Armed Conflict)",""],[1,"113","25","Holistic Child Labor Eradication Initiative","Implement a holistic approach to eradicate child labor",""],[1,"117","2","Expanded Social Protection Delivery in GIDAs","The national government, in coordination with the LGUs, shall intensify the provision of SP programs in geographically isolated and disadvantaged areas (GIDAs).",""],[1,"117","2","Convergent Service Delivery for GIDAs","The convergent delivery of services by all concerned agencies (e.g., basic infrastructure by the Department of Public Works and Highways [DPWH] and Department of Transportation) shall be undertaken","Department of Public Works and Highways | Department of Transportation"],[1,"117","2","NGO and Civil Society Partnership for GIDAs","The government shall likewise tap NGOs and other civil society sectors that target people in GIDAs.",""],[1,"117","4","Child Labor Response Programs","A holistic and multi-stakeholder approach shall be implemented for key programs addressing child labor in the country;",""],[1,"117","5","Philippine National Multi-Sectoral Plan for Children in Street Situation","Issues of street children, estimated at 369,242,37 will be addressed through the Philippine National Multi-Sectoral Plan for Children in Street Situation 2021-2025 launched by the Council for the Welfare of Children and its partners in 2021.",""],[1,"117","5","Support for Children in Situations of Armed Conflict under RA 11188","RA 11188 was also passed to respond to the needs of children in situations of armed conflict, and shall be continued.",""],[1,"117","5","Child Mental Health and Psychosocial Support Services","Mental health and psychosocial services shall also be provided to children, especially those who are left behind by OFW parents, those in situations of armed conflict, and in conflict with the law, as well as those who have experienced trauma during disasters.",""],[1,"120","4","Anticipatory Support Programmes for IDPs and Persons of Concern","The government will provide anticipatory programs that will address the needs of internally displaced persons IDPs and persons of concern (POCs) especially in situations",""],[1,"120","5","Dynamic Registry and Early Warning Systems for Conflict-Affected Areas","These will include establishing a dynamic registry, strengthening early warning and delivery systems, and building local capacities of affected areas.",""],[1,"120","6","Implementation Strengthening for Protection Services for POCs and Children in Armed Conflict","Strengthen the implementation of Executive Order 163, series of 2022 (Protection Services for POCs) and RA 11188 (Special Protection of Children in Situations of Armed Conflict)",""],[1,"120","7","Resource Support for Implementation of the New Executive Order and Law","The government shall increase efforts to provide the necessary human and financial resources in the implementation of the new executive order and law.",""]],"26":[[1,"191","31","Transport Digitalization Promotion","Promote digitalization in transport and",""],[1,"194","3","24/7 Port and Airport Agency Operations Streamlining","Streamline requirements and procedures and implement 24/7 operations of agencies at ports and airports to reduce transport and logistics costs.","DTI | Civil Aeronautics Board | Bureau of Customs | Bureau of Animal Industry | Bureau of Plant Industry | Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources"],[1,"194","9","Transportation Safety Board Establishment","Establish a Transportation Safety Board to serve as an independent investigatory, research, and standards-setting agency dedicated to promoting safety in all modes of transportation (i.e., land, sea, air, and railway).",""],[1,"198","4","Foreign Capital Mobilization for Infrastructure Modernization","Secure foreign capital to modernize infrastructure, fleet, and equipment and position the Philippines as a strategic hub for aviation, shipping and maritime, and logistics services",""],[1,"198","5","Public Services and Transport Regulatory Reform for Investment Attraction","Leverage the Public Services Act, FIA, and RTLA amendments to attract global partners and innovators (See Chapter 9), to modernize services and to reduce overall transport and logistics costs.",""],[1,"198","6","Foreign Capital Support for Aviation, Maritime, and Shipping Capacity Expansion","Foreign capital shall be utilized to increase the capacity of the aviation, maritime, and shipping companies to: (a) invest in green, modern, and resilient hubs, equipment, and fleet; (b) build capabilities to participate in the transportation GVCs (design, maintenance, repair, and overhaul); (c) upgrade and align education and training programs with international standards; (d) promote best safety and security practices; and (e) develop modernized gateways and clusters to attract international logistics, retail, IT-BPM, and tourism companies.",""],[1,"198","7","24/7 Business and Logistics Operations Initiative","Promote 24/7 operations of businesses, including brokerage houses, distribution centers, warehouses, shipping lines offices, and banking facilities.","BOC | BAI | BPI | BFAR"],[1,"198","8","Technology-Enabled Logistics Coordination","Increase utilization of technology in logistics processes to improve coordination among stakeholders (brokers, shipping lines, airlines, cargo consolidator and freight forwarders, and government).","DTI"],[1,"199","1","Digital Trade Transparency and Real-Time Monitoring Initiative","shall collaborate to increase the use of digital technologies, disseminate correct information, and promote real-time monitoring for improved transparency and efficiency in the mobility of goods.",""],[1,"199","2","Transport Terminal Modernization Participation Expansion","Expand participation in the modernization of existing airports, ports, and land transport terminals to reduce overall transportation costs and shipment delays (See Chapter 12).",""],[1,"200","19","Shipping Charge Regulation Reform","This will address the expensive shipping rates in the Philippines due largely to the imposition of \"excessive, arbitrary, and unreasonable\" shipping charges by foreign shipping lines, such as the \"destination and origin charges,\" container deposit fees, container cleaning fees, detention and demurrage charges, and port congestion charges.",""],[1,"305","3","Nautical Highway Improvement Programme","The nautical highway will be improved.",""],[1,"305","3","Seaport Construction and Expansion Programme","Seaports will be constructed and expanded to support economic sectors such as agriculture and trade.",""],[1,"305","3","New Port Linkage and Site Assessment","New linkages and strategic location of new ports will be assessed to create new rural growth areas.",""],[1,"305","3","RORO Facility Capacity Expansion and Digitization","The capacity of RORO facilities will be increased and processes digitized to address congestion and delays.",""],[1,"305","3","Large-Capacity RORO Port Construction","Larger RORO ports will be constructed to accommodate larger-capacity RORO vessels.",""],[1,"305","3","Passenger Ancillary Facilities Upgrade","These will be supported with modern ancillary facilities for passengers.",""],[1,"305","3","Electronic Terminal Management System Streamlining","The application of electronic terminal management systems such as electronic ticketing and manifest submissions will be streamlined.",""],[1,"305","3","Maritime Fleet Replacement and Retrofit Programme","Aging fleets will also be replaced or retrofitted to mitigate the risk of maritime accidents.",""],[1,"305","3","Maritime Industry Development Plan Implementation","Implementation of the Maritime Industry Development Plan will be continued to achieve a more sustainable and globally competitive maritime sector through maritime education, technology, and innovations.",""],[1,"305","5","Nautical Highway Network Development","nautical highway network will be pursued.",""],[1,"305","6","Airport Improvement and Expansion Programme","Existing airports will be improved and new ones will be strategically developed to address future demand.",""],[1,"305","6","Airport Safety Standards Upgrade","Existing airports will be upgraded to meet aerodrome design safety standards set by international and local airport authorities, including development and improvement of access roads.",""],[1,"305","6","Airport PPP Bundling Initiative","Bundling of airports as possible PPP projects will be pursued to encourage private sector investments.",""],[1,"305","7","Gateway and Feeder Airport Development Programme","Gateway airports will be developed and connected to feeder airports to facilitate access to the country's various tourist destinations.",""],[1,"305","7","New Airport Siting and Expansion Planning","Development of new airports will consider optimal sites outside urban areas to allow rooms for future expansion and possible upgrade to international airports.",""],[1,"305","8","Airport Service Standards Adoption","Level of service standards will be adopted in all airports to quantitatively measure the adequacy of airport passenger facilities and plan for the applicable interventions.",""],[1,"305","8","Airport Night-Rating Continuation","To alleviate airport traffic congestion, \"night-rating\" of airports will be continued.",""],[1,"430","14","Integrated Maritime Industry Development Framework","to steer the country's maritime industry toward global competitiveness and sustainable growth through the prioritization of international commitments in the maritime transportation sector and the adoption of integrated approach to development by pooling together the expertise and resources of concerned government agencies, the private sector, and the civil society.",""],[1,"430","16","Integrated IMO Conventions Ratification and Accession Framework","The Executive Order No. 159, s. 2021 was issued to adopt an integrated approach in the ratification and accession to International Maritime Organization Conventions and Instruments, and Reconstitute the Inter-Agency Coordinating Committee for the Purpose.",""],[1,"430","18","Modular Route Capacity Measurement System Development","Aims to develop and design a modular software and other related tools for an effective route capacity measurement system, as part of the modernization plan of Maritime Industry Authority (MARINA) for the Philippine maritime industry through the development of the NAVIS software and incorporation of the necessary models and concepts related to maritime transportation (DOST).","Maritime Industry Authority (MARINA) | DOST"]],"27":[[1,"301","26","Fleet Modernization and Ancillary Services Improvement","Modernize the fleet and provide quality ancillary services",""],[1,"305","1","Public Transport Service Reform and Consolidation","Reforms in the provision of public transport services will be strengthened.",""],[1,"305","2","Public Utility Vehicle Modernization Program Redesign","The Public Utility Vehicle Modernization Program will be re-designed so that the supply of modern public transport can be increased while managing its resulting fiscal impact.",""],[1,"312","4","Electric Vehicle Transition Promotion","The shift from vehicles that rely on conventional fuel modes to electric vehicles will be pursued.",""],[1,"312","5","Comprehensive Roadmap for Electric Vehicle Industry","will implement the Comprehensive Roadmap for Electric Vehicle Industry.",""],[1,"387","2","Public Transport Electrification and Renewable Energy Transition","scaling up and prioritizing electrification of public transport and transition to renewable energy (See Chapter 12)",""]],"28":[[1,"37","7","Local Road Network Development","Communities should be linked to these opportunities through the development of local road networks that reduce the costs of transport, while also adopting active mobility options and e-vehicles.",""],[1,"41","1","Multimodal Transport and Logistics Investment","investments in the sector to promote the interconnectedness of multimodal transport and logistics, particularly for perishable products.",""],[1,"41","5","Transport and Logistics Regulatory Streamlining","Streamlining regulations to allow 24/7 operations of transport and logistics operations will also increase demand.",""],[1,"151","16","Physical and Digital Infrastructure Improvement","Improve physical and digital infrastructure",""],[1,"154","2","Rationalization of AFF Infrastructure Investments","The government will rationalize investments in AFF infrastructure through the",""],[1,"154","3","Agricultural and Fisheries Digitalization and Logistics Upgrade","These are geared toward (a) building more and improving the interconnectedness of multimodal transport and logistics, especially those required for perishable products; (b) upgrading processing, postharvest, and storage facilities with emphasis on cold chain technology, including the operationalization of community fish landing centers across the country; (c) establishing sustainable infrastructures, such as green ports; (d) integrating and improving the interoperability of AFF information systems to harness the Fourth Industrial Revolution technologies (e.g., big data, block chain, and Internet of Things); and (e) promoting and strengthening the capacity of farmers and fisherfolk to use mobile- and web-based platforms for marketing, payment, and product delivery (e.g., Co-opBiz,12 e-KADIWA, GCash).","DA"],[1,"158","16","Farm-to-Market Road Development Program Institutionalization","This seeks to institutionalize the Farm-to-Market Road Development Program and funding commitment.",""]],"29":[[1,"103","7","National Single Window Upgrade and Integration","Moreover, the Bureau of Customs' National Single Window shall be improved and linked with the DA's Trade System.",""],[1,"103","7","Review and Rationalization of Non-Tariff Measures","Overlapping and redundant non-tariff measures shall also be reviewed and rationalized.",""],[1,"103","7","Investment in Manpower and Border Examination Facilities","To improve the efficiency in the implementation of critical non-tariff measures, sufficient investment for manpower and border examination facilities (e.g., Cold Examination Facility in Agriculture) shall be provided.",""],[1,"104","6","Strategically Located Logistics and Postharvest Facilities","the government will strengthen the establishment of strategically located facilities such as interconnected transport systems, wholesale food terminals and trading centers, and other production and postharvest facilities (e.g., complementary food production facilities of the DOST-FNRI)",""],[1,"104","6","Private Sector Food Storage and Marketing Investment Support","Also critical will be complementary private sector investments such as warehouses, cold chains, cold storage and refrigeration facilities, mobile storage, cloud kitchens and mobile marketplaces, rolling stores, processing facilities, and digital marketing channels.",""],[1,"104","7","Promotion of Planning Tools and Information Systems","the use of planning tools and information systems such as the Agricultural and Biosystems Engineering Management Information System,13 shall be promoted",""],[1,"104","7","Streamlining of Facility Registration and Food Safety Requirements","the registration processes required for the construction, establishment, or operation of the necessary facilities and logistics as well as food safety and quality requirements shall be streamlined",""],[1,"277","10","National Single Window Trade Facilitation System","The BOC will intensify its work in facilitating trade using the National Single Window on automated and integrated licensing, permit, clearance, and certification systems.",""],[1,"277","10","National Action Plan on Paperless Trade Agreement Implementation","The BOC's implementation of the National Action Plan on Paperless Trade Agreement will complement this program.",""],[1,"278","1","Customs Process Digitalization Programme","The remaining 15 processes, which include a public auction, issuance of a certificate of shipment, and certification of re-exportation commitment, will also be digitalized.",""],[1,"278","2","Digital Transformation Implementation","The BIR will focus on improving a digital infrastructure for seamless electronic data transmission.",""],[1,"290","2","Unified Logistics Pass and Port Transport Accreditation System","To upgrade the country's logistics network, Unified Logistics Pass (ULP) was launched in 2022 that features a quick response (QR) code issued to cargo trucks.",""],[1,"306","3","Integrated ULP and TAPPP Implementation","The implementation of the ULP and Transport Accreditation, Permit and Pass for Ports (TAPPP) will be made seamless and well-integrated.",""],[1,"441","15","Single Accreditation and Access Pass System for Transport Service Providers","Serves as a single certificate of accreditation (CA), permit to operate (PTO), and vehicle access pass for transport service providers; and is required of transport service providers doing business at ports under the jurisdiction of the Philippine Ports Authority (PPA).",""]],"30":[[1,"297","5","Long-Haul Freight Rail and Waterway Transport Lines","pursuing the plans to establish long-haul freight rail and waterway transport lines will speed up the transport of goods across the country.",""],[1,"304","2","Intermodal Transport Facilities Construction and Upgrade","Intermodal transport facilities will be constructed and upgraded to achieve seamless connectivity.",""],[1,"304","2","Intermodal Linkage and Hub Rationalization","Rationalizing intermodal linkages and hubs will provide order in passenger movement and decrease traffic congestion inside urban centers and across regions.",""],[1,"304","2","Medium- and Long-Distance Rail and Bus Service Provision","Trains and buses shall serve medium- and long-distance travel demands.",""],[1,"304","3","Transit Station and Interchange Design Standards","Design standards for transit stations and interchanges shall be adopted with emphasis on convenient transfers, high levels of service, universal accessibility, gender inclusivity, and sustainability.",""],[1,"304","3","National Automated Fare Collection System Regulation","The standards and regulation for a national automated fare collection system shall be adopted to establish interoperability across all transport modes.",""],[1,"304","7","Metropolitan Mass Transportation Development","Applicable mass transportation systems (i.e., railways, road-based, and ferry systems) will be developed in metropolitan areas.",""],[1,"304","7","Planned Rail Infrastructure Roll-out","The roll-out of the planned rail infrastructure projects will be pursued aggressively.",""],[1,"304","7","National Railway Expansion and Inter-City Rail Construction","Railways will be expanded from north to south and from east to west, connecting growth nodes and strategic infrastructure.",""],[1,"304","7","Specialized Spare Parts and Supplies Policy","Policies will be adopted to ensure availability of highly specialized spare parts and supplies.",""],[1,"304","8","Bus Rapid Transit System Adoption","Bus rapid transit systems will be adopted to enhance the efficient use of public transport vehicles and existing road spaces.",""],[1,"304","8","Ferry System Upgrade and Waterway Transport Development","Existing ferry systems will be upgraded and other coastal and inland waterways transport systems will be established as an alternative sustainable transport mode to further improve the connectivity of ports to the national transport system.",""],[1,"305","5","Road Network Completion and Inter-Island Bridge Construction","The missing links in the road network will be completed and viable inter-island bridges will be constructed.",""],[1,"305","5","Transport Corridor Upgrading and Weighbridge Installation","Road transport corridors leading to airports and ports will be upgraded, including installation of weighbridges to prevent overloading.",""],[1,"305","9","Cargo and Freight Rail Infrastructure Development","Cargo and freight rail infrastructure to connect strategic infrastructure such as ports will be developed and expanded.",""],[1,"305","9","Cargo and Freight Railway Prioritization","Railway development for cargo and freight will be prioritized, particularly for long-distance deliveries.",""],[1,"305","9","Truck Route Establishment for Medium- and Short-Distance Deliveries","Meanwhile, truck routes will be established to service medium- and short-distance deliveries.",""],[1,"306","1","Freight Rail Connection for Inland Cargo Terminals","inland cargo terminals will be connected by freight rail to ease the movement of goods to or from the ports.",""],[1,"306","2","Cold Chain Logistics and Management Facilities Development","Cold chain logistics and management facilities will be developed.",""]],"31":[[1,"306","4","Transport Hub Safety Upgrade","The government will ensure that transport hubs are equipped with additional safety features such as closed-circuit television, baggage scanner, proper lighting, and real-time passenger information system.",""],[1,"306","4","Philippine Coast Guard Modernization Program","The Philippine Coast Guard will pursue its modernization program involving, among others, the procurement of modern air and floating assets and interoperable communication systems.",""],[1,"306","4","Transport Corridor Safety Audits","Safety audits on transport corridors will be continued to inform the allocation of sufficient budgetary support.",""],[1,"306","4","Transport Safety Financing Exploration","Other potential financing sources from congestion pricing and parking levies, among others, will be explored.",""],[1,"317","11","Philippine Transportation Policy Framework","This aims to help achieve a safe, secure, efficient, competitive, dependable, integrated, environmentally sustainable, and people-oriented Philippine transportation system by setting forth policies that will serve as boundary conditions to guide all entities involved in the transportation sector in the exercise of their functions, including the creation of metropolitan transit authorities, and clarifying the roles and responsibilities of national and local governments.",""],[1,"317","14","Public Transportation Rights and Service Standards Framework","This seeks to address the long-standing plight of Filipinos in public transportation by laying down the rights of the commuting public; promoting an efficient, safe, convenient, accessible, and inclusive public transportation system; and setting key performance indicators and service standards for commuters.",""],[1,"317","18","Separation of Regulatory and Operational Functions in Transport","This seeks to separate the regulator and operations functions of existing government entities; empowering local government units to assume greater responsibility and accountability for transportation and mobility outcomes",""],[1,"317","19","Independent Transport Safety and Security Body","Creating an independent body for transport safety and security",""],[1,"317","20","Independent Transport Safety and Security Authority","This will place all transport safety and security matters under a single independent body that will, among others, investigate transport accidents and provide transport safety recommendations, thereby eliminating conflicting and overlapping functions of existing agencies or entities.",""]],"32":[[1,"81","2","Motor Vehicle Inspection Strengthening","strengthening of motor vehicle inspection",""],[1,"81","2","Mass Transport Improvement Initiative","improving mass transport",""],[1,"81","2","Electric Vehicle Promotion Framework","institutionalizing the promotion of e-vehicles through passing the Electric Vehicle Industry Development Act",""],[1,"81","2","Active Mobility Infrastructure Provision","providing the necessary infrastructure to enable active mobility",""],[1,"88","4","Safe and Multi-Modal Road System Design","Road systems shall be designed to provide safe routes in time of emergencies, ample drainage, and sufficient allocation for motorized vehicles, bicycles, and pedestrian uses.",""],[1,"88","7","Public Utility Vehicle Modernization Program Strengthening","These include the strengthening of the existing public utility vehicle modernization program, and expansion of existing mass transport systems and networks.",""],[1,"88","7","Mass Transport System Expansion","These include the strengthening of the existing public utility vehicle modernization program, and expansion of existing mass transport systems and networks.",""],[1,"88","7","Local Road Network and Active Mobility Planning","LGUs shall integrate in their land use plans and infrastructure program the allocation and development of local road networks that adopt active mobility options, such as walking and cycling.",""],[1,"88","7","Local Public Transport Route Planning and Relocation Cost Offset Mechanisms","LGUs shall also reflect in their local public transport route plans the transit options for their communities and adopt mechanisms to offset the impact of increased transportation costs arising from relocation.",""],[1,"88","7","E-Vehicle Adoption with Solar-Powered Charging Stations","LGUs shall adopt the use of e-vehicles supported by solar-powered charging stations to service communities (See Chapter 12).",""],[1,"288","5","Active Transport Promotion and Bicycle Facility Standards","The Department of Health (DOH) has issued guidelines promoting the safe use of active transport, while the Department of Public Works and Highways (DPWH) has issued an order prescribing the standards on the design of bicycle facilities along national roads.","Department of Health | Department of Public Works and Highways"],[1,"288","5","Bike Lane and Active Transport Facilities Financing","To fund the building and maintenance of bike lanes and other active transport facilities, the government allocated total of PHP 3 billion from 2020 to 2022.",""],[1,"296","7","Gender-Responsive Accessible Transport Facility Design","Achieving universally accessible and gender-responsive transport facility designs needs a shift in construction priorities and practices, and in carrying out coordination and advocacy.",""],[1,"304","2","Last-Mile Active Transport Connectivity Enhancement","Last mile connectivity through active transport shall be enhanced to improve access to transit stations and encourage mass transportation usage.",""],[1,"304","4","Active Transport Network Development","Active transport networks will be developed.",""],[1,"304","5","Active Mobility Network Development","Safe and well-connected active mobility networks will be established.",""],[1,"304","6","Pedestrian- and Bike-Friendly Development Incentive Program","Local government units and private developers will be incentivized to have pedestrian-friendly and bikeable developments and programs.",""],[1,"304","6","Local Walkability and Accessibility Measurement Initiative","LGUs will also be encouraged to measure walk scores, walkability, bikeability, and accessibility within their jurisdictions.",""],[1,"307","3","Gender Mainstreaming and Accessibility in Transport Projects","Gender mainstreaming, inclusion, and accessibility will be main considerations in all stages of transport project implementation.",""],[1,"307","3","Integration of Philippine Harmonized Gender and Development Guidelines","The Philippine Harmonized Gender and Development Guidelines (HGDG) will be integrated in all phases of infrastructure project development and implementation.",""],[1,"307","4","Inclusive Mobility Facilities for Commuters","Facilities for the mobility needs of women and men commuters from all sectors (i.e., PWDs, senior citizens, , and indigenous peoples) will be provided.",""],[1,"307","4","Gender and Social Inclusion Monitoring and Evaluation Integration","Gender mainstreaming, inclusion, and accessibility will be integrated in the monitoring and evaluation (M&E) mechanism.",""],[1,"307","4","Sex-Disaggregated and Social Inclusion Data Collection Strengthening","Collection of sex-disaggregated data and other gender and social inclusion data will be strengthened.",""],[1,"307","5","Digital Accessibility and Assistive Technology Promotion","To help in building a digitally connected and inclusive society, the government will promote accessibility and assistive technology innovations.",""],[1,"317","15","Active and Sustainable Transport Law and Standards Reform","Enactment of a law institutionalizing the use of bicycles and other active and sustainable modes of transportation, including updating standards for accessible and safe pathways, and green open spaces",""],[1,"317","16","Non-Motorized Transport Integration Programme","This will be done by providing the necessary infrastructure and support services, establishing safety and design standards for universally accessible and safe pathways and green open spaces, and increasing public awareness on road safety and road sharing among motorists, cyclists, and pedestrians.",""],[1,"323","7","Active Transport Integration Policies","Currently, two major policies have been issued for the continued integration of active transport in the transport infrastructure network: DOH-DILG-DPWH-DOTr Joint Administrative Order No. 2020-0001 covering the promotion and safe use of all types of active transport during and after the COVID-19 pandemic; and DPWH Department Order No. 88, Series of 2020, that prescribes standards for bicycle operating spaces and classification of bicycle facilities in our roadways.",""]],"33":[[1,"323","10","Maritime Route Rationalization and Information System","The Maritime Route Rationalization and Information System estimates the number of vessels required per route through a route capacity measurement system, and determines the number of possible trips, passenger capacity, and perceived profitability of the fleet in a selected route.",""]],"34":[[1,"19","6","Competition and Regulatory Efficiency Reform","enhancing competition and improving regulatory efficiency (Chapter 10)",""],[1,"37","4","Servicification Policy for Economic Clusters","pursuing policies that will build ecosystems around economic clusters identified as potential sources of high growth, to attract more investments and expand its demand for higher productivity jobs.",""],[1,"42","4","Business Regulatory Environment and Level Playing Field Reform","Businesses will be assured of a healthy regulatory environment and a level playing field (Chapter 10).",""],[1,"42","5","Competition Law Enforcement and Regulatory Impact Assessment","consistent enforcement of the Philippine Competition Act and competition-related issuances.",""]],"35":[[1,"167","29","Technology-Enabled Entrepreneurship Promotion","Pursue entrepreneurship leveraging technology-enabled",""],[1,"167","31","Business Network Activation Across Industries","Activate business networks across industries",""],[1,"168","2","Local Domestic Investment Promotion and Business-Matching Activities","Scale up domestic investment promotion and business-matching activities at the local level.","Department of Trade and Industry"],[1,"172","2","Targeted MSME Support Programme","targeted support to MSMEs will be provided to ensure that they remain competitive as they face the challenges of the new normal.",""],[1,"172","3","Business Mentoring and Entrepreneurship Training Program","Business mentoring, and entrepreneurship training to help establish more MSMEs.","DTI"],[1,"196","8","R&D and Startup Ecosystem Support","Increase access to funds and incentives for R&D and startup ecosystem development",""],[1,"196","9","Startup and Innovation Financing Support","Provide funds and incentives, such as low-interest loans, scholarships, research grants, training subsidies to promote startups, digital technology careers, innovations, and research projects that address industry needs.",""],[1,"196","9","Science, Technology, and Innovation Legal Support Framework","Financial capital is provided under the Corporate Recovery and Tax Incentives for Enterprises Act, Innovation Act, Innovation Startup Act, and Digital Workforce Competitiveness Act.",""],[1,"196","9","Technology Commercialization and R&D Capacity Strengthening","These legislations support startup entrepreneurs, scientists, and researchers to achieve STI interventions, accelerate the transfer and commercialization of generated technologies, and strengthen the capability of human resources and institutions to undertake R&D.",""],[1,"196","10","Startup Ecosystem Development Program","Craft and implement programs to build the startup ecosystem.",""],[1,"197","1","Startup Policy Alignment and Harmonization","government agencies toward the alignment and harmonization of startup policies and programs.",""],[1,"197","1","Startup Innovation and Entrepreneurship Promotion","The government shall also provide strong focus on promoting innovation and entrepreneurship, create a more enabling business environment for startups, and allow more foreign participation.",""],[1,"209","20","Business Mentoring Programs","Accelerate business mentoring programs",""],[1,"209","32","Financial and Entrepreneurial Literacy Investment Expansion","Increase investments in financial and entrepreneurial literacy",""],[1,"209","33","Venture Capital Investment Expansion","Increase venture capital investments",""],[1,"214","4","Startup Innovation Financing Support","The private sector will provide support for startup technology innovators through \"angel\" investors (i.e., wealthy individuals with experience in starting up new companies), and venture capital firms specialized in early-stage or \"seed\" investments.",""],[1,"215","2","Startup Mentorship and Coaching Expansion","Strengthen current mentorship and coaching programs for science and technology startups by tapping large corporations to teach the different aspects of business operations.",""],[1,"215","7","Mandatory Credit Allocation for Innovation Development","the private sector will operationalize the Mandatory Credit Allocation for Innovation Development.",""],[1,"216","1","Startup and MSME Loan Support for Innovative Technologies","Subject to applicable regulations of the government, the business and MSME sectors are encouraged to avail of loans under this program to invest in innovative and market-oriented technologies.",""],[1,"216","2","Startup Finance and Entrepreneurship Training Programme","The private sector will increase investments and strengthen programs to enable science and technology startups to make sound financial decisions and expand their business development skills.",""]],"36":[[1,"172","4","MSME-Startup and MNC Linkage Programme","To accelerate innovation and digital transformation, the DTI will link MSMEs with startups through the continued implementation of the Innovative Start Up Act, particularly those that could help improve MSMEs' digital transformation.","DTI"],[1,"172","4","MSME Partnership and Upgrading Support","Tie-ups between MSMEs and large domestic enterprises and multinationals will be strengthened, to facilitate the transfer of know-how, the upgrading of products and processes conforming to international standards or best practices, and the upscaling of MSMEs.",""],[1,"172","4","MSME-Startup Funding and Innovation Partnership Linkages","Similarly, MSMEs and startups will be linked for funding and innovation partnership opportunities.",""],[1,"173","2","MSME Access to Finance Expansion","To address the limited financial resources for the digital transformation of MSMEs, access to finance will be expanded by improving the credit information, collateral registry, and insolvency regime.",""],[1,"173","2","Digital MSME Credit Reporting System Improvement","Government will improve credit reporting systems by enabling the digitalization of MSME data and expanding the movable collateral registry (See Subchapter 11.1).",""],[1,"173","2","Central Bank Risk Database for MSME Lending","The implementation of a central bank risk database will enable de-risking lending to MSMEs.",""],[1,"173","2","Insolvency Regime Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening key agencies' capacity for implementation of the insolvency regime should also be pursued.",""],[1,"173","5","Consumer Protection Regulatory Oversight","provide an environment with sufficient checks from the government to ensure consumer protection",""],[1,"173","6","Enterprise Resilience Capacity-Building and Technical Assistance","The National Wages and Productivity Commission and other relevant agencies will provide capacity building through its Productivity Toolbox, which in turn will aid in the preparation of business continuity plans and strengthen their entrepreneurial capabilities.","National Wages and Productivity Commission | other relevant agencies"],[1,"173","6","Enterprise Supply Chain and Inventory Resilience Support","The government, through capacity-building and technical assistance, will help equip enterprises with skills to improve their ability to tap alternative suppliers, and beef up inventory capacity to insulate against vulnerabilities.",""],[1,"185","10","Improving Access to Finance for Women-Led MSMEs","Particular attention should also be given to improving access to finance of women-led MSMEs.",""],[1,"253","15","MSME Financial Support and Technical Capacity-Building Program","To support the recovery and growth of MSMEs, especially those hit hard by the pandemic, the amendment of the Magna Carta for MSMEs will provide access to support services, including financial support and technical capacity- building programs and reduce barriers to entry of new MSMEs by streamlining permitting requirements.",""],[1,"253","15","MSME Permitting Streamlining Reform","the amendment of the Magna Carta for MSMEs will provide access to support services, including financial support and technical capacity- building programs and reduce barriers to entry of new MSMEs by streamlining permitting requirements.",""],[1,"263","8","Cooperative Technology Adoption for Cost Reduction and Service Access","Adoption of technological innovations will enable cooperatives to reduce costs and improve accessibility of services to the members.",""]],"37":[[1,"19","6","Trade and Investment Promotion Strategy","promoting trade and investments (Chapter 9)",""],[1,"42","1","Trade and Investment Promotion Strategy","Trade and investments will be promoted to improve the competitiveness of domestic industries, increase demand for Philippine products and generate more jobs (Chapter 9).",""],[1,"42","1","International Trade Expansion Strategy","International trade will continue to be a major strategy to expand markets, diversify sources for the cumulation of raw and intermediate materials, and increase competitiveness.",""],[1,"42","1","Regional Trade Agreement Negotiation Policy","Thus, government will adopt a purposive, assertive, and forward-looking position in negotiating regional trade agreements.",""],[1,"42","3","International Investment Promotion Campaign","Government will launch an international campaign (\"Make it Happen in the Philippines\") to raise awareness of the new business climate given the amendments to the FIA, RTLA, PSA, and the CREATE Law.",""],[1,"42","3","Inter-agency Investment Promotion Coordination Committee","The Inter-agency Investment Promotion Coordination Committee will ensure proper alignment of promotion strategies and various ordinances among national and local governments and investment promotion agencies.",""],[1,"178","9","High-Impact Free Trade Agreement and Investment Facilitation Strategy","Trade strategies that support industrial development include pursuing high-impact Free Trade Agreements (FTA) and arrangements to create the enabling environment for facilitating investments from target-source countries, like the United States and South Korea, in terms of capital and technology.",""],[1,"178","9","RCEP and Philippines-South Korea FTA Implementation","The Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) Agreement and the Philippines-South Korea FTA are trade agreements that will be signed and fully implemented.",""],[1,"179","2","International STI Negotiation and Investment Attraction Initiative","The Philippine government will also actively participate in the negotiations with the innovation- and technology-rich countries that will complement STI-driven strategy and, in parallel, aggressively attract investments from global companies in the TMT, IMT,",""],[1,"179","3","Participation in Digital Economy and E-Commerce Negotiations","the Philippines will participate in negotiations to come up with relevant disciplines on the digital economy and e-commerce.",""],[1,"181","6","RCEP Ratification","Ratification of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP)",""],[1,"226","3","Support for Survival, Growth, and Expansion of Local Export Firms","On one hand, renewed focus will be given to the survival, growth, and expansion of local firms in the export",""],[1,"226","10","Targeted Export Promotion Strategies","Implement targeted, more granular strategies to increase :selected: exports on three fronts: global value chain (GVC) export clusters (industrial, manufacturing, and transportation [IMT], technology, media, and telecommunications [TMT], and health and life sciences [HLS]); food and agri-marine; and labor-intensive manufacturing",""],[1,"226","11","Export Linkage Diversification Initiative","Significantly diversify exports by fortifying the sectoral backward and forward linkages",""],[1,"226","12","Regional Trade Agreements Strategy Advancement","Advance purposive, assertive, and forward-looking Regional Trade Agreements strategies",""],[1,"228","1","Targeted Export Expansion Strategies","Implement targeted, granular strategies to increase exports on three fronts: global value chains, food and agri-marine, and labor-intensive manufacturing",""],[1,"228","2","Export Strategy Sharpening and GVC Entry Point Identification","strategies will be further sharpened to make them credible for local and foreign investors.",""],[1,"228","3","Targeted Support Programs for Agri-Marine and Labor-Intensive Manufacturing","renewed focus and targeted support programs will be implemented for agri-marine-based and labor- intensive manufacturing, such as processed food and garments.",""],[1,"228","4","Support for Local Firms with Linkage Roles","The shrinking export product space will be transformed by identifying and supporting local firms that have trigger roles in linking upstream and downstream sectors in the economy.",""],[1,"228","5","Regional Expansion of Shared Services Facilities","This will entail the expansion of government agencies assistance and work toward implementing these in the regions, such as DTI's Shared Services Facilities to include common business services (e.g., marketing, digitization, administrative and finance, promotions, logistics, distribution, assistance in consolidation), especially for MSMEs and cooperatives with potential export transitions.","DTI"],[1,"228","5","Inclusive Value Chain Development and Partnership Brokering","Value chain interventions will go beyond mere provision of physical inputs but focus on organizational development, and brokering multi-sectoral partnerships to capacitate smallholders and make value chains inclusive.",""],[1,"228","6","Local Supplier Substitution Indicator Development","Concrete indicators will be developed to gauge the ability of local suppliers to replace a significant share of inputs imported by GVC subsidiaries.",""],[1,"229","2","Free Trade Agreement Strategy Development","Advance purposive, assertive, and forward-looking free trade agreement strategies",""],[1,"229","3","FTA Sustainability Impact Assessment and Utilization System","A Free Trade Agreement (FTA) Sustainability Impact Assessment and FTA Utilization System will be institutionalized and led by the DTI to define short-, medium- and long-term opportunities in specific sectors and markets as well as provide easy access for timely data on trade in goods and services and utilization of Philippine FTAs.","DTI"],[1,"229","3","FTA Promotion and Exporter Utilization Support Programs","The system, on the other hand, will assist government and relevant private stakeholders in designing programs and activities to promote FTAs and optimize utilization by exporters.",""],[1,"229","3","FTA Stakeholder Safety Net Formulation","This assessment will also identify possible stakeholders and industries that will be adversely affected and accordingly formulate safety nets for these sectors.",""],[1,"229","4","Trade Negotiation Strategy for Market Access Expansion","Trade negotiations will be employed as a decisive tool in pushing the frontiers of our markets as defined by current origin rules.",""],[1,"229","4","FTA Negotiations on Non-Tariff Measures","FTA negotiations will also be utilized to distinguish between legitimate and trade-restricting non-tariff measures.",""],[1,"229","5","Trade Preference and Rules of Origin Negotiation Strategy","The government will therefore actively seek derogations for EU GSP+ and similar mechanisms (e.g., cumulation), pursue liberal rules of origin for products of interest, and seek inclusion of export pillars in zero tariffs product liberalization of countries' FTAs.",""],[1,"232","7","RCEP Ratification","Urgent ratification of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership [RCEP] Agreement",""],[1,"232","14","Targeted Local Industry Export Competitiveness Support","Amendments to the law will provide targeted and strategic policy, program, and project support, including non-fiscal incentives, for the development of local industries toward export competitiveness.",""],[1,"441","7","Business Intelligence Platform for Exporters","Business intelligence platform that aims to deliver timely and relevant information and assistance to existing and potential exporters to enhance their capabilities and competitiveness as suppliers of quality goods and services to global markets.",""]],"38":[[1,"178","2","National Quality Infrastructure Law","To address this, the passage of the NQI law will be pursued.",""],[1,"178","4","Adoption of International Standards and Certification","Adopt international standards and international certification",""],[1,"178","5","MSME Accreditation and Standards Awareness Campaigns","Information campaigns targeting MSMEs will be launched to promote the benefits of accreditation and conformance to international standards.",""],[1,"181","10","Standardization and Conformity Assessment Services","The bill intends to establish standardization, metrology, accreditation, and conformity assessment services necessary to provide acceptable evidence that products and services meet defined requirements, demanded either by authorities or the marketplace.",""],[1,"181","10","Regulatory Approval Acceleration for Goods and Services","Moreover, it seeks to hasten regulatory approvals for the release and sale of goods and services into the markets, and ascertain protection of consumers from trade malpractices and substandard or hazardous products.",""],[1,"200","9","Update the Intellectual Property Code","Update RA 10372 [An Act Amending Certain Provisions of RA 8293, otherwise known as the \"Intellectual Property Code of the Philippines, and for Other Purposes\"]",""],[1,"209","19","Intellectual Property Management Support and Incentives","Provide support and incentives for IP management",""],[1,"213","5","Innovation and Intellectual Property Awareness Program","Accelerate programs to increase awareness among policymakers, private sector, university researchers, and the general public of the value and contribution of innovation and IP to economic and social development.",""],[1,"213","5","Intellectual Property Unit Network Strengthening","It will strengthen a network of IP units delivering timely, high quality, and accessible IP management services that benefit technology",""],[1,"213","6","Private Sector Intellectual Property Capacity Building","It will improve the capacity of the private sector to create, protect, utilize, commercialize and enforce their IP rights.",""],[1,"213","6","Patent Mapping and Analytics Support Service","The Intellectual Property Office of the Philippines (IPOPHL) will provide businesses with patent mapping and analytics tools that identify trends and gaps in the technological landscape, which can be used as a basis for strategic direction and business decisions for pursuing R&D and investments in technology development.",""],[1,"213","7","Research Commercialization Support Platforms","Provide public research institutions and state universities and colleges with platforms, including avenues to pitch their R&D products and technology developed, to successfully commercialize their technologies.",""],[1,"213","7","Private Sector Technology Commercialization Programmes","Programs will also be implemented which involve private sector participation through the promotion, utilization, and commercialization of investments in these products.",""],[1,"216","11","National Measurement Infrastructure System Strengthening and Metrology Act Amendment","Strengthening the National Measurement Infrastructure System Amending Republic Act 9236 also known as the National Metrology Act of 2003 and for Other Purposes",""],[1,"216","12","Metrological Standards Harmonization and Mutual Recognition Arrangements","The bill supports the harmonization of national metrological standards with international standards, mutual recognition arrangements and statistical controls as envisioned in the ASEAN economic integration, the World Trade Organization, and international agreements and covenants, resulting to globally competitive and quality products and services.",""],[1,"226","14","Whole-of-Government National Quality Infrastructure Access Initiative","Ensure integrated, whole-of-government commitment to :selected: deliver broad access to National Quality Infrastructure",""],[1,"229","6","National Quality Infrastructure Strengthening through FTA Partnerships","The government will negotiate sharing of knowledge, technology, and best practices to comply with standards in foreign markets and maximize the market access offered through FTAs.",""],[1,"230","3","Whole-of-Government National Quality Infrastructure Access Initiative","Ensure integrated, whole-of-government commitment to deliver broad access to the National Quality Infrastructure",""],[1,"230","4","National Quality Infrastructure Harmonization Reform","The government will definitively integrate and harmonize national standards and certification policies, and agencies in order to open up the path for many local firms (especially SME) toward quality-exigent foreign markets.",""],[1,"230","4","National Quality Infrastructure Act Passage","the government will strongly pursue passage of the NQI Act",""],[1,"230","4","Institutional Fragmentation Reduction for Quality Infrastructure","direct relevant agencies to address institutional fragmentation and pursue adoption of harmonized quality infrastructure.",""],[1,"232","3","Standards and Certification Schemes Task Force","The task force will spearhead the work in building transparent and credible Standards and Certification schemes by stimulating dynamic institutional entrepreneurship in this arena.",""],[1,"232","11","National Quality Infrastructure Establishment","Establishment of an NQI will help boost best practices and competitiveness.",""]],"39":[[1,"38","5","Private Sector Incentives and Enabling Business Environment","The government's role is to provide calibrated incentives to priority industries and foster an enabling business environment to allow job- generating businesses and industries to grow.",""],[1,"41","3","Business Matching and Servicification Support Programme","This entails enhancing business- matching activities and intensifying support through the provision of common service facilities, marketing assistance and even time-bound performance-based incentives.",""],[1,"41","3","Industry 4.0 and IoT Servicification Promotion Initiative","Servicification will be promoted, including the adoption of Industry 4.0, IoT, etc.",""],[1,"41","3","Industry-Service-Academia Collaboration Platform","This will be done through co-locating industry and service enterprises, and including academic institutions, and providing more platforms for collaboration.",""],[1,"41","5","MSME Value-Addition and Accreditation Support","Value-adding to diversify \"product\" offering and improve \"consumption\" experience will be encouraged by instituting accreditation protocols; improving access to physical and digital infrastructure; and developing technology parks, centers of creative excellence and innovation, creative talent hubs, and improved shared service facilities for MSMEs.",""],[1,"41","5","Capacity Upgrading for Business Advisory Institutions and Host Communities","Finally, capacities of institutions providing business advisory services, and of communities and LGUs hosting the investments and events will be continuously upgraded.",""],[1,"168","1","Private Sector Collaboration for Common Service Facilities and Agribusiness Roadmaps","These strategies will induce the private sector to work with government in establishing common service facilities, in updating and implementing agribusiness roadmaps, and in undertaking industry-specific research and development (R&D) and technology adoption.",""],[1,"168","4","Domestic Market Marketing Assistance and Shared Services Facilities Expansion","To address this, the government hosts provincial and national trade fairs for domestic manufacturers and food processors.",""],[1,"169","6","Agribusiness Shared Service Facilities Expansion and Upgrading","SSFs for agribusiness will likewise be expanded and upgraded.",""],[1,"170","6","Common Service Facilities for MSME Storage and Logistics","Common service facilities for storage and logistics, such as handling and cold storage services, will be established to help ease the burden of high storage and logistics costs borne by MSMEs.",""]],"40":[[1,"175","5","Priority GVC-Oriented Industry Cluster Implementation","the DTI, in collaboration with other government agencies, will implement the following four industry clusters seen as potential sources of growth in the country: (a) Industrial, Manufacturing and Transport (IMT); (b) Technology, Media, and Telecommunication (TMT); (c) Health and Life Science (HLS); and (d) Modern Basic Needs (MBN), Resilient Economy.","DTI | other government agencies"],[1,"176","2","Targeted Policies to Increase Participation in the TMT GVC Cluster","the 82 percent share of Philippine BPOs and shared services centers in the global market will be leveraged by targeted policies to increase the country's participation in the TMT GVC cluster.",""],[1,"178","6","Mining Value-Addition and Downstream Industry Development","Develop value-adding activities and downstream industries of the mining sector",""],[1,"178","8","Domestic and Global Value Chain Expansion","Manufacturers need to expand domestic linkages while exploring further participation in the global value chains.",""]],"41":[[1,"178","7","Domestic Mineral Processing for Industrial Value Addition","The mineral resources of the country will be primarily used for industrial value-addition.",""]],"42":[[1,"83","3","Social Cohesion and Community Safety Strengthening","Social cohesion shall be strengthened to broaden community participation, secure community safety, ensure gender- and culture-responsive interventions, and promote the welfare of and prevent acts of violence against vulnerable groups including women; children; elderly; lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender or transsexual, queer or questioning, intersex, and allied, asexual, aromantic, or agender (LGBTQIA); as well as indigenous peoples (IP), among others.",""],[1,"83","7","Community Safety and Violence Prevention Initiative","Community safety from crimes and violence shall be ensured through the involvement of the youth and community members in organized sports, recreational activities, and volunteer opportunities.",""],[1,"83","7","Substance Abuse Treatment and Illicit Trade Prosecution","Substance abuse shall be treated as a health problem (See Subchapter 2.1) while illegal trade of these goods shall be prosecuted as part of the endeavors to remove criminality in the community.",""],[1,"83","7","Multi-Stakeholder Community Peace and Safety Collaboration","Overall, collaboration of communities, LGUs, businesses, civil society, and other sectors shall be strengthened to achieve peace, security, and safety, while being mindful of the contexts and needs of vulnerable groups (See Subchapter 13.1).",""],[1,"331","2","National Action Plan on Preventing and Countering Violent Extremism","Key strategies in the National Action Plan on Preventing and Countering Violent Extremism were also rolled out.",""],[1,"331","5","Bureau of Fire Protection Modernization Act","The recently enacted Bureau of Fire Protection Modernization Act (Republic Act 11589) is expected to upgrade fire protection services in the country.",""],[1,"331","5","Oplan Ligtas na Pamayanan","The Bureau of Fire Protection also initiated the Oplan Ligtas na Pamayanan to capacitate barangays with systemic and comprehensive methods and procedures to prevent and respond to fires and other emergency and disaster risks.",""],[1,"331","5","Public Safety Training for Barangay Peacekeeping and NGO Teams","In addition, trainings on public safety were given to Barangay Peacekeeping Action Teams and non-government organization teams in areas.",""],[1,"333","1","Security, Cybersecurity, and Disaster Response Strengthening","security and law enforcement operations, cybersecurity, and disaster response will be strengthened so that the quality of life is safeguarded from criminality; protection and safety from natural hazards and other threats will be ensured",""],[1,"333","12","Capacity Building for Security Forces and LGUs in Disaster Response","Improve the capacity and capability of security forces and LGUs on humanitarian assistance and disaster response and protection services to mitigate the impacts of natural hazards and other emergencies",""],[1,"333","16","Community Police Engagement Expansion","Strengthen and expand police engagements with communities on crime deterrence, reporting, and resolution",""],[1,"333","23","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Security Assessment and Response","Strengthen the capacity of institutions in security assessment, operations, and response relative to geopolitical developments",""],[1,"333","25","Counterterrorism and Counter-Extremism Mechanisms","Establish appropriate mechanisms to counter threats from terrorism, radicalization, and violent extremism",""],[1,"335","4","Counter-Terrorism and Violent Extremism Mechanisms","Establish appropriate mechanisms to counter threats from terrorism, radicalization, and violent extremism",""],[1,"335","5","Threat Assessment Capacity Strengthening","national and local agencies will strengthen their threat assessment",""],[1,"335","6","Institutionalize Preventing and Countering Violent Extremism Interventions","institutionalizing preventing and countering violent extremism interventions in national and local bodies",""],[1,"335","6","Neutralization Operations Against Armed Threat Groups","sustaining neutralization efforts against armed threat groups including law enforcement operations, case build-up against high-value targets, legal offensive, intelligence cooperation, military operations, and neutralization ofillicit financial sources",""],[1,"335","6","National Task Force on Disbandment of Private Armed Groups","sustaining the efforts of the National Task Force on Disbandment of Private Armed Groups",""],[1,"335","6","De-radicalization Program for GICA Communities","developing a de-radicalization program for GICA communities",""],[1,"335","8","Reward and Punishment Reform in Police and Drug Enforcement Institutions","the government will: (c) strengthen the reward and punishment mechanism in police and drug enforcement institutions.",""],[1,"335","8","PNP Modernization Program","The PNP modernization program will continue giving stronger emphasis on professionalization, rights-based policing, and",""],[1,"335","10","Community Police Engagement Expansion","Strengthen and expand police engagements with communities on crime deterrence, reporting, and resolution",""],[1,"335","11","Community Policing and Police Station Expansion","Law enforcement will be strengthened by expanding police presence in communities and establishing more police stations in strategic areas.",""],[1,"335","11","Community and Service-Oriented Policing Scheme","Barangay Peacekeeping Action Teams, civil society organizations, and community volunteers will be engaged through community and service-oriented policing scheme.",""],[1,"336","1","Integrated Patrol and Law Enforcement Operations","agencies will converge efforts in patrolling, internal security, and law enforcement operations, both in land and at sea.",""],[1,"336","1","Crime and Emergency Response System Improvement","Systems for responding to crime and emergencies will be made more efficient and relevant.",""],[1,"336","1","Sustained Operations Against Criminal Groups","Likewise, neutralization efforts against criminal groups will be sustained, internal cleansing in security institutions will be continued, and executive and legislative oversight over the police and other uniformed personnel will be enforced.",""],[1,"336","1","Internal Cleansing in Security Institutions","internal cleansing in security institutions will be continued",""],[1,"336","1","Executive and Legislative Oversight of Police and Uniformed Personnel","executive and legislative oversight over the police and other uniformed personnel will be enforced.",""],[1,"336","3","Counter-Radicalization Programs","Context-specific programs will be initiated to address radicalization efforts of violent extremist groups.",""],[1,"336","4","Intensified Law Enforcement Engagements Against Violent Extremist Groups","Bilateral and multilateral engagements in law enforcement and defense against violent extremist groups will be intensified",""],[1,"336","5","Capacity Building for Humanitarian Assistance, Disaster Response, and Protection Services","Improve capacity and capability of security forces and LGUs on humanitarian assistance and disaster response and protection services to mitigate the impacts of natural hazards and other emergencies",""],[1,"336","7","BFP Modernization Act Implementation","The BFP Modernization Act will be fully implemented to ensure more responsive fire protection services across the country.",""],[1,"336","7","Citizen Volunteerism in Disaster Response Program","A program to enhance citizen volunteerism in disaster response will be established, with resources and training support and using the AFP Reservists Act35 and the National Service Reserve Corps36 as platforms.",""],[1,"336","7","LGU Disaster Risk Exposure and Vulnerability Assessment Expansion","The assessment of the exposure and vulnerabilities of LGUs to disaster risks will be expanded.",""],[1,"336","7","Public Safety and Disaster Preparedness Capacity Building","Likewise, capacity building on public safety and disaster preparedness will be intensified.",""],[1,"336","7","Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Response Cooperation","Local and international cooperation in humanitarian assistance and disaster response operations, joint exercises,",""],[1,"337","1","Training and Information Sharing Scale-Up","training activities, and information sharing will be scaled up.",""],[1,"338","8","LGU Good Governance Compliance and Security Institution Human Rights Oversight","Sustain compliance of LGUs to good governance principles and of security institutions on human rights and rule of law",""],[1,"338","9","Local Government Unit Governance Strengthening","The government will foster efficient, inclusive, and accountable LGUs",""],[1,"338","10","Community Partnership and Human Rights-Based Security Institution Strengthening","to boost the confidence of people toward the government and human rights-based security institutions in strengthening partnership with communities.",""],[1,"338","10","Reward, Mainstreaming, and Penalty Measures for Security Institutions","In addition, better reward schemes, intensified mainstreaming efforts, and appropriate penalties on violators will be put in place.",""]],"43":[[1,"375","1","Natural Resource Rehabilitation and Protection Programme","Rehabilitation and protection of natural resources will be accelerated to sustain the provision of ecosystem goods and services.",""],[1,"379","17","Climate and Disaster Risk Adaptive Approaches","adaptive approaches will be implemented considering the different levels of climate and disaster risks.",""],[1,"379","17","Ecosystem Rehabilitation and Nature-Based Management Programme","Rehabilitation, protection, and management of ecosystems will be intensified through nature-based solutions and integrated approaches, e.g., integrated water resources management and ecosystem-based approach.",""],[1,"381","1","Degraded Ecosystem Rehabilitation and Resilience Program","rehabilitation of degraded ecosystems (e.g., forest, water, mangrove, wetlands, seagrass, coral reefs, land) will be accelerated to restore and enhance ecosystem services, particularly the ability of natural systems to protect communities against the negative impacts of climate change.",""],[1,"381","2","Ecosystem Protection, Rehabilitation, and Management","Intensify ecosystem protection, rehabilitation, and management",""],[1,"381","3","Integrated Natural Resource Management and Nature-Based Solutions","The government will continue to strengthen the management and sustainable use of land, water, biodiversity, and other natural resources using integrated and ecosystem-based approaches and nature-based solutions",""],[1,"381","4","Carrying Capacity Assessments for Protected Areas and Ecotourism Sites","This covers the conduct of carrying capacity assessments to inform appropriate management interventions especially in protected areas and ecotourism sites.",""],[1,"381","4","Integration of Indigenous Knowledge in Ecosystem Management","Indigenous knowledge, systems, and practices will also be employed to complement science-based approaches in managing ecosystems.",""],[1,"381","5","Sustainable Land Management Integration","scaling up the integration of sustainable land management approaches (e.g., soil and water conservation measures, climate-smart technologies) in local plans and policies will be pursued to address climate change impacts on land and water resources.",""],[1,"382","1","Marginal Sector Participation for Sustainable Production and Environmental Conservation","representatives from marginal sectors, such as women, youth and indigenous peoples, will be bolstered to (a) secure sustainable production, (b) accelerate rehabilitation and conservation efforts, (c) strengthen enforcement of environmental rules and regulations, and (d) boost the contribution of ecosystems in climate change adaptation and mitigation.",""],[1,"387","9","Reforestation and Forest Rehabilitation Programme","The bill aims to enhance forest ecosystems through reforestation and forest rehabilitation to mitigate climate change, improve and conserve biodiversity, enhance ecosystem functions and services, and provide long-term economic benefits.",""],[1,"387","13","Integrated Coastal Management National Strategy","This bill aims to institutionalize ICM as a national strategy to ensure the holistic and sustainable management of various ecosystems and natural resources through the \"ridge- to-reef\" approach.",""],[1,"387","13","Integrated Coastal Management Framework for Local Governments","In addition, the bill pursues the development of an ICM Framework as a guide for local government units in building the resiliency of coastal communities to climate change and other hazards.",""]],"44":[[1,"264","23","Sustainable Finance Taxonomy and Pipeline Database","Continuously improve the sustainable finance definition, its principles-based taxonomy, and establish a sustainable pipeline database",""],[1,"264","28","Sustainable Finance Investment Mobilization","Increase investments of retail and institutional players in sustainable finance",""],[1,"267","4","Sustainable Finance Mainstreaming Framework","The government will continuously improve the mainstreaming of sustainable finance through the adoption of a principles-based taxonomy, the establishment of a sustainable pipeline database, and the promotion of sustainable financial products.",""],[1,"267","4","Institutionalization of Sustainability Principles in Financial Institutions","Financial institutions will need to institutionalize sustainability principles in their management and governance frameworks and will have to consider, where relevant and applicable, strategies, priorities, and guiding principles contained in the Philippines Sustainable Finance Roadmap and Philippine Sustainable Finance Guiding Principles.",""],[1,"267","4","Private Sector Sustainable Finance Promotion","Moreover, the private sector can support this strategy by promoting investments in sustainable finance to their retail and institutional clients and their own asset management groups.",""],[1,"375","1","Sustainable and Green Investment Scaling Initiative","the government will collaborate with the private sector and international community to scale up sustainable and green investments that propel economic transformation for a prosperous, inclusive, and resilient society.",""],[1,"375","3","Sustainable and Green Finance Mobilization Framework","These include the adoption of a framework and guidelines to mobilize sustainable and green finance, such as the Sustainable Finance Framework and Roadmap, and Securities and Exchange Commission Guidelines on the issuance of Green and Sustainability Bonds.",""],[1,"381","1","Philippine Action Plan for Sustainable Consumption and Production Operationalization","Also, the Philippine Action Plan for Sustainable Consumption and Production (PAP4SCP) will be operationalized.",""],[1,"381","4","Monitoring of Extractive Industry Environmental Compliance","the Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR) will strengthen the monitoring of extractive industries' compliance, including mining and quarrying, to existing environmental laws, rules, and regulations.","Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR)"],[1,"382","4","Payments for Ecosystem Services Mechanism","the government will partner with other stakeholders to establish market-based mechanisms, such as payments for ecosystem services (PES) that support natural resource conservation measures and accelerate ecosystems and habitat rehabilitation and restoration",""],[1,"382","4","Mandatory Environmental Compliance Enforcement","The government will also ensure increased compliance with mandatory regulations (e.g., reporting of environmental protection expenditures)",""],[1,"382","4","Private Sector Environmental Offset and Compensation Measures","and encourage the private sector to adopt flexible methods to offset and compensate the ecological and social impacts of their operation and production-including extractive industries (e.g., mining and quarrying-and improve social and environmental standards to fulfill corporate responsibility",""],[1,"383","5","Resource-Efficient and Cleaner Production Support","The abovementioned strategies will support businesses in adopting resource-efficient and cleaner production measures and pursuing",""],[1,"384","1","Supply Chain Greening Initiatives","supply chain-greening initiatives that optimize the use of natural resources, minimize emissions and waste, and reduce risks to people and communities.",""],[1,"384","1","Resource-Efficient and Cleaner Production Support","The promotion of resource-efficient and cleaner production, particularly in the energy, transport, and industry sectors, will be supported by the full implementation of incentive mechanisms under existing laws, such as the Renewable Energy Act, Energy Efficiency and Conservation Act, Electric Vehicle Industry Development Act, Organic Agriculture Law, and Green Jobs Act",""],[1,"384","5","Green Public Procurement and Certification Schemes","The implementation of the green public procurement program, ecolabelling, and other green certification schemes will be strengthened (e.g., green hotels and resorts, green buildings, sustainable agriculture) to guide consumer behavior toward green and sustainable products and services.",""],[1,"386","3","Gender-Responsive Climate Project Pipeline Development","This includes developing a sustainable, bankable, and gender-responsive pipeline of projects;",""],[1,"386","3","Blended Climate Financing Mechanism","implementing a blended approach in climate financing (e.g., grants, investments, and subsidies);",""],[1,"386","3","Program Convergence Budgeting Expansion","and expanding the government's program convergence budgeting approach.",""],[1,"386","3","Private Sector Investment Mobilization through Public Spending","Public spending will be structured such that it stimulates private sector investments, while regulations and guidelines on accessing government finance facilities will be streamlined to facilitate improved access, especially by women.",""],[1,"386","3","Streamlining Access to Government Finance Facilities","regulations and guidelines on accessing government finance facilities will be streamlined to facilitate improved access, especially by women.",""],[1,"386","3","Private Sector Risk Reduction for Green Investments","Further, the government will work closely with the private sector to minimize the risks (i.e., physical and transition risks) that affect the bankability of green",""],[1,"386","4","Green Investment Promotion and Risk Assessment Capacity Building","investments by: (a) providing information on emerging climate technologies, and climate and environmental uncertainties; (b) building capacity on conducting risk assessments among investors, capitalists, and borrowers; and (c) developing and institutionalizing tools and approaches to integrate environmental externalities into economic analyses and environmental impact assessments-allowing a holistic accounting of the economic costs and benefits of associated investments.",""],[1,"386","4","Public-Private Partnership Promotion for Green Investment","In addition, public-private partnerships will be encouraged to attract more investors.",""],[1,"386","4","Green Investment Bank Establishment","The establishment of more Green Investment Banks will also be promoted to support the development of green markets.",""],[1,"386","5","Expanded Disaster Risk Financing and Insurance Support","The government will expand disaster risk financing beyond the NDRRMF by working with relevant institutions in financing and insurance and supporting LGUs in accessing the same, especially for localized preparedness, relief, early recovery, and reconstruction efforts.",""],[1,"386","5","Green Financing and Risk Insurance Support for Vulnerable Groups","In addition, critical support for accessing green financing and risk insurance will be given to hazard-prone communities and highly vulnerable sectors such as micro, small, and medium enterprises and small-scale farmers and fisherfolk.",""],[1,"386","5","Climate Justice Access to International Climate Finance","The country will also continue to uphold the principle of climate justice in accessing international climate finance for adaptation and loss and damage.",""],[1,"418","7","Sustainable Tourism and Energy-Efficient Operations Mainstreaming","this aims to mainstream sustainable tourism and energy efficient operations in the tourism sector in the country.","Department of Tourism"]],"45":[[1,"82","12","Waste Disposal Facility Expansion","Increase access to proper waste disposal facilities",""],[1,"84","4","Waste Minimization Compliance and Behavioral Change Program","Waste minimization shall involve ensuring compliance and steering behavioral change at the individual, household, and societal levels toward sustainable production and consumption practices.",""],[1,"84","4","Ecological Solid Waste Management Act Compliance Enforcement","Compliance with the Ecological Solid Waste Management Act (RA 9003), which mandates LGUs to divert more than 25 percent of solid wastes from waste disposal facilities, shall be pursued.",""],[1,"84","5","Waste Recovery and Recycling Intensification Programme","recycling and other recovery programs-such as community composting and recovery of rare metals from waste electrical and electronic equipment (urban mining) programs-will be intensified to improve resource efficiency and promote a circular economy.",""],[1,"84","5","Green Technology and Secondary Raw Materials Investment Support","This shall enable public and private investments (e.g., development of green technologies and establishment of facilities) in waste recovery, reuse, and recycling as well as manufacturing and production using secondary raw materials (See Chapter 6).",""],[1,"85","1","E-waste Materials Promotion for Renewable Energy Technologies","materials from e-waste as raw materials for renewable energy technologies will likewise be promoted (See Chapter 12).",""],[1,"85","1","Extended Producer Responsibility Program Implementation","The implementation of the EPR Act of 2022 will require private companies, particularly large enterprises, to initiate their EPR programs to minimize waste from plastic packaging.",""],[1,"85","1","National Action Plan on Marine Litter Monitoring","Moreover, the implementation of the National Action Plan on Marine Litter shall be monitored and pave the way to promote and mainstream circular economy and stimulate sustainable consumption and production.",""],[1,"85","1","Environmental Education and Communication Campaigns","Environmental education, and communication programs will also be intensified using traditional and social media, school-based campaigns, and government social development and grassroots programs to help steer the desired behavioral change.",""],[1,"85","2","Integrated Waste Management Service Expansion","Solid, organic, and health care and hazardous wastes will be effectively managed to prevent possible adverse health, economic, and environmental impacts in communities.",""],[1,"85","2","Local Government Waste Management Service Expansion","The delivery of waste management services by LGUs will be increased, making proper waste disposal accessible to a larger population base.",""],[1,"85","2","Solid Waste Management Plan Fast-Tracking","The approval of SWM plans will also be fast-tracked.",""],[1,"85","2","Web-Based Solid Waste Monitoring System","A web-based monitoring system will be established to track progress and compliance by LGUs with solid waste regulations, including their waste diversion mandate.",""],[1,"85","2","LGU Capacity Building for Solid Waste Management","DENR will continue to build the capacity of LGUs through trainings, guidelines, implementation mechanisms, and technology transfer, among","DENR"],[1,"85","3","Local Government Unit Clustering for Common Facilities","LGU clustering shall be facilitated in the implementation of appropriate common facilities-including material recovery facilities, SLFs, and facilities for health care and hazardous wastes, among others.",""],[1,"85","3","Waste-to-Energy Technology Assessment and Regulatory Framework","the viability of waste-to-energy technologies will continue to be studied and the appropriate environmental regulatory framework will be put in place.",""],[1,"91","12","Single-Use Plastic Phase-Out","Phase out single-use plastic",""],[1,"104","3","Community Composting Facilities, Equipment, and Capacity Building","The provision of facilities, equipment, and capacity building for community composting (e.g., Bureau of Soils and Water Management Composting Facilities for Biodegradable Wastes) will be continued",""],[1,"301","33","Solid Waste Management Solutions","Pursue optimal solid waste management (SWM) solutions",""],[1,"316","3","Local Government Unit Clustering for Common Waste Management Facilities","Facilitate clustering of LGUs to take advantage of economies of scale.","Department of Environment and Natural Resources"],[1,"316","5","Solid Waste Management Program Intensification","Supporting SWM programs will be intensified.",""],[1,"316","5","LGU Solid Waste Management Capacity-Building Program","Capacity-building programs will be undertaken to develop the technical capacities of LGUs to undertake waste analysis and characterization studies and assess technical and financial options for implementing SWM projects.",""],[1,"316","5","Waste Diversion Information and Communication Campaigns","Information, education, and communication campaigns will be aggressively conducted to promote greater waste diversion, thus, optimizing the use of disposal sites and enhancing willingness to pay for SWM services.",""]],"46":[[1,"19","6","Climate Adaptation and Disaster Resilience Strategy","accelerating climate adaptation and strengthening disaster resilience (Chapter 15)",""],[1,"28","2","Resilience-Building Strategy Implementation","we need to fast-track investments in ... effective resilience-building strategies",""],[1,"43","8","Climate Resilience and Adaptive Capacity Strengthening","The priority is to enhance the adaptive capacity of communities and ecosystems that are most vulnerable to natural hazards and climate change.",""],[1,"61","7","Risk-Based Regulation for Climate-Related Health Actions","Risk- based regulation is particularly important for actions addressing health consequences of climate change.",""]],"47":[[1,"138","2","Green Jobs Database Development","the government shall intensify creating a database of green jobs",""],[1,"138","2","Green Jobs Human Resource Development Plan","implement the Green Jobs Human Resource Development Plan",""],[1,"138","2","Green Competencies Mainstreaming in TVET and Education","intensify the integration and mainstreaming of green competencies in TVET and education programs",""],[1,"138","2","PQF Revision for Environmental Sustainability and Green Qualifications","the government shall revisit the PQF for proper integration of environmental sustainability and green qualifications as an objective",""],[1,"138","3","Green Sector Investment and Ecozone Development","Key stakeholders shall ensure stability in the macroeconomy, adequacy of investments in green sectors, feasibility of creating green ecozones, and sustainability of human capital investments.",""],[1,"138","3","Just Transition Social Protection for Unskilled Workers","Because of job dynamics in identified green sectors, adequate levels of social protection shall be in place to address the just transition of unskilled workers.",""],[1,"138","3","Worker Transition Support for Brown Occupations","As economies become more involved in greening processes and structures, those who belong to brown occupations may need assistance transitioning to other occupations.",""]],"48":[[1,"385","4","Natural Capital Accounting Institutionalization Roadmap","The Roadmap to Institutionalize Natural Capital Accounting (NCA) in the Philippines will be implemented to better inform planning and programming toward increasing the resilience of ecosystems and communities and comprehensively accounting for the country's",""],[1,"386","1","Natural Capital and Ecosystem Accounts Development","the Philippine Statistics Authority will develop, compile, and regularly update natural capital and ecosystem accounts",""],[1,"386","2","National Geospatial Database and Data Management System for Natural Resources","The DENR will establish and maintain a national geospatial database and data management system for natural resources.","DENR"],[1,"386","2","Environmental Data Collection and LGU Geospatial Capacity-Building","The academe, private sector, and civil society organizations will be tapped and capacitated in collecting timely, updated, and robust environmental data, and in assisting LGUs to generate and use local geospatial information.",""],[1,"386","2","Applied Research Collaboration on NCA","The government will also collaborate with said stakeholders in conducting applied research on NCA.",""]],"49":[[1,"295","6","Waste-to-Energy Facility Guidelines and Promotion Policies","The Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR) has issued guidelines governing waste-to-energy (WtE) facilities for the Integrated Management of Municipal Solid Wastes.","Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR)"],[1,"295","6","Waste-to-Energy Power Sector Participation Program","DOE has issued policies and implemented programs that aim to promote WtE facilities as baseload RE and prescribed policies and programs to enhance the participation of the electric power industry players in the development of WtE facilities.","DOE"],[1,"316","4","Solid Waste Management Technology and Financing Options Development","Explore technology options and financing schemes for SWM based on updated LGU waste data.",""],[1,"316","4","Low-Carbon Waste Technology Promotion and Adoption","Results of scientific research and development, and of demonstration projects shall guide the promotion and adoption of low-carbon (See Chapter 15), new modern, and innovative technologies, including WtE.",""],[1,"316","4","Regular Waste Analysis and Characterization Studies","Alongside these, waste analysis and characterization studies will be regularly conducted.",""],[1,"318","26","Waste-to-Energy Regulatory Framework","this bill will provide the necessary regulatory framework for facilities utilizing WtE",""]],"50":[[1,"301","19","Integrated Water Resources Management Implementation Strengthening","Strengthen integrated water resources mangement (IWRM) implementation",""],[1,"307","6","Integrated Water Resource Management for Water Governance","The strategy in the water sector is to implement effective water governance through integrated water resource management (IWRM) as applied in the planning and management of land, water, and coastal resources.",""],[1,"308","9","Integrated Water Resources Management Instruments","For integrated water resource management (IWRM), management instruments include water resources assessment, data collection networks, allocation and conflict resolution, allocation through market instruments, risk management tools, regulatory instruments,",""],[1,"309","3","Water Resources Sector Institutional Reform","The institutional fragmentation of the water resources sector shall be addressed.",""],[1,"309","4","Scientific Research Capacity Strengthening","The government's capacity to conduct continuous scientific studies will be ensured.",""],[1,"309","5","Science-Based Water Resources Decision Support System","Decision support system for purposes of science-based water resources planning and management as well as for multi-stakeholder consultation and public participation will be developed and maintained.",""],[1,"309","7","University-Based Water Resource Research and Training Support","University- or college-based water resource centers will be tapped to undertake problem-oriented research, development, extension, and training activities related to the water sector on a sustained basis.",""],[1,"309","8","National Water Data Monitoring Network","Investments in data monitoring systems will be made.",""],[1,"310","3","Water Infrastructure Services and Financing for Water and Sanitation Projects","Invest in water infrastructure services provision and provide accessible financing for water supply and sanitation projects",""],[1,"310","4","Public-Private Partnership Water Infrastructure Delivery","Public-private partnerships will be tapped to deliver needed water infrastructure facilities and services.",""],[1,"310","4","Water Supply and Sanitation Regulatory Reform","for water supply and sanitation projects, the economic regulatory environment will be rationalized and strengthened to address the fragmented,",""],[1,"310","5","Water Supply and Sanitation Regulatory Reform","This entails, among others, the consolidation and harmonization of tariff-setting methodologies, setting of performance and technical standards, and establishing policies and processes for the granting and revocation of licenses.",""],[1,"310","6","Water Supply and Sanitation Resource Allocation Framework","a framework for rationally allocating resources for WSS will be established",""],[1,"318","2","Water Sector Institutional Streamlining and Regulatory Separation","This will address the weak and fragmented institutional set-up in the sector by streamlining all water-related functions in the government, and separate resource regulation from economic regulation.",""],[1,"318","4","Water Supply and Sanitation Tariff Regulation Reform","The body will create a business and regulatory environment that is fair, transparent, and conducive for public and private domestic and foreign investment in water supply and sanitation services by implementing fair, just, and reasonable tariffs, rates, and charges for water supply and sanitation services.",""]],"51":[[1,"88","5","Water Supply and Sanitation Program Evaluation","The government shall evaluate the effectiveness of its programs in accelerating access to water supply and sanitation services,",""],[1,"88","6","Local Government Water Service Provider Operations","The government shall also encourage the operation of water service providers as economic enterprises run by LGUs and/or with private partners (See Chapter 12).",""],[1,"301","18","Water Infrastructure Upgrade and Expansion","Upgrade and expand water infrastructure",""],[1,"301","27","Water Infrastructure Services Investment","Invest in water infrastructure services provision",""],[1,"301","31","Accessible Financing for Water Supply and Sanitation Projects","Provide accessible financing for water supply and sanitation projects",""],[1,"307","7","Water Infrastructure and Management Improvement","ensure water availability through efficient water infrastructures and management;",""],[1,"307","10","Sanitation and Drainage Improvement","ensure good sanitation and drainage (including proper disposal);",""],[1,"307","14","Philippine Water Supply and Sanitation Master Plan Implementation","Implement the Philippine Water Supply and Sanitation Master Plan (PWSSMP), the National Irrigation Master Plan",""],[1,"308","3","Water Supply and Sanitation Institutional Capacity Development","Adequate institutional capability to efficiently operate and maintain WSS systems in terms of service coverage, performance, and financial sustainability will be developed.",""]],"52":[[1,"83","6","Community Participation in Cultural, Recreational, and Sports Activities","Communities shall also be encouraged to participate in cultural, recreational, and sports activities.",""],[1,"83","6","Local Culture and Arts Councils for Cultural Heritage Conservation","Local culture and arts councils will be promoted to plan and implement conservation and preservation of cultural property and conduct cultural activities.",""],[1,"83","6","National Grassroots Sports Program","A strong national grassroots program will be institutionalized by the Philippine Sports Commission on community-driven sporting and recreational activities in line with its mandate to set the priorities and direction of a national sports agenda, giving emphasis to grassroots participation.","Philippine Sports Commission"],[1,"83","8","Awareness, Knowledge, and Skills Development Initiative","The government will raise awareness, knowledge, and skills of individuals, families, enterprises, and other community stakeholders",""]],"53":[[1,"39","28","Strengthening Higher-Education Institutions as Innovation Hubs","Higher-education institutions will be strengthened to perform a greater role in knowledge co-creation, and serve as innovation hubs and incubation centers.",""],[1,"69","25","Higher Education Career System Design","Design a higher education career system",""],[1,"69","27","Transnational Knowledge Co-Creation Linkages with Higher Education Institutions","Pursue transnational knowledge co-creation linkages with HEIs",""],[1,"69","30","University Innovation Hub and Incubation Center Strengthening","Optimize the roles of universities as innovation hubs and incubation centers",""],[1,"69","31","Regional University Systems Establishment","Establish regional university systems",""],[1,"69","32","Research-Oriented Scholarships and Grants","Provide more research-oriented scholarships and grants",""],[1,"73","1","Transnational Higher Education Act Implementation","The Transnational Higher Education Act (RA 11448) will be fully implemented to support the internationalization of Philippine HEIs.",""],[1,"73","1","Higher Education and TVET Internationalization Framework Operationalization","The higher education and TVET internationalization frameworks will be operationalized and implemented.",""],[1,"73","2","National Innovation and Research Support Framework","The government shall create a strong national environment for innovation and knowledge creation to promote participation in the knowledge-based global economy and advance research in higher education.",""],[1,"73","3","Integration of SUCs into Regional University Systems","The integration of SUCs into regional university systems or specialized institutions will contribute to improved program delivery efficiency, reduce duplication, and foster complementarity between and among public and private HEIs.",""],[1,"73","3","Collaborative Arrangements for SUCs","Various modalities of appropriate collaborative arrangements among SUCs shall be designed and implemented (e.g., research cooperation, faculty exchange, sharing of laboratory facilities, equipment, and other resources).",""],[1,"73","4","National Innovation and Knowledge Production Ecosystem","the government will establish a strong national ecosystem for innovation and knowledge production.",""],[1,"73","4","Scholarships and Grants-in-Aid for Graduate Research","It will continue and expand the provision of scholarships, including grants-in-aid programs, to encourage graduate students, research staff, and faculty of HEIs to pursue basic and applied research",""],[1,"73","5","Online and Mixed Learning Continuity in Higher Education","The use of online and mixed learning modalities in higher education will be continued to promote learning continuity amidst possible future disruptions.",""],[1,"73","5","Adult Learning Delivery Through Digital and Alternative Media","Adult learning will be facilitated through the use of technologies such as online video-sharing platforms, learning management systems, and digital learning tools.",""],[1,"73","5","Alternative Learning Delivery for Low-Connectivity Areas","Other options, such as television, radio, printed materials, and mobile training laboratories, will be made available in areas with limited internet connectivity.",""],[1,"74","1","Open Online Courses Promotion","open online courses will be promoted as an optional mode of learning for students who have difficulty accessing traditional education.",""],[1,"74","2","Alternative Online Assessment and Certification System","To evaluate student performance, identify skill gaps, and validate learned skills, alternative assessment and certification procedures- i.e., online assessment, micro-credentials, etc .- will be developed and institutionalized.",""],[1,"74","2","Micro-Credentials Standards Framework","The development of micro-credentials will be supported through the establishment of common standards that will ensure their quality, transparency, recognition, and international comparability (See Chapter 4).",""],[1,"74","3","Higher Education Student Affairs and Services Strengthening","Higher education institutions shall strengthen their student affairs and services programs in order to provide them a peaceful, safe, secure and healthy learning environment.",""],[1,"74","3","Student Transition Support System","The student support systems of HEIs shall ensure that their students can effectively transition from graduation to employment or entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"74","3","Student Internship Implementation Improvement","Furthermore, the implementation of the student internship in the Philippines and abroad shall be improved so that students are able to translate their theoretical learnings to practice.",""],[1,"75","5","Higher Education Leadership Career System","A higher education career system will be designed and implemented for individuals occupying leadership positions in HEIs.",""]],"54":[[1,"39","27","Transformative Lifelong Learning Expansion","Opportunities for transformative lifelong learning will be expanded (Subchapter 2.2).",""],[1,"39","27","Education Quality Improvement Measures","The quality of education at all levels will be improved by expanding access to quality learning resources, enhancing the curriculum, and improving the competencies of teachers.",""],[1,"39","27","Learning Outcomes Evaluation Reform","The evaluation protocol for learning outcomes will also be improved by involving third-party institutions to assess students' proficiency",""],[1,"68","2","Second Education Commission","In 2022, over three decades later, a second Education Commission will be convened to address the education crisis.",""],[1,"69","13","Early Childhood Care and Development Curriculum Enhancement","Enhance Early Childhood Care and Development (ECCD) curriculum",""],[1,"69","16","Catch-Up Learning Programs","Develop and implement catch-up programs to address learning losses",""],[1,"69","18","School-Based Management Strengthening and Learning Materials Improvement","Strengthen School-based Management Develop and improve learning materials in line with international standards and trends",""],[1,"69","20","Teacher Competency Improvement Programme","Improve competencies of teachers",""],[1,"69","23","School-Based Feeding Program Strengthening","Strengthen school-based feeding program to address malnutrition",""],[1,"69","26","Private-Public Complementarity in Basic Education","Strengthen private-public complementarity in the provision of quality basic education",""],[1,"69","28","Third-Party Student Proficiency Assessment and Monitoring Partnership","Partner with independent third-party institutions in assessing and monitoring the progress of students' proficiency across all levels",""],[1,"70","1","Early Childhood Care and Development Curriculum Enhancement","Enhance early childhood care and development curriculum",""],[1,"70","2","Preschool Curriculum Recalibration for Early Childhood Care and Development","Early childhood care and development (ECCD) programs will be enriched by recalibrating the curriculum for preschool, focusing on the first 1,000 days of life.",""],[1,"70","2","Barangay Day Care Center Expansion","Barangay day care centers will be established in every barangay33 to provide a conducive learning environment for preschoolers.",""],[1,"70","2","Day Care Worker and Preschool Teacher Capacity Building","Capacity building will be provided for day care workers and preschool teachers.",""],[1,"70","2","Socioemotional and Healthy Habits Development in Preschool","Development of socioemotional skills and acquisition of healthy habits, such as good personal hygiene and eating nutritious food, will be emphasized to improve the resistance of learners to sickness and diseases.",""],[1,"70","3","Catch-Up Learning Programs","Develop and implement catch-up programs to address learning losses",""],[1,"70","4","Alternative Learning System Expansion","Access to Alternative Learning System will be expanded by establishing additional community learning centers in municipalities and cities.",""],[1,"70","4","Guidance Counselor Support for School Retention","The role of guidance counselors in encouraging the students to stay in school will be enhanced.",""],[1,"70","6","Textbook and Teacher Manual Provision","The Department of Education (DepEd) and LGUs will ensure that all public school students have a full set of textbooks for their grade level and all teachers receive a full set of manuals.","Department of Education (DepEd) | LGUs"],[1,"70","6","National Education Portal for Learning Materials","The National Education Portal (NEP) will be developed as the online repository for all quality-assessed learning materials for teachers and learners available for dissemination.",""],[1,"70","6","Inclusive Digital Learning Materials Development","Inclusive and interactive e-books with embedded videos, audio, and even sign language translations to attend to the needs of differently-abled children will be made available in the NEP.",""],[1,"70","6","Emergency Self-Learning Module Provision","To respond better to class disruptions during emergency situations, self-learning modules shall be made available in print and digital form, in addition to the textbooks provided to schools.",""],[1,"70","6","Blended Learning Promotion Policy","As a policy, the delivery of blended learning, utilizing both printed and digital resources will be promoted.",""],[1,"70","6","Special Education Fund Learning Resource Support","The Special Education Fund will also be utilized to provide such learning resources.",""],[1,"70","7","Teacher Training on Open Educational Resources and Gamified Learning","Training on the adoption of open educational resources (OER), gamification of learning, and other new pedagogical practices will be implemented to enhance the competencies of teachers.",""],[1,"70","7","Revision of Pre- and In-Service Teacher Training","Pre- and in-service training of teachers will be revisited to ensure that capacity-building programs are up-to-date, agile, and responsive to emerging skills and other needs.",""],[1,"71","1","Full Implementation of the Education Act","Education Act (RA 11713) will be fully implemented.",""],[1,"71","1","Teacher Education Scholarships","This law strengthens the Teacher Education Council, establishes scholarship for students in the teacher education program, and institutionalizes the National Educators' Academy of the Philippines (NEAP) as provider of quality professional development programs for in-service teachers, school leaders, and other teaching-related personnel in all public and private basic education institutions.",""],[1,"71","1","Institutionalization of the National Educators' Academy of the Philippines","This law strengthens the Teacher Education Council, establishes scholarship for students in the teacher education program, and institutionalizes the National Educators' Academy of the Philippines (NEAP) as provider of quality professional development programs for in-service teachers, school leaders, and other teaching-related personnel in all public and private basic education institutions.",""],[1,"71","2","School-Based Feeding Program Strengthening","With the support of the LGUs, the school-based feeding program, including those of the barangay day care centers, will be improved and strengthened.",""],[1,"71","3","Education Voucher Expansion","The voucher system will be expanded to promote complementarity between the public and private education systems and provide students more options on which school to attend.",""],[1,"71","3","Private Investment Promotion in Basic Education","Private investment in basic education will be encouraged to prevent overcrowding and stretching the resources of public schools.",""],[1,"71","3","Education Spending Increase","Government spending on education will be increased to four to six percent of GDP in line with the Education 2030 Framework for Action.",""],[1,"71","3","Basic Education Quality Standards Enforcement","Quality of basic education will be improved by observing minimum standards of service delivery, e.g., maintaining ideal",""],[1,"71","5","Additional Learning Spaces Expansion","Additional learning spaces will be set up in partnership with education stakeholders in the private and voluntary sectors-including civil society organizations (CSO), individual volunteers, philanthropists, and development practitioners-to address the current shortage of roughly 91,000 classrooms.",""],[1,"71","5","ICT-Enabled Learning Continuity Measures","Learning continuity will be ensured amidst possible future disruptions through the use of information and communication technology (ICT).",""],[1,"71","5","Future Classroom Learning Space Upgrade","Learning spaces will be designed, configured, and equipped to emulate the classroom of the future.",""],[1,"71","5","Library Online Learning Management Systems","Equipping libraries with online learning management systems will be initiated in collaboration with LGUs drawing from the Special Education Fund, and with partners from the private sector and civil society.",""],[1,"71","5","Inclusive Learning Resource Centers for Learners with Disabilities","Inclusive Learning Resource Centers (ILRC) for differently abled learners will be set up in all cities and municipalities pursuant to RA 11650 or the Instituting a Policy of Inclusion and Services for Learners with Disabilities in Support of Inclusive Education Act.",""],[1,"71","5","Basic School Water, Sanitation, Electricity, and Internet Provision","At the minimum, schools will be provided with water, sanitation, and hygiene facilities; electricity; and stable internet connectivity.",""],[1,"75","1","School-Based Management Strengthening","Strengthen school-based management",""],[1,"75","2","School-Based Management through School Governing Councils","school-based management through the School Governing Council will be promoted to further deepen the link between the school and the community.",""],[1,"75","2","Expanded School-Based Management Grants","School-based management grants of DepEd will be expanded and enhanced to augment funding for programs and projects that are more responsive in catering to the specific needs of individual schools.","DepEd"],[1,"75","3","Learning Materials and Curriculum Update Programme","Learning materials shall be continuously updated and improved based on recent trends in international education frameworks and standards (e.g., promotion of civic education, Education for Sustainable Development, and global citizenship education with emphasis on human rights, gender equality and social inclusion, environmental sustainability, and social justice in the curriculum).",""],[1,"75","3","Competency-Based Curriculum and Pedagogical Development","The aligned competencies of systems thinking, anticipatory thinking, normative competence, strategic competence, and interpersonal competence will be the focus of curriculum and pedagogical development.",""],[1,"75","3","SUC and HEI Learning Materials Development Support","SUCs and HEIs shall be utilized in developing learning materials that adopt new pedagogical practices across all levels.",""],[1,"75","3","School Textbook Evaluation and Updating Initiative","Continuous evaluation and updating of school textbooks shall be given specific attention.",""],[1,"75","3","Mother Tongue-Based Learning Materials Pilot","Appropriate approaches shall be used in developing mother tongue-based learning materials and will be piloted, assessed, and evaluated in selected schools.",""],[1,"75","4","Teacher Workload Review and Reallocation Reform","The workload of teachers will be reviewed to enable them to focus on teaching rather than preparing routine reports, performing administrative tasks, and being utilized by other agencies for program implementation as frontline government personnel.",""],[1,"75","4","Teacher Capacity Building Interventions","Teachers shall focus more on addressing the learning losses, coping with the new pedagogical practices, and enhancing their competencies through participation in capacity building interventions in accordance with international standards.",""],[1,"75","4","School Human Resources Restructuring","The human resources complement of schools and other education institutions will be restructured (i.e., hiring more administrative and other non-teaching staff) to ensure effective and efficient service delivery without putting undue burden on the teachers.",""],[1,"75","6","Third-Party Student Proficiency Assessment and Monitoring Partnership","Partner with independent third-party institutions in assessing and monitoring the progress of students' proficiency across all levels",""],[1,"75","7","Independent Student Competency Assessment Mechanism","Independent third-party organizations will be tapped to guarantee objective assessments of students' competencies at all education levels.",""],[1,"76","6","K-12 Curriculum Reform","The proposed law seeks to revisit the K-12 curriculum to make the graduates more readily employable, better equipped with critical thinking and problem-solving skills, and imbued with the skills and capacities needed to be productive and active citizens of the country.",""],[1,"76","8","Expansion of the National Feeding Program in Secondary Schools","Expansion of the National Feeding Program in secondary schools",""],[1,"76","9","Expansion of the School-Based Feeding Program","The proposed law addresses what is identified as among the biggest problems of the student population by expanding the coverage of the School-Based Feeding Program, as mandated by RA 11037, to include learners from Grades 7 to 12",""],[1,"76","11","Expansion of Government Assistance to Students and Teachers in Private Education to Elementary Level","Expansion of the Government Assistance to Students and Teachers in Private Education [GASTPE) to Elementary Level",""],[1,"76","12","Expansion of Government Assistance for Private Education","the measure aims to expand the existing government assistance for high school students and teachers in private education to include students in private schools in the kindergarten up to Grade 6 level.",""],[1,"76","12","Teacher Salary Subsidy Expansion for Private Elementary Schools","The Teacher Salary Subsidy [TSS) is also proposed to be expanded to cover teachers employed in private elementary schools.",""]],"55":[[1,"39","28","TVET Program Improvement for Industry Responsiveness","TVET programs will be improved to make them more responsive to industry needs.",""],[1,"69","14","Future-Ready TVET Programme Design and Implementation","Design and implement future-ready technical and vocational education and training (TVET) programs",""],[1,"69","17","Structural Reforms to Strengthen LUC-TVET Linkages","Implement structural reforms in LUCs to strengthen linkages with TVET communities",""],[1,"69","21","Private Sector Participation in TVET","Increase involvement/participation of industry and private sector in TVET",""],[1,"69","24","Enterprise-Based Training and Micro-Credentials Expansion","Improve enterprise-based training and bolster micro-credentials",""],[1,"72","1","Future-Ready TVET Program Design and Implementation","Future-ready TVET programs will be designed and implemented to prepare trainees for the world of work, Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR), and the global knowledge economy.",""],[1,"72","1","Ladderized Education Promotion","Ladderized education programs will be promoted.",""],[1,"72","1","Expanded TVI Course Offerings in Agri-Entrepreneurship and Modern Agri-Fisheries","agri-entrepreneurship, tropical agriculture farming management, and modern agri-fisheries technologies will be included among the course offerings of technical-vocational institutes (TVI).",""],[1,"72","1","TVI Human Resource Scaling and Rightsizing","The human resource complement of TVIs should also be scaled up and rightsized to ensure availability of trainers capable of implementing these new course offerings and pursuing wider clientele.",""],[1,"72","2","Community-Responsive TVET Delivery","Local government units, particularly their LUCs, and polytechnic institutions will be tapped to deliver TVET programs responsive to the needs of local communities and expand opportunities for adult learning.",""],[1,"72","2","LUC Capacity Building for TVET Management","This will be supported by capacity building programs for LUCs in setting up, managing, and implementing TVET programs and establishing linkages in the communities.",""],[1,"72","3","Private Sector Participation in TVET","Increase involvement/participation of industry and private sector in TVET",""],[1,"72","4","Industry-Private Sector TVET Partnership Strengthening","Industry participation in the design, development, implementation, and assessment of TVET programs will be intensified to respond to the needs of the national and international labor markets.",""],[1,"72","4","Private Sector Collaboration Mechanism for TVET","Partnership with the private sector, particularly with critical industry players, will be built and strengthened through improving collaborative mechanisms.",""],[1,"72","4","TVET Partner Customer Relationship Management System","A customer relationship management system that will monitor existing and potential partners will be established35 (See Chapter 4).",""],[1,"72","5","Enterprise-Based Training Expansion and Promotion","Enterprise-based training (EBT) will be expanded and promoted as a dominant mode of TVET delivery to improve workforce employability.",""],[1,"76","13","TVET Strengthening through Apprenticeship, Dual Training, and Enterprise-Based Training","Strengthening of the Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET) in the Philippines by incorporating Apprenticeship and Dual Training System, providing for Continuous Training of the Unemployed, and Expanding the Provision of Enterprise-Based Education and Training",""],[1,"76","14","Enterprise-Based Training Program Expansion","This proposed measure aims to incorporate the existing programs under the \"Enterprise-Based Training Program\" administered by the Technical Education and Skills Development Authority [TESDA) and expand the provision of training programs being implemented within companies.","Technical Education and Skills Development Authority"],[1,"76","14","University-TESDA-TVET Partnership Strengthening","Strengthening partnerships among local universities and colleges, TESDA, and TVET institutions are suggested to be highlighted to ensure that programs will cater to community needs and priorities, including agri- entrepreneurship.","Technical Education and Skills Development Authority"],[1,"87","2","Housing Human Resources Skills Program","DHSUD shall develop a human resources skills program to meet housing production needs.","DHSUD"],[1,"129","5","Training Standards and Curriculum Update for Priority Occupations","Update contents of training standards, modules, and curricula for human capital development based on emerging, in-demand, and hard-to-fill occupations in identified key employment generators",""],[1,"129","7","TVET, Apprenticeships, and Higher Education Modernization","Develop modern and responsive TVET, apprenticeships, and higher education aligned with emerging trends or demands in the labor market",""],[1,"129","9","Investment in TVET, Higher Education, Digitalization, and Innovation Facilities","Increase investments in TVET human resources, higher education, digitalization initiatives, and innovation facilities",""],[1,"129","12","National Lifelong Learning Policy","Develop and promote a national policy for lifelong learning",""],[1,"129","13","Skills Assessment and Prior Learning Certification Mechanism","Establish skills assessment mechanisms and certification programs to recognize prior learning",""],[1,"129","15","TVET Industry Collaboration Strengthening","Strengthen collaboration with industry boards and industry associations in TVET",""],[1,"129","16","Professional Standards and Licensure Examination Alignment","Align professional standards and licensure examinations with international standards",""],[1,"129","30","TVET Awareness Campaign","Create awareness of TVET programs implemented by the government",""],[1,"131","2","TVET, Higher Education, Digitalization, and Innovation Investment Programme","Increase investments in TVET human resources, higher education, digitalization initiatives, and innovation facilities",""],[1,"131","4","TVET Innovation Centers","The establishment of TVET Innovation Centers has already started in some parts of the country.",""],[1,"131","4","Community Training and Employment Coordinator Institutionalization","The government shall promote the role of community training and employment coordinators (CTEC) in monitoring and addressing local skills needs.",""],[1,"131","4","CTEC Institutionalization for TESDA Devolution","The government shall also institutionalize CTEC to support devolution strategies of the Technical Education and Skills Development Authority (TESDA).",""],[1,"132","2","National Micro-Credentials Marketplace","The government shall study the establishment of a national micro-credentials marketplace as part of emerging initiatives to promote lifelong learning",""],[1,"132","3","Digital Accreditation System Using Blockchain","a system must leverage available technologies that facilitate digital accreditation.",""],[1,"132","4","Micro-Credential Competency-Based Award System","A competency-based system will be developed through which workers and labor entrants are awarded micro-credential via training or recognition of prior learning.",""],[1,"138","8","TVET Marketing and Promotion Strategy","The TVI can formulate marketing strategies to promote jobs that only TVET programs render achievable.",""],[1,"138","8","TVET Skills Fairs and Competitions","within TVI networks, participants may need to organize skills fairs or competitions, showcasing technical capabilities and other attributes.",""],[1,"138","8","Digital Platforms for TVET Promotion","Moreover, TVI can create digital platforms that popularize TVET programs, focusing on sustaining the economy's ability to cater to emerging skills.",""]],"56":[[1,"197","5","Curriculum Revision and Development Support for Educational Institutions","Appropriate funds for educational institutions that will revise or develop new curricula to address learning gaps.",""],[1,"197","6","Incentives for Academic Research Grants in the Services Sector","DepEd, CHED, and TESDA shall continue to extend incentives to academic institutions that provide funds and grants for the research of their students and faculty on the development and promotion of the services sector.","DepEd | CHED | TESDA"],[1,"197","7","Private Sector Mentoring and STEM-STEAM Career Promotion Initiative","Strengthen collaboration with the private sector in mentoring programs; promotion of science, technology, engineering, entrepreneurship, arts, and mathematics careers; and interventions to build talent in differentiated services proposition.",""],[1,"197","7","Financial, Digital, and Cybersecurity Literacy Development Programme","This initiative aims to increase financial, digital, and cybersecurity literacy; and develop entrepreneurial and creative skills from early schooling by revising curricula (inclusion of mandatory basic computer education, introduction of relevant electives and/or micro-credentials across courses) to support IT-BPM upgrading.",""],[1,"200","2","Academe-Government-Industry Skills Collaboration","Strengthen collaboration among academe, government, and industry boards in talent and skills development",""],[1,"200","3","Curriculum Revision and Industry-Aligned Course Design","Revise existing curricula or design new courses based on the needs of the industries.",""],[1,"200","3","Tracer Studies and Immersion and Internship Programmes","The private sector will work closely with the academe and government agencies in the conduct of tracer studies; design and implementation of immersion and internship programs for faculty and students in the country and abroad; and facilitation of",""],[1,"200","5","International Talent Transfer and Exchange Programmes","Expand talent pool through the transfer of international talents and skills, and exchange programs for faculty and students (See Chapter 4).",""],[1,"200","5","Private Sector Diversity and International Network Partnership Initiative","Promote diversity to nurture creativity in the private sector by partnering with international networks of suppliers, buyers, and educational institutions.",""],[1,"200","6","Philippine Skills Framework Initiative","Provide information and expert advice on the must-have skills and competencies under the Philippine Skills Framework (PSF) Initiative to boost the capacity of the Philippines in skills of the future.",""],[1,"200","6","PSF Logistics and Supply Chain Course Development","Under the PSF on logistics and supply chain, the first to be launched by the DTI under the initiative, the sector will collaborate with TESDA to develop course modules and assessment tools.","DTI | TESDA"],[1,"218","9","Digital Workforce Competitiveness and Skills Upgrading Act","Act to Enhance the Digital Workforce Competitiveness aims to ensure that citizens are provided with the necessary digital skills and competencies that are at par with global standards and shall encourage digital innovations and entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"229","7","Rapid Digital Skills Development Initiative","This would entail a credible and coordinated commitment both from the private and public sectors to invest in the rapid development of digital skills in order to build a concentration of digital talents in the country.",""],[1,"230","2","Regional Digital Talent Hub Development","The government, by mobilizing its regional growth centers, will create a visible concentration of digital savvy pool of talents in various parts of the country.",""],[1,"230","2","Multi-Stakeholder Digital Talent Partnership","This will entail tight partnerships among industry players, knowledge institutes, LGUs, and the national government.",""],[1,"230","2","Digital Talent Retention Incentive Measures","new incentive measures will be designed to try and arrest this trend.",""]],"57":[[1,"130","6","Explore a Market of Competencies","The feasibility of establishing a market of competencies to address emerging skills needs in the short term shall be explored (See Subchapter 2.2).",""],[1,"130","8","Forward-Looking Skills Anticipation System","The government shall pursue the development of forward-looking systems that anticipate emerging skills and educational qualifications and complement industry efforts to inform training regulation development (See Subchapter 2.2).",""],[1,"135","1","Skills Anticipation and Curriculum Alignment","Identifying and anticipating skills needed for priority sectors of the economy shall precede training decisions so that skills required are relevant for the labor market.",""],[1,"135","1","Agricultural Sector Skills Foresight for Transformation","For example, to align with the agricultural sector transformation, the government will anticipate and address the implications from mechanization, diversification, bio-based inputs production, and waste management.",""],[1,"135","1","High-Technology Upskilling and Reskilling Initiatives","In the high-technology sector, upskilling and reskilling initiatives can focus on advanced manufacturing, robotics, artificial intelligence, the Internet of Things, and blockchain.",""],[1,"135","2","Private Labor Market Assessment Tools and Information Investment","investing in private labor market assessment tools and information",""],[1,"137","4","Institutionalized Stakeholder Engagement for Skills Anticipation","To make LMIS more dynamic and forward-looking, the government shall institutionalize systematic stakeholder engagement with social partners to focus on skills anticipation systems and policy development.",""],[1,"137","5","Labor Administration Capacity Assessment","Thus, assessing the capacity of labor administration to maintain such an ecosystem shall be prioritized.",""],[1,"137","5","Skills Development Authority Mandate Review","The government shall evaluate the mandate of the skills development authority given an environment continuously shaped by climate change, automation, and increased digitalization.",""]],"58":[[1,"129","29","Lifelong Learning Integration in Human Resource Development Programs","Integrate lifelong learning processes in human resource development programs",""],[1,"131","7","National Lifelong Learning Policy","Develop and promote a national policy for lifelong learning",""],[1,"131","10","Lifelong Learning Institutionalization Master Plan","The government shall sustain efforts to develop a master plan for institutionalizing lifelong learning beyond formal education.",""],[1,"131","10","Local Government Lifelong Learning Integration","It shall encourage local government units (LGU) to plan and integrate lifelong learning programs to transform their jurisdictions into learning communities.",""],[1,"131","10","Lifelong Learning Governance and Awareness Campaigns","One important aspect of this initiative is that by institutionalizing governance mechanisms and awareness campaigns that advance lifelong learning initiatives, LGUs can promote inclusive learning in the workplace and foster a culture of learning among its constituents.",""],[1,"137","5","Responsive Education, Lifelong Learning, and Skills Governance Mechanisms","Sustaining an education, lifelong learning, and skills ecosystem require responsive and innovative policies and mechanisms to oversee programs and anticipate problems or supply bottlenecks.",""],[1,"138","6","Lifelong Learning Integration in Human Resource Development Programs","Integrate lifelong learning processes in human resource development programs",""],[1,"139","11","Lifelong Learning Development Framework","Develop a Lifelong Learning Development Framework through the Philippine Qualifications Framework-National Coordinating Council (PQF-NCC).",""],[1,"141","10","Learning Cities and Municipalities Initiative","One of the main objectives of Senate Bill No. 129 is establishing learning cities and municipalities.",""]],"60":[[1,"76","16","Mandatory Reserve Officers Training Corps Revival","reviving the Mandatory Reserve Officers Training Corps and/or integrating disaster risk response and management training in the curriculum of students (See Chapter 13)",""],[1,"76","16","Disaster Risk Response Curriculum Integration","integrating disaster risk response and management training in the curriculum of students (See Chapter 13)",""],[1,"76","18","Mandatory Reserve Officers Training Corps Revival","reviving the Mandatory Reserve Officers Training Corps and/or integrating disaster risk response",""],[1,"76","18","Disaster Risk Response Integration","reviving the Mandatory Reserve Officers Training Corps and/or integrating disaster risk response",""],[1,"339","8","Unified Citizens' Civil and Military Training Program","This aims to unify the three training programs of the current National Service Training Program into a single and comprehensive citizens' civil and military training in the first two [2] years of a baccalaureate degree program.",""]],"61":[[1,"82","20","Inclusive and Resilient Housing and Community Design Integration","Integrate accessibility, health, culture, and resilience outcomes into design of housing and communities",""],[1,"88","1","Inclusive and Resilient Housing and Community Design Integration","Integrate accessibility, health, culture, and resilience outcomes into design of housing and communities",""],[1,"88","2","Review of Socialized and Economic Housing Standards","The socialized and economic housing standards (Batas Pambansa 220) shall be reviewed to consider minimum health standards; accessibility; cultural appropriateness; climate and disaster resilience; energy efficiency; green spaces; active mobility; innovative technologies; urbanization trends; and changing housing preferences (i.e., halfway homes, first-time homebuyers, young professionals, and permanent family homes).",""],[1,"88","2","Enforcement of Open Space and Community Facility Requirements","The implementation of open spaces such as parks, playgrounds, and community facilities and amenities45 shall be strictly enforced, which could likewise be used as green spaces.",""],[1,"88","3","Green Building Features Adoption in Housing and Community Design","Green features in housing and community design shall be adopted-such as renewable energy, green roofs, rainwater harvesting systems, rain gardens, permeable pavement, green construction materials, nature-based storm drainage systems, gray water recycling system, and energy-efficient windows (with reference to the Green Building Code).",""],[1,"88","5","Building and Construction Utilities Readiness Standards","Improvements in building and construction milestones shall be instituted to ensure that utilities (water, electricity, telecommunications, and sanitation) are available ahead of occupancy.",""],[1,"94","11","Residential Subdivision Open Space Requirement","44 PD 1216 requires the developer or owner of a residential subdivision one hectare or more to allocate 30 percent of the gross area for open space.",""],[1,"94","12","Residential Subdivision Open Space Requirement","45 PD 1216 requires the developer or owner of a residential subdivision one hectare or more to allocate 30 percent of the gross area for open space.",""]],"62":[[1,"19","6","Critical Infrastructure Expansion and Upgrading","expanding and upgrading critical infrastructure (Chapter 12)",""],[1,"19","7","Digital and Physical Connectivity Investment","enhancing and investing in digital and physical connectivity",""],[1,"37","8","Airport Capacity Expansion","Increasing the capacity of airports can revitalize tourism;",""],[1,"37","8","Port Upgrading and Maritime Safety Improvement","upgrading ports and improving maritime safety can facilitate the movement of goods, thereby promoting trade and making the country more attractive to investments.",""],[1,"38","5","Public-Private Partnership Reconfiguration","Reconfiguring public-private partnerships (PPP) can also help in addressing cross-cutting issues of a weak competition environment and the digital divide, as well as boost the country's campaign to attract foreign investments.",""],[1,"38","5","Expanded Public-Private Partnerships for Infrastructure","The tight fiscal space that will constrain public investments for the next few years provides a rationale for favoring PPPs in enhancing and upgrading infrastructure.",""],[1,"38","5","Private Sector Participation in Housing, Transport, and Digital Infrastructure","Larger private sector participation in areas such as housing, transport, digital, and other related large infrastructure can free up public funds for investments in human capital to address, for instance, the scarring from the pandemic in health care and education.",""],[1,"43","2","Infrastructure Investment Programme","Investments in the appropriate infrastructure can help reduce the cost of electricity, ensure water security, and lower the cost of logistics.",""],[1,"43","2","Public-Private Partnership Promotion","Given the limits to government resources and capabilities, PPPs will be further encouraged.",""],[1,"43","2","Infrastructure Sectoral Master Plans and Road Maps","Infrastructure sectoral master plans and road maps will be prepared to provide a more comprehensive understanding of the infrastructure gaps and needs, and thus serve as a sound basis for identifying priority infrastructure programs, activities, and projects, including those that may be best pursued through PPP modalities.",""],[1,"76","16","Education Infrastructure Legislation","Key legislations improving education infrastructure (See Chapter 12], reviving the Mandatory Reserve Officers Training Corps and/or integrating disaster risk response and management training in the curriculum of students (See Chapter 13), promoting upskilling and reskilling of labor force (See Chapter 4), and advancing R&D and innovation (See Chapter 8).",""],[1,"76","18","Education Infrastructure Improvement and Lifelong Learning Legislation","Also important for ensuring lifelong learning opportunities are key legislations improving education infrastructure (See Chapter 12), reviving the Mandatory Reserve Officers Training Corps and/or integrating disaster risk response",""],[1,"397","1","Infrastructure Expansion and Upgrading Programme","the Infrastructure Committee will pursue the expansion and upgrading of the country's infrastructure",""],[1,"433","2","Intermodal and Multimodal Transport Network Development Plan","Plan that serves as the roadmap that will guide the rational development of an intermodal/multimodal transport network in the country, which will connect major and emerging economic growth centers and transport hubs using actual post-pandemic data on travel demand and supply.",""]],"63":[[1,"302","6","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Planning and Investment Mainstreaming","Climate resilience will be mainstreamed in infrastructure planning and investment so that climate risks are considered and managed across all types of infrastructure and throughout the lifecycle of infrastructure assets and operations.",""],[1,"302","6","Nature-Based and Innovative Infrastructure Design","Moreover, innovative technologies, including nature-based solutions (NBS), will be employed in infrastructure planning and design.",""],[1,"303","4","Climate Risk Integration in Infrastructure PPP Planning","the government will clarify allocation of responsibilities to integrate climate risks in planning, management, or operation of infrastructure.",""]],"64":[[1,"313","6","Indigenous Energy Resource Utilization and PCECP Implementation","The government will maximize utilization of indigenous energy resources.",""],[1,"313","6","Upstream Petroleum Exploration Challenge Response","Moving forward, the government will address the challenges of the upstream sector related to exploration activities in the West Philippine Sea.",""],[1,"324","11","West Philippine Sea Activity Clearance Requirement","PSC holders are required to secure clearance from the National Task Force - West Philippine Sea; and the Security, Justice, and Peace Coordinating Cluster prior to any activity to be conducted in the West Philippine Sea area.",""],[1,"435","10","Petroleum Service Contract Awarding Mechanism","The PCECP is a transparent petroleum service contract awarding mechanism that allows the government to develop and utilize indigenous petroleum resources under a service contract with qualified local and international exploration companies.",""],[1,"435","10","PCECP Local Roadshow Outreach","The PCECP local road shows are scheduled to be held in Palawan on 20 September, Davao on 27 September and Zamboanga in October 2018.",""]],"65":[[1,"310","9","Green Energy Option Program Full Implementation","The full implementation of the Green Energy Option Program- RCOA's counterpart with emphasis on RE- also empowers consumers with a 100-kilowatt (kW) demand to choose RE as their preferred power supply.",""],[1,"311","3","Renewable Portfolio Standards Implementation","The recent issuance on the Renewable Portfolio Standards furthers utilization of renewables as the policy provides a quota for consumers (through the mandated participants) to purchase RE from 1 percent to 2.52 percent annually starting 2023.",""],[1,"312","7","Energy Transition Enabling Environment and Market Incentive Reform","The government will endeavor to provide an enabling environment for an efficient energy transition that respects technological neutrality and a level playing field.",""],[1,"313","2","Foreign Ownership Liberalization for Renewable Energy Generation","Liberalization of foreign ownership of RE generation will be pursued to stimulate investments toward efficient energy transition.",""],[1,"313","3","Renewable Energy Intermittency Management Measures","To facilitate the entry of more renewables, intermittency problems shall be addressed.",""],[1,"313","3","Mandatory and Preferential Renewable Energy Dispatch","The mandatory and preferential dispatch of RE is expected to facilitate the increase in RE investments.",""],[1,"313","3","Capacity Market Development for Flexible Generation","Capacity markets shall be developed to allow for more generation plants with flexibility to adjust generated output as needed to compensate for the intermittency of renewable sources.",""],[1,"318","23","Coal Revenue-Sharing and Incentive Reform","This will revise the income/sharing scheme and incentives granted to industry stakeholders; to increase the government share in coal operations and define the role of mining operators in environmental protection.",""],[1,"323","34","Preferential Dispatch for Renewable Energy Generators","A recent policy issuance accorded preferential dispatch to all qualified and registered generating units utilizing RE in the wholesale electricity spot market.",""],[1,"426","2","Green Energy Auction Program","The Green Energy Auction Program (GEAP) was undertaken to support and facilitate immediate and timely investments in new or additional renewable energy capacities to ensure provision of adequate supply and competitive rates of electricity in the country.",""],[1,"426","4","Green Energy Option Program","The Green Energy Option Program (GEOP) is a Renewable Energy (RE) policy mechanism which shall provide end-user the option to choose RE resources as their source of energy.",""],[1,"432","6","Energy Conservation and Efficient Utilization Policy","A declared policy of the government to promote the judicious conservation and efficient utilization of energy resources through adoption of the cost-effective options toward the efficient use of energy to minimize environmental impact.",""],[1,"437","19","Retail Competition and Open Access Establishment","The establishment of RCOA is mandated by the Electric Power Industry Reform Act of 2001 (EPIRA) to offer options to the end-users and grow the market.",""]],"66":[[1,"192","3","Tourism Product Development Manual Rollout and LGU Training","The Department of Tourism (DOT) will accelerate the roll out of the product development manual and training modules for local government units (LGU) to increase the readiness of products and destinations for safe, smart, and sustainable tourism.","Department of Tourism (DOT)"],[1,"192","4","International Tourism Promotion and Investment Mission Partnerships","Increase participation in high-impact international events and dedicated investment missions to build on positive perceptions and success stories of destinations and people.","Department of Trade and Industry (DTI) | Department of Foreign Affairs"],[1,"192","5","Local Tourism Governance Transformation","Improve local tourism governance by transforming LGUs into destination management organizations with strong private sector partnership.",""],[1,"192","6","Local Tourism Planning and Tourism Office Institutionalization","local tourism plans and institutionalization of tourism offices for sustainability.","DOT | Tourism Infrastructure Enterprise Zone Authority"],[1,"192","7","Holiday Economics Promotion and Domestic Tourism Campaign","Promote \"holiday economics\" and invest in year-round, domestic, multi-media campaign together with the LGUs, private sector, and educational institutions to encourage Filipinos to travel, promote pride of place and culture, and become ambassadors of Philippine tourism.",""],[1,"192","9","National Tourism Accreditation and Certification Promotion","Promote national accreditation such as the progressive accreditation system and ANAHAW Philippine Sustainable Tourism Certification to build the confidence of markets and enterprises.",""],[1,"192","9","Sustainable Tourism Services Promotion","Advocate enterprises to offer sustainable services as key differentiators of Philippine tourism using international standards for low-carbon emission tourism value chains.",""],[1,"192","10","Capacity Building for DOT Regional Offices and LGUs","Increase the capacity of the DOT regional offices and the LGUs to assist enterprises'",""],[1,"193","1","Enterprise Quality Standards Accreditation Initiative","The initiative aims to increase the number of enterprises that embrace quality standards in facilities and services for the benefit of tourists and enterprise owners.",""],[1,"193","2","Tourism Knowledge Transfer and Sustainable Tourism Partnerships","In partnership with the DOT, the private sector will promote partnerships between large enterprises and micro, small, and medium enterprises (MSME) to propagate high service quality in tourism, curate mutually beneficial authentic tourism experiences with local communities, and scale up sustainable tourism practices.","DOT"],[1,"193","4","Active Promotion of Tourism, Culture, Creative Industries, and IT-BPM Sector","Spearhead the active promotion of tourism, culture, creative industries, and the information technology and business process management sector",""],[1,"193","5","Creative Industries Tourism Branding and Marketing Expansion","Harness the creative industries to increase positive perception of tourism destinations and build the distinctly Filipino brand of tourism and culture.",""],[1,"193","5","Domestic and International Tourism Promotion Campaigns","Expand marketing thrusts by actively participating in domestic and international travel trade shows, familiarization trips, and consumer activation programs supported by the government.",""],[1,"193","6","International Market Access Partnership for Philippine Destinations and Creative Products","Partner with international organizations and networks of global Filipino communities to increase market access of Philippine destinations and Filipino creative designs and products.",""],[1,"197","3","Philippine Tourism Human Capital Development Plan","Implement the Philippine Tourism Human Capital Development Plan 2021-2025 to ensure the steady supply of trained human resources.",""],[1,"197","3","Filipino Brand of Service Excellence Program","The Filipino Brand of Service Excellence Program of the DOT will continue to promote the best qualities and positive values of Filipino hospitality.","DOT"],[1,"198","1","Physical Connectivity Improvement","Facilitate physical connectivity (aviation, shipping and maritime, and land) and convenience to move people and goods",""],[1,"198","2","Sustainable Tourism Transport and Digital Services Upgrade","Increase access to tourist destinations through an improved and sustainable transportation network, and digitalization of tourist services to increase yields from higher spending and length of stay in a wide range of destinations.",""],[1,"198","2","Inter- and Multi-Modal Tourism Routes Development","Develop and expand inter- and multi-modal tourism routes (air, shipping and maritime, land) supported by the DOT, Department of Transportation, and Department of Public Works and Highways.","DOT | Department of Transportation | Department of Public Works and Highways"],[1,"198","2","National Cruise Tourism Strategy Update Support","Provide support for update of the National Cruise Tourism Strategy to enhance the contributions of local and international cruise tourism and maritime industries to the Philippine blue ocean economy and jobs.",""],[1,"198","3","Barrier-Free Tourism Support Services","Promote barrier-free tourism by providing technology-enabled real-time information and assistance, and the Filipino brand of service excellence and care to visitors, particularly those with special needs.",""],[1,"199","10","Digital Data Collection Capacity Building for Tourism Stakeholders","Increase the capacities of destination stakeholders to adopt digitally enabled data collection tools and measures.",""]],"67":[[1,"381","1","Climate-Informed Spatial Planning Measures","Planning and implementation of interventions that address vulnerabilities across ecosystems and improve their resilience will be science- and evidence-based and risk-informed, such as the use of climate-adjusted hazard maps in spatial planning.",""],[1,"381","5","Land Administration and Titling Reform","Strengthening and improving the efficiency of land administration, particularly the streamlining of regulatory mechanisms for land titling, will also be prioritized to ensure land tenure security, thereby increasing people's adaptive capacity to climate change and natural hazards.",""],[1,"387","2","Hazard-Prone Area Construction Controls and Green Space Allocation","limiting construction in hazard-prone areas, allocating green spaces (See Subchapter 2.3), and improving regulation in building codes and permits",""],[1,"387","6","Forestland Boundary Delineation and Tenure Security Policy","The bill intends to delineate the specific limits of forestlands for the conservation, protection, and development of the country's forest resources.",""],[1,"387","11","Land Administration and Records Modernization","This bill aims to upgrade, systematize, and integrate the administration, management, and operations of the country's land resources.",""],[1,"387","11","Land Records, Titling, and Information System Reform","It also aims to improve, rationalize, and systematize land records, titling, documentation, and information systems into an open, updated, and reliable system.",""]],"68":[[1,"19","7","Digitalization Acceleration Strategy","expediting digitalization",""],[1,"28","2","Digital Technology Investment","we need to fast-track investments in ... technology-particularly digital technology-and innovation",""],[1,"36","7","Government Digital Transformation","Digital transformation of government will result in more efficient and faster service delivery to the people, more",""],[1,"43","7","Bureaucratic Efficiency and Public Sector Reengineering","the government must pursue bureaucratic efficiency to maximize the benefits from public spending.",""],[1,"89","4","Local Government Digital Governance and Service Delivery","Local government units shall use the national digitalization platform, aligning with digitalization programs of national government agencies (e.g., digitalization of business processes), and adopt digital governance.",""],[1,"89","4","Local Constituents Digital Skills Strengthening","LGUs shall likewise strengthen the digital skills of their respective constituents.",""],[1,"366","2","Digital Government Transformation","Accordingly, the government will adopt digital technologies for the optimization and integration of its services to improve efficiency and rightsize the government.",""],[1,"366","2","E-Governance Legal and Institutional Reform","To accelerate digital transformation, the government will strengthen its legal and institutional framework; adopt paperless, cashless, and data-empowered transactions at all levels; and develop civil service capacity for implementation.",""],[1,"366","2","Integrated E-Governance Network Law","the government will pass an e-Governance law to establish an integrated, interconnected, and interoperable information, resource- sharing, and communications network to deliver public services.",""],[1,"366","2","Digital Government Payments Adoption","the government will ensure the effective implementation of policies and programs such as the adoption of digital payments for government disbursements",""]],"69":[[1,"397","7","Philippine Statistics Development Program","The Philippine Statistics Development Program will remain the primary mechanism to address the data requirements for the monitoring of the PDP and other sectoral plans and regional plans.",""],[1,"420","16","Community-Based Disaggregated Data System","An organized technology-based system of collecting, processing, and validating necessary disaggregated data that may be used for planning, program implementation, and impact monitoring at the local level while empowering communities to participate in the process.",""],[1,"432","8","Online RSBSA Registry Update System","An online application being used to update the Registry System for Basic Sectors in Agriculture (RSBSA).",""]],"70":[[1,"367","1","Public Servant Capacity Development","Transformation in government systems and mechanisms will not be possible without the development of public servants' competence, motivation, agility, and resilience.",""],[1,"367","2","Public Sector Competency Framework Development","the government will adopt a purposive and programmatic approach to developing new competency frameworks for the public sector.",""],[1,"367","3","Career Executive Service Competency Framework Development","the Career Executive Service Board (CESB) will develop the new competency","Career Executive Service Board (CESB)"],[1,"367","4","Civil Service Executive System Strengthening and Leadership Development Program","The CES system will be strengthened through merit and fitness, and continuous updating of its program offerings.",""],[1,"367","5","Pandemic-Responsive Learning and Development Program","Learning and development52 (delivered through pandemic-responsive modalities); and awards and incentives53 programs will support public servants at all stages of their careers while advocating for higher levels of employee engagement.",""],[1,"367","5","Awards and Incentives Program for Public Servants","Learning and development52 (delivered through pandemic-responsive modalities); and awards and incentives53 programs will support public servants at all stages of their careers while advocating for higher levels of employee engagement.",""],[1,"367","5","Meritocracy and Excellence in Human Resource Management Program","Contributing to the strategy implementation are the CSC's Program to Institutionalize Meritocracy and Excellence in Human Resource Management55 and the CES system.",""],[1,"367","5","Career Executive Service System","Contributing to the strategy implementation are the CSC's Program to Institutionalize Meritocracy and Excellence in Human Resource Management55 and the CES system.",""],[1,"371","24","Public Sector HRM Excellence Program","This program aims to elevate public sector HR management to a level of excellence through the assessment, assistance, and awarding processes of HRM Systems, Practices, and Competencies using HRM maturity level indicators that are at par with global HRM standards.",""]],"71":[[1,"361","20","Anti-Corruption Law and Program Implementation and Monitoring","Strengthen implementation and monitoring of anti-corruption laws and programs",""],[1,"363","5","Integrity and Anti-Corruption Strategy Implementation","the government will implement strategies that will foster higher levels of trust, satisfaction, and political efficacy among the public.",""],[1,"364","4","Whole-of-Government Anti-Corruption Capacity and Coordination Reform","This involves the sectoral capacity assessment of the anti-corruption infrastructure in the country; strengthening and harmonizing the development, implementation, monitoring, and evaluation of anti-corruption programs and laws; and developing a dynamic and multi-disciplinary information technology-enabled, multi-year innovation plan.",""],[1,"364","4","Integrity Management and Public Integrity Campaigns","The Office of the Ombudsman, the CSC, and their partner agencies and stakeholders will build on lessons learned from programs such as the Integrity Management Program; Integrity, Transparency, and Accountability in Public Service; Statement of Assets, Liabilities, and Net Worth declaration; and public integrity campaigns.","Office of the Ombudsman | CSC"],[1,"364","4","Government Integrity and Corruption Control Capacity Development","The observance of a code of conduct for all government employees and capacity development in integrity management and corruption controls will be pursued to reduce corruption vulnerabilities.",""],[1,"364","4","Local Anti-Corruption Oversight and Complaint Handling","The DILG will also enable and monitor the local Sangguniang Bayan or municipal council's quasi-judicial functions and act on various corruption-related complaints filed against local officials.","DILG"],[1,"370","28","Campus Integrity and Anti-Corruption Campaigns","Campaigns include the OMB's Campus Integrity Crusaders, Sikhay Laban sa Korupsyon, and Aral at Asal Project (with the University of the Philippines System and the Commission on Higher Education).",""],[1,"428","15","Anti-Corruption Program","An anti-corruption program of the government, which aims to establish a systematic approach in building, improving, reinforcing and sustaining a culture of integrity in public sector institutions that is rooted in acceptable values, principles and standards of good governance.",""]],"72":[[1,"329","4","Justice Sector Coordination for Economic Justice","It asserts that economic justice is a pillar of a strong and vibrant economy and requires a sector-based approach anchored on strong coordination among justice sector institutions, agencies, and actors to drive public engagement and trust in the justice system.",""],[1,"341","7","Justice System Legislative and Regulatory Reforms","the Philippines has enacted and amended legislations and regulations toward improvement in the justice system.","Department of Justice (DOJ)"],[1,"342","1","Judicial Procedure and Evidence Rule Reforms","The Judiciary has also issued guidelines to ensure that the disposition of actions and proceedings is just, prompt, and inexpensive.",""],[1,"342","3","Justice Sector Coordinating Council and Justice Zones","It has achieved better coordination through the Justice Sector Coordinating Council (JSCC), which has facilitated thoughtful identification of common problems and development of sector-based solutions in selected areas called Justice Zones.",""],[1,"342","4","Case Decongestion and Delay Reduction Reforms","Both the National Prosecution Service (NPS) of the DOJ and the Supreme Court have adopted reforms in case decongestion and delay.","National Prosecution Service (NPS) of the DOJ | Supreme Court"],[1,"343","11","Sector Coordination Mechanisms Strengthening","Establish and/or strengthen coordination mechanisms to improve sector efficiency and accountability",""],[1,"343","28","Specialized and Multi-Party Case Disposition Rules Streamlining","Streamline the rules on the disposition specialized and multi-party cases",""],[1,"344","1","Sector Coordination and Accountability Mechanisms","Establish and/or strengthen coordination mechanisms to improve sector efficiency and accountability",""],[1,"344","2","Justice Zone Expansion and Coordination Mechanism","The JSCC will launch a new Justice Zone per quarter within the plan period, while existing Justice Zones expand functions to include monitoring and assessment of their coordination mechanisms, implementation of reporting to the JSCC, and sharing of best practices.",""],[1,"344","2","Criminal Investigation, Prosecution, and Case Management Streamlining","The DOJ, together with relevant law enforcement agencies or through the JSCC, will streamline criminal investigation, prosecution, and case management processes, including those for heinous crimes and illegal drugs.","DOJ"],[1,"344","4","Prosecutor-Law Enforcer Cooperation Reform","legislative and policy reforms will be pursued to institutionalize cooperation between prosecutors and law enforcers such as the PNP and NBI, among others.",""],[1,"344","5","Case Build-Up and Prosecution Support Cooperation","cooperation will facilitate case build-up through proper collection, preservation, and presentation of evidence, and will ensure successful prosecution, inclusive of legal and technical guidance.",""],[1,"344","8","JSCC Enabling Law for Justice Sector Human Resource Planning","A JSCC enabling law that adopts a sector- based approach will be enacted.",""],[1,"345","1","Establishment of New Courts and Prosecution Offices","appointments, as well as establishment of new courts and prosecution offices, among others.",""],[1,"345","1","Data Analytics for Planning Process Enhancement","Likewise, data analytics will be adopted to enhance the planning process.",""],[1,"345","2","Sector-Based Commercial Dispute Settlement Approach","A sector-based approach will be adopted in the settlement of commercial disputes, which include intra-corporate cases, intellectual property cases, cases involving admiralty and maritime laws, financial rehabilitation and liquidation of insolvent debtors, competition cases, and cybercrime cases, among others.",""],[1,"345","2","Sectoral Capacity Building and Information Exchange for Case Disposition","It will support the conduct of sectoral capacity building and information exchange activities to facilitate case disposition with the least delay, while still providing all relevant information required by the courts that are in the control and custody of various agencies in the Executive Department.",""],[1,"346","8","Specialized and Multi-Party Case Disposition Rules Streamlining","Streamline the rules on the disposition of specialized and multi-party cases",""],[1,"346","9","Land Dispute Procedure Streamlining","The rules on land disputes will be streamlined to impose the mandatory consolidation of causes of action relating to the same real property, whether for possession, ownership, or damages.",""],[1,"347","1","Judicial Clarification for Expropriation Partial Judgments","also be clarified to ensure that courts are compliant with issuing partial judgments at the different stages of an expropriation case.",""],[1,"347","1","Special Courts for Land Dispute Settlement Study","Furthermore, the Supreme Court will study the need to designate special courts on land dispute settlement.",""],[1,"347","2","Special Procedures for Multi-Party Cases","To handle multi-party cases, special rules of procedure will be crafted.",""],[1,"350","10","Justice Sector Coordination Commission Formalization","This aims to formally recognize the JSCC as a government body, with a permanent secretariat, to be charged with institutionalizing coordination mechanisms in the justice sector.",""],[1,"350","13","Justice Sector Staffing Expansion","This adopts a sector-based approach to creating positions in the justice sector by matching the creation of courts with corresponding increases in the number of prosecutors, public attorney's positions, etc .; and creates more justice sector positions to deal with workload and case congestion.",""],[1,"351","1","Unified Penal Institutions Agency","This aims to unify all penal institutions under one agency, with close collaboration among courts for the disposition of detention prisoners and convicted offenders.",""],[1,"351","8","Probation and Parole Workforce Strengthening","This will strengthen human resource allocation and improve or promote the social, moral, and economic well-being of probation and parole workers",""],[1,"397","2","Justice Sector Coordination and Oversight Mechanism","the Justice Sector Coordinating Council will have oversight on enhancing administration",""]],"73":[[1,"342","5","Electronic Court Filing and Service Reform","the Supreme Court amended the 1997 Rules of Civil Procedure, allowing an electronic mode of filing, service of pleadings, and court submissions.",""],[1,"342","5","National Justice Information System Expansion","The National Justice Information System (NJIS), which has been implemented to address case delays particularly in criminal actions, is also being expanded to include the Single Carpeta System (Inmate Management Information System) and is laying the groundwork for a unified penology system.",""],[1,"342","6","Justice Sector Automation and Digitalization","Procedures in the justice sector should likewise be automated and digitalized to expedite proceedings and for data accuracy and consistency.",""],[1,"343","14","Central Evidence Unit","Create a Central Evidence Unit to store and handle evidence in criminal cases",""],[1,"343","25","Justice Sector Digital ICT Architecture Development","Maximize the use of digital technology and build a robust, efficient, and disaster-resilient ICT architecture for the justice sector",""],[1,"343","27","Unified Crime Data Integration","Implement the integration of the unified crime index uniformity of crime data",""],[1,"344","6","Central Evidence Unit","Create a Central Evidence Unit to store and handle evidence in criminal cases",""],[1,"344","7","Central Evidence Unit Establishment","Relevant justice sector agencies will pursue the establishment of a Central Evidence Unit as a main component of the Justice Hubs, which will serve as the main repository of all evidence in criminal cases including storage of electronic evidence.",""],[1,"344","7","Integrated Evidence Processing System","To address inefficient processing of evidence, an integrated system handled by sector-representative personnel will be put in place.",""],[1,"345","5","Justice Sector Digital Transformation and ICT Resilience","Maximize the use of digital technology and build a robust, efficient, and disaster-resilient ICT architecture for the justice sector",""],[1,"345","6","Justice Sector Digital Infrastructure and Court Automation","Robust internet infrastructure will be established within the justice sector to further support online hearings and case management systems.",""],[1,"345","6","Court Automation and Digital Service Upskilling","The courts will be automated, and personnel will be upskilled to support a suite of digitalized services, such as video conferencing hearings.",""],[1,"345","6","National Justice Information System Implementation","The NJIS will be fully implemented through the Single Carpeta System as the first step in information sharing among justice sector actors.",""],[1,"345","6","Justice Sector Digital Transformation Financing and Human Resource Support","To facilitate full implementation of the NJIS, the government will allocate sufficient financial and human resources for digital transformation initiatives across the justice sector, which include the implementation of the Criminal Justice Information Exchange (CjiX) as the platform that will bridge the NJIS and the eCourt System (See Box 13.2.1).",""],[1,"346","1","Simplified Court Document Template System","In conjunction with the eCourt System and NJIS, the justice sector will also adopt a simplified system of court-bound and court-issued papers, where templates are",""],[1,"346","2","Trial Courts Automation Project","made available in the eCourt system portal and publicly, through the Trial Courts Automation Project.",""],[1,"346","3","National Justice Information System Development","The National Justice Information System (NJIS)- led by the Department of Justice (DOJ) and supported by the Department of Information and Communications Technology, and funded by Congress since 2012-is a project that involves the development and setup of core agency information management systems and inter-agency exchange mechanisms.","Department of Justice | Department of Information and Communications Technology"],[1,"346","4","Criminal Justice Information Exchange Establishment","The Criminal Justice Information Exchange (CJiX) will be established linking all justice sector agencies.","DOJ | Department of the Interior and Local Government | the judiciary"],[1,"346","5","Unified Crime Index Integration","Implement the integration of the unified crime index to improve uniformity of crime data",""],[1,"346","6","Unified Crime Index Database and Technology-Based Case Management Rollout","A unified crime index database will be utilized in all applicable processes to support the rollout of technology-based case management solutions.",""],[1,"346","7","Index Database Capacity Building and Integration","partnership with the DILG and the Supreme Court, will conduct capacity building on the use of the index database, including its integration to existing data-related processes.","DILG | the Supreme Court"]],"74":[[1,"199","3","Internet Speed and Coverage Expansion","Increase internet speed, coverage, and network",""],[1,"199","4","Fiber-Optic, Broadband, and 5G Network Expansion","Expand fiber-optic, broadband, and 5G network in areas identified by industries on a priority basis",""],[1,"199","5","Broadband Expansion for Underserved Areas","Build and operate broadband facilities to offer internet services in underserved and unserved areas.",""],[1,"199","5","Satellite Connectivity for Businesses and Tourism Sites","Use direct access to all satellite systems, whether fixed, mobile, international, or domestic, to connect local businesses and tourism sites with their developing markets and to build resilience.",""],[1,"218","9","Public Telecommunications Development and Governance Policy","Public Telecommunications Policy Act aims to promote and govern the development of Philippine telecommunications and the delivery of public telecommunications services;",""],[1,"251","6","Broadband and Digital Technology Expansion for MSMEs","Expand access to broadband internet and digital technologies to enhance consumer choice and facilitate digitalization and innovation among micro, small, and medium enterprises",""],[1,"251","8","National Broadband Plan Implementation","the DICT will ensure the continuity and implementation of the National Broadband Plan to provide quality broadband throughout the country.","DICT"],[1,"251","8","Restriction of Exclusive ISP Arrangements","The PCC will continue to discourage, and where warranted, prohibit exclusivity arrangements between property developers and ISPs to ensure that consumers are able to subscribe to their preferred service providers","PCC"],[1,"251","8","Digital Transformation Support for MSMEs","The DTI will continue and intensify its programs to facilitate the digital transformation of MSMEs and conduct capacity-building activities to train MSMEs in digital marketing, digital payments, and cybersecurity, among other skills and knowledge.","DTI"],[1,"252","5","Digital Market Competition and Regulatory Reform","The government will address competition and regulatory constraints that hinder the development of digital markets to meet the increasing need for digital transformation and improve the country's ability to leverage growth opportunities during the recovery.",""],[1,"252","5","Open Access and Competition-Enhancing Spectrum Policy","The passage of open access and competition- enhancing spectrum policies will be prioritized to provide affordable broadband all over the country, especially in geographically isolated and unserved areas.",""],[1,"252","6","Comprehensive Spectrum Management Policy","The DICT will issue a comprehensive spectrum management policy, which will be implemented by the NTC in consultation with the PCC.","DICT | NTC | PCC"],[1,"252","7","Spectrum Allocation and User Fee Reform","This policy will facilitate the effective and efficient use of the country's spectrum or radio frequencies.",""],[1,"252","8","Digital Regulatory Law Amendment and Repeal Reform","These policies shall be complemented by the amendment or repeal of increasingly obsolete laws, which are ill-suited for the regulatory challenges of the digital age, such as the Public Telecommunications Policy Act of 1995 (RA 7925) and Radio Control Law of the Philippines (RA 3846).",""],[1,"253","2","NTC Modernization Law","The government will prioritize the enactment of an NTC Modernization Law to equip the NTC with greater authority and legal protection in the recall of idle and underused spectrum.",""],[1,"253","6","NTC Modernization Act for Spectrum Management","Passing the NTC Modernization Act will provide greater protection for the NTC and strengthen its ability to implement policies effectively through clear and enforceable powers to recall, reallocate, and reassign spectrum bands, as well as to regularly carry out spectrum use audits.",""],[1,"253","9","Open Access in Data Transmission Act","Passing the Open Access in Data Transmission Act will liberalize the telecommunications and broadband sectors by removing the legislative franchise requirement, allowing players to build their own network and gain access to spectrum.",""],[1,"301","30","Digital Infrastructure Expansion and Open Access Support","Invest in advancing and expanding access to digital infrastructure, and support open access through strategic collaboration",""],[1,"306","6","Digital Infrastructure Modernization and Expansion","Digital infrastructure will be modernized and expanded.",""],[1,"306","8","Regulatory Review and Open-Access Network Policy Reform","Review the regulatory landscape and strengthen the policy and regulatory environment to encourage just and transparent interconnection among the industry players and establish effective open-access network,",""],[1,"306","9","Facilities-Based Competition Promotion","Nurture and promote facilities-based competition so that industry players consistently invest to advance their digital infrastructures, thereby benefitting the general public, and,",""],[1,"307","1","Broadband Infrastructure Roll-out Support","To facilitate the roll-out of broadband infrastructure in less profitable or remote areas, the government will strategically use of its existing assets and adequately invest to help meet the requirements in the domestic backbone and middle-mile segments.",""],[1,"307","1","Infrastructure Sharing Promotion","It will also encourage infrastructure sharing among industry players.",""]],"76":[[1,"57","16","Health System Leadership and Emergency Resilience Capacity Building","Enhance national and local capacity for health system leadership, management, anticipatory governance, and resilience to public health emergencies",""],[1,"61","3","Health System Leadership and Emergency Resilience Capacity Building","Enhance national and local capacity for health system leadership, management, anticipatory governance, and resilience to public health emergencies",""],[1,"61","5","Local Government Unit Epidemiology and Surveillance Capacity Enhancement","Resilience to public health emergencies will be increased by enhancing LGU capacity and capability for basic epidemiology, disease surveillance, and event-based surveillance.",""],[1,"61","5","Center for Disease Control and Public Health Laboratory System Establishment and Strengthening","Health system structures that contribute to the ability to respond quickly to diseases of public health concern, such as the Center for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) and the Philippine Public Health Laboratory System, will be established and strengthened.",""],[1,"63","5","Medical Reserve Corps Establishment","Establishment of a Medical Reserve Corps [MRC]",""],[1,"63","6","Medical Reserve Corps Nationwide Mobilization Mechanism","The President will have the authority to order the nationwide mobilization of the MRC to complement the Armed Forces of the Philippines Medical Corps in case of declaration of a state of war, state of lawless violence, or state of calamity.",""],[1,"63","9","Creation of the Philippine Center for Disease Control and Prevention","Creation of the Philippine Center for Disease Control and Prevention [CDC]",""],[1,"63","10","Creation of the CDC under the DOH","creation of the CDC under the DOH for policy and program coordination","DOH"],[1,"63","10","Health System Preparedness for Disease Forecasting and Control","ensuring the health system is well prepared to forecast, prevent, monitor, and control diseases, injuries, and disabilities both of national and international concern",""],[1,"63","10","Recentralization of Local Epidemiology and Surveillance Units","recentralization of local epidemiology and surveillance units",""],[1,"63","10","Strengthening Epidemiology and Public Health Surveillance Capacity","strengthening epidemiology, public health surveillance, and research capacities",""],[1,"63","10","Public Health Emergency Preparedness Investment","ensuring investments to better equip the country in response to public health emergencies",""],[1,"63","11","Creation of the Virology and Vaccine Institute of the Philippines","Creation of the Virology and Vaccine Institute of the Philippines",""],[1,"63","12","National Virology Laboratory and Coordination Institute","This Institute will be an attached agency of the Department of Science and Technology and will serve as the country's principal virology laboratory, providing investigations, research, and technical coordination of the entire network of virology laboratories across the country","Department of Science and Technology"],[1,"316","2","Health System Preparedness and Response Structures","Health system structures that contribute to the ability to prepare for and respond to diseases of public health concern will be established and/or strengthened.",""]],"77":[[1,"40","1","Food Security and Nutrition Support Measures","A sufficient and stable supply of food will be ensured, primarily through improved productivity of agri-food systems, including storage, transport, and logistics.",""],[1,"40","1","Supplementary Feeding and Nutrition Promotion Campaigns","Measures to prevent and address wasting, stunting, and obesity will be implemented through supplementary feeding, nutrition education, and nutrition promotion campaigns.",""]],"78":[[1,"442","11","Urban Development and Housing Program","This mandates the State to undertake, in cooperation with the private sector, a comprehensive and continuing Urban Development and Housing Program.",""]],"79":[[1,"79","1","Livable Communities Development Initiative","By 2028, livable communities are established and support the AmBisyon Natin 2040 aspiration of Filipinos for a strongly rooted, comfortable, and secure life.",""],[1,"82","25","Community Livability Planning and Implementation","Sustain community livability planning and implementation",""],[1,"89","5","Community-Driven Livability Planning","Community-driven planning for the livability of communities shall be sustained.",""],[1,"90","2","Comprehensive Land Use Planning and Mixed-Use Community Development","The comprehensive land use plan (CLUP) shall help shape the livability of communities while ensuring that sectoral concerns-such as ancestral lands, cultural heritage, and biodiversity-are preserved.",""],[1,"90","2","Mixed-Use and Compact Community Development Promotion","Mixed-use as well as integrated use of space that offer the convenience of walkable, bikeable, compact, and connected communities to reduce travel time and energy footprint shall be promoted.",""],[1,"90","6","Metropolitan Area Governance Framework","Governance of these metropolitan areas will need to be put in place, building upon the good practices and lessons from existing metropolitan governance models (e.g., Metro Manila, Metro Cebu, and Metro Iloilo-Guimaras Economic Development Council).",""],[1,"90","7","Update the National Urban Development and Housing Framework","The National Urban Development and Housing Framework and the National Spatial Strategy shall be updated to consider emerging trends in green and resilient development and promote multisectoral needs (e.g., housing, transport, telecommunications, and public works) for urban and regional development.",""],[1,"90","7","Update the National Spatial Strategy","The National Urban Development and Housing Framework and the National Spatial Strategy shall be updated to consider emerging trends in green and resilient development and promote multisectoral needs (e.g., housing, transport, telecommunications, and public works) for urban and regional development.",""]],"80":[[1,"19","6","Research, Development, Technology, and Innovation Strategy","The PDP identifies strategies for advancing research and development, technology, and innovation (Chapter 8)",""],[1,"19","7","Innovation Ecosystem Development","supporting the creation of dynamic innovation ecosystems",""],[1,"28","2","Research and Development Investment","we need to fast-track investments in ... research and development",""],[1,"28","2","Innovation Promotion Investment","we need to fast-track investments in ... innovation",""],[1,"37","6","Innovation Ecosystem Development Support","Government will support the creation of innovation ecosystems and their evolution to becoming a dynamic ecosystem that eventually generates not only more, but quality jobs.",""],[1,"41","6","Innovation Ecosystem Development Programme","Over the medium term, government will (a) provide a nurturing environment for basic research and development, and knowledge creation; (b) support market-driven and customer-centered R&D; (c) scale up technology adoption, utilization, and commercialization; and (d) promote an innovation culture and entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"41","6","Financial and Technical Support for Innovation Institutions and Startups","Government will make use of a combination of financial and technical support to academic and skills training institutions, business incubators, and startups.",""],[1,"41","6","Innovation Collaboration Platforms","Government will also establish physical and digital platforms to encourage greater collaboration between and among the ecosystem players.",""],[1,"57","21","Integrated Innovation Establishment","Establish integrated, innovative,",""],[1,"76","16","Research, Development and Innovation Advancement","and advancing R&D and innovation (See Chapter 8).",""],[1,"207","1","High-Value R&D, Technology, and Innovation Development Strategy","strategies will be pursued to develop high-value R&D products, technologies, and innovations that will boost the efficiency and competitiveness of various sectors.",""],[1,"207","2","Integrated R&D, Technology, and Innovation Strategy","The sector will implement a set of integrated strategies to (a) advance R&D, technology, and innovation from knowledge creation to commercialization of R&D products; and (b) reinforce the innovation and entrepreneurship ecosystem.",""],[1,"209","16","STI Product Commercialization Acceleration","Accelerate commercialization of market-oriented and inclusive STI products",""],[1,"209","21","National R&D and Commercialization Investment Scale-Up","Aggressively increase national expenditure in R&D and its commercialization",""],[1,"209","22","R&D, Technology, and Innovation Collaboration Initiative","Carry out R&D, technology, and innovation in mutually beneficial collaborations",""],[1,"209","23","Publicly Funded Technology Transfer and Commercialization Programme","Intensify the technology transfer, extension, and commercialization of publicly-funded technologies",""],[1,"209","24","Implementation of the Philippine Innovation Act","Accelerate the Implementation of the Philippine Innovation Act",""],[1,"209","26","Innovation Hubs Establishment and Promotion","Establish and promote innovation hubs",""],[1,"209","27","Strengthening Provincial Science and Technology Offices","Strengthen the provincial S&T Offices",""],[1,"209","28","Innovation Project Financing Support","Increase financing opportunities for innovation projects",""],[1,"209","30","International Research Collaboration and Corporate R&D Investment Promotion","Aggressively increase international collaborators and global corporate R&D investors",""],[1,"209","31","Public-Private Partnerships for R&D Commercialization","Increase public-private partnerships for the utilization and commercialization of R&D products",""],[1,"210","1","Human Capital Reform for Research and Innovation","An important starting point is to increase the quantity and develop the quality of the country's human capital that can produce basic research contributing to knowledge generation, accelerate investments in R&D, and initiate meaningful reforms in the formation of human capital in basic, technical-vocational, and higher education.",""],[1,"210","2","Research and Innovation Infrastructure Development","The government, in partnership with the private sector, will build laboratories, science and technology research facilities, Knowledge, Innovation, Science and Technology (KIST) Parks, university science and technology parks, technology business incubators, and other infrastructure that can reduce the complexity and upfront costs and risks for private R&D.",""],[1,"210","2","Balik-Scientist Program Strengthening","The government will strengthen the Balik-Scientist Program and its support to the diaspora of Filipino scientific communities in other parts of the world.",""],[1,"210","2","Faculty Research Rewards and Recognition Scheme","It will provide a program of rewards and recognition for state university and college faculties who devote at least eight hours a week to research work and writing.",""],[1,"210","2","University-Industry and International Research Linkage Support","It will enhance its policy to strongly support institutional and individual faculty initiatives to establish linkages with industry, foreign universities, and research institutes.",""],[1,"210","3","Expanded Public Funding for Full-Time Researchers","will expand the sources of public funding for full-time researchers who are working on areas or domains under the national harmonized research agenda.",""],[1,"210","3","Administrative Process Streamlining for Publicly Funded R&D","The government will address bottlenecks in administrative processes, including procurement and similar concerns that may hamper the conduct of publicly funded R&D.",""],[1,"210","6","National R&D and Commercialization Investment Scale-Up","Aggressively increase national expenditure in R&D and its commercialization",""],[1,"210","7","National Research and Development Investment Expansion","Increase investments in R&D that can benefit the entire country, which can also invigorate private R&D expenditures in related fields.",""],[1,"211","1","Research and Development for Higher Value-Added Production","Moreover, it will pursue R&D that seeks to improve the production of higher value-added goods and services, reduce",""],[1,"211","3","Pagtanaw 2050 STI Foresight and Strategic Planning Project","Pagtanaw 2050, which literally translates to \"Looking Ahead,\" is the first inter-disciplinal and trans-disciplinal project on Philippine-focused science-technology-innovation (STI) foresight and strategic plan.",""],[1,"212","2","Human Resources Capacity Building for R&D, Technology, Innovation, and Entrepreneurship","Capacitate human resources on the R&D, technology, and innovation continuum and entrepreneurship to encourage the interaction of scientific, social, and creative talents, and intellectual capital in multidisciplinary collaborations.",""],[1,"212","3","Public-Private R&D and Innovation Collaboration Support","Support and recognize collaborative work of public researchers and private firms on R&D, technology, and innovation.",""],[1,"212","4","University Intellectual Property Licensing and Royalty Sharing Scheme","Facilitate the licensing of IP generated by public universities and research institutes, including a royalty sharing scheme and/or selling, if necessary, with the industry.",""],[1,"212","4","International R&D Partnership Programme","It will establish partnerships with countries on pioneering R&D in specific sectors that will provide open access to global best practices, which can then be customized to suit the Philippine context.",""],[1,"212","5","Private Sector R&D Feedback Mechanism","The private sector will be encouraged to share its observations, knowledge, and insights on people's motivations and preferences, and product trends to help improve R&D products in terms of function, aesthetic impressions, and market value.",""],[1,"212","6","Private Sector Support for Government R&D and STI Collaboration","The private sector will contribute to government R&D by: (a) guiding researchers and scientists on consumer trends and market system requirements; (b) addressing market challenges and opportunities; (c) leveraging private investments in STI activities; (d) seeking solutions to broad national challenges such as climate change, public health, green growth, and energy efficiency; (e) investing or locating knowledge, science and technology parks, incubators, and entrepreneurship cells; and (f) improving academia-industry linkages.",""],[1,"212","7","International Research Collaboration and Corporate R&D Investment Expansion","Aggressively increase international collaborators and global corporate R&D investors",""],[1,"212","8","International R&D Collaboration for Innovation","Seek international R&D collaborations to develop innovative products and services.",""],[1,"213","2","Domestic Technology Adoption and Reengineering Initiative","the domestic adoption, implementation, and reengineering of new technologies from domestic and international sources.",""],[1,"213","4","Technology Diffusion and Commercialization Support","Provide funding for the diffusion (i.e., extension and promotion) and commercialization of products of both publicly and privately funded STI products.",""],[1,"213","4","Innovation Fund Administration","The National Innovation Council (NIC) will continue the administration of the Innovation Fund under the Philippine Innovation Act to support the commercialization of publicly or privately funded and domestically developed technologies and innovations.",""],[1,"213","8","Technology Transfer Framework for Public R&D Outputs","The government will seek the most effective modes of technology transfer of commercially ready, and publicly funded R&D outputs from qualified private entrepreneurs and enterprises.",""],[1,"214","1","Intellectual Property Asset Valuation Procedures for R&D Institutions and SUCs","procedures for research and development institutions and SUC for valuing their IP assets shall be adopted.",""],[1,"214","2","Fast-Track Implementation of the Provincial Science and Technology Offices Act","Fast track the implementation of Republic Act 11914 or Provincial Science and Technology Offices (PSTO) Act.",""],[1,"214","3","Private Sector Technology Commercialization Partnership","Working with state universities and colleges and public research institutes, the private sector will help facilitate the transition from the laboratory to the marketplace, and from demonstration of technical \"proof of concept\" to commercial introduction of a new technology product or service in the marketplace.",""],[1,"215","2","Specialized Laboratory Access Expansion","It will expand access to the One-stop Laboratory Services for Global Competitiveness, Shared Service Facilities, Advanced Device and Testing Laboratory, Electronics Product Development Center, Regional Standards and Testing Laboratories, and other specialized laboratories for product development and improvement.",""],[1,"215","3","Researcher-Industry Innovation Pitch Venue","Provide a venue where researchers and technology developers can meet and pitch their products to possible investors or industries.",""],[1,"215","3","Industry Demand and Consumer Preference Exchange Platform","the venue will also provide a platform for industries and investors to share market demands and consumer preferences where R&D, technology development, and innovation can be directed.",""],[1,"215","4","National Innovation and Agenda Strategy Document","the NIC will formulate and implement the National Innovation and Agenda Strategy Document (NIASD), which will set the country's innovation goals and provide the strategies and action plans for improving the country's innovation governance.",""],[1,"215","4","National Innovation Fund Administration","The Council will also continue to administer the National Innovation Fund",""],[1,"215","5","National Innovation Communication Plan","the NIC will also develop a National Innovation Communication Plan.","NIC"],[1,"215","5","Innovation Policy and Program Monitoring Mechanism","The NIC together with the Regional Research, Development, and Innovation Committee of the Regional Development Councils will monitor innovation policies and programs (i.e., NIASD), as guided by the National Innovation Monitoring and Evaluation Matrix.","NIC | Regional Research, Development, and Innovation Committee of the Regional Development Councils"],[1,"215","5","Diaspora for Innovation Development Program","Further, the NIC will establish the Diaspora for Innovation Development Program to engage high level experts, especially overseas Filipinos.","NIC"],[1,"215","6","Industry-Academe Centers and RIICs for Digital Transformation","Establish industry-academe centers that seek fundamental, and multi- and interdisciplinary solutions with high societal relevance.",""],[1,"217","5","Science for Change Program","Establishing the Science for Change Program and Appropriating Funds Therefor",""],[1,"217","6","Science for Change Program Institutionalization","The bill seeks to institutionalize the Science for Change (S4C) Program of the DOST to address the inadequacies in the field of research and development","DOST"],[1,"218","9","Philippine Innovation Promotion Policy","\"Philippine Innovation Act\" declares the policy of the state to foster innovation as a vital component of national development and sustainable growth;",""],[1,"218","9","Science for Change Research and Development Funding Expansion","Science for Change Program (S4CP) Act (Senate Bill No. 1548) seeks for increased budget of PHP 21 billion for R&D (from 5.8B) for 2018, to double yearly for 5 years, capped at PHP 672 billion by 2022.",""],[1,"396","33","National Innovation Council Implementation of Innovation Measures","The National Innovation Council will steer the implementation of measures to advance research and development, technology, and innovation (Chapter 8: Advance Research and Development, Technology, and Innovation), driving an innovation-based transformation for various sectors.",""],[1,"426","22","Prioritization of Research Programs and Projects","Serves as a guide for the prioritization of research programs and projects that will be pursued by the country to address the societal needs.","DOST"]],"81":[[1,"329","6","Peace Agreement Implementation and Reintegration Support","Investing in peace and security continues.",""],[1,"330","4","Combatant Demobilization and Decommissioning","The third phase is currently ongoing, aiming to decommission 91 percent of the combatants and their weapons.",""],[1,"330","4","Camps Transformation Plan","Likewise, the Camps Transformation Plan 2021-20266 is presently implemented, outlining the efforts toward a meaningful transformation of camps into productive and resilient communities.",""],[1,"330","5","Bangon Marawi Comprehensive Rehabilitation and Recovery Program","strategic interventions under the Bangon Marawi Comprehensive Rehabilitation and Recovery Program are being implemented in areas affected by the 2017 siege.",""],[1,"330","6","Peace Process and Development Interventions for Affected Communities","The peace process with non-state armed groups7 and development interventions for affected communities are in various stages of implementation.",""],[1,"330","6","Socioeconomic and Livelihood Support for Affected Areas","In the affected areas, socioeconomic and livelihood interventions continue to be implemented.",""],[1,"331","1","Enhanced Comprehensive Local Integration and Community Development Support","Communist rebels who surrendered are provided with socioeconomic and legal assistance support through the Enhanced Comprehensive Local Integration Program (E-CLIP) and community development interventions such as the Payapa at Masaganang Pamayanan (PAMANA) Program10 and the Barangay Development Program (BDP).",""],[1,"332","1","Former Combatant Reintegration Support","There are also challenges in the process of assisting former combatants in their return to civilian life",""],[1,"333","10","Implementation of Signed Peace Agreements","Complete the implementation of all signed peace agreements",""],[1,"333","15","Former Combatant Reintegration and Community Rehabilitation Programme","Expedite normalization and reintegration of former combatants and their families and the rehabilitation of conflict-affected communities, including Marawi City",""],[1,"333","29","Implementation of Signed Peace Agreements","Complete the implementation of all signed peace agreements",""],[1,"333","30","Implementation of Signed Peace Agreements","The government will remain steadfast in completing the commitments under all signed peace agreements.",""],[1,"334","1","Support for Peace Agreement Coordination and Normalization Mechanisms","the national government will support the coordinating committees and security mechanisms on the remaining commitments under the 1996 Government of the Philippines-Moro National Liberation Front (MNLF) Final Peace Agreement and support the political track and normalization mechanisms in the implementation of the Comprehensive Agreement on the Bangsamoro.",""],[1,"334","4","Former Combatant Reintegration and Community Rehabilitation Programme","Expedite normalization and reintegration of former combatants and their families, and the rehabilitation of conflict-affected communities, including Marawi City",""],[1,"334","5","Bangsamoro Normalization and Transformation Programs","Normalization and transformation programs for the Bangsamoro, 22, 23 as supported by the Inter-Cabinet Cluster Mechanism on Normalization (ICCMN),24 will continue.",""],[1,"334","5","Demobilization and Arms Demilitarization Program","Demobilization of former combatants25 and former violent extremists,26 including the demilitarization of arms and munition, will be completed.",""],[1,"334","6","Socioeconomic Support Package Delivery Improvement","in the delivery of socioeconomic support packages for decommissioned combatants, their families, and communities, and vulnerable groups (children, elderly, persons with disabilities [PWD], indigenous groups, internally displaced persons) will be made more efficient and effective.",""],[1,"334","7","Community Rehabilitation and Catch-Up Development Interventions","the government will fast-track the rehabilitation and catch-up development of communities through the implementation of various interventions, such as E-CLIP, PAMANA, and BDP.",""],[1,"334","7","Marawi Recovery Assistance Delivery","the government will complete the delivery of social, financial, and socioeconomic assistance necessary for the recovery of affected individuals in Marawi.",""],[1,"334","7","Marawi Infrastructure and Permanent Housing Completion","The government will complete infrastructure projects such as bridges; schools; health centers; markets; ports; and the 2,800 permanent housing units for Marawi's most affected to be utilized by target beneficiaries by 2024.",""],[1,"335","2","Healing, Reconciliation, and Transitional Justice Interventions","Advance healing and reconciliation, social cohesion, and transitional justice interventions as key components of peacebuilding",""],[1,"335","3","Amnesty Facilitation for Qualified Individuals","The legal process, including granting of amnesty to qualified individuals, will be facilitated.",""]],"82":[[1,"113","26","Comprehensive Pathway for Returning OFWs","Develop a comprehensive pathway for returning OFWs",""],[1,"117","3","Legal Documentation and Overseas Migration Coordination","The government shall ensure that Filipinos going overseas, whether as temporary migrant workers or seeking permanent residency in host countries, will have proper and legal documentation.","DOLE | Department of Foreign Affairs | Department of Migrant Workers | OWWA | Commission on Filipinos Overseas"],[1,"117","3","Enforcement of Bilateral and Regional Migration Agreements","The government shall also strengthen the enforcement of bilateral and regional agreements through better arrangements with host countries.",""],[1,"118","6","OFW Reintegration Program Rationalization and One-Stop Shop","The government shall review and reorganize the various programs available for OFWs into a coherent package.","Department of Migrant Workers"]],"83":[[1,"343","24","Expansion of ADR Mechanisms","Advance the use of ADR mechanisms at all levels",""],[1,"343","30","Automated Consumer Complaints Handling System","Automate consumer complaints handling",""],[1,"343","31","Private Sector-Led Redress Mechanisms","Provide private sector-led redress mechanisms",""],[1,"345","3","Rules of Court ADR Exhaustion Filter","The Supreme Court will revisit the Rules of Court to include a filtering mechanism that will require litigants to first exhaust all available Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR) mechanisms before judicial recourse.",""],[1,"345","3","Alternative Dispute Resolution Capacity Building and Advocacy","the Office for Alternative Dispute Resolution (OADR) will continue to undertake capacity building, and advocacy and informative programs on different ADR mechanisms, including the Katarungang Pambarangay.",""],[1,"345","3","Legal Framework Harmonization for ADR","It will update, harmonize, and improve the Philippine legal framework to strengthen the use of ADR in the public and private sectors in accordance with international standards.",""],[1,"345","4","Barangay Justice System Jurisdiction Expansion Review","the Katurungang Pambarangay or the Barangay Justice System will be explored to consider expansion of its existing jurisdiction",""],[1,"345","4","Review of Katarungang Pambarangay Criminal Case Exemptions","The exemption of criminal cases involving offenses punishable by a maximum penalty of imprisonment exceeding one year or a fine over PHP5,000 from the Katarungang Pambarangay will also be revisited to ensure alignment with Republic Act No. 10951",""],[1,"347","3","Consumer Complaints Handling Automation","Automate consumer complaints handling",""],[1,"347","4","Philippine Online Dispute Resolution System","The Department of Trade and Industry (DTI) will develop and implement the Philippine Online Dispute Resolution System,","Department of Trade and Industry (DTI)"],[1,"347","5","Web-Based Consumer Complaint Portal and Automated Complaints Handling System","which will serve as a web-based consumer complaint portal and automate the entire consumer complaints-handling process of the government.",""],[1,"347","6","Consumer Welfare Desk Establishment Incentive Program","Through the Bagwis Awards Program of the DTI, business owners will be encouraged to establish consumer welfare desks or an equivalent customer relations office inside their establishments.","DTI"],[1,"347","6","Consumer Complaint Redress Mechanism","These desks or offices will provide a mechanism for the speedy resolution of consumer complaints, among other parameters that seek to provide immediate redress and at the same time prevent additional cases for the court.",""],[1,"350","14","Expand Barangay Justice System","Expand Katarungang Pambarangay",""],[1,"350","15","Review of Lupong Tagapamayapa Case Exemptions","This will reassess exemptions of cases that may be brought before the Lupong Tagapamayapa, particularly with respect to residence and thresholds of criminal cases.",""],[1,"429","4","Barangay Dispute Resolution System","A system of dispute resolution instituted in all barangays in the Philippines that seeks to promote, among others, the speedy administration of justice, by providing all avenues to an amicable settlement of community-level disputes.",""],[1,"430","7","Barangay Peace-Making Body for Katarungang Pambarangay","A peace-making body organized in every barangay to administer Katarungang Pambarangay and composed of the punong barangay as chairman, with a minimum of ten and a maximum of 20 members.",""]],"84":[[1,"343","12","Free Legal Services Access Initiative","Promote free legal services access",""],[1,"343","15","Free Legal Aid Public Directory and Referral System","Establish free legal aid public directory and referral system",""],[1,"343","17","Justice on Wheels Program Expansion","Expand Justice on Wheels Program",""],[1,"343","19","Victim Legal Protection and Assistance Strengthening","Strengthen victim legal protection and assistance",""],[1,"347","7","Legal Aid Clinics under the Revised Law Student Practice Rule","The government will fully implement the Revised Law Student Practice Rule under Rule 138-A of the Rules of Court for the under- privileged to address scarce legal services.",""],[1,"347","9","Legal Aid Services Mapping and Online Provider Database","the Supreme Court, together with the DOJ, PAO, Integrated Bar of the Philippines, Philippine Association of Law Schools, and other legal aid clinics will map available legal aid services per locality.","Supreme Court | DOJ | PAO"],[1,"348","1","DOJ Action Centers in the Regions","To ensure the expansion of legal services, the DOJ will also establish the DOJ Action Center in the regions.","DOJ"],[1,"348","2","Justice on Wheels Program Expansion","The Supreme Court will expand the scope of the Justice on Wheels Program to address specialized issues like tenurial disputes in agrarian reform, and climate and environmental cases.",""],[1,"348","3","Inclusive Access to Justice Assistance Mechanisms","Access to justice will be made more inclusive especially among marginalized sectors such as women, children, PWDs, senior citizens, and indigenous peoples through victim-centered, child-friendly, and gender-sensitive assistance mechanisms.",""],[1,"348","3","Justice Sector Coordination for Witness Protection and Victim Assistance","Coordination among the DOJ, the PNP, and the Department of Social Welfare and Development will be strengthened to address fragmented mechanisms in existing witness protection and victim assistance programs.","DOJ | PNP | Department of Social Welfare and Development"],[1,"348","3","Victims Compensation Program Expansion and Legal Amendment","The DOJ will intensify the Victims Compensation Program by pursuing the amendment of Republic Act No. 7309.","DOJ"],[1,"348","4","Access to Justice Empowerment Initiative","the Commission on Human Rights (CHR) will intensify its efforts to improve access to justice by: (a) empowering the poor and marginalized to seek responses","Commission on Human Rights (CHR)"]],"85":[[1,"19","6","Peace, Security, and Justice Administration Strengthening","ensuring peace and security and enhancing the administration of justice (Chapter 13)",""],[1,"421","21","Justice Sector ICT Systems Interoperability Framework","The system that provides justice sector agencies the flexibility to develop their own ICT Systems according to their needs and contemporaneously provides the framework that will generate the \"commonalities\" for easy interchange of crime-related data.",""],[1,"432","14","Integrated Criminal Justice Information System","A integrated information system that is intended to address and remedy the current information gaps in the Philippine criminal justice system by enabling effective sharing of data between the police, judiciary, probation services, custodial authorities, and criminal information registries, at key decision points in the criminal justice system process.",""],[1,"439","7","Integrated Inmate Information Management Database","An integrated database of inmate information management for BJMP, BPP, and PPA.",""]],"86":[[1,"193","3","Formation of the Philippine Creative Industries Development Council","Support the formation of the Philippine Creative Industries Development Council (CIDC) as provided under Republic Act No. 11904.",""],[1,"193","3","Creative Industries Development Planning and Road-Mapping","The CIDC will prepare the Creative Industries Development Plan, Creative Industries Investments Priority Plan, and undertake road-mapping efforts for the different identified creative sectors under the nine domains of the PCIDA.",""],[1,"196","6","Philippine Creative Industries Development Plan","The DTI as Chair of the CIDC will lead the formulation and implementation of a Philippine Creative Industries Development Plan mandated under RA 11904.","DTI"],[1,"196","7","Malikhaing Pinoy Creative Market Acceleration Program","Promote the Malikhaing Pinoy Creative Market Acceleration Program, which is a handholding program and support for trade and investment promotion to increase value chain participation of creative industries.",""],[1,"197","4","Creative Educational Plan","Establish a Creative Educational Plan in partnership with the private sector and the academe.","Department of Education (DepEd) | Commission on Higher Education (CHED) | Technical Education and Skills Development Authority (TESDA) | CIDC"],[1,"197","8","Intellectual Property Rights Capacity-Building and Protection Support","Provide capacitybuilding measures through the CIDC and partners in facilitating the registration of patents, and monitoring and protection of intellectual property rights, traditional cultural skills of Filipino creative industry stakeholders, and indigenous cultural communities against infringement.",""],[1,"197","9","Ratification of the UNESCO Convention on the Protection and Promotion of the Diversity of Cultural Expressions","Accede to the 2005 United Nations Educational, Scientific, and Cultural Organization Convention.",""],[1,"199","11","Creative Industry Collaboration Networks","Councils and networks such as the Philippine Creative Cities Network and the Local Culture and Arts Council for the development of the local creative industries under the PCIDA will advance collaboration and competitiveness by enhancing linkages between industries and government.",""],[1,"200","1","Creative Industry Data and Information Management System","Through the CIDC, lead the development of the Creative Industry Data and Information Management in coordination with the Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA) and other relevant national government agencies to set up a satellite account for creative industries that also covers data collection and management.","Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA) | other relevant national government agencies"],[1,"200","10","Technology Commercialization and Creative Industries Development","This aims to commercialize technologies and support the development of creative industries.",""],[1,"200","10","Intellectual Property Protection and Anti-Piracy Measures","This will enhance the attractiveness of the Philippines as an investment destination that places high value on intellectual property creation, protection, utilization, and commercialization, as well as prevent piracy in the physical and digital markets.",""],[1,"217","2","Copyright Code Amendment for Digital Infringement","The bill seeks to amend the following sections of the IP Code: [a] Section 177 to consider rampant digital reproduction of copyrightable works; and [b] Section 216 of the IP Code, as amended, to address increasing concerns on secondary liability and online copyright infringement issues, such as those related to P2P networks and ISPs.",""],[1,"421","11","Protection of Literary, Artistic, and Software Works","Protects literary and artistic works, such as books and other writings, musical works, films, painting, and other works and computer programs.",""],[1,"421","13","Creative Industries Human Resource Development and Capacity-Building Plan","The plan to be established by the Department of Education, Commission on Higher education, Technical Education and Skills Development Authority toward human resource development, audience capacity-building, and consumer empowerment in the countr's creative industries, in partnership with the private sector and the academe.","Department of Education | Commission on Higher education | Technical Education and Skills Development Authority"],[1,"421","16","Philippine Creative Industries Development Plan","The plan to be created by the Philippine Creative Industries Development Council to set forth the objectives, targets, strategies, and activities on the development and promotion of Philippine creative industries.",""],[1,"421","18","Creative Industries Incentives Plan","The plan to be created by the Philippine Creative Industries Development Council that contains a list of specific activities in the creative industries that may qualify for incentives.",""],[1,"430","2","Local Creative Industries Council Establishment","This council to be established by all local government units in coordination with the Philippine Creative Industries Development Council and the Department of Interior and Local Government shall exercise functions and powers in addition to those provided under existing statues, memoranda, and other issuances.","Department of Interior and Local Government"],[1,"430","11","Malikhain Pinoy Program Expansion","One of the four initiatives under the Malikhain Pinoy Program of the Department of Trade and Industry, which will, among other things, include three additional initiatives.","Department of Trade and Industry"],[1,"435","12","Philippine Creative Cities Mutual Support and Collaboration Program","This is a permanent program of the Philippine Creative Industries Development Council that shall serve as an avenue of mutual support, exchange of ideas, and collaboration among the country's cities.",""]],"87":[[1,"153","1","Fisheries Management Area Operationalization","fully operationalizing the fisheries management areas (FMA), especially the convening of FMA management bodies and developing and implementing the fisheries management plans",""],[1,"154","1","Blue Economy Resource Mobilization and Fisheries Development Measures","DA, DTI, DENR, DOST, and other relevant agencies, will emphasize and allocate the needed resources to harness the full potential of the blue economy","DA | DTI | DENR | DOST"]],"88":[[1,"151","11","Climate- and Disaster-Resilient Technology Development","Create and adopt climate- and disaster-resilient technologies",""],[1,"151","17","Early Warning Systems and Anticipatory Mechanisms Mainstreaming","Develop and mainstream early warning systems/anticipatory mechanisms",""],[1,"151","19","Climate and Disaster Risk Integration in AFF Planning and Programming","Integrate climate and disaster risks in AFF planning and programming",""],[1,"155","4","Climate- and Disaster-Resilient Technology Development","Create and adopt climate- and disaster-resilient technologies",""],[1,"155","5","Climate-Resilient Research and Development Investments","more investments for RDE on climate-resilient technologies and nature-based solutions will be pursued",""],[1,"155","5","Sustainable Agricultural Production Intensification","Alternate wetting and drying method and the use of decentralized renewable energy in AFF production (e.g., solar, biological, and wind) shall also be intensified.",""],[1,"155","8","Disaster Prediction Technology Localization and Deployment","Thus, the government will further invest and continue the localization and deployment of these technologies",""],[1,"156","1","Risk-Informed Primary Producer Decision Support","guide primary producers in making decisions (e.g., time and place of planting/fishing).",""],[1,"156","1","Technology-Based Supply Chain Disruption Prediction","mainstream the use of technologies (e.g., remote sensing) to predict supply chain disruptions;",""],[1,"156","1","Climate Outlook and Weather Forecast Dissemination","adopt site-specific, timely, and simplified climate outlook (e.g., La Niña and El Niño updates) and weather forecasts that can be easily and readily adopted by primary producers;",""],[1,"156","1","Biosecurity and Transboundary Disease Control Measures","improve biosecurity measures and strengthen facilities/efforts to prevent and control outbreaks of transboundary plant and animal diseases (e.g., ASF, AI, and banana fusarium wilt);",""],[1,"156","1","Livestock and Poultry Vaccine Development Acceleration","accelerate the development of vaccines to control livestock and poultry diseases.",""],[1,"156","2","Climate Risk Integration in Agri-Fishery Planning","The DA will integrate the results of the Climate Risk and Vulnerability Assessment in agri-fishery plans and programs and intensify the use of tools, such as Sustainable Land Management, Expanded Vulnerability and Suitability Assessment and Value Chain Analyses for commodity prioritization.","DA"],[1,"156","2","Climate and Disaster Risk Planning Capacity Building","Further, the DA, in partnership with relevant agencies (e.g., DOST, Climate Change Commission, National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council), will train planners on the use of available tools for integration of climate and disaster risks (e.g., hazard maps) in AFF plans, programs, and projects.","DA | DOST | Climate Change Commission | National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council"],[1,"156","2","Climate-Resilient Farm Structures and Retrofitting","Local climate change trends and projections will also be considered in the construction of disaster- and climate-resilient farm structures and retrofitting of existing ones (e.g., small-scale irrigation systems).",""]],"89":[[1,"152","4","Digital Land Titling and Indigenous Land Rights Protection","digital technologies will be harnessed to hasten the titling of collectively-owned land and supports programs for sustainable use of forestlands (e.g., through agro-forestry) and ancestral lands.",""],[1,"157","2","Land Administration and Management Rationalization","rationalizing land administration and management functions;",""],[1,"157","5","Land Titling Process Acceleration Measures","To hasten the land titling process, the following will be pursued: (a) finalization of the Joint Administrative Order (JAO) between DAR and National Commission on Indigenous Peoples on the parcelization of collective CLOA in ancestral domain; and (b) implementation of the JAO between DAR and Land Registration Authority on the processing period for the generation, issuance, and registration of computerized CLOA titles.","DAR | National Commission on Indigenous Peoples | Land Registration Authority"],[1,"158","6","Land Administration and Management Services Improvement","This will improve land administration and management services for agricultural and non-agricultural lands.",""],[1,"158","6","Individual Land Title Distribution under CARP","This will also contribute to fast-tracking the distribution of individual titles under the Comprehensive Agrarian Reform [CARP).",""],[1,"158","8","Idle Land Productive Use Promotion","This is to promote the productive use of idle lands, even if temporary, but without prejudice to the rights of owners to security of tenure.",""],[1,"158","14","Agrarian Reform Debt Condonation","This aims to free Agrarian Reform Beneficiaries from the debt burden through the condonation of unpaid principal amortization payments for the lands awarded under CARP.",""]],"90":[[1,"151","23","Government Agency Coordination and Convergence in Planning, Programming, and Budgeting","Improve coordination and convergence of government agencies in planning, programming, and budgeting",""],[1,"157","1","Government Agency Coordination and Convergence in Planning, Programming, and Budgeting","Improve coordination and convergence of government agencies in planning, programming, and budgeting",""],[1,"157","2","Agricultural Agency Restructuring and Service Delivery Reform","This focuses on (a) restructuring and reorganizing DA to enable a more efficient implementation of AFF plans and programs at the national and local levels; (b) filling the gaps in services (e.g., \"last mile\" delivery of extension services);","DA"],[1,"157","2","National Convergence Initiative Revitalization","reinvigorating the National Convergence Initiative and including the DTI in its composition;","DTI"],[1,"157","2","Public RDE Support System Streamlining","streamlining public RDE support system and addressing duplications among relevant agencies;",""],[1,"157","2","Registry and Information System Upgrading","completing and regular updating of registry and information systems to provide reliable data sources that will assist the government in identifying investment gaps and making sound and data-driven decisions.",""],[1,"160","13","NFFRS Digitalization Project","The NFFRS is the flagship digitalization project of the DA.","DA"]],"91":[[1,"386","6","Climate Change Adaptation and Disaster Preparedness Actions","This includes sustaining actions on climate change adaptation and mitigation and disaster preparedness, relief, recovery, and reconstruction, such as: (a) crop diversification, effective fishery management,",""],[1,"387","1","Climate-Resilient Agricultural Technology and Practice Promotion","and other climate-resilient technologies and practices to improve agricultural productivity while reducing GHG emissions (See Chapter 5);",""],[1,"387","1","Flood Regulation and Efficient Irrigation Investment","(b) flood regulation, setting up storage systems, and promoting efficient irrigation system to reduce groundwater extraction, sedimentation, and siltation (See Chapter 12);",""],[1,"387","1","Renewable Energy Investment Scale-Up","(c) scaling up investments in renewable energy and",""],[1,"419","5","Rice Inventory for Emergency and Disaster Relief","Optimal level of rice inventory that shall be maintained at any given time to be used for emergency situations and to sustain the disaster relief programs of the government during natural or man-made calamities.",""],[1,"424","11","Small Farmers and Fishers Clustering and Consolidation Program","A program which seeks to advance the inrest and condition of Filipino small farmers and fishers by encouraging them to adopt the strategy of clustering and consolidation of their production, processing, and marketing activities as community business enterprise, including the pooling of assets, labor and other resources.",""],[1,"432","12","Operation and Maintenance of Irrigation Facilities","Large and medium schemes of irrigation facilities which are operated and maintained by the National Irrigation Administration (NIA) for the continuous delivery of water to farmlands.",""],[1,"436","9","Provincial Agricultural Extension Hub","Extension services where the province serves as an extension hub that synchronizes agricultural plans and programs as well as orchestrate the activities of the various stakeholders.",""]],"92":[[1,"264","30","National Payment System Promotion","Promote safe and efficient National Payment System (NPS)",""],[1,"264","35","Adoption of the BSP Roadmap for the National Payment System","Support and adopt the BSP Roadmap for the NPS",""],[1,"266","2","Regulatory Framework for Retail Payment System Participation","The government will develop and implement a regulatory framework for the participation of qualified MFIs, non-government organizations, and cooperatives in retail payment systems governed by a payment system",""],[1,"269","1","National Payment System Development","An efficient and secure national payment system (NPS) will enable and support the growth of financial transactions.",""],[1,"271","8","Digital Payments Adoption Support Framework","This aims to provide ample legal support for all government institutions to adopt digital payments in collections and disbursements, including the provision of the corresponding budgetary requirement and appropriations to support the transformation of payments received and disbursed into digital form; and to grant authority to relevant government institutions to develop an incentive mechanism that would encourage merchants to adopt digital payments in their operations, among others.",""],[1,"283","4","InstaPay Real-Time Low-Value Payment Scheme","InstaPay is a real-time low-value EFT credit push payment scheme.",""]],"93":[[1,"190","3","Information Technology and Business Process Management Sector Growth Initiative","growth trajectory of the information technology and business process management (IT-BPM) sector (8% revenue growth per year in the next six years) to create one million direct and additional 1.1 million indirect jobs by 2028",""],[1,"193","7","IT-BPM Market Presence Strengthening","Further strengthen presence in markets such as North America where the Philippines enjoys strong market shares in products, such as contact centers and financial and professional services.",""],[1,"193","7","Protection of IT-BPM Market Position","Protect the country's dominant position in service in these markets, with the IT and Business Process Association of the Philippines, subsector associations, and firms as prime movers guided by the industry roadmap, i.e., The Big PH IT-BPM Leap: The Philippine IT-BPM Industry Roadmap 2028.",""]],"94":[[1,"78","4","ECCD Information and Monitoring Systems Utilization","Early CHildhood Care and Development [ECCD] Information System, National Child Development Center Enrollment Tracking and Information System, National ECCD Monitoring Evaluation and Accountability System [will be fully utilized during the 2nd term of the Philippine Development Plan]",""]],"95":[[1,"129","19","Government-Private Partnership for TVET Strengthening","Strengthen government-private partnership on TVET",""],[1,"129","20","Skills Information Sharing and Dissemination Initiative","Share and disseminate information on emerging, critical, and in-demand skills",""],[1,"129","23","Skills Development Program Harmonization","Harmonize skills development programs in the government",""],[1,"130","1","Alignment of Education and Training with Labor Market Needs","Align development objectives for basic, technical and vocational education and training (TVET), and higher education based on labor market requirements",""],[1,"130","3","Training Standards and Curriculum Update for Priority Occupations","Update contents of training standards, modules, and curricula for human capital development based on emerging, in-demand, and hard-to-fill occupations in identified key employment generators",""],[1,"130","4","Training Module Development and Skills Transferability Review","In developing training modules, the government will consider the transferability of skills.",""],[1,"130","4","Upgrade of Common Competencies in Training Regulations","Common competencies in training regulations7 shall be upgraded, reflecting economic transformation.",""],[1,"130","5","TVET Program and Credentialing Assessment","A comprehensive assessment of key TVET programs, credentialing mechanisms, and company-based training shall be undertaken",""],[1,"130","6","Benchmark Skills Standards and Certification Against International Standards","Skills standards, competency assessments, and certification shall be benchmarked with international standards.",""],[1,"130","6","Strengthen Admission Criteria for Private Technical Vocational Institutions","The government shall improve the criteria for admitting private technical vocational institutions (TVI) to ensure that new programs match the complexities of sectoral economic transformation.",""],[1,"130","6","Human Resource Development and Planning Improvement","Human resource development and planning improvements shall be implemented to keep up with the demand for quality instruction.",""],[1,"130","7","Modern and Responsive TVET, Apprenticeships, and Higher Education Alignment","Develop modern and responsive TVET, apprenticeships, and higher education aligned with emerging trends or demands in the labor market",""],[1,"131","5","TVET Human Resources Quality Improvement","The government shall enhance the quality of TVET human resources by improving qualification and competency requirements and updating training requirements.",""],[1,"132","1","Skills-Occupations Mapping and Curriculum Alignment","Employers may proactively convey how changing workplace requirements should be integrated into academic curricula and training regulations.",""],[1,"132","5","TVET Industry Collaboration Strengthening","Strengthen collaboration with industry boards and industry associations in TVET",""],[1,"132","6","Industry Boards and Associations for TVET Support","Achieving lifelong learning and skills development objectives across industries can be facilitated by industry boards and industry associations.",""],[1,"132","7","Establishment and Capacity Building of Industry Boards","the national government shall organize industry boards13 in key or strategic sectors identified by the National Technical Education and Skills Development Plan and the PSF Initiative.",""],[1,"132","7","Skills Anticipation and Training Regulation Support for Industry Boards","It shall capacitate industry boards in skills anticipation, certification design, and training regulation formulation.",""],[1,"132","7","Professional Standards Development for Emerging Occupations","Industry boards and associations shall also work to establish professional standards for emerging occupations.",""],[1,"132","8","Professional Standards and Licensure Examination Alignment","Align professional standards and licensure examinations with international standards",""],[1,"133","1","Professional Standards and Licensure Alignment Reform","The government shall continue improving professional standards in all regulated professions and ensure that licensure examinations are aligned with international standards.",""],[1,"133","1","International Benchmarking for Philippine Profession Recognition","The government shall maximize the recognition of Philippine professions by benchmarking with international standards and improving the quality of education, training, and skills development (See Subchapter 2.2).",""],[1,"133","3","Curriculum Network and Training Excellence Centers","networks within select curricular areas to promote program efficiency and relevance, improve quality access, share information about curricular design, and develop lifelong learning processes.",""],[1,"133","3","Industry-Led Centers of Training Excellence","With government direction and guidance, key industry players may form centers of training excellence to help adapt to changing industry conditions and address emerging skills needs.",""],[1,"137","2","Education and Skills Partnership Strengthening","The government shall sustain and strengthen partnerships with industry associations, workers' organizations, and other institutions to improve feedback mechanisms, promote innovative practices, complement efforts to operationalize the PQF and PSF Initiative, improve skills anticipation and certification, and deliver in-factory consultations and practical workplace training.",""],[1,"137","2","TESDA-Higher Education Summer Course Linkages","Part of the modes will include TESDA linkages with higher education institutions for courses to be offered in summer, wherein graduates will not just receive a baccalaureate degree but also a National Certificate, which in turn enhances their skills and employability, thereby enhancing their income-earning ability.",""],[1,"138","7","Recognition of Prior Learning and Employee Training","Employers are enjoined to recognize prior learning outcomes obtained in micro-formal or formal training and provide relevant training to employees.",""],[1,"139","6","Enterprise-Based Training Harmonization and Expansion","Harmonize the existing EBT modalities and expand the provision of training programs being implemented within companies which can be a mix of workplace training and classroom- Institute further reforms on the apprenticeship program to make them more attractive based learning.",""],[1,"139","6","Apprenticeship Program Reform","Institute further reforms on the apprenticeship program to make them more attractive based learning.",""],[1,"178","1","Skills-Based Learning System Reform","hence, the need to shift to a skills-based system that can provide more efficient mechanisms.",""],[1,"178","1","Academe-Industry Skills Development Collaboration","The academe-industry collaboration will also serve as a main avenue to improve skills development",""],[1,"181","13","Philippine Qualifications Framework Update and Integration","The Philippine Qualifications Framework will be updated to incorporate the Philippine Skills Framework and will serve as a common reference that employers and workers share to ensure the match between jobs and skills.",""]],"96":[[1,"129","22","Youth Employability Program Participation Expansion","Intensify participation in youth employability programs",""],[1,"131","1","Enterprise-Based Training Policy Review","The government shall conduct policy reviews of enterprise-based modalities.",""],[1,"131","1","Apprenticeship Law Amendment Reform","the government shall advocate for amendments to existing apprenticeship law, which modernizes applicable provisions of the Labor Code to enhance employability.",""],[1,"133","4","Employability Promotion and Area-Based Skills Partnerships","Educational institutions shall proactively seek effective interventions or programs that promote employability, particularly those in senior high school.",""],[1,"135","4","Youth and Vulnerable Groups Employment Programmes","Intensify employment programs for the youth, marginalized, disadvantaged, and vulnerable sectors",""],[1,"135","5","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Promotion","Technical and vocational education and training can be promoted to address the high incidence of youth NEET.",""],[1,"135","5","Special Program for Employment of Students Review","For example, the Special Program for Employment of Students can be reviewed to rationalize the targeting and selection of grantees, and to align program outcomes with lifelong learning objectives.",""],[1,"135","5","JobStart Philippines Expansion","In addition, the JobStart Philippines program shall be intensified to accommodate more participants from disadvantaged, marginalized, and vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"135","5","Career Development Support Program","The Career Development Support Program, which aims to provide career support to individuals, makes use of timely and relevant information on the dynamics of labor markets to address gaps in employability dimensions (i.e., personal and environmental factors, job search skills, skills gaps).",""],[1,"141","14","First-Time Jobseekers Assistance Act","The First Time Jobseekers Assistance Act seeks to help first-time jobseekers secure pre-employment documents that will lessen their financial burden in obtaining said documents.",""],[1,"141","15","JobStart Philippines Youth Employment Support Programme","JobStart Philippines is designed to provide opportunities to at-risk youth, who are provided with life skills training, career guidance and coaching, technical internships, and training with private sector employers.",""]],"97":[[1,"113","13","Unemployment Insurance Expansion","Increase coverage and benefits of unemployment insurance schemes",""],[1,"113","37","Social Insurance Product Expansion","Enhance and promote social insurance products to encourage coverage for all Filipinos",""],[1,"114","5","Review of Emergency Cash Assistance, Livelihood, and Social Insurance Programs","Among the programs that shall be reviewed are those on emergency cash assistance, livelihood, and social insurance.",""],[1,"114","5","Rationalization of Mandatory Contributory Social Insurance","there is scope for rationalizing the mandatory contributory",""],[1,"118","1","Review of Social Security Programs and Expansion Scheme Design","The current programs by SSS and GSIS shall be reviewed, and alternative schemes to increase coverage and benefits shall also be proposed.",""],[1,"120","16","Uniformed Personnel Pension System Reform","This bill seeks to provide an equitable and sustainable pension system for uniformed personnel.",""],[1,"121","1","Unemployment Insurance Expansion","Expansion of Unemployment Insurance",""],[1,"121","2","Unemployment Insurance Expansion","This will expand the coverage and benefits of unemployment insurance under the Social Security System [SSS) and Government Service Insurance System (GSIS).",""]],"98":[[1,"28","2","Early Warning Systems Investment","we need to fast-track investments in early warning systems",""],[1,"82","16","Community Disaster Preparedness and Resilience Programme","Build disaster preparedness and resilience of communities (Ch. 3.2, 11, 15)",""],[1,"84","1","Community-Based Disaster Risk Management and Preparedness","This will build resilience through community-based disaster risk management and preparedness measures.",""],[1,"84","1","Integrated Early Warning, Evacuation, and Evacuation Center Provision","Individual, family, and community preparedness will be supported by complementary and integrated actions at all government levels on early warning systems, preemptive evacuation protocols, and provision of permanent evacuation centers to limit or totally avoid the use of school facilities for evacuation.",""],[1,"84","1","Community Volunteer Disaster Frontliner Capacity Building","Local governments shall continue to organize and capacitate community volunteers to become frontliners in disaster",""],[1,"84","2","Community Resilience Programs and Projects","The Local Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Plan and the Local Climate Change Action Plan shall incorporate community programs and projects to build adaptive and other resilience capacities, and reduce risks from hazards and climate change.",""],[1,"84","2","Post-Disaster Rehabilitation and Recovery Framework","The Post-Disaster Rehabilitation and Recovery Framework shall be operationalized to ensure full recovery of households and communities affected by disasters.",""],[1,"84","3","Priority Access for Vulnerable LGUs to Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Adaptation Programs","National government shall prioritize highly vulnerable, low-income LGUs to access national programs and funds for disaster risk reduction, climate change adaptation, and disaster preparedness.",""],[1,"84","3","Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Resilience Infrastructure Package","These include flood control, coastal protection, early warning systems, operations center, permanent evacuation centers, critical infrastructure and facilities, and climate-resilient livelihood, among others (See Chapters 11 and 15).",""],[1,"104","1","Household Disaster Preparedness IEC Campaign","the government shall also develop the necessary information, education, and communication (IEC) materials and conduct IEC campaigns.",""],[1,"118","7","Strengthen Disaster Risk Reduction Coordination and Collaboration","Further strengthen the coordination and collaboration among NDRRMC, Climate Change Commission, local government units, and the private and/or civil society sector",""],[1,"118","8","Emergency Response Coordination and Synergy Optimization","The government shall tighten emergency response by optimizing synergies of the various programs of key stakeholders.",""],[1,"118","9","Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Coordination Framework","disaster risk reduction and management shall be determined.",""],[1,"379","6","Local Disaster Prevention and Preparedness Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the capacity of LGUs and communities in disaster prevention and preparedness",""],[1,"380","2","Local Government and Community Disaster Preparedness Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the capacity of LGUs and communities in disaster prevention and preparedness",""],[1,"380","3","Geographically Disaggregated Climate Data Update and Capacity-Building Program","Geographically disaggregated climate data and related information will be updated and capacity-building programs will be conducted to better prepare communities for slow and rapid onset events and identify priority interventions.",""],[1,"380","3","Local Climate and Disaster Risk Plan Updating","Subsequently, LGUs are expected to update their respective Local Climate Change Action Plans and Local Disaster Risk Reduction Management Plans.",""],[1,"380","3","Program Convergence Budgeting for Local Government Units","Program convergence budgeting will also be enhanced to efficiently address the needs of LGUs, especially those that are highly vulnerable to natural hazards, climate change, and El Nino-Southern Oscillation (ENSO).",""],[1,"380","3","Disaster Preparedness and Resilient Infrastructure Investment Program","In addition, investments in disaster preparedness and prevention, such as resilient infrastructure (e.g., roads, schools, evacuation centers, hospitals, water supply and sanitation facilities, and green-grey infrastructure) will be increased to enable communities affected by disasters, especially women, children, and other marginalized groups, build forward better (See Chapter 12).",""],[1,"380","6","Sectoral Vulnerability and Risk Assessment System","and sectoral vulnerability and risk assessments that incorporate public health parameters;",""],[1,"380","6","Climate Change and Natural Hazard Risk Data System","compiling and disseminating risk data and information including reports on damage and losses through a comprehensive and interoperable climate change and natural hazard database and information system;",""],[1,"380","6","Local Government Risk Information Capacity Building","capacitating LGUs to utilize risk information for developing, implementing, and monitoring relevant policies and programs;",""],[1,"380","6","End-to-End Early Warning and Communication Systems","maximizing the use of end-to-end early warning and communication systems for preparedness and prevention measures;",""],[1,"385","2","Operationalize Climate Monitoring and Evaluation System","The NCCAP's results-based monitoring and evaluation system will also be updated and operationalized.",""],[1,"385","2","Develop Climate Resilience Measurement Framework","A framework and methodology to measure resilience will also be developed to effectively monitor the climate resilience-building efforts from the national down to the local level.",""],[1,"385","2","Establish Local Climate and Disaster Risk Data Systems","The government will also support the establishment of local climate change and disaster risk reduction data management systems and climate",""],[1,"385","3","Climate and Natural Hazard Information Centers","change and natural hazard information centers to enhance the accessibility of climate information and gender-transformative early warning systems by communities, which will also facilitate the scaling up of public and private resources in resilience building.",""],[1,"385","3","National Risk Registry Development","The government will also develop a National Risk Registry that outlines and identifies location-specific hazards, exposure, and vulnerability, complementary to the development of localized climate models and projections.",""],[1,"420","9","Climate Vulnerability Assessment Framework","A comprehensive assessment framework for vulnerability assessment linked to climate risks.",""]],"99":[[1,"331","6","National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Plan Update","The updating of the National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Plan 2020-2030 outlines actions to ensure coordination and efficient logistics operations before and during disasters.",""],[1,"336","6","Full Implementation of the National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Plan 2020-2030","To manage disaster risks, the National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Plan 2020-2030 will be fully and effectively implemented.",""],[1,"336","6","Integration of the National Chemical, Biological, Radiological, and Nuclear Action Plan into Disaster Planning","The National Chemical, Biological, Radiological, and Nuclear Action Plan will be integrated in national and local disaster mitigation and response planning, together with the established protocols and standard operating procedures in dealing",""]],"100":[[1,"39","29","Livable Communities Development and Upgrading Program","Social development will be pursued through livable communities (Subchapter 2.3).",""],[1,"169","3","Housing Production Incentive Support","Support for construction and housing will be sustained through fiscal and non-fiscal incentives directed toward housing production confronted with deficits.",""],[1,"169","3","Socialized and Low-Cost Housing Support","This includes supporting socialized urban, economic and low-cost housing;",""],[1,"169","3","Housing Sector Information Technology Systems","developing and implementing information technology (IT) systems that support general operations from amortization collection and marketing;",""],[1,"169","3","Housing Industry Standards Development","developing globally accepted housing industry standards;",""],[1,"169","3","Building Component Standardization","and standardizing building components.",""]],"101":[[1,"273","2","Progressive and Simplified Tax System Reform","The country's socio-economic development needs will continue to be financed through a progressive and simplified tax system and more efficient tax administration through the adoption of digital technology.",""],[1,"273","2","Digital Tax Administration Modernization","The country's socio-economic development needs will continue to be financed through a progressive and simplified tax system and more efficient tax administration through the adoption of digital technology.",""],[1,"274","3","Tax System Reform","To sustain sound fiscal management, the following outcomes will be pursued: (a) productive, equitable, and simple tax system; (b) efficient and inclusive budget system; (c) stronger local government finance; and (d) sustainable management of debt (see Figure 11.2.1).",""],[1,"274","18","Tax System Progressivity and Productivity Reform","Strengthen the progressivity and productivity of the tax system",""],[1,"274","22","Benefit Taxation Expansion","Pursue greater use of benefit taxation",""],[1,"274","27","Tax Compliance Simplification and Service Enhancement","Increase tax compliance to tax laws and regulations by simplifying tax rules and enhancing services of the BIR and BOC to taxpayers and other stakeholders",""],[1,"274","30","Tax and Customs Administration Automation","Streamline and fully automate major processes in tax and customs administration",""],[1,"275","1","Tax System Progressivity and Productivity Reform","Strengthen the progressivity and productivity of the tax system",""],[1,"275","2","Tax Base Broadening and Tax Mapping Reform","Continuously broaden the income and value-added (VAT) tax bases through stronger taxation of the self-employed.",""],[1,"275","3","Digital Tax Law and Regulation Reform","Tax rules will be reviewed to broaden the concept of \"permanent establishment,\" evaluate the formula for profit allocation, and require digital platforms for firms, including non-resident firms doing business in the Philippines, to register with tax authorities",""],[1,"275","4","VAT Collection and Record-Keeping for Fulfillment Houses","Fulfillment houses or third-party warehouses responsible for handling goods on behalf of foreign suppliers will also be required to keep records.",""],[1,"275","4","Cross-Border Transaction Monitoring Coordination","The BIR and Bureau of Customs (BOC) will complement each other's efforts in monitoring cross-border transactions.",""],[1,"275","5","VAT Implementation for Non-Resident Digital Service Providers","Its efficient implementation will be clearly planned and laid out so that the estimated PHP9.6 billion gains from the measure can be realized.",""],[1,"275","6","Inclusive Framework Membership Assessment Study","a study will be conducted to assess the country's possible membership in the Inclusive Framework (IF) on Base Erosion and Profit Shifting",""],[1,"275","7","Review of Tax Exemptions and Preferential Treatment","Continuously review exemptions and preferential treatment provided by tax laws.",""],[1,"276","1","Review of VAT Zero-Rating and Exemptions","The zero-rating of goods and the remaining exemptions in the Tax Code will be reviewed to limit exemptions to raw food, agriculture, education, and health.",""],[1,"276","2","Expansion of Excise Tax Coverage for Non-Essential Goods","Broaden the coverage of goods subject to the excise tax on non-essential articles.",""],[1,"276","3","Excise Tax Expansion and Rate Review for Motor Vehicles","The inclusion of other motor vehicles, such as motorcycles and pick-up trucks, under the excise tax regime will be considered.",""],[1,"276","4","Passive Income and Financial Intermediary Taxation Bill","The Passive Income and Financial Intermediary Taxation bill complements the reforms introduced by the Tax Reform for",""],[1,"276","5","Acceleration and Inclusion Tax Simplification Law","Acceleration and Inclusion Law to simplify the taxation of financial transactions.",""],[1,"277","7","Tax Compliance Simplification and Service Enhancement","Increase tax compliance to tax laws and regulations by simplifying tax rules and enhancing services of the BIR and BOC to taxpayers and other stakeholders",""],[1,"277","8","Tax and Customs Process Digitalization and Simplification","Voluntary compliance in filing tax returns and paying taxes will be facilitated by simplifying rules and processes.",""],[1,"277","9","Tax Registration and Filing Simplification Reform","The BIR will ramp up its efforts to simplify registration, invoicing, and accounting requirements.",""],[1,"277","9","Portable Tax Filing and Payment Reform","It will enhance the portability of tax transactions by removing venue restrictions in the filing and payment of taxes.",""],[1,"277","11","Tax Education Curriculum Program","The government can include in the educational curriculum programs that will enable better public appreciation of how taxes are spent, thus encouraging positive tax compliance behavior.",""],[1,"277","11","Improved Taxpayer Service Delivery by Revenue Agencies","At the same time, revenue-collecting agencies will meet taxpayers' expectations through the provision of honest, helpful, and efficient services.",""],[1,"278","3","Compliance Check and Audit Selection Automation Program","Program will be fast-tracked to automate compliance checks and audit selection processes.",""],[1,"281","7","Digital Taxation Framework","Digital Taxation Framework to ensure a level playing field between traditional industries and the digital economy given the expected shift to online transactions.",""],[1,"281","7","Simplification of Financial Transaction Taxation","Passive Income and Financial Intermediary Taxation has provisions to simplify the taxation of financial transactions by proposing to reduce the number of tax rates per se and the number of differential tax rates.",""],[1,"281","7","Tax Administration Modernization Measures","Other tax administration measures that will improve the ease of paying taxes and authorize the automatic exchange of information for tax purposes.",""]],"102":[[1,"264","31","SME, Corporate, and PPP Public Listing Incentives","Incentivize SMEs, Corporates, and PPPs to publicly list Promote enabling regulations for fintech",""],[1,"264","36","Equity and Bond Issuance Promotion","Promote new equity and bond issues for investment",""],[1,"269","6","Capital Market Listing Promotion and Privatization Initiative","In this endeavor, the SEC, together with the Philippine Stock Exchange, will educate corporates about the easing of listing requirements.",""],[1,"269","6","SME and PPP Public Listing Incentive Scheme","Moreover, the government will incentivize small and medium enterprises and public-private partnerships to become publicly-listed firms",""],[1,"269","6","State-Owned Enterprise Privatization and Public Listing Review","and will privatize selected government-owned and controlled corporations and consider publicly listing those which can be attractive to retail and institutional equity investors.",""],[1,"269","7","Domestic Credit Market Development Support","the government will support the development of a local credit market",""],[1,"270","1","Local Government Unit Credit Rating System","credible and independent local government unit (LGU) credit rating system, including the conduct of a comprehensive preliminary study on the development of an LGU bond market",""],[1,"270","1","LGU Bond Market Development Study","including the conduct of a comprehensive preliminary study on the development of an LGU bond market",""],[1,"270","1","Overseas Filipino Remittance Mobilization for Development","As a source of funds, the government can leverage OF remittances for strategic development",""],[1,"270","2","Capital Markets Development Road Map Implementation","The private sector and government, working jointly in the Capital Markets Development Council, will continue to implement the strategies outlined in the current Capital Markets Development Road Map.",""],[1,"270","2","Corporate Equity and Bond Financing Promotion","Banks can encourage their medium and large corporate clients to strengthen their capital structure by raising equity in the stock market; or for corporates to leverage their balance sheets, raising long-term funding via bond issuances.",""],[1,"270","2","Retail and Institutional Investment Product Promotion","Banks can also promote new equity and bond issues for investment through their retail and institutional clients, including small investors who should be able to access these investment products through the banks' digital services.",""],[1,"271","10","Capital Market Development and Financial Literacy Promotion","It will expand capital market by developing robust institutional investor base, strengthening regulatory environment, and promoting financial literacy.",""],[1,"273","4","Capital Market Development for Funding Diversification","Sources of funding will be diversified through the development of the capital market, including the local government bond market.",""],[1,"274","29","LGU Bond Market Development and Credit Rating System","Develop the LGU bond market and establish an LGU credit rating system",""],[1,"280","2","LGU Bond Market Development and Credit Rating System","Develop the LGU bond market and establish an LGU credit rating system",""],[1,"280","3","Local Government Bond Financing Mechanism","Bond financing can provide LGUs with access to direct funding sources, and in the process, require them to practice discipline in transparency, accounting, and auditing finances.",""],[1,"280","4","LGU Bond Market Development Study","conduct a comprehensive preliminary study on the development of the LGU bond market to assure the confidence of possible bondholders.",""],[1,"280","5","Local Credit Market and LGU Credit Rating System Development","The national government will also support the development of a local credit market and an LGU credit rating system",""],[1,"280","6","Domestic Capital Market Deepening for Government Financing","Corporate, institutional, and individual savings can be mobilized to finance government programs through the deepening and broadening of the domestic capital market",""],[1,"280","6","Financial Literacy and Government Securities Awareness Programme","supplemented with financial literacy programs ... to spread awareness of and improve access to government securities as alternative investment vehicles",""],[1,"280","6","Digital Finance Technology Promotion","the promotion of digital finance technology",""],[1,"280","7","Innovative Government Securities Borrowing Strategy","The government will explore creative and innovative borrowing structures to spur participation in the government securities market, especially of non-traditional Filipino investors such as small savers domiciled in the Philippines and abroad, to broaden the government's investor base.",""],[1,"280","8","Competitive Tax Regime for Interest Income","A more competitive tax regime on interest income that is harmonized with regional peers will also encourage foreign participation in the domestic bond market.",""],[1,"280","10","Official Development Assistance Maximization and International Bond Market Diversification","The government will continue to maximize available Official Development Assistance due to its favorable borrowing terms up until the country reaches upper-middle-income status.",""],[1,"280","10","International Bond Market Presence and Diversified Borrowing Strategy","The government will also maintain its presence in the international bonds market to provide flexibility in its financing options and to facilitate efficient bond pricing for local borrowers with foreign currency requirements.",""],[1,"280","10","Diversification of International Borrowing Instruments and Markets","Moreover, borrowing in the international bonds market will be diversified across various markets and in different instrument formats to attenuate supply-related escalation in borrowing costs.",""],[1,"280","10","Exploration of New International Bond Instruments","New instrument formats will also be explored to reach new markets and investors.",""],[1,"281","2","Contingent Liabilities Accounting and Domestic Debt Market Development Program","program will provide a comprehensive accounting of contingent liabilities and sufficient support for the development of the domestic debt market.",""]],"103":[[1,"239","2","Full Implementation of the Philippine Competition Act","The Philippine Development Plan 2023-2028 emphasizes the full implementation of the Philippine Competition Act through strategies that allow businesses to leverage existing or emerging digital technologies.",""],[1,"239","4","National Competition Policy Implementation","AO 44, s. 2021 mandates a whole-of-government effort in fostering competition through three key elements: (a) pro-competitive policies and government interventions; (b) competitive neutrality; and (c) enforcement of competition-related laws and policies.","National Economic and Development Authority | PCC"],[1,"242","6","Competition Policy and Regulation for Digital Markets","Moving forward, competition policies and regulations shall address these emerging concerns, balanced against the undeniable value that digitalization creates.",""],[1,"243","1","Digital Market Competition Enhancement","Enhancing competition in the digital markets will improve quality, lower costs, and provide greater choice of new technologies and tools that MSMEs can use to compete more effectively and thrive in the post-COVID environment.",""],[1,"243","2","Competition Law Enforcement and Regulatory Efficiency Reform","Firm and consistent enforcement of the PCA and competition-related issuances shall be sustained to discourage and penalize cartel agreements, abuse of dominance by firms, anticompetitive M&As, and other anticompetitive behaviors.",""],[1,"243","2","Open and Competitive Markets Policy Reform","Reducing barriers to entry and re-entry by adopting policies that promote open and competitive markets and ensure level playing fields will also be pursued.",""],[1,"243","2","Regulatory Efficiency Improvement Initiative","Finally, enhancing regulatory efficiency will help ensure that laws and regulations are implemented in a manner that contributes rather than hampers ease of doing business in the country.",""],[1,"243","9","Competition Enforcement Strengthening and Expansion","Strengthen and expand competition enforcement",""],[1,"243","10","Research and Development for Competition and Regulatory Issue Resolution","Leverage research and development efforts to identify and address competition and regulatory issues in priority sectors",""],[1,"243","15","Significant Market Power Regulatory Framework","Develop framework for the determination of significant market power (SMP), and the specification of obligations on entitles with SMP",""],[1,"243","16","Competition Impact Assessment Institutionalization","Institutionalize the use of Competition Impact Assessment Manual/Toolkit",""],[1,"243","19","Competition Compliance Program Adoption","Ensure compliance with the Philippine Competition Act (PCA) through adoption of competition compliance programs",""],[1,"243","24","National Competition Policy Implementation","Pursue full implementation of the National Competition Policy",""],[1,"243","25","Public Awareness and Support Campaign for PCA and Philippine Competition Commission","Increase awareness, understanding, and support for the PCA and Philippine Competition Commission",""],[1,"243","26","Monitoring and Analysis of Emerging Technologies, Markets, and Business Models","Enhance monitoring and understanding of emerging technologies, markets, and business models",""],[1,"243","28","Digital Market Competition and Regulatory Efficiency Policy","Adopt policies to improve competition and regulatory efficiency in digital markets",""],[1,"244","1","Anticompetitive Conduct Investigation and Prosecution Strengthening","Strengthen and expand investigation, detection, and prosecution of anticompetitive conduct and agreements",""],[1,"244","2","Competition Law Enforcement Capacity Building","Governmentagencies with competition-related mandates will continue to build human resources and institutional capacity to enforce the PCA and other related issuances.",""],[1,"244","2","Interagency Cartel Investigation and Prosecution Coordination","With the interagency arrangements firmly in place to foster cooperation and coordination in the investigation and prosecution of cartels, the PCC and the Department of Justice (DOJ), through its National Bureau of Investigation (NBI) and Office for Competition (OFC), will continue to work together and complement each agency's resources and competencies.","PCC | Department of Justice (DOJ) | National Bureau of Investigation (NBI) | Office for Competition (OFC)"],[1,"244","3","Strengthened Enforcement Against Anticompetitive Conduct","Enforcement actions against anticompetitive conduct and agreements will be ramped up to strengthen fair competition, deter anticompetitive practices, and bolster the reputation and credibility of the PCC and other agencies with competition mandates.",""],[1,"244","3","Bid-Rigging Intelligence Gathering and Detection Enforcement Project","To detect bid-rigging activities effectively, the PCC, in coordination with the Government Procurement Policy Board, will continue to strengthen the Bid-Rigging Intelligence Gathering and Detection Enforcement project.","PCC | Government Procurement Policy Board"],[1,"244","4","Interagency Cooperation Mechanism for Anticompetitive Conduct Enforcement","a cooperation mechanism will be forged among agencies involved in the investigation, detection, and prosecution of anticompetitive conduct and agreements",""],[1,"244","5","Inter-Agency Mandate Harmonization and Accountability Reform","These agencies will work together to harmonize and clarify their mandates, tasks, and responsibilities under their respective charters, and ensure accountability.","Department of Trade and Industry (DTI)"],[1,"244","6","Efficient Merger and Acquisition Review","the Commission will undertake the efficient review of notified transactions and expedite the motu proprio review of completed transactions",""],[1,"244","7","Enhanced Merger Review Framework for Digital Competition","The merger review framework will also be enhanced to monitor and prevent anticompetitive acquisitions of nascent competitors by larger incumbent players.",""],[1,"244","7","Digital Competition Enforcement Capacity Building","In both enforcement and merger review, the PCC will address new digital-specific issues that could have an adverse impact on competition, such as the exploitation of data as an essential facility, or its misuse as a barrier to entry.",""],[1,"244","7","Competition Authority Analytical Tools Upgrade","The agency will be equipped with the knowledge and analytical tools needed in unraveling \"zero pricing\" and the proper valuation of \"data as",""],[1,"245","1","Algorithmic Discriminatory Preferencing Regulation","Algorithm-based discriminatory preferencing, and its consequences for data protection and privacy, shall be coherently addressed in coordination with the National Privacy Commission (NPC).",""],[1,"245","2","Market Studies for Pro-Competition Reform","The PCC, NEDA, and DTI will continue to conduct market studies in sectors or industries such as telecommunications, e-commerce, energy, water, health, and food and agriculture","PCC | NEDA | DTI"],[1,"245","2","Competition and Regulatory Capacity Building for Digital Markets","The PCC, Department of Information and Communications Technology (DICT), NPC, DOJ-OFC, DTI, and ARTA will continue to build their institutional and human resource capacity to assess competition and regulatory issues arising in fast-evolving digital markets","PCC | Department of Information and Communications Technology (DICT) | NPC | DOJ-OFC | DTI | ARTA"],[1,"245","3","Competition and Regulatory Reform in Specific Economic Sectors","The government will continue ongoing research and action to address competition and regulatory issues in specific sectors of the economy.",""],[1,"245","4","Electricity Market Abuse Monitoring","In energy, the PCC will work with the Energy Regulatory Commission (ERC) and continue to monitor potential abuses of market power in distribution and generation to address high rates and limited capacity in electricity markets (See Chapter 12).","Energy Regulatory Commission (ERC)"],[1,"245","4","Food Price Manipulation Enforcement","In the agriculture and food sectors, the PCC and DTI will address issues of price manipulation and exploitative pricing to protect consumers and support food security in the country (See Subchapter 3.1).","DTI"],[1,"245","4","Pharmaceutical Competition Inquiry and Monitoring","In the pharmaceutical industry, the PCC will continue to monitor and pursue an inquiry into possible anticompetitive practices that may exist in the different segments of the supply chain to ensure competition and improve the affordability, quality, and accessibility of medicines in the country (See Subchapter 2.1).",""],[1,"245","5","Frameworks for Determining Significant Market Power","The PCC will work with sector regulators to develop frameworks, including guidelines and principles, to define and determine the existence of SMP in key markets",""],[1,"246","1","Ex Ante Regulation Framework for SMP Obligations","The framework shall also provide guidance for when, what, and how to impose obligations on entities with SMP to protect competition in any given sector.",""],[1,"246","2","Competition Compliance Program Adoption","Ensure compliance with the Philippine Competition Act through adoption of competition compliance programs",""],[1,"246","3","Competition Compliance Program Adoption","The PCC will prioritize the adoption of competition compliance programs to provide guidance and prevent anticompetitive agreements and behavior by and among",""],[1,"246","4","Competition Compliance Toolkit Development and Awareness Programme","It will develop and promote competition compliance toolkits, and partner with national and regional associations and chambers of commerce and industry to expand private sector awareness and understanding of competition laws.",""],[1,"246","4","Corporate Governance Sanctions Operationalization","It will operationalize Section 26 of the Revised Corporation Code (RA 11232), which provides the PCC with authority to impose qualifications or disqualifications on directors, trustees, or officers of corporations to promote good corporate governance, or as a sanction in its administrative proceedings.",""],[1,"246","9","Retail Competition and Open Access Implementation","the ERC will hasten the full implementation of the Retail Competition and Open Access, as provided under the EPIRA, which will enable households to choose their preferred electricity provider",""],[1,"247","1","Competition Impact Assessment Manual/Toolkit Mainstreaming","The PCC, ARTA, and NEDA will work to harmonize and mainstream the use of a Competition Impact Assessment Manual/Toolkit in the law-making process of Congress and the policy- and rule-making processes of other government agencies, sector regulators, and LGUs.","PCC | ARTA | NEDA | Department of Budget and Management (DBM)"],[1,"249","4","Competition Policy and Regulatory Review","All government agencies will review their existing policies and regulations and identify issuances that restrict competition in markets, hinder the entry of new players, facilitate collusion, or provide undue advantage to specific firms.",""],[1,"249","4","Competition Principles Training for Government Agencies","National government agencies, regulatory agencies, and LGUs will be encouraged to utilize the free online training courses developed by the PCC on the NCP.",""],[1,"249","5","Competitive Neutrality Implementation","The government will also pursue the effective implementation of the competitive neutrality principle, which requires that all enterprises face the same set of rules and compete on equal terms.",""],[1,"249","6","Review and Remove Undue GOCC Support Measures","to GOCCs in the form of regulatory treatment, tax exemptions, and other state support measures will be reviewed, and removed if warranted, to ensure that GOCCs do not enjoy undue competitive advantages over private market participants.",""],[1,"249","7","Review of GOCC Mandates and State Participation Framework","The mandates of GOCCs will also be reviewed to rationalize direct state participation in the economy.",""],[1,"249","8","Local NCP Adoption Capacity and Incentive Programme","The government will capacitate and incentivize the active adoption of NCP at the local",""],[1,"250","1","Mainstreaming of the National Competition Policy in Performance Incentives and Local Government Agreements","Pursuant to AO 44, the Civil Service Commission (CSC), the Career Executive Service Board (CESB), and the Department of Interior and Local Government (DILG), will integrate the adoption of and compliance with the NCP and its key elements as part of the good governance conditions criteria for the grant of the PBB to government personnel and the SGLG to LGUs.","Civil Service Commission (CSC) | Career Executive Service Board (CESB) | Department of Interior and Local Government (DILG)"],[1,"250","1","Definition of PBB and SGLG Implementation Parameters","The CSC, CESB and the DILG, in consultation with the PCC, will clearly define the parameters for the implementation of the PBB and SGLG incentives.","Civil Service Commission (CSC) | Career Executive Service Board (CESB) | Department of Interior and Local Government (DILG) | PCC"],[1,"250","1","Competition Policy Coordination Agreements with Local Government Leagues","The PCC and LGU leagues will enter into agreements to facilitate mainstreaming of the NCP and ensure effective coordination and consultation in areas of concern.","PCC | LGU leagues"],[1,"250","1","Competition Policy Capacity Building for Local Government Officials","The PCC and NEDA will work with the DILG Local Government Academy to provide adequate capacity building on competition policy for local government officials.","PCC | NEDA | DILG Local Government Academy"],[1,"250","2","Institutional Linkages for Competition Law Capacity Building","the government will continue to build and leverage its institutional linkages with foreign and local centers of excellence in fields relevant to competition law and economics.",""],[1,"250","2","Capacity Building to Foster Competition Project","The PCC will continue to implement the Capacity Building to Foster Competition Project to strengthen its institutional capacity and that of other agencies with competition-related mandates.",""],[1,"250","2","Competition Law Research Centers of Excellence","it will continue to develop academic centers of excellence, including such a center in the University of the Philippines College of Law.",""],[1,"250","4","Regional Competition Policy Dialogue and Network Development","the PCC will broker knowledge and cultivate policy dialogue among competition authorities, sector regulators, business, and other non-governmental actors in the region.",""],[1,"250","5","Competition Law Awareness and Support Campaign","Increase awareness, understanding, and support for the Philippine Competition Act and Philippine Competition Commission",""],[1,"250","6","Competition Advocacy and Compliance Promotion Programme","the PCC will expand its advocacy to build alliances of champions in the private sector, particularly among the business community.",""],[1,"250","6","Competition Education and Public Awareness Campaign","To develop an effective educational campaign promoting competition, the PCC will also highlight the benefits and gains from competition cases acted and decided upon by the agency.",""],[1,"250","6","Citizen Monitoring and Reporting of Anticompetitive Practices","It will continue to engage citizens, especially MSMEs, to play an active role in monitoring and reporting anticompetitive practices through various online and offline channels.",""],[1,"252","2","Competition Promotion and Enforcement Cooperation","Similar efforts to promote greater competition have successfully been achieved by the PCC acting alone, as well as in partnership with other government agencies and regulators.",""],[1,"253","1","Competition Enforcement and Market Access Facilitation","The PCC, in consultation with the NTC, will work to address any anticompetitive practices, penalize abuses of dominance, and facilitate the access of smaller players to the incumbents' essential facilities based on fair,",""],[1,"253","15","Competition Mainstreaming in MSME Development Council","To mainstream competition issues among MSMEs, the Amendment will also include the PCC in the Micro, Small and Medium Enterprise Development Council.",""],[1,"306","7","Competition Reform Agenda","the government will strongly push for necessary reforms and undertake the following:",""],[1,"396","34","Trade and Investment Promotion Strategy","The transformation agenda will also be supported by strategies that promote trade and investments (Chapter 9: Promote Trade and Investments), to be steered by the Inter-Agency Investment Promotions Coordination Committee",""],[1,"396","34","Tariff and Non-Tariff Policy Reform","the tariff and non-tariff policies to be tackled by the Committee on Tariff-Related Matters",""],[1,"396","34","Competition and Regulatory Efficiency Reform","Policies promoting competition and improving regulatory efficiency (Chapter 10: Promote Competition and Improve Regulatory Efficiency) will be led by the Inter-Agency Committee on Good Governance",""],[1,"420","17","National Competition Policy for GOCC Competitive Neutrality","One of the key elements of the National Competition Policy, which recognizes that GOCCs shall not enjoy net competitive advantages or be subjected to advantages over private sector businesses simply by virtue of public sector ownership, unless it can be clearly demonstrated that the greater public interest will be served and there is lack of commercial viability (NEDA-PCC JMC No. 1 on the National Competition Policy, 2020).",""],[1,"425","4","Zero-Duty Incentive Arrangement for Sustainable Development and Good Governance","It is a special incentive arrangement for sustainable development and good governance in the form of zero duties.",""]],"104":[[1,"329","4","Whole-of-Government Peace and Security Approach","The Philippine Development Plan (PDP) 2023-2028 puts forward the premise that a whole-of-government approach with cross-cutting strategies is required in ensuring peace and security.",""],[1,"329","7","Localized Peace Engagements","In areas not covered by peace agreements, localized peace engagements will be intensified, with local government units facilitating a whole-of-society approach.",""],[1,"331","2","Whole-of-Government and Whole-of-Nation Conflict Response","The implementation of a whole-of-government and whole-of-nation approach fostered a more holistic and cohesive government response, addressing the interrelated drivers of armed conflict in the country.",""],[1,"331","2","NTF-ELCAC Cluster and Task Force Activation","Various clusters and regional and local task forces under the National Task Force to End Local Communist Armed Conflict (NTF-ELCAC) were activated.",""],[1,"333","2","Integrated Peace and Security Policy","These outcomes will be realized through an integrated, transparent, people-centered, and human rights-based peace and security policy, supported by relevant cross-cutting strategies.",""],[1,"333","18","Program Convergence and Conflict-Sensitive Development Mainstreaming","Strengthen convergence of programs and ensure that development interventions are conflict-sensitive and peace-promoting",""],[1,"334","8","Conflict-Sensitive and Peace-Promoting Development Interventions","ensure that development interventions are conflict-sensitive and peace-promoting",""],[1,"334","8","Program Convergence Strengthening","Strengthen convergence of programs",""],[1,"334","9","Conflict-Sensitive Compliance Monitoring and Evaluation Tool","To improve conflict-sensitive and peace-promoting compliance, a monitoring and evaluation tool for GICA areas will be developed.",""],[1,"334","9","Localized Project Targeting and Implementation Strategy","Project targeting and implementation strategies will be further localized to ensure greater ownership of local communities.",""],[1,"334","9","Infrastructure Rollout in GICA Areas","More infrastructure projects will be rolled out in GICA areas and coordination between LGUs' Peace and Order Councils and Local Development Councils will be strengthened.",""],[1,"334","9","Coordination Strengthening Between Peace and Development Councils","More infrastructure projects will be rolled out in GICA areas and coordination between LGUs' Peace and Order Councils and Local Development Councils will be strengthened.",""],[1,"335","6","Local Peace Engagement and Transformation Program for Former Rebels","institutionalizing local peace engagements and transformation program for former rebels",""],[1,"335","6","Strengthen Local Government Peace and Order Councils","strengthening the LGUs' peace and order council (POC)",""]],"105":[[1,"353","10","PAMANA Peace and Development Convergence Program","PAMANA is the government's peace and development convergence program, which extends development interventions to communities in isolated and hard-to- reach conflict-affected and conflict-vulnerable areas.",""],[1,"353","11","Barangay Development Program","The Barangay Development Program (BDP) is a peace and development program that aims to provide socioeconomic interventions, e.g., farm to market roads, school buildings, health stations, and livelihood support to barangays cleared from CPP-NPA-NDF.",""],[1,"353","14","Beneficiary Support Package","Support to beneficiaries include scholarships, health insurance, educational assistance, livelihood support.",""],[1,"353","23","MILF Camp Normalization Program","Including the normalization of MILF camps, transformation program of MNLF communities, socioeconomic support to communities, and employment provision for former combatants.",""],[1,"353","23","MNLF Community Transformation Program","Including the normalization of MILF camps, transformation program of MNLF communities, socioeconomic support to communities, and employment provision for former combatants.",""],[1,"353","23","Socioeconomic Support for Conflict-Affected Communities","Including the normalization of MILF camps, transformation program of MNLF communities, socioeconomic support to communities, and employment provision for former combatants.",""],[1,"353","23","Employment Support for Former Combatants","Including the normalization of MILF camps, transformation program of MNLF communities, socioeconomic support to communities, and employment provision for former combatants.",""],[1,"353","24","Inter-Cabinet Cluster Mechanism Support for Normalization and MNLF Transformation Programs","The Inter-Cabinet Cluster Mechanism on Normalization and its member agencies are mandated to support the Normalization Program as provided for in E.O. 79, s. 2019.",""],[1,"421","8","Conflict Sensitivity and Peace Promotion in Local Development Planning","The ability to understand the conflict context, understand how interventions interact with the conflict context, and act upon that understanding to minimize negative impacts and maximize positive impacts of interventions (DILG-Office of the Presidential Adviser on the Peace Process [OPAPP] JMC No. 1-2020 Conflict Sensitivity and Peace Promotion (CSPP) in the Comprehensive Development Plan (CDP) of LGUs in Conflict-Affected and Conflict-Vulnerable Areas).","DILG-Office of the Presidential Adviser on the Peace Process [OPAPP]"],[1,"430","3","Local Peace Engagement Capacity-Building Guidebook","The process which aims to strengthen capacities of national and local governance actors to effectively address socio-economic divides and reduce armed violence in communities to be able to facilitate the delivery of government service, with a long- term view of settling the root causes of conflict in their respective areas.",""]],"106":[[1,"329","7","Strengthened Law Enforcement Operations and Disaster Response","Affirmative action on law enforcement operations on land and at sea including disaster response will be strengthened.",""],[1,"329","7","Modernization of the Armed Forces and Security Sector Agencies","Ongoing modernization of the armed forces and other security sector agencies will be intensified to protect the country's territorial integrity.",""],[1,"332","6","Security Sector Modernization and Capability Upgrade","Hence, support for the modernization of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), Philippine Coast Guard, and other relevant security sector agencies is critical, underscoring the force structure, capability and materiel upgrade needed to be more effective in undertaking internal and external security functions.",""],[1,"338","2","Armed Forces Capacity and Materiel Upgrade","Capacity and materiel upgrade will be pursued to achieve a minimum deterrence capability of the AFP.",""],[1,"338","3","Self-Reliant Defense Posture Program Revival","The self-reliant defense posture program will be revived and supported to rebuild the defense industry.",""],[1,"338","4","Defense Science and Industry Technology Development","and technology development in defense science and industry, including space science and technology applications.",""],[1,"338","5","Security Institutions Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen capacity of institutions in security assessment, operations, and response relative to geopolitical developments",""],[1,"338","6","Maritime Security and Territorial Defense Capacity Building","The government will increase the capacity of security institutions on maritime security and territorial defense, particularly on intelligence and counterintelligence operations, and intensify international cooperation.",""],[1,"339","6","National Defense Department Streamlining and Professionalization Reform","This aims to amend Commonwealth Act No. 1 [National Defense Act of 1935) by streamlining and further professionalizing the Department of National Defense [DND] and its bureaus.",""],[1,"339","10","Defense Industry Development Support and Incentive Scheme","This aims to strengthen the capabilities of the DND to support the development of the defense industry and provide incentives for firms to participate in the effort.","DND"]],"107":[[1,"333","11","Holistic Drug Control Approach","Promote a holistic approach to countering the proliferation of illegal and dangerous drugs",""],[1,"335","7","Holistic Drug Control Approach","Promote a holistic approach in countering the proliferation of illegal and dangerous drugs",""],[1,"335","8","Science-Health-Security Approach to Drug Abuse Control","the government will: (a) use a science-health-security based approach to curbing drug and illegal substance abuse, alongside restorative interventions for drug users and their dependents;",""],[1,"335","8","Stakeholder Partnership Strengthening for Drug Abuse Response","the government will: (b) strengthen partnership with stakeholders;",""]],"108":[[1,"307","12","Water and Coastal Hazard Protection Measures","protect life and property from water and coastal hazards including dam-related hazards;",""],[1,"307","13","Flood Management and Drought Mitigation with Sediment Control","manage flood effectively (with sediment control) and mitigate droughts.",""],[1,"308","1","Revision and Adaptive Updating of Water Security and Flood Master Plans","As necessary, the master plans should be revised and modified based on location-specific conditions and prioritization and timing of investments.",""],[1,"308","4","Water Storage Reservoir and Multipurpose Dam Development","Water storage reservoirs for water supply and drought mitigation, or multi-purpose dams with flood control functions.",""],[1,"308","5","Piped Irrigation System Prioritization","These will be prioritized rather than open channel or gravity canals to eliminate sedimentation problems.",""],[1,"308","7","Hybrid Flood Control and Coastal Protection Infrastructure","Flood control and coastal protection infrastructures with hybrid systems, that is, a combination of nature-based solutions (NBS) and engineered or gray structures.",""],[1,"308","8","National Rainwater Harvesting Guidelines","Country-wide guidelines shall be developed for rainwater harvesting considering seasonal availability and regional variability of rainfall associated with water use, storage requirement, and economic benefit.",""],[1,"308","8","Smart Water Metering and Demand Management Investment","Investments in smart metering and pricing of household water use and demand management shall be promoted.",""],[1,"308","8","Public-Private Partnership Promotion for Water Infrastructure","Public-private partnerships (PPP) shall be encouraged to enhance and strengthen investments in managing and developing water infrastructures and services.",""]],"109":[[1,"310","7","Electricity Cost Reduction Reform","Implement game-changing reforms to bring down the cost of electricity",""],[1,"310","8","Completion of Electric Power Industry Reform Act Reforms","Reforms stipulated in the Electric Power Industry Reform Act (EPIRA) will be completed.",""],[1,"310","8","Retail Competition and Open Access Implementation","fast-track the full implementation of Retail Competition and",""],[1,"310","9","Retail Competition in Open Access Liberalization","The end goal is to set up a competitive retail sector serving households and commercial customers by relaxing the requirements for participation of end-users in RCOA.",""],[1,"311","1","VAT Rationalization for Electricity Billing","The tax (value-added tax) base will be rationalized so that consumers are not taxed for the electricity they do not consume.",""],[1,"311","1","Asset Privatization Acceleration","The government shall endeavor to accelerate the privatization of assets, strengthen the competitive selection process in securing bilateral power supply contracts, and revisit the rules and regulations on cross-ownership between retail electricity suppliers and generation companies or distribution utilities.",""],[1,"311","1","Competitive Power Contracting and Cross-Ownership Regulation Reform","The government shall endeavor to accelerate the privatization of assets, strengthen the competitive selection process in securing bilateral power supply contracts, and revisit the rules and regulations on cross-ownership between retail electricity suppliers and generation companies or distribution utilities.",""],[1,"311","2","Phased Electricity Market Competition Mechanism","The government will explore ways to open and set up new windows of competition: the forward market, reserves market, and capacity market.",""]],"110":[[1,"311","3","Transmission Network Readiness and Oversight","As more entrants venture into the sector, the country's transmission network will need to be prepared as well.","DOE"],[1,"311","5","Power Plant Reliability and Maintenance Scheduling Improvement","The government will enhance the reliability of existing power plants and improve their maintenance scheduling.",""],[1,"311","5","Power Generation and Distribution Performance Assessment and Audit","The government will also pursue the conduct of the Performance Assessment and Audit for power generation facilities and distribution utilities to identify the issues, challenges, and appropriate policy measures to improve power systems operations.",""],[1,"311","5","Climate Risk Integration in Energy Infrastructure Operations and Maintenance","Finally, the government will take measures to incorporate climate risks in energy infrastructure operations and maintenance.",""],[1,"311","6","Energy Delivery Coordination and Investment Alignment","Enhance the delivery of energy by coordinating investment in generation, transmission, and distribution",""],[1,"311","7","National Electrification and Power Infrastructure Coordination Plan","The government will endeavor to enhance the market's ability to coordinate investment in generation, transmission, and distribution infrastructure and achieve total electrification across the country.",""],[1,"312","2","Transmission and Distribution Network Modernization","The government will facilitate the upgrading and modernization of transmission and distribution lines to support efficient transition to cleaner energy.",""],[1,"312","2","Transmission Congestion Resolution Measures","The government will also resolve transmission congestion, especially between Luzon and the Visayas grid, whether by adding transmission lines or avoiding subsidies that cause the build-up of excess capacity.",""],[1,"312","2","Transmission Financing and Tariff Reform","Once the government has the needed fiscal space, it should revisit and reevaluate financing investment in transmission.",""]],"111":[[1,"314","1","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Act Implementation","The Energy Efficiency and Conservation (EEC) Act will be fully implemented",""],[1,"314","1","Energy Efficiency Roadmap and Plan Update","The EEC Roadmap and the National Energy Efficiency and Conservation Plan will be updated and enhanced to provide the policy and program direction on making EEC a way of life for all energy consumers.",""],[1,"314","2","Government Energy Management Program","The government will lead by example through the Government Energy Management Program, which promotes fuel and electricity consumption reduction by 10 percent.",""],[1,"314","2","Demand Side Management Circular","In the medium term, a Demand Side Management Circular will be issued on initiatives and technologies that will encourage consumers optimize their energy use.",""],[1,"314","2","Assessment of Energy Efficiency and Conservation Projects","The government will collaborate with the energy service companies and the private sector to assess the implementation of their respective EEC projects.",""],[1,"314","3","Expansion of Energy Efficiency Coverage and Demand-Side Participation","Program will be expanded to cover more energy-consuming products.",""],[1,"318","18","Biofuels Component Suspension or Reduction Mechanism","This aims to provide for time-bound suspension or reduction of the biofuels component in the event that oil prices are lower than biofuels.",""]],"112":[[1,"315","4","Basic Education Facilities Fund Implementation Improvements","Issues in the implementation of the Basic Education Facilities Fund will be addressed.","Department of Education (DepEd) | DPWH"],[1,"315","4","Local Classroom Gap Identification and Planning Coordination","The Department of Education (DepEd), in coordination with LGUs, will improve the identification of classroom gaps at the local level to better inform the planning and programming, and facilitate the implementation by DPWH.","Department of Education (DepEd) | LGUs | DPWH"],[1,"315","4","Uniform School Building Pricing and Specification Review","DPWH will revisit the uniform pricing and specifications for school buildings to account for possible variances in prices and technical requirements","DPWH"],[1,"315","6","Modern Learning Spaces and Classroom Expansion","Adopt modern learning spaces.",""],[1,"315","7","Universal School Basic Utilities and Facilities Upgrade","In all schools, universal access to basic utilities such as electricity, internet and water supply will be pursued.",""],[1,"315","7","Provision of School Learning Facilities","Provision of basic facilities, including water, sanitation, and hygiene facilities, libraries, and science laboratories will be ensured.",""],[1,"315","7","Future Classroom Learning Space Modernization","Learning spaces will be designed, configured, and equipped to emulate the classroom of the future.",""],[1,"315","7","Education Financing Prioritization and Resource Mobilization","Government allocation for education spending will be prioritized while aid and resources from the private sector, non-government organizations, and civil society organizations will be sought.",""],[1,"318","25","Digital Infrastructure Investment in Public Schools","This aims integrate digital technology and innovation into public basic education by, among others, ensuring adequate investment in digital and technological infrastructure in public schools.",""],[1,"418","16","Basic Education Facilities Fund School Building Program","An annual budget of the Department of Education (DepEd) for its school building program, which covers the improvement and maintenance of school facilities.","Department of Education (DepEd)"],[1,"427","14","Inclusive Learning Resource Center for Learners with Disabilities","Inclusive Learning Resource Center of Learners with Disabilities (ILRC) refers to a physical or virtual center that provides support and related services to teaching and learning, using appropriate, accessible, disability, linguistically-culturally-, and gender- sensitive instructional learning materials, tools, devices, gadgets, and equipment to facilitate and enhance learning, and assessment tools and instruments, to evaluate developmental domains and specific areas of concern to determine appropriate services and placement decisions, with support and related services from medical, health, and allied professionals for care, rehabilitation, and development of learners with disabilities.",""],[1,"438","9","School Governing Council Coordination for School-Based Management","School-Governing Council is the overall coordinating body of all committees, associations, and organizations in their schools that shall translate the principle of shared governance enshrined in RA 9155 and contribute in strengthening the implementation of School-Based Management.","Department of Education"]],"113":[[1,"81","2","Air Pollution Monitoring Technology Development and Incubation","the government initiated the development and incubation of new technologies for monitoring air pollutants",""],[1,"82","17","Air and Water Quality Standards Monitoring and Enforcement","Expand monitoring and enforcement of air and water quality standards",""],[1,"85","4","Integrated Water Resource Management for Water Pollution Control","An integrated water resource management approach to address water pollution shall be adopted.",""],[1,"85","4","Environmental User Fee Expansion for Non-point Pollution","The environmental user fee system shall be expanded to cover non-point pollution sources.",""],[1,"85","4","Multi-stakeholder Water Quality Improvement Initiatives","Multi-stakeholder initiatives to improve water quality, such as massive clean-up, monitoring of industries, and rehabilitation of esteros or rivers, shall continue to be implemented.",""],[1,"85","4","Inter-LGU Collaboration for Shared River Clean-up","Inter-LGU collaboration on clean-up of shared river ecosystems shall be pursued.",""],[1,"85","4","Adopt-an-Estero Program Institutionalization","The adopt-an-estero program shall be institutionalized at the barangay level.",""],[1,"85","4","Septage Management Ordinance Adoption","More LGUs shall enact septage management ordinances to prevent untreated sewage from contaminating water bodies as directed by DILG MC 2019-62.",""],[1,"85","5","Ambient Air Quality Monitoring and Standards Enforcement Upgrade","Moreover, ambient air quality monitoring and enforcement of standards shall be improved.",""],[1,"86","1","Ambient Air Monitoring Station Expansion","To expand coverage ofmonitoring, partnerships with private stakeholders and HUCs shall be pursued in setting up ambient air monitoring stations and through outsourcing from private service providers.",""],[1,"86","1","Air Quality Action Plan Implementation","Monitoring results shall guide Monitoring Airshed Governing Boards and concerned LGUs to implement action plans to improve air quality.",""],[1,"86","1","Indoor Air and Workplace Noise Policy Development","The government will explore the development or improvement of policies to ensure healthy levels of environmental noise and indoor air quality in the workplace and in households.",""]],"114":[[1,"87","6","Informal Settler Resettlement Programmes","On-site, in-city, and near-city resettlement programs shall be adopted.",""],[1,"87","6","Vertical Housing for Informal Settlers","vertical housing for ISFs in metropolitan areas and HUCs shall be an option.",""],[1,"87","7","Halfway Homes and Dormitories for the Homeless","The government may provide halfway homes or dormitories for the homeless who cannot afford formal housing tenures, such as homeownership or rental housing.",""],[1,"87","7","Resettlement Support for Informal Settler Families in Danger Zones","The resettlement option will be provided for ISFs living in danger zones while the community mortgage program will be an option for the rest of the ISFs with community organizations.",""],[1,"87","7","Expanded Housing Programs for Vulnerable Sectors","The government shall continue programs that specifically cater to certain sectors- such as the police, military personnel, and public-school teachers-and expand to vulnerable sectors, such as low-income women, IPs, indigent elderly, and people with disability.",""],[1,"87","8","Operationalization of the National Resettlement Policy Framework","The National Resettlement Policy Framework shall be operationalized in local resettlement plans and programs to ensure that resettlement communities are livable and livelihood are restored.",""],[1,"89","5","People's Plan Expansion for Resettlement Programs","The People's Plan46 adopted for on-site, in-city, and near city resettlement programs to address the urban sprawl shall be broadened to improve livability elements.",""],[1,"94","13","People's Plan Community Development and Social Preparation Process","A social preparation process is needed to craft a People's Plan.",""],[1,"418","9","Socialized Housing Requirement for Subdivision and Condominium Projects","A system whereby owners and/or developers of proposed subdivision and condomimium projects shall be required to develop an area for socialized housing.",""],[1,"432","18","Resettlement and Socialized Housing Implementation Framework","It serves as an overarching framework that outlines common procedures and guidelines for the implementation of resettlement and socialized housing plans and projects for informal settler families (ISFs) and other displaced persons in need of resettlement due to natural or human-induced calamities, emergencies, or crises.",""]],"115":[[1,"264","14","Financial Inclusion Expansion for Previously Excluded Sectors","Improve access to financial services, including digital services, among previously excluded sectors",""],[1,"264","15","SME Financing, Microfinance, and Microinsurance Efficiency and Innovation Initiative","Encourage efficiency and innovation in SME financing, microfinance, and microinsurance",""],[1,"264","22","Cash Agent Service Expansion and Affordability Initiative","Increase ubiquity and affordability of cash agent services",""],[1,"264","25","Financial Products and Services Awareness Campaigns","Enhance awareness campaigns on financial products and services",""],[1,"265","4","Alternative Financial Literacy Platforms","The government will develop alternative platforms for financial literacy programs, including for OFs e.g., through the BSP, Land Bank and other government financial institutions, and other financial regulators, such as the Cooperative Development Authority, Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC), Insurance Commission, and Philippine Deposit Insurance Corporation.","BSP | Land Bank | Cooperative Development Authority | Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) | Insurance Commission | Philippine Deposit Insurance Corporation"],[1,"265","5","Financial Product and Service Awareness Campaigns","financial institutions (FIs)-both banks and non-banks-can enhance the awareness campaigns on financial products and services.",""],[1,"265","6","Financial Inclusion Expansion for Previously Excluded Sectors","Improve access to financial services, including digital services, among previously excluded sectors",""],[1,"265","7","PhilSys Financial Sector Onboarding Expansion","The government will enable broad-based access to both traditional and digital financial services by accelerating the implementation of PhilSys and expanding its use in the financial sector.","Philippine Statistics Authority"],[1,"265","8","Support for Innovation and Competition in Remittance and Digital Financial Services","the government can in turn help foster through greater support for innovation and competition in the sector",""],[1,"265","8","Improvement of Digital Platforms and Remittance Services","Promoting more savings and investments among OFs and their families may be achieved through improved digital platforms and remittance services",""],[1,"265","8","Development of Interoperable Offline Digital Payment Solutions","In off-grid areas, the BSP will promote the development of interoperable 'offline' digital payment solutions",""],[1,"266","1","Offline Digital Financial Transactions","that would enable financial transactions to take place without the need for internet connection, consequently boosting financial inclusion in these areas.",""],[1,"266","3","Shared Agent Network Framework","Moreover, the government will promote a shared agent network framework primarily to increase the ubiquity and affordability of cash agent services.",""],[1,"266","7","SME Financing, Microfinance, and Microinsurance Efficiency and Innovation Initiative","Encourage efficiency and innovation in small and medium enterprise financing, microfinance, and microinsurance",""],[1,"266","8","MSME and Cooperative Inclusive Financing Programs","The government will create an enabling environment and adopt programs to promote financing products responsive to the needs of micro, small and medium enterprises (MSME) and cooperatives which may not have the necessary documents, credit history, or collateral to access the usual financing sources.",""],[1,"267","1","Credit Surety Fund Cooperative Strengthening","Additionally, the government will enhance the implementation of the Credit Surety Fund through the organization and strengthening of Credit Surety Fund Cooperatives to assist in credit risk mitigation for MSMEs.",""],[1,"267","2","MSME and Cooperative Credit Guarantee Facilities","enhanced support for MSMEs and cooperatives, especially in the regions, can be achieved through the provision of credit guarantee facilities under the Philippine Guarantee Corporation (PHILGUARANTEE)",""],[1,"267","2","Crowdfunding Promotion and Securities Market Rules","the SEC will encourage crowdfunding by continuously promoting competition in the market through the promulgation of rules for registration (e.g., granting of more permits) and licensing of innovative and other trading markets for innovative securities, securities of small and medium growth and venture enterprises, and technology-based ventures","SEC"],[1,"267","3","Microfinance and Microinsurance Capacity Building and Digital Transformation","The government will support the capacity building and digital transformation of microfinance and microinsurance companies",""],[1,"267","3","Disaster-Risk Microinsurance Product Development","will promote the development of microinsurance products that cover disaster risks",""],[1,"267","3","Agriculture Insurance Expansion","The expansion of agriculture insurance will be promoted through greater private sector participation",""],[1,"267","3","InsurTech Adoption for Affordable Financial Products","The private sector can adopt insurance technology (InsurTech) to develop affordable and responsive financial products",""],[1,"267","3","Expansion of Social Insurance and Pension Mechanisms","Markets and mechanisms for risk protection shall likewise be expanded, including social insurance and pension",""],[1,"267","3","Strengthening Mission-Driven Financial Service Providers","the capabilities of Financial Service Providers (FSP) that are mission-driven and strategically positioned to serve rural and low-income communities shall also be strengthened",""],[1,"268","6","Capital Markets Development and Financial Inclusion Expansion","The development of the capital markets, through progressive and innovative products and policies, will provide more investment opportunities to retail investors, broadening and deepening financial inclusion and at the same time improving",""]],"117":[[1,"264","13","Macroprudential and Microprudential Financial Stability Measures","Pursue financial stability through macro and micro prudential measures",""],[1,"264","18","FSCC Effectiveness Strengthening","Strengthen the effectiveness of the FSCC",""],[1,"264","21","Financial System Supervision and Regulation Enhancement","Enhance supervision and regulation of the financial system",""],[1,"264","24","Financial Fraud Awareness Campaigns","Enhance awareness campaigns on financial frauds, scams, and recourse measures",""],[1,"268","2","Financial Stability Coordination Council Macroprudential Oversight","the BSP will continue pursuing its mandate to maintain financial stability through the Financial Stability Coordination Council (FSCC), an inter-agency council tasked to ensure financial stability through macro-prudential measures to manage systemic risk.",""],[1,"268","3","Financial Sector Supervision and Regulatory Coordination","Efforts of financial regulators to enhance supervision and regulation of the financial system through information sharing, harmonization of regulations, and coordinated supervisory measures under bilateral arrangements and of the Financial Sector Forum are likewise critical in promoting financial stability.",""],[1,"268","3","Bank Supervision and Microprudential Consumer Protection","The BSP will also maintain close supervision of banks and adopt microprudential measures to ensure the protection of customers and other stakeholders.",""],[1,"268","4","Financial Consumer Protection Act Implementation","The government will intensify financial consumer protection by effectively implementing the Financial Products and Services Consumer Protection Act, including more effective client recourse and stronger cybersecurity measures.",""],[1,"268","4","Regulatory Capacity Enhancement for Financial Services","The continued enhancement of the regulatory environment and capacities will promote greater innovation, competition, and consumer protection across all FSPs.",""],[1,"268","4","Financial Fraud Awareness Campaigns","Meanwhile, private FIs can ramp up awareness campaigns on financial frauds, scams, and recourse measures.",""],[1,"269","1","Technology-Enabled Financial Sector Reporting and Supervision","Finally, the use of technology for reporting, supervision, and compliance will facilitate financial inclusion and innovation and more importantly, ensure a well-functioning financial sector.",""],[1,"269","5","Digital Transformation Framework for Financial Institutions","BSFIs will adopt and implement the digital transformation framework laid out in the BSP DPTR.",""],[1,"269","5","Regulatory Capacity Building for Digital Payment Systems","the BSP will continue to build capacity to ensure that it adopts regulatory frameworks and policies that remain dynamic amidst innovations in and digitalization of the country's payment system.",""],[1,"270","3","RegTech and Supervisory Technology Adoption","BSP will continue to promote the use of regulatory technology (RegTech) by supervised entities and adopt supervisory technology as it digitalizes reportorial requirements and uses artificial intelligence for its supervisory functions.",""],[1,"271","4","Banking System Capacity Strengthening for Financial Crime Prevention","This bill will strengthen the banking system's capacity to effectively combat tax evasion, money laundering, and other financial crimes.",""],[1,"271","13","Consumer Protection and Financial Cybercrime Penalty Reform","It aims to strengthen consumer protection and impose higher penalties for financial cybercrimes.",""]],"118":[[1,"30","7","Universal Health Care Implementation","Another crucial reform, the Universal Health Care Act (RA 11223), which registers all Filipino citizens to a national health insurance program, is still in the process of developing a progressive health care system within the next six years.",""],[1,"60","2","Universal Health Care Financing Reform","Securing predictable, sustainable, and equitably financed funding for UHC reforms is critical.",""],[1,"60","2","Health Insurance Awareness and Enrollment Campaign","In parallel, awareness of social health insurance benefits and membership obligations will be enhanced, along with the adoption of transparent and fixed co-payment and co-insurance policies.",""],[1,"61","1","Increased Public Investment in Health","Increase national and local government investments for health",""],[1,"439","13","Social Health Insurance Scheme","The social health insurance scheme is established by a specific public law, defining, among others, the eligibility, benefit package and rules for the contribution payment.",""],[1,"440","5","Health Services and Health System Operations Financing Pool","A pool of financial resources at the P/-CWHS intended to finance health services and health system operations.",""]],"119":[[1,"39","26","Comprehensive Community Health Care Strategy","Health care strategies will be comprehensive and will focus on building an ecosystem in communities for health care providers, and an environment where individuals can make healthy choices (e.g., nutritious affordable food and health literacy).",""],[1,"57","12","Increase Health Investments","Increase national and local government investments for health",""],[1,"57","14","Whole-of-Government and Whole-of-Society Health Approach","Foster a whole-of government, whole-of-society approach to health",""],[1,"58","2","Healthy Living Environment and Social Determinants of Health Strategy","Strategies include enabling active transport environments, livable communities, and efficient transportation; promoting safe and conducive working and learning spaces for all Filipinos; and ensuring access to safe drinking water, basic sanitation, and nutritious food choices",""],[1,"58","5","Multisectoral Health Promotion and Healthy Settings Collaboration","Multisectoral and multistakeholder approaches are also needed to intensify health promotion activities.","Department of the Interior and Local Government | Department of Labor and Employment | Civil Service Commission | education agencies | National Nutrition Council"],[1,"58","6","Targeted Health Literacy and Behavior Change Communication Campaigns","Well-designated, targeted, gender- and culture-sensitive social and behavior change communication campaigns using multiple",""],[1,"58","7","Health Promotion Communication Campaign","communication media will continuously be implemented to encourage individuals and households to live healthily and make good choices for health.",""],[1,"58","7","Health Promotion Through Family Development Sessions","Existing platforms, such as but not limited to the Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Program's Family Development Sessions, will be maximized for health promotion and advocacy among poorer households.",""],[1,"59","1","Demand-Generation Strategies for Primary Health Services","demand-generation strategies will be pursued for primary services like immunization, MFP, and maternal health.",""],[1,"59","2","Health Care Seeking and Awareness Empowerment","Households and individuals will be empowered with the knowledge and resources to recognize when medical care is necessary, and to seek care at the appropriate levels when needed.",""],[1,"59","3","National Patient Navigation and Referral System","National patient navigation and referral systems will ensure a continuum of appropriate and coordinated care from primary to tertiary and across geopolitical networks.",""],[1,"59","3","Primary Care Provider Registration Facilitation","Facilitating the registration of Filipinos to public or private primary care providers of their choice can promote the efficient use of health services and reduce wastage at other levels of care.",""],[1,"59","5","Primary Health and Community Facility Infrastructure Investment","Infrastructure investments will also be prioritized to improve primary health and community facilities, supplies and equipment, and information technology systems (See Chapter 12).",""],[1,"59","5","Technical Capacity Support for Primary Health Care Workers","This also includes national and local support to enhancing technical service capabilities of primary health care (PHC) and community workers for increased responsiveness to local health needs.",""],[1,"60","1","Patient-Centered Primary Health Care Incentives","incentivize patient-centered PHC and create incentives for improving quality and efficiency in health service delivery.",""],[1,"60","1","Health Technology Assessment Process Strengthening","Timely, rigorous, and transparent health technology assessment processes will also be ensured and supported for the adoption of cost-effective technologies.",""],[1,"60","4","Integrated Innovative Quality Health Care Delivery Systems","Establish integrated, innovative, and quality health care delivery systems",""],[1,"60","5","Integrated Primary Health Care Service Delivery","this means ensuring the accessibility of gender- and culture-sensitive PHC services across the life stages and different levels of care, providing integrated packages of health, nutrition, immunization, family planning (FP), tuberculosis (TB), human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)/ acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS), and adolescent health services, among others.",""],[1,"60","5","Essential Medicines and Health Technologies Supply Assurance","Delivery systems will also ensure availability, accessibility, and affordability of safe, efficacious, and quality essential medicines and other needed health technologies.",""],[1,"60","6","Targeted Access Interventions for Underserved Communities","access interventions will prioritize geographically isolated and disadvantaged areas, marginalized populations, and indigenous peoples communities.",""],[1,"60","6","Telemedicine and Remote Health Service Partnerships","Multisectoral partnerships with resolved payment mechanisms will be pursued to deliver telemedicine, capability support for community health care workers, remote health care services, and other innovations for health.",""],[1,"60","6","Emergency Medical Transport Services","Emergency medical services including paramedic, ambulance, and other patient transport services are also crucial to reaching more underserved and unserved areas with timely health care.",""],[1,"61","2","Primary Health Care Investment and Financing Strengthening","Significant investments are necessary to ensure sustainable human and material resources for PHC.",""],[1,"61","2","LGU Health Investment Safeguards","safeguards will be established to ensure continuous and sustained LGU investments for health.",""],[1,"61","2","Health Matching and Performance Grant Schemes","Shifting to matching grants, performance- based grants, and similar incentive schemes will help steer spending for health and improve LGU capacity to deliver both population and individual-based health services, as well as increase accountability to local health systems.",""],[1,"61","2","Special Health Fund Implementation","Implementation of the Special Health Fund to pool resources for health at the province or city level will enable both the national and local governments to maximize economies of scale and pursue more strategic planning, allocation, and management of local resources.",""],[1,"61","2","Health Human Resources Investment","Increases in health investments will also be matched with investments in HRH.",""],[1,"61","2","Local Health Personnel Hiring Reform","To allow LGUs to hire more local health personnel, the Personnel Services cap in the Local Government Code will be adjusted.",""],[1,"61","2","Sustainable UHC Financing Arrangements","At the national level, sustainable financing arrangements in support of UHC will be pursued and both available and emerging financing opportunities will be maximized.",""],[1,"67","3","Executive Order on Integration","The targets will be based on the EO on Integration, which will be issued by the President following the evaluation study on the overall benefits of the local health system integration by Joint Congressional Oversight Committee on UHC.",""]],"120":[[1,"359","3","National Government Portal and Online Government Services Expansion","the National Government Portal and its subsequent provision of over 200 online government services;",""],[1,"359","3","Open Data Expansion Initiative","the expansion of open data features of government information.",""],[1,"359","3","Nationwide Free Public Wi-Fi Expansion","the increase in free public Wi-Fi hotspots nationwide",""],[1,"362","6","Open Data and Internet Access Expansion","Broadening public access to information not merely entails publicizing more information, but also observing open data formats, removing barriers to internet connectivity, and",""],[1,"363","1","Open Data Philippines Expansion","The Department of Information and Communications Technology (DICT) will also enhance the volume and scope of information in Open Data Philippines (online repository of open data from different government agencies),","Department of Information and Communications Technology (DICT)"],[1,"363","1","Nationwide Free Public Wi-Fi Provision","and the provision of free public Wi-Fi services nationwide.","Department of Information and Communications Technology (DICT)"],[1,"368","7","ICT-Enabled Government Service Delivery and Data Access","This will promote the use of information and communications technology in improving government service delivery and providing access to reliable data and information.",""],[1,"423","13","Government ICT for Public Services and Knowledge Society Framework","Use of information and communication technologies in government to provide public services, to improve managerial effectiveness and to promote democratic values; as well as a regulatory framework that facilitates information intensive initiatives and fosters the knowledge society.",""],[1,"432","10","One-Stop Government Digital Services Portal","A one-stop -shop of government data, information, and services.",""]],"121":[[1,"261","1","National Government Spending Efficiency Reform","Due to limited fiscal space, national government spending shall also be made more efficient while budget priorities will be aligned with the administration's socio-economic agenda.",""],[1,"273","3","Public Expenditure Efficiency and Budget Alignment Reform","National government spending will be made more efficient while budget priorities will be aligned with the administration's socioeconomic agenda.",""],[1,"274","19","Private Sector Participation in Government Procurement","Increase participation of the private sector in the procurement of government projects",""],[1,"274","24","Timely Completion of Awards and Projects","Ensure timely completion of awards and projects",""],[1,"278","5","Private Sector Participation in Government Procurement","Increase participation of the private sector in the procurement of government projects",""],[1,"278","8","Modernized Government Procurement System Implementation","The full implementation of the Modernized Philippine Government Procurement System, automation of procurement-related reports, and simplification of bidding documents will help streamline procurement processes and improve budget utilization.",""],[1,"278","8","Budget Modernization Bill","A Budget Modernization Bill has also been introduced in Congress, seeking to institutionalize reforms in the Cash Budgeting System and Public Financial Management (PFM).",""],[1,"278","8","Public Financial Management Reform","PFM reforms will institute fiscal discipline to ensure that budget proposals from line agencies will undergo extensive preparation, and will be implemented on time.",""],[1,"278","8","Government Procurement Reform Act IRR Review","The IRR of the Government Procurement Reform Act will likewise be further reviewed to address procurement delays.",""],[1,"281","11","Budget Modernization Bill","Budget Modernization Bill: Seeks to institutionalize an efficient Cash Budgeting System and other key Public Financial Management reforms.",""],[1,"368","8","Cash-Based Budgeting System Institutionalization","This seeks to institutionalize the cash-based budgeting system to strengthen fiscal discipline in the allocation accountability. and use of budget resources.",""],[1,"371","11","Budget and Treasury Management System within IFMIS","The Budget and Treasury Management System is a core element of the Integrated Financial Management Information System, which seeks to: (a) facilitate an efficient and secure government financial transactions and (b) strengthen the monitoring and reporting of financial and fiscal data.",""],[1,"419","17","Annual Appropriations Budgeting System","Budgeting system where the annual appropriations limit the incurrence of obligations and payments for goods delivered, services, and civil works delivered/rendered, inspected, and accepted within the current fiscal year or the transition period as approved by the President as recommended by the DBM.","DBM"]],"122":[[1,"361","23","National Governance Assessment Improvement","Improve national governance assessments",""],[1,"365","1","Governance Assessment and Policy Learning Strengthening","As a cross-cutting strategy, the government will ensure the effective and timely conduct of governance assessments and improve the policy learning environment at all government levels.",""],[1,"365","2","National Governance Index Roll-out","roll-out of a National Governance Index29 and intensify the National Evaluation Policy Framework.",""],[1,"365","2","Seal of Good Local Governance Assessment","The DILG and the Council of Good Local Governance will maintain the implementation of the Seal of Good Local Governance assessment of LGUs.","DILG | Council of Good Local Governance"],[1,"366","4","Productivity Performance Framework Strengthening","the government will strengthen productivity performance frameworks across government sectors and levels and translate these into more coherent capacity development programs and incentive structures.",""],[1,"366","4","National Governance Assessment Development","The Government Quality Management Program assessments, Citizen Satisfaction e-Survey,48 and Business Satisfaction e-Survey49 will contribute to the development of broader national governance assessments.",""],[1,"366","4","Citizen-Centered Service Improvement Support","guidance and assistance will be pursued in utilizing data from the national satisfaction surveys to identify standards and improvement priorities as well as balancing outside-in and inside-out approaches to improve citizen-centered design and delivery performance.",""],[1,"425","18","Public Sector Quality Management System","Aims to effect advancement in public sector performance by ensuring the consistency of products and services that government agencies deliver through the application of processes that can be achieved through an effective Quality Management System.",""],[1,"438","15","LGU Awards, Incentives, Honors, and Recognition Program","An award, incentive, honor and recognition-based program for all LGUs and is a continuing commitment for LGUs to continually progress and improve their performance.",""]],"123":[[1,"19","7","Local-National Government Collaboration Mechanism","fostering greater collaboration between local and national governments",""],[1,"19","7","Private Sector Partnership Facilitation","facilitating stronger partnerships with the private sector",""],[1,"38","1","Local Government Partnership in Development Agenda","bring local governments in as equal partners in the development agenda of the country.",""]],"124":[[1,"273","3","Civil Service Rightsizing and Devolution Support","Rightsizing of the bureaucracy will be pursued, consistent with the devolution of services to local governments.",""],[1,"279","1","National Government Rightsizing Program","The government will embark on a National Government Rightsizing Program (NGRP) that will result in a more agile, efficient, and technology-adept workforce.",""],[1,"361","14","Rightsizing and Whole-of-Government Systems Re-engineering","Pursue rightsizing and the whole-of-government approach in re-engineering systems and procedures",""],[1,"365","3","Rightsizing and Digitalization of Government Functions","Strategies for this outcome include rightsizing and digitalizing government functions, while enhancing productivity.",""],[1,"365","4","Rightsizing and Whole-of-Government Systems Re-engineering","Pursue rightsizing and the whole-of-government approach in re-engineering systems and procedures",""],[1,"365","5","National Government Rightsizing Program","The government will enact the National Government Rightsizing Program33 to implement structural and procedural reforms in the executive branch and advocate rightsizing among LGUs, the legislature, the",""],[1,"365","6","Government Role and Agency Re-engineering Review","appropriate diagnostic frameworks, upholding economic principles, and strategic reviews of the role, mandates, functions, and structure of government will be employed.",""],[1,"365","6","National Agency Performance Optimization and Public Service Delivery Improvement","The government will also optimize the performance of national agencies' core functions, and ensure the effective and efficient implementation of public services.",""],[1,"365","6","GOCC Reorganization and Streamlining Authority","agencies will improve the implementation of complementary policies such as the authority of the Governance Commission for Government- Owned or -Controlled Corporations (GOCCs) to reorganize, streamline, abolish, or privatize GOCCs;",""],[1,"365","6","Whole-of-Government Re-engineering Manual Mainstreaming","ARTA's mainstreaming of the Whole-of-Government Re-engineering Manual;",""],[1,"365","6","Audit and Systems Development Streamlining Across Agencies","streamlining of audits and systems development across agencies.",""],[1,"365","7","Strategic Delineation of National Agency Functions and Staffing","the government will facilitate the strategic delineation of functions, structure, and staffing of national agencies",""],[1,"366","1","Agency Transition to Policy Oversight and Capacity Support","Led by the DBM and DILG, concerned national agencies will expedite their respective transitions into capable policy development and oversight bodies that can provide sound and timely service delivery standards and capacity development interventions for LGUs.","DBM | DILG"],[1,"366","1","Streamlining of Subnational Transition Support Bodies","The functions of inter-agency and multi-stakeholder bodies and committees that support the transition at the subnational levels will be streamlined as part of the functions of the Regional Development Councils.",""],[1,"368","3","Priority Bills for Good Governance and Bureaucratic Efficiency","Table 14.1 contains priority bills for the 19th Congress during the Plan period to practice good governance and improve bureaucratic efficiency.",""],[1,"368","6","Public Sector Institutional Streamlining Reform","This will implement transformational improvements to streamline the functions, mandates, structure, and staffing of departments and agencies and simplify systems and processes to deliver public goods and services in the most efficient, effective, and economical manner.",""],[1,"428","20","Intergovernmental Relations Coordination and Dispute Resolution Mechanism","The mechanisms for coordination and resolution of issues on intergovernmental relations through regular consultation and continuing negotiation in a non-adversarial manner between the national and Bangsmoro governments.",""],[1,"429","2","Inter-Agency Coordination and Information-Sharing Body","An inter-agency body composed of the Judiciary, the Department of Justice, the Department of the Interior and Local Government, and their relevant attached agencies, which serves as a joint forum for dialogue on issues of common interest and mechanism for effective coordination and sharing of information for planning and implementation of joint initiatives.","Judiciary | Department of Justice | Department of the Interior and Local Government"]],"125":[[1,"368","10","National Evaluation Policy Framework Institutionalization","This will strengthen legal and institutional frameworks for the regular measurement, reporting, and utilization of the results of public policies, programs, and projects toward supporting evidence-based decisions, ensuring program improvement, and promoting transparency and accountability in the government.",""],[1,"395","2","Whole-of-Government Economic Transformation Coordination and Monitoring","This economic transformation calls for a whole-of-government and whole-of-society collaboration, which will be enabled through good governance, transparency, accountability, and evidence-based decision-making.",""],[1,"395","3","Policy and Regulatory Alignment for PDP Implementation","The government will set the necessary policies and regulatory environment and implement concrete programs, activities, and projects to achieve the targets set in the PDP 2023-2028.",""],[1,"395","3","Executive Order for Agency Plan and Budget Alignment","An executive order will be issued directing all government instrumentalities to adopt and align agency plans, roadmaps, and budgetary programs with the Plan.",""],[1,"395","3","NEDA Strategy Prioritization and Legislative Coordination","The National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) Secretariat will work with implementing agencies on the prioritization of identified strategies, policies, programs, and projects, including the proposed legislation.","National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) Secretariat"],[1,"395","4","Inter-Agency Plan Implementation and Coordination Committees","inter-agency committees were identified to lead and coordinate the implementation of the Plan.",""],[1,"395","5","NEDA Board Implementation Oversight","The NEDA Board will oversee the implementation of measures that directly contribute to the achievement of the headline targets as enumerated in Chapter 1: A Plan for Economic and Social Transformation.",""],[1,"395","7","Social Development Committee Implementation Oversight","The Social Development Committee will take the lead in ensuring that strategies are implemented to achieve the targets under Chapter 2: Promote Human Capital and Social Development.",""],[1,"396","35","Development Budget Coordination Committee for Macroeconomic Stability","the Development Budget Coordination Committee will ensure that fiscal and financial policies",""],[1,"397","5","Annual Socioeconomic Report Preparation","the NEDA Secretariat shall annually prepare the Socioeconomic Report (SER) to present actual accomplishments in terms of outputs and outcomes as contained in the PDP and the RM.",""],[1,"397","5","Regular Review and Updating of the Results Matrix","The RM is a living document that should be referred to and updated regularly to ensure responsiveness to the country's continuously evolving development landscape.",""],[1,"397","6","Plan Monitoring Gap Identification in SER","To address the gaps, the following strategies will be employed:",""],[1,"397","8","Monitoring Data Analysis, Reporting, and Use Improvement","Improving analysis, reporting, and use of monitoring data.",""],[1,"398","1","Online PDP Monitoring Data Platform","Following the open data policy of the government, the creation of such a platform shall improve the accessibility and comprehension of PDP monitoring data.",""],[1,"398","2","Plan Monitoring Capacity Enhancement","The reporting agencies identified in the RM should continue to enhance their capacities to monitor the Plan toward ensuring the provision of quality and timely data.",""],[1,"398","3","National Evaluation Policy Framework","NEDA and the Department of Budget and Management (DBM) adopted the National Evaluation Policy (NEP) Framework in 20151 in line with the government's continuing efforts to strengthen its results orientation","NEDA | Department of Budget and Management (DBM)"],[1,"398","5","PDP Progress Assessment and Monitoring","the agency is in the strategic position to be at the helm in the systematic, rigorous, and impartial assessment of its progress.","NEDA"],[1,"399","9","National Evaluation Agenda","A national evaluation agenda will be crafted to set out the priority evaluations that the government will pursue as a means of measuring and obtaining evidence on results derived from strategies and priority interventions laid out in the plan and the RM.",""],[1,"399","10","Scoping and Evaluation Studies for Priority Programs and Projects","Undertake scoping studies to identify knowledge gaps and the corresponding evaluation studies to create evidence that will inform the implementation of priority programs and projects of this administration.",""],[1,"399","11","Evaluation Data Collection and Use Strengthening","Strengthen the collection, analysis, and use of evaluation data to promote evidence-based and data-driven decision-making.",""],[1,"400","2","National Evaluation Policy Enactment","Support the enactment of a National Evaluation Policy to accelerate efforts in institutionalizing evaluation practice in the government.",""],[1,"400","3","Evaluation Capacity-Building and Training Program","Strengthen the capacity of agencies to conduct and utilize evaluations.",""],[1,"400","4","Evaluation Findings Communication and Utilization System","Effectively communicate evaluation findings to increase utilization and influence of evaluations.",""],[1,"400","4","Institutionalized Agency Evaluation Units","This entails having an institutionalized evaluation unit to manage and advocate for evaluation activities within each agency of the bureaucracy.",""],[1,"400","4","Integration of Evaluation Prioritization into Planning and Project Development","This unit will ensure that prioritization and utilization of evaluations are integrated into higher-level processes such as agency planning and project development.",""],[1,"400","4","Monitoring, Evaluation, and Learning Documentation System","Documentation of monitoring and evaluation activities and learning also ensure that new program teams can leverage institutional knowledge built from previous projects.",""],[1,"400","5","PDP Strategy Assessment Consultation and Advisory Committee Review","The NEDA Secretariat will also consult with the PDP Advisory Committee on the assessment of strategies and their effectiveness in achieving the targets and outcomes.",""]],"126":[[1,"83","2","Quality Job Creation and Upskilling Programme","Communities shall benefit from national programs to scale up quality job creation such as upskilling to increase employability and increased opportunities in agriculture and agribusiness, industries, services, and sustainable resource-based livelihoods.",""],[1,"127","1","Workforce Development and Employment Facilitation","Increasing the income-earning ability of Filipinos involves developing the workforce and increasing their employability in the market, ensuring that skills are aligned not just with the current in-demand requirements but also with critical and emerging skills.",""],[1,"127","1","Employment Facilitation Process Improvement","Effective and efficient employment facilitation processes will also enable faster and more strategic job search.",""],[1,"127","1","Social Partnership for Labor Market Efficiency","A vibrant social partnership, based on shared responsibility for achieving a responsive, fair, and efficient labor market, will also be crucial.",""],[1,"129","4","Employment Facilitation Services Integration and Strengthening","Integrate and strengthen all employment facilitation services, including career development support",""],[1,"129","6","Labor Market Information System Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen technical capacity to develop dynamic and responsive labor market information systems",""],[1,"129","18","PhilJobNet Labor Market Information Update","Provide updated labor market information to PhilJobNet",""],[1,"133","6","Employment Facilitation Services Integration and Strengthening","Integrate and strengthen all employment facilitation services, including career development support",""],[1,"133","8","Integrated Employment Services and Labor Market Information Platform","the government shall integrate all employment program monitoring systems, career development support, and labor market information systems in the PhilJobNet to provide a complete employment journey for target clients.",""],[1,"133","8","Employment, Career Counseling, and Skills Training Partnership","potentially transition to offering a full range of employment, career counseling, and training services for specific in-demand skills through a partnership with TESDA and educational institutions.",""],[1,"133","8","Returning Overseas Filipinos Employment Integration Services","Returning Overseas Filipinos will also have access to these services, facilitating their integration back to the domestic economy.",""],[1,"134","1","PESO Network Linkage and Labor Market Intelligence System","Strengthening linkages among PESO centers can create a hub of information exchange on best practices in employment facilitation.",""],[1,"134","1","PESO Portal for Labor Mobility","Labor mobility can also be enhanced by creating a PESO portal, highlighting the ability of PESOs to facilitate labor reallocation across regions.",""],[1,"134","2","Public Employment Service Office Service Delivery Strengthening","The government shall ensure that PESOs can deliver vital services mandated by local ordinances and national laws.",""],[1,"134","3","PESO Service Expansion and Promotion","To ensure the maintenance, expansion, and promotion of PESO services, increased allocation of local budgets may be necessary.",""],[1,"134","3","Digital Local Labor Market Information Platforms","LGUs can consider investing in digital platforms that automatically update the state of local labor markets and highlight job trends.",""],[1,"134","3","PESO Digital Registration and Application Platform Enhancement","Similar platforms can also be made more responsive to the needs of PESO constituents by facilitating registration, access, and application.",""],[1,"134","4","Dynamic Labor Market Information Systems Investment","Investing in dynamic labor market information systems (LMIS) will result in efficient information flow, better skills anticipation, and competency forecasts.",""],[1,"134","4","Forward-Looking Labor Market Information Services","Timely delivery of labor market information services requires forward-looking information systems.",""],[1,"134","4","Digital Skills and Occupation Mapping Framework","the government can leverage digital technology by mapping changing skills and qualifications, as well as identifying pathways to improving competencies through a framework for classifying similar jobs or occupations.",""],[1,"134","5","PhilJobNet Labor Market Information System Upgrade","The PhilJobNet is envisioned as a one-stop-shop for labor market information, allowing employers to post vacancies, and workers to search for jobs.",""],[1,"134","6","PhilJobNet Employer Enrollment and System Linkage","Unregistered employers can consider enlisting as part of PhiljobNet to avail of the services, such that labor search costs can be reduced and staffing needs can be addressed.",""],[1,"134","6","Labor Market Intelligence and Data Quality Improvement","Moreover, the participation of employers can contribute to local development by enriching labor market intelligence.",""],[1,"134","6","PhilJobNet Data Linkage and Local Labor Market Reporting","Linking to PhilJobNet improves the data quality and ensures proper characterization of local labor market conditions.",""],[1,"134","6","Secure Employer System Integration","Industry associations can also explore ways to reliably and securely link systems that continuously provide updates.",""]],"127":[[1,"36","8","Expansion of the Automated Job and Applicant Matching System","and better link job seekers to employment opportunities through the expansion of the automated job and applicant matching system, PhilJobNet, created by the Department of Labor and Employment (DOLE).","Department of Labor and Employment (DOLE)"],[1,"40","4","Continuous Updating of Training Modules and Curricula","Contents of training modules and curricula for human capital development will be continuously updated to match the needs of emerging in-demand occupations.",""],[1,"40","5","Employment Facilitation Services Enhancement","Employment facilitation services will be enhanced to include career development",""],[1,"40","7","Anti-Discrimination Law Enforcement for Income-Earning Opportunities","Everyone will have access to opportunities to increase their income-earning abilities by the effective enforcement of anti-discrimination laws.",""],[1,"76","16","Labor Force Upskilling and Reskilling Programme","promoting upskilling and reskilling of labor force (See Chapter 4)",""],[1,"76","19","Curriculum-Based Management Training, Workforce Upskilling and R&D Promotion","and management training in the curriculum of students (See Chapter 13), promoting upskilling and reskilling of labor force (See Chapter 4), and advancing research and development and innovation (See Chapter 8).",""],[1,"384","2","Green Jobs Human Resource Development Plan","The implementation of the Green Jobs Human Resource Development Plan will be prioritized, including the provision of support and training opportunities (e.g., retooling, upskilling, or reskilling on sustainable practices and processes) for workers and enterprises affected by the transition to a sustainable and green economy.",""],[1,"429","14","Client-Specific Labor Market Information and Career Guidance Materials","Provides timely relevant and accurate signals on the current labor market such as in-demand jobs and skills shortages by developing client-specific LMI, Education and Communication materials.","DOLE"],[1,"429","16","Employment Facilitation and Placement Schemes","Labour market interventions aim to give gainful employment to citizens through employment facilitation and placement schemes, active labour market programmes, emergency and guaranteed employment and unemployment insurance.",""],[1,"429","16","Active Labour Market Programmes","Labour market interventions aim to give gainful employment to citizens through employment facilitation and placement schemes, active labour market programmes, emergency and guaranteed employment and unemployment insurance.",""],[1,"429","16","Emergency and Guaranteed Employment Scheme","Labour market interventions aim to give gainful employment to citizens through employment facilitation and placement schemes, active labour market programmes, emergency and guaranteed employment and unemployment insurance.",""],[1,"429","16","Unemployment Insurance","Labour market interventions aim to give gainful employment to citizens through employment facilitation and placement schemes, active labour market programmes, emergency and guaranteed employment and unemployment insurance.",""],[1,"429","16","Sector-Specific Employment and Entrepreneurship Support Measures","These programs should also respond to specific needs of sectors.",""],[1,"429","16","Informal Economy Worker Security of Tenure Measures","government should adopt measures aimed at enhancing employment and entrepreneurial opportunities and providing security of tenure for the workers in the informal economy.",""],[1,"435","18","Workforce Reskilling and Upskilling Partnership","The PSF builds upon the partnership among national government agencies and a key outcome of the signed MOU in 2019 between DTi, TESDA, and Skills Future Singapore to cooperate on human capital development and the reskilling and upskilling of the workforce.","DTi | TESDA | Skills Future Singapore"]],"128":[[1,"129","10","Youth and Vulnerable Groups Employment Program Expansion","Intensify employment programs for the youth, marginalized, disadvantaged, and vulnerable sectors",""],[1,"129","11","Labor Market Discrimination Reduction Programs and Policies","Develop programs and policies that address all forms of labor market discrimination in work, education, and training",""],[1,"129","14","Emergency Employment and Training Support for Displaced Workers","Provide emergency employment and training support to displaced workers due to human-induced disasters and natural calamities",""],[1,"136","4","Emergency Employment and Training Support for Displaced Workers","Provide emergency employment and training support to displaced workers due to human-induced disasters and natural calamities",""],[1,"136","5","Emergency Employment Support for Displaced Workers","Two notable active labor market interventions include the provision of emergency employment for displaced workers (Tulong Panghanapbuhay sa Ating Disadvantaged/Displaced Workers or TUPAD)","DOLE"],[1,"136","5","Training for Work Scholarship Program","Two notable active labor market interventions include ... the Training for Work Scholarship Program.",""],[1,"136","5","Employment and Certification Skills Training Packages for Calamity-Prone Areas","DOLE and TESDA continue to roll out employment and national certification skills training packages to calamity-prone areas to ensure social safety net and employment opportunities for affected residents.","DOLE | TESDA"],[1,"136","5","Convergence Study of Livelihood and Community-Based Training Programs","DOLE and TESDA shall study the convergence of their livelihood training programs and community-based training programs, respectively, to avoid duplication.","DOLE | TESDA"],[1,"136","8","Training Program Inventory and Convergence Initiative","The creation of an inventory of all training programs shall pave the way toward the convergence of programs with similar objectives;",""],[1,"136","8","Training Program Impact Evaluation Studies","Impact evaluation studies to determine the degree of program effectiveness and identify areas of reform shall be conducted.",""],[1,"137","5","Income-Generating Ability Enhancement Interventions","The government shall remain proactive in formulating innovative and effective interventions that enhance income-generating ability throughout the worker's life cycle, especially those of the vulnerable groups and communities.",""]],"129":[[1,"415","10","Special Program for Employment of Students","Special Program for Employment of Students",""]],"130":[[1,"165","1","Industry Sector Revitalization and Industrial Linkage Strengthening","the industry sector will be revitalized by expanding the domestic market and supplier base, moving up the value chain, and enhancing linkages across sectors.",""],[1,"167","4","Industry Sector Revitalization","the industry sector will be revitalized through expanding the domestic market and supplier base, moving up the value chain, and enhancing linkages across sectors",""],[1,"167","32","Industry-Specific Undertaking","Undertake industry-specific",""],[1,"168","1","Integrated Industrial Policy for Domestic Production Expansion","This entails enhancing business-matching activities across the regions, intensifying support to industries producing for the domestic market, and providing targeted and time-bound incentives to establish labor-intensive industries and businesses.",""],[1,"168","3","Cross-Sector Value Chain Linkage Strategy","Government will facilitate the linking of the upstream segments to the downstream segments through capacity development and assistance to meet technical requirements.",""],[1,"171","4","Manufacturing Roadmap Implementation Intensification","The implementation of the manufacturing roadmap will be intensified to address value chain gaps in industry.",""],[1,"171","4","Furniture Manufacturing Supply Hub Establishment","the DTI, in coordination with the DOST, will facilitate the establishment of supply hubs for raw and natural materials in furniture manufacturing.","DTI | DOST"],[1,"171","4","Iron and Steel Industry Integration with Mining Programmes","the DTI and the Mines and Geosciences Bureau will undertake programs to enhance the integration of the iron and steel industry with mining, to include increasing","DTI | Mines and Geosciences Bureau"],[1,"174","2","Industrial Clustering of Knowledge- and Technology-Intensive Industries","Intensify the clustering of existing knowledge-and-technology intensive industries (KTI).",""],[1,"178","8","Cross-Sector Industrial Linkage Strengthening","Industries need to increase their linkages with agriculture and services sectors.",""],[1,"178","8","Trade and Industrial Policy Coordination","The link between trade and industrial policy will also be strengthened.",""],[1,"180","5","Inter-Industry Demand Strengthening for Servicification","government will further strengthen the inter-industry demand between industry and service sectors to encourage more servicification.",""],[1,"180","5","Demand-Side Measures for Servicification","Developing product standards, protecting consumer preferences, reducing regulatory demands or requirements, enhancing export orientation & GVC participation, and utilizing government procurement are examples of demand-side strategies, which the government can implement.",""],[1,"181","3","Industry Ecosystem Collaboration and Linkage Strengthening","A more active interface and collaboration with the industry ecosystem will be established among these business networks.",""],[1,"396","32","Acceleration of Production Sector Transformation Measures","The EDC will also expedite the implementation of measures to transform the production sectors, as identified in Chapter 5: Modernize Agriculture and Agribusiness, Chapter 6: Revitalize Industry, and Chapter 7: Reinvigorate Services.",""]],"131":[[1,"226","9","Preventive Measures for Distressed Firms","Proactively monitor and implement preventive measures and :selected: interventions for distressed firms",""],[1,"227","5","Distressed Firms Monitoring and Preventive Intervention Program","Proactively monitor and implement preventive measures and interventions for distressed firms",""],[1,"227","6","Early Warning and Rapid Assistance Mechanism for Exporting MSMEs","The government will design and implement an effective Early Warning System;7 Rapid Assistance mechanisms; and farsighted preventive measures to support export pillar sectors as well as micro, small, and medium enterprises (MSME), which are in critical stages of transition (e.g., local to foreign markets; scale shifts).",""],[1,"227","6","Customized Support Programs for Distressed Export Sectors","This will be the basis for developing customized programs, especially for sectors and firms in distress, as well as support measures to assist exporters in maximizing opportunities in key markets.","Department of Trade and Industry (DTI)"],[1,"231","2","Early Warning System for Approved Investments","This will likewise be monitored by an Early Warning System, especially to help increase the realization rates of approved investments.",""]],"132":[[1,"226","16","Alignment of National and Local Investment Promotion Strategies","Maximize synergy and decisively align national and local :selected: government investment promotion strategies",""],[1,"226","17","Make It Happen in the Philippines Campaign","Launch an aggressive \"make it happen in the philippines\" campaign and raise awareness of the new business climate ushered in by most recent structural reforms",""],[1,"226","18","Strategic Investment Priority Plan","Leverage the Strategic Investment Priority Plan (SIPP)",""],[1,"226","19","Rural Locational Asset Development for FDI Attraction","Heighten the country's attractiveness for foreign direct investments (FDI) by developing unique locational assets especially in the rural areas",""],[1,"226","20","Foreign and ESG Investment Promotion","Position the Philippines as a prime destination of foreign :selected: investments against climate change or environmental, social, and governance (ESG) investments",""],[1,"226","21","Public-Private Social Partnership Reconfiguration","Re-configure public-private social partnerships to build :selected: strong collaboration infrastructure that will serve common investment promotion campaigns, and longer-run joint strategies to improve the country's business climate",""],[1,"230","5","Inter-Agency Investment Promotion Coordination Committee","The establishment of the Inter-Agency Investment Promotion Coordination Committee under the Amended Foreign Investments Act (Republic Act 11647) will be hastened in order to integrate all the promotion and facilitation efforts to encourage foreign investments and make the new investment environment credibly improved for investors.",""],[1,"230","7","Business Climate Branding and Awareness Campaign","Launch an aggressive branding campaign and raise awareness of the new business climate ushered in by most recent structural reforms",""],[1,"230","8","FDI Reform Communication Campaign","an all-out campaign is needed to bring across the message that a new FDI regime exists, making the country truly open for business.",""],[1,"231","1","Investment Law Information Dissemination and Communications Campaign","government will maximize the opportunities opened up by the Corporate Recovery and Tax Incentives for Enterprises (CREATE) Act, the amended Foreign Investment Act (RA 11647), the Retail Trade Liberalization Act (RA 11595), and the Public Service Act (RA 11659), through local and international user-friendly information dissemination programs, and coordinated communications campaign done in collaboration with the private sector and social partners.",""],[1,"231","1","Internal Investment Promotion Campaign for LGUs","However, an equally strong internal campaign is likewise needed, especially among LGUs.",""],[1,"231","2","Strategic Investment Priority Plan Promotion","Promotion of the Strategic Investment Priority Plan (SIPP) through sector-focused and company-specific promotion in target markets will be intensified.",""],[1,"231","2","SIPP Implementation Incentive Framework","The implementation of SIPP, pursuant to the CREATE Act, will incentivize highly attractive investments and will yield more diversified, complex, and sophisticated products and services in the country.",""],[1,"231","3","Rural Locational Asset Development for FDI Attraction","Heighten the country's attractiveness to foreign direct investment by developing unique locational assets, especially in the rural areas",""],[1,"231","4","Regional Investment Promotion and Domestic Investor Partnership Support","The role of domestic investor firms especially in rural areas in drawing foreign partnerships in greenfield investments will be strengthened.",""],[1,"231","5","Rural Investment Promotion and LGU Capacity-Building","bring investments to the countryside.",""],[1,"231","7","Institutionalization of Local Economic Development and Investment Promotion Offices","The Local Economic Development and Investment Promotion Offices in all LGUs (province, cities, and municipalities) will be institutionalized to facilitate and coordinate local economic development and investment promotion advocacies, policies, programs, projects, and activities.",""],[1,"232","2","ESG Investments Task Force","an ESG Investments Task Force will be established.",""],[1,"232","16","Investment Facilitation Mechanism","Executive Order [EO) for a whole- of-government, harmonized, and structured Investment Facilitation Mechanism, including resolution of critical issues and concerns for identified priority investments.",""],[1,"232","17","Cross-Cutting Facilitation Services for Priority Investments","Issuance of an EO will provide cross-cutting facilitation services for priority investments.",""]],"133":[[1,"42","7","Financial Inclusion and Innovation Support Measures","The strategies aim to broaden and deepen financial inclusion, and accelerate financial innovation, while ensuring financial sector health.",""],[1,"42","7","Regulatory Sandbox and RegTech Promotion","On financial innovation, governmentinstitutions will adopta \"regulatory sandbox\" approach for new innovations, promote RegTech, and address information gaps to encourage innovations.",""],[1,"42","7","Financial Consumer Protection and Prudential Oversight","To ensure financial health, government institutions will intensify consumer protection, and undertake macro- and micro-prudential measures.",""],[1,"113","36","Financial Literacy Promotion","Promote financial literacy for better awareness and use of financial instruments",""],[1,"115","5","Financial Literacy Promotion","Promote financial literacy for better awareness and use of financial instruments",""],[1,"115","6","Financial Literacy Expansion Initiative","National and local governments, in partnership with the private and civil society sectors, shall ramp up efforts toward financial literacy (See Subchapter 11.1).",""],[1,"115","7","Innovative Insurance Product Development through Partnerships","the introduction of innovative insurance products can be done through public-private-civil society sector partnerships",""],[1,"264","34","Credit Database Development and Regulatory Framework Update","Develop, enhance, and promote the use of credit database Adopt regulatory framework and policies that remain relevant amidst innovation and digitalization",""],[1,"269","2","Credit Database and Financial Data Sharing Framework","The government will promote the use of credit databases; develop frameworks and tools for collecting and sharing the financial data of agriculture-related firms, MSMEs and cooperatives for credit evaluation; fully operationalize the movable collateral registry system; and promote the secure sharing of financial data among stakeholders.",""],[1,"269","2","Warehouse Receipts Law Implementation","The passage of the Warehouse Receipts law can significantly enhance MSMEs' access to short-term financing, including value-chain financing for exports and agriculture.",""],[1,"269","2","Credible Registry for Borrowers and Lenders","The government will establish a credible registry to increase the participation of both borrowers and lenders, raise liquidity, and allow greater access to financing by MSME borrowers and more investment outlets for retail investors.",""],[1,"269","3","Open Finance Promotion and Oversight Mechanism","The government, through the Open Finance Oversight Committee, shall promote non-discriminatory membership by ensuring that key areas of interest of the financial industry are adequately represented",""],[1,"269","4","Tiered Open Finance Implementation Approach","the BSP intends to approach the implementation in a tiered manner (e.g., by data sensitivity, data type, and data holder type) to ensure that risk spillovers are mitigated and benefits of open finance are optimized.",""],[1,"271","15","Warehouse Receipt System Overhaul and Online Registry","This will overhaul the present warehouse receipt system and provide an online registry system where all electronic warehouse receipts can be registered and accessed.",""]],"134":[[1,"191","44","Consumer Interest Group Formation","Encourage creation of consumer interest groups",""],[1,"194","7","Cybersecurity Legal and Information Security Standards Framework","Adopt a legal framework to strengthen cybersecurity and policies on minimum information security standards to protect critical information infrastructure and the ICT systems of public institutions, transportation, and e-commerce transactions, and increase capacity of the private sector to mitigate piracy of creative outputs.",""],[1,"194","8","Financial Consumer Protection Act Implementation","Implement the Financial Consumer Protection Act that better enables financial regulators to address consumer complaints on cybercrimes and enforce sanctions against erring entities.",""],[1,"195","2","Secure E-Payment and Online Consumer Protection System","Establish secure e-payment systems and ensure consumer and supplier protection online to promote trust and confidence in the digital uptake.",""],[1,"195","3","Cybersecurity Awareness and Culture Promotion","Promote cybersecurity culture.",""],[1,"195","4","Consumer Interest Group Formation","Encourage creation of consumer interest groups",""],[1,"195","5","Community Participation and Competition Promotion Partnerships","Expand the participation of communities in promoting competition in services through coalition-building, alliances, and partnerships.",""],[1,"195","6","Consumer and Producer Rights Protection and Dispute Resolution Reform","Promote consumer and producer rights protection by streamlining processes for resolution of disputes and complaints that may be related to defective goods, fraud, cybercrime, payment security issues, and security of websites.",""],[1,"200","16","E-commerce Regulatory Framework","The bill aims to define the scope and coverage of internet transactions, apart from the sale or exchange of digital products, and lay down the code of conduct and qualifications for businesses who wish to engage in e-commerce.",""],[1,"200","16","E-commerce Bureau for Consumer Complaints","It also proposes the creation of an E-commerce Bureau to handle complaints on internet transactions, protect consumer rights, and facilitate the speedy resolution of complaints, among others.",""]],"135":[[1,"375","1","Cross-Sectoral Climate and Disaster Risk Management Framework","the government will strengthen cross-sectoral convergence and coordination and implement a comprehensive risk management approach to reduce intersecting vulnerabilities and address complexities in managing the compounding and cascading risks posed by climate change across different sectors.",""],[1,"375","1","Climate and Disaster Resilience Governance Improvement","improved governance will underpin the country's collective effort to ensure long-term climate and disaster resilience.",""],[1,"375","3","National Climate and Disaster Risk Management Planning","Plans and guidelines have also been formulated to better manage climate and disaster risks, including the National Climate Risk Management",""],[1,"375","4","National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Planning Framework","National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Plan (NDRRMP) 2020-2030, and Guidelines for Mainstreaming Disaster Risk Reduction (DRR) and Climate Change Adaptation (CCA) in the Comprehensive Development Plan.",""],[1,"378","4","Climate and Disaster Risk Governance and Resilience Strategy","The strategies discussed below aim to achieve the following outcomes: (a) climate and disaster risk resilience of communities and institutions increased; (b) ecosystem resilience enhanced; and (c) low carbon economy transition enabled.",""],[1,"379","16","Whole-of-Society All-Hazard Adaptation Framework","The operationalization of the above framework will require a whole-of-society and all-hazard approaches where the knowledge and capacity of academic institutions, non-government or civil society organizations, and vulnerable groups are harnessed or enabled by increased public investment.",""],[1,"379","18","Climate and Disaster Resilience Strengthening","The government will foster the resilience of communities and institutions through improved public-private-community engagements, increased public awareness and understanding of risk and vulnerability, and strengthened implementation of National Climate Risk Management Framework.",""],[1,"380","4","Multistakeholder Knowledge Partnership for Climate Adaptation and Disaster Risk Reduction","Boost multistakeholder partnership in building and translating knowledge to climate change adaptation and disaster risk reduction",""],[1,"380","5","Local Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Research Collaboration","The National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council (NDRRMC) and the Climate Change Commission (CCC) will collaborate with the private sector and academic institutions in (a) conducting local",""],[1,"380","6","Climate Change and DRR Integration in Education","enhancing the integration of climate change and DRR in the education system.",""],[1,"380","6","Access to Climate Resilience Financing Facilities","These strategies will help LGUs better access available financing facilities (e.g., People's Survival Fund) for building community resilience.",""],[1,"380","7","Private Sector ESG Alignment Support","Private sector partners will be supported in aligning their respective ESG8 targets and investments (e.g., corporate social responsibility programs) with local priorities and targets on CCA and DRR to efficiently allocate limited resources toward building resilience.",""],[1,"380","7","SDG Stakeholders' Chambers Coordination Platform","The SDG Stakeholders' Chambers under the Sub-committee on Sustainable Development Goals of the Development Budget Coordination Committee of the NEDA Board (DBCC SC-SDG) will be utilized as platform for discussing the rationalization of these efforts.",""],[1,"380","7","Sustainability and ESG Reporting Capacity Building","To enable accounting of contributions to broader sustainability goals, the DBCC SC-SDG will conduct capacity building programs on sustainability and/or ESG reporting for the members of the SDG Stakeholders' Chambers and other stakeholders.",""],[1,"385","1","Cross-cutting Climate and Disaster Resilience Measures","Cross-cutting measures will be pursued to enable the implementation of strategies aimed at ensuring resilient communities, institutions, and ecosystems, and fostering a low-carbon economy.",""],[1,"385","2","Update National Climate Change Strategy and Action Plan","The National Framework Strategy on Climate Change and National Climate Change Action Plan (NCCAP) will be updated, and the National Adaptation Plan will be completed based on the latest climate science and aligned with the country's commitments under the 2015 Paris Agreement.",""],[1,"387","15","Institutionalization of the National Climate Assessment","This bill aims to enable greater stakeholder engagement and sustain budgetary support for the implementation of NCA activities at the national and subnational levels.",""],[1,"389","1","Climate Risk Management Coordination Framework","Provides the framework for harmonizing and integrating efforts of various sectors and stakeholders on climate risk management and strengthening the country's early action system in view of the increasing losses and damages from recurring extreme weather events.",""],[1,"397","3","Climate Change, Adaptation, Mitigation, and Disaster Risk Reduction Cluster","the acceleration of climate action and disaster resilience (Chapter 15: Accelerate Climate Action and Strengthen Disaster Resilience) will be steered by the Cluster on Climate Change, Adaptation, Mitigation, and Disaster Risk Reduction",""],[1,"431","23","Climate Risk Management Coordination Framework","Framework for harmonizing and integrating efforts of various sectors and stakeholders on climate risk management, and strengthening the country's early action system in view of the increasing losses and damages from recurring extreme weather events.",""]],"136":[[1,"102","14","Digital Platform Promotion and Adoption Initiative","Ramp up the promotion and use of digital platforms for marketing, delivery, and payment transactions",""],[1,"105","1","Expansion of Online Food Access Platforms","Thus, efforts will be pursued to expand these online platforms, especially in areas outside of the National Capital Region, and ensure that stakeholders (e.g., consumers, producers, and food businesses) can easily access these platforms (See Chapter 5).",""]],"137":[[1,"100","5","Nutrition Service Delivery Continuity Guidelines","To mitigate the pandemic's impact, the Nutrition Cluster issued guidelines in 2020 to ensure the continued provision of nutrition service delivery during the pandemic and in any future emergencies.",""],[1,"101","1","School Feeding Program Institutionalization","the Masustansyang Pagkain para sa Batang Pilipino Act (RA 11037),11 which institutionalizes the feeding programs of the DSWD and Department of Education (DepEd)","Department of Social Welfare and Development | Department of Education"],[1,"102","20","Nutrition Prevention and Treatment Measures","Implement measures to prevent and address wasting, stunting, and obesity",""],[1,"102","21","Nutrition-Specific, Nutrition-Sensitive, and Enabling Interventions","Strengthen nutrition-specific, nutrition-sensitive, and enabling interventions especially at the local level",""],[1,"107","3","Nutrition Malnutrition Prevention and Response Measures","Implement measures to prevent and address wasting, stunting, and obesity",""],[1,"107","4","Integrated Nutrition Services Convergence","The government shall promote the convergence of services to counter the causes of the triple burden of malnutrition.",""],[1,"107","5","Emergency Coverage for Critical First 1,000 Days Services","services critical to the first 1,000 days of life will be ensured especially during emergencies.",""],[1,"107","6","Nutrition-Specific, Nutrition-Sensitive, and Enabling Interventions","Strengthen nutrition-specific, nutrition-sensitive, and enabling interventions especially at the local level",""],[1,"107","7","First 1,000 Days Nutrition and Health Interventions","LGUs, in coordination with the DOH and National Nutrition Council (NNC), will ensure that appropriate nutrition and health-related interventions and services will be given during the first 1,000 days of life, which includes pregnancy and the infant's first two years of life.","DOH | National Nutrition Council (NNC)"],[1,"107","8","Nutrition-Specific Interventions Fortification","Implementation of nutrition-specific interventions shall be fortified, such as the Infant and Young Child Feeding, Philippine Integrated Management of Acute Malnutrition, National Dietary Supplementation Program,25 National Nutrition Promotion Program for Behavior Change, Micronutrient Supplementation,26 Mandatory Food Fortification, Nutrition in Emergencies, and Overweight and Obesity Management and Prevention Program.",""],[1,"116","7","Nutritious Food Provision for Disaster Victims and Feeding Program Beneficiaries","The government shall ensure that food provided to victims of disasters and beneficiaries of supplemental and school feeding programs are healthy, nutritious, and appropriate for their physical conditions and life stages.",""],[1,"117","5","Nationwide Child Nutrition Programs","Nutrition programs implemented nationwide shall also be sustained to reduce the stunting and wasting of children.",""],[1,"122","25","Milk Feeding and Supplementary Nutrition Program","Milk feeding program to community and school-based children, nourishment of pregnant women (e.g., Tutok Kainan), and day care and school children supplementation program, among others.",""],[1,"122","26","Micronutrient Supplementation Programme","Micronutrient supplementation for all under-five and school children, including pregnant and lactating women, among others.",""]],"138":[[1,"102","25","Nutrition Governance Strengthening in Local Government Units","Improve nutrition governance especially in local government units",""],[1,"108","2","Nutrition Governance Strengthening in Local Government Units","Improve nutrition governance especially in local government units",""],[1,"108","3","Horizontal and Vertical Coordination for Intervention Convergence","Convergence of interventions, through horizontal and vertical coordination, will",""],[1,"108","4","Barangay Nutrition Scholar Program Strengthening","nutrition governance will be improved by strengthening barangay nutrition scholar programs",""],[1,"108","4","Local Government Nutrition Office Establishment","establishing LGU nutrition offices",""],[1,"108","4","Local Nutrition Committee and Worker Capacity Strengthening","enhancing the functionality of all local nutrition committees and capacities of local nutrition workers",""],[1,"108","4","National-Local Nutrition Coordination System Strengthening","strengthening the coordination system between the national and local government through the NNC",""],[1,"108","13","Strengthening Barangay Nutrition Scholars","Amendment of Presidential Decree 1569 or Strengthening Barangay Nutrition Scholars (BNS]",""],[1,"108","14","BNS Qualification, Incentives, and Tenure Reform","The amendment will upgrade the qualification standards, incentives, and benefits, and ensure the security of tenure of BNS.",""],[1,"108","15","Establishment of Local Government Unit Nutrition Offices","Establishment of LGU nutrition offices",""],[1,"108","16","Nutrition Office Staffing and Local Nutrition Focal Point Deployment","The presence of a Nutrition Office with adequate and competent staff complement will ensure that local governments have nutrition focal persons on the ground for nutrition programs to be properly implemented and able to benefit the targeted beneficiaries, especially the vulnerable and high-risk groups.",""],[1,"122","6","Health Subcluster for Disaster Risk Reduction and Management","This is composed of partner agencies from government, the United Nations, and non-government organizations (NGO), which guides the implementation and monitoring of programmatic measures to reduce nutrition- related mortality and morbidity because of emergencies (like COVID-19) and impact of disasters on public health, economy, and social aspects.",""],[1,"122","8","Multi-Sectoral Hunger and Malnutrition Eradication Movement","A multi-sectoral movement founded to help eradicate hunger and malnutrition in the Philippines by 2030.",""]],"139":[[1,"63","3","Industrial Trans Fat Ban","The proposed measure will ban all forms of industrial trans fatty acids; prohibit the sale, manufacture, importation, and distribution of partially hydrogenated oils and oil and fats with high trans-fat acid content.",""],[1,"102","13","Whole-of-Society Healthy Lifestyle Promotion","Adopt a whole-of-society approach in promoting healthy lifestyle and a culture of active health-seeking behavior among Filipinos across age groups and income classes",""],[1,"106","5","Whole-of-Society Healthy Lifestyle Promotion","Adopt a whole-of-society approach in promoting healthy lifestyle and a culture of active health-seeking behavior among Filipinos across age groups and income classes",""],[1,"106","6","Multi-sectoral Nutrition and Healthy Lifestyle Promotion","Multi-sectoral approaches and enabling environments for nutrition will be fostered across all life stages and consumer groups (e.g., Muslims, Christians, and Buddhists).",""],[1,"106","6","Healthy Lifestyle and Nutrition Literacy Promotion","Promotion of a healthy lifestyle (e.g., dietary diversity guided by Pinggang Pinoy22 by age group) will first improve nutrition and health literacy, and second, promote health-seeking behavior among Filipinos.",""],[1,"106","6","Social and Behavior Change Communication for Nutrition","Social and behavior change and communication for nutrition should be advocated at the individual, community, environmental, and structural levels to improve outcomes.",""],[1,"106","7","Nutrition Information, Education, and Communication Campaign","with other stakeholders (e.g., private sector, non-government organizations [NGOs], and development partners), shall intensify IEC activities that emphasize the benefits of eating nutritious food.",""],[1,"107","5","Healthy Eating and Lifestyle Promotion Initiative","The promotion of healthy eating environments and healthy lifestyles shall also be strengthened to manage and prevent malnutrition and obesity.",""],[1,"108","18","School Food Marketing Restriction Law","This proposed law prohibits selling, promoting, marketing, or advertising unhealthy foods or junk foods and sugary drinks within 100 meters of school premises in all public and private preparatory, elementary, and junior and senior high schools.",""],[1,"122","17","Malnutrition Cause Identification and Vulnerability Assessment Tool","A program and tool by the National Nutrition Council (NNC), which aims to identify causes of malnutrition and vulnerable people.","National Nutrition Council (NNC)"]],"140":[[1,"99","1","Food Supply Diversification and Price Stabilization Measures","This will be pursued by diversifying food supply sources, strengthening buffer stocks for emergencies, optimizing digital platforms for the marketing and delivery of food, and proactively monitoring the supply and demand for key commodities.",""],[1,"101","1","Pilipinas Kontra Gutom Campaign Implementation","spearheaded the implementation of the Pilipinas Kontra Gutom campaign","Department of Social Welfare and Development"],[1,"101","1","Enhanced Partnership Against Hunger and Poverty Program","the Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD) pursued convergence projects with other agencies through the Enhanced Partnership Against Hunger and Poverty Program","Department of Social Welfare and Development"],[1,"102","1","Food Security and Nutrition Supply and Access Measures","To ensure food security and proper nutrition of Filipino families and their members, concerted efforts of the government, private sector, and other stakeholders will be geared toward (a) attaining sufficient and stable supply of food commodities; (b) expanding access of",""],[1,"102","11","Diversification of Food Supply Sources","Diversify food supply sources by augmenting domestic supply through international trade and maximizing the use of non-traditional agricultural areas",""],[1,"102","12","Private Investment in Food Logistics and Distribution Facilities","Promote private investment in facilities, transport, and logistics systems to bring safe and nutritious food closer to consumers",""],[1,"102","15","Food Transportation and Distribution Improvement","Improve food transportation and distribution processes to hasten and ensure unhampered movement of food products",""],[1,"102","17","Trade Regulatory Measures Streamlining and Improvement","Streamline and improve the implementation of trade regulatory measures",""],[1,"102","19","Food Commodity Price and Supply Monitoring","Strengthen price and supply monitoring of food commodities",""],[1,"103","3","Food Supply Diversification through Trade and Non-Traditional Agriculture","Diversify food supply sources by augmenting domestic supply through international trade and maximizing the use of non-traditional agricultural areas",""],[1,"103","4","Temporary Tariff Reduction and Minimum Access Expansion","The temporary and short-term reduction of tariffs and expansion of minimum access volume shall be pursued to complement insufficient local production of food commodities, especially when disasters and other shocks (e.g., Russia-Ukraine conflict, pandemic, and transboundary animal diseases) occur.",""],[1,"103","4","Commodity Supply-Demand Forecasting and Monitoring System","To assess the necessity of such measures, the government shall proactively monitor and enhance supply-demand forecasting of key commodities (e.g., rice, meat, fish, vegetables, and sugar) to anticipate possible shortages.",""],[1,"103","4","Anticipatory Food Supply Response Mechanism","An anticipatory mechanism will facilitate the timely implementation of appropriate measures to enhance domestic supply and forestall the sudden or sharp uptick in domestic food prices.",""],[1,"104","5","Private Investment in Food Logistics and Distribution Facilities","Promote private investment in facilities, transport, and logistics systems to bring safe and nutritious food closer to consumers",""],[1,"105","2","Food Transportation and Distribution Improvement","Improve food transportation and distribution processes to hasten and ensure unhampered movement of food products",""],[1,"105","3","Food Transport Coordination and Logistics Facilitation Measures","Coordination among government agencies (e.g., DA, Department of Trade and Industry [DTI], and LGUs) in the transportation and delivery of food products shall be further strengthened.","DA | Department of Trade and Industry [DTI] | LGUs"],[1,"105","4","Strengthened Goods Delivery Programs","The DTI and DA, in collaboration with LGUs, manufacturers, and distributors, shall strengthen the implementation of programs that facilitate the delivery of goods to consumers such as Kadiwa ni Ani at Kita,","DTI | DA"],[1,"105","6","Mobile and Web-Based Price Monitoring Applications Expansion","The DA and DTI shall expand the use of mobile- and web-based price monitoring applications such as DA's Bantay Presyo Ni Ani at Kita14 and DTI's e-Presyo.15","DA | DTI"],[1,"105","6","Reactivation of Local Price Coordinating Councils","Furthermore, the Local Price Coordinating Councils (LPCC)16 in each province or municipality shall be reactivated through the issuance of Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG) memorandum circular.","Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG)"],[1,"105","7","Food Security Monitoring Tools Strengthening","existing tools that help monitor the food security status of the country shall be continued and strengthened to better guide the formulation and implementation of programs (e.g., Local Nutrition Early Warning System17 and Integrated Food Security Phase Classification18).",""],[1,"105","7","Food Supply and Demand Dashboard","A dashboard that links supply- (e.g., areas where commodities are planted and expected volume of production) and demand-side information (e.g., volume of food requirements per area) shall also be created (See Chapter 5).",""],[1,"106","1","Consumer Price Monitoring and Enforcement","The DA and DTI, in coordination with LGUs and accredited consumer groups, shall also intensify monitoring and enforcement activities to protect consumers from price manipulation and ensure that prices of basic necessities like rice and prime commodities are kept within reasonable levels.","DA | DTI"],[1,"122","15","Online Price Monitoring System","The Online Price Monitoring System of the DTI where consumers can check the prevailing prices of necessities and prime commodities that DTI is monitoring.","DTI"]],"141":[[1,"113","12","Disability Cost Cash Grants","Establish cash grants to cover disability costs and fully implement the mandatory membership and exclusive package in PhilHealth",""],[1,"116","8","Disability Cash Grant Support","Establish cash grants to cover disability costs",""],[1,"116","8","PhilHealth Mandatory Membership and Exclusive Package Implementation","fully implement the mandatory membership and exclusive package in the social health insurance program (PhilHealth) (RA 11288)",""],[1,"116","9","Disability Support Allowance and PhilHealth Coverage Expansion","The government shall provide disability support allowance to persons with disability to enable them to defray part of the costs incurred due to their special conditions.",""],[1,"120","18","Cash Subsidy for Households with Persons with Disabilities","The bill seeks to grant a cash subsidy to supplement incomes of households with persons with disability.",""]],"142":[[1,"113","14","Coordination and Collaboration Strengthening Mechanism","Further strengthen coordination and collaboration among NDRRMC, CCC, LGUs, and the private/CSOs",""],[1,"113","15","Integration of Safeguards into Development Interventions","Integrate safeguards into development interventions",""],[1,"113","33","SP Communication Plan and Strategy","Implement an SP Communication Plan and Strategy",""],[1,"113","35","Stakeholder Synergy for Program Design and Delivery","Create synergies among stakeholders in designing and delivering programs",""],[1,"115","3","Whole-of-Society Social Protection Initiative Support","The national government shall encourage and promote similar initiatives to reach more people in need.",""],[1,"120","2","Built-in Safety Nets for Development Projects and Reform Policies","the government shall continue to ensure built-in safety nets with adequate financing in such projects to compensate for or mitigate the impacts of such projects and policies on affected sectors.",""],[1,"138","9","Government-Industry Association Participation for Employment and Skills Policy Implementation","Actively participate in government-industry associations promoting and implementing employment and skills development policies and strategies",""],[1,"139","9","Inter-Agency Council for Jobs and Investments","Create an Inter-Agency Council for Jobs and Investments co-headed by the Department of Trade and Industry, Department of Labor and Employment [DOLE), and TESDA, with representatives from employers' organizations and labor groups; and establish working groups that will focus on developing employment recovery and job creation in specific industries and emerging sectors, such as but not limited, to construction, tourism, agriculture, information technology and business process management, and manufacturing.","Department of Trade and Industry | Department of Labor and Employment | TESDA"]],"143":[[1,"82","13","Housing Needs Resource Mobilization","Mobilize private sector and government resources to meet housing needs",""],[1,"82","18","Affordable Housing Access Expansion","Increase access of informal settler families, homeless, and underprivileged to housing",""],[1,"86","4","Housing Needs Resource Mobilization","Mobilize private sector and government resources to meet housing needs",""],[1,"86","5","Annual Housing Finance Mobilization for One Million Units","The Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development (DHSUD) targets the financing of one million housing units annually to narrow the housing deficit.","Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development (DHSUD)"],[1,"86","6","Fiscal Incentive Facilitation for Socialized Housing","Availment of fiscal incentives under the Urban Development and Housing Act (RA 7279) shall be facilitated to encourage more private sector participation in socialized housing.",""],[1,"86","6","Rationalization of Shelter Agency Funding","Allocation of funds to key shelter agencies (KSA) (e.g., NHA, Socialized Housing Finance Corporation, and the National Home Mortgage Finance Corporation [NHMFC]) will be rationalized to ensure that increased allocation is matched with increased absorptive capacities.",""],[1,"86","6","NHMFC Secondary Mortgage Market Program Strengthening","The secondary mortgage market program of the NHMFC shall be strengthened",""],[1,"87","1","Housing Credit Guarantee Program Enhancement","the housing credit guarantee programs of the Philippine Guarantee Corporation shall be enhanced.",""],[1,"87","1","Local Government Housing Financing Schemes","LGUs shall tap financing schemes available to them such as bond flotation and credit financing to raise funds for housing.",""],[1,"87","3","Housing Affordability Subsidy Measures","Subsidies in the form of mortgage financing, direct housing production, and community-driven development will be continued to ensure housing affordability.",""],[1,"87","3","Additional Subsidies for ISFs Study","Additional subsidies for ISFs will be studied to improve affordability of housing for this segment of the population.",""],[1,"87","4","Rental Subsidy Support for Low-Income Families","Rental subsidy will be an option for low-income ISFs and starting families, or as support for families that may be temporarily displaced by",""],[1,"87","5","Alternative Tenure Options for Public Housing Rental","Other forms of tenure will also be explored to address uncertainties and make public housing rental viable.",""],[1,"91","5","Housing Land Availability Reform","Address suitable land availability constraints for housing development by legislating options such as removing the Comprehensive Agrarian Reform Program [CARP) restrictions to land consolidation while maintaining land ownership by beneficiaries, completing inventory of protected areas to ascertain land for development, and tapping idle or unutilized private lands.",""],[1,"91","8","Affordable Housing Access Improvement","Improve access to and affordability of housing especially for the informal settler families, homeless, and underprivileged",""],[1,"91","10","National Housing Authority Charter Renewal and Mandate Expansion","Renew the NHA Charter and strengthen its organizational structure and functions.",""]],"144":[[1,"59","7","Human Resources for Health Welfare and Supply Expansion","This is done by providing standardized and competitive compensation, protection, benefits, and incentives and ensuring gender equality in the health workforce.",""],[1,"59","7","Needs-Based Human Resources for Health Forecasting","Needs-based HRH forecasting and production approaches will be applied, in cooperation with the Commission on Higher Education (CHED), the Professional Regulation Commission, and health professional organizations.","Commission on Higher Education (CHED) | Professional Regulation Commission"],[1,"59","7","Clinical Rotation Partnerships and Scholarship Expansion","Partner institutions for clinical rotations and expanded scholarships and training fellowships with return service agreements will also help increase HRH supply.",""]],"145":[[1,"351","3","Strengthening the CHR as a National Human Rights Institution","This will strengthen the CHR as a National Human Rights Institution, compliant with the requirements of the United Nations Paris Principles, United Nations Convention against Torture, and Optional Protocol to the Convention Against Torture.",""],[1,"423","10","Online Video-Calling System for Inmates","An online video-calling system that aims to give the inmates who are visitorless, especially those who are indigent, sick and/or aged the opportunity to communicate with and see family members.",""],[1,"425","14","Sentence Reduction Incentive for Compliance in Detention Facilities","An act that allows for a reduction of sentences of persons deprived of liberty, depending on how well they abide by rules and regulations inside any penal institution, rehabilitation, or detention center or any other local jail.",""]],"146":[[1,"216","18","Self-Reliant Defense Posture Strengthening Program","Providing for the Development of a National Defense Industry through the Strengthening and Revitalizing of the Self-Reliant Defense Posture (SRDP) Program, Incentivizing In- country Enterprises, Rationalizing Defense Acquisition, and Creating the Office of the Undersecretary for Defense Technology Research and Industry Development under the Department of National Defense, and Providing Funds therefor","Department of National Defense"],[1,"216","19","SRDP Program Revitalization","The bill aims to revitalize the SRDP Program, incentivize in-country enterprises, rationalize defense acquisition, and create the Office of the Undersecretary for Defense Technology Research and Industry Development under the Department of National Defense.","Department of National Defense"],[1,"216","19","In-Country Enterprise Incentive Measures","The bill aims to revitalize the SRDP Program, incentivize in-country enterprises, rationalize defense acquisition, and create the Office of the Undersecretary for Defense Technology Research and Industry Development under the Department of National Defense.","Department of National Defense"],[1,"216","19","Defense Acquisition Rationalization Reform","The bill aims to revitalize the SRDP Program, incentivize in-country enterprises, rationalize defense acquisition, and create the Office of the Undersecretary for Defense Technology Research and Industry Development under the Department of National Defense.","Department of National Defense"],[1,"216","19","Office of the Undersecretary for Defense Technology Research and Industry Development","The bill aims to revitalize the SRDP Program, incentivize in-country enterprises, rationalize defense acquisition, and create the Office of the Undersecretary for Defense Technology Research and Industry Development under the Department of National Defense.","Department of National Defense"],[1,"438","18","National Defense Industry Development","The development of a national defense industry by incentivizing in-country enterprises and rationalizing defense acquisition.",""]],"147":[[1,"301","16","Integrated Master-Planning Development and Convergence Programs","Implement integrated master-planning development and covergence programs",""],[1,"301","17","Transport and Digital Infrastructure Modernization and Expansion","Move people, goods, and information through modernized and expanded transport and digital infrastructure",""],[1,"302","1","Infrastructure Master Plan Harmonization and Integration","master plan formulation for infrastructure will be harmonized and strategically integrated to guide the planning, programming, budgeting, and implementation of infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"302","1","Government Master Planning Coordination Reform","The different government master planning processes will be enhanced and rationalized to ensure that master plans are coordinated across all government levels, and remain synergistic, responsive to the emerging issues and consistent with priority development strategies of the sector.",""],[1,"302","2","Infrastructure Convergence Programs","the government will continue to implement convergence programs to ensure complementarity of efforts in the roll out of infrastructure identified in sectoral or spatial master plans.",""],[1,"302","3","Devolution of Local Infrastructure Planning and Development","Over a reasonable transition period, the responsibilities for local infrastructure planning and development will be fully devolved to local governments.",""],[1,"302","3","Capacity Building for Local Infrastructure Governance","Capacities of local governments to assume the responsibility and accountability for infrastructure outcomes within their jurisdictions will be built.",""],[1,"303","7","Transport and Digital Infrastructure Modernization and Expansion","Move people, goods and information through modernized and expanded transport and digital infrastructure, with active participation of the private sector",""],[1,"303","8","National Transportation Master Plan Formulation and Adoption","A National Transportation Master Plan will be formulated and adopted.",""],[1,"303","9","Integrated Land Use and Urban Planning for Intermodal Transport Network Development","will integrate land use and urban planning methodologies (e.g., transit-oriented development, township approach, and high-density development), will guide the rational development of an intermodal transport infrastructure network that takes into consideration compatibility, economic feasibility, comparative advantages, climate",""]],"148":[[1,"278","6","Public-Private Partnership Projects","The expertise and efficiency of the private sector will increasingly be harnessed through PPP projects.",""],[1,"278","6","Private Sector Co-Ownership Partnerships","Partnerships will encourage the private sector to co-own the responsibilities of fostering development.",""],[1,"278","6","Sustainable Funding for Infrastructure and Service Delivery","PPPs will ensure that infrastructure development and service delivery will have a sustainable funding source.",""],[1,"278","7","PPP Project Development Framework","The Congress is currently deliberating on a bill that aims to develop PPP projects that are well-structured and are consistent with development goals and the climate change agenda.",""],[1,"278","7","Build-Operate-Transfer Law IRR Revision","Further, the revision of the implementing rules and regulations (IRR) of the Build-Operate-Transfer Law will reflect best investment policies and practices.",""],[1,"301","29","Partnerships for Investment Financing","Undertake partnerships for financing investments",""],[1,"303","2","Sustained Public Infrastructure Financing","Over the next Plan implementation period, annual spending on infrastructure will be sustained at 5 percent to 6 percent of GDP.",""],[1,"303","2","Infrastructure Financing Mechanism Mobilization","the government will continue to tap viable funding mechanisms to augment the public resources in financing critical infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"303","3","Public-Private Partnership Financing for Priority Infrastructure Projects","By leveraging the private sector's efficiency, resources, expertise, and innovativeness, the government can reinvigorate PPPs in financing priority infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"303","5","Strategic Engagement with Development Partners for External Financing","The government will continue to strategically engage multilateral and bilateral development partners for external financing to capitalize on their comparative advantages and benefit from knowledge and technology transfers.",""],[1,"303","6","Technical Assistance and Service Delivery Standards for LGUs","the national government will assist LGUs by providing technical assistance and setting service delivery standards.",""],[1,"303","6","Cost-Sharing Arrangements for Devolved Infrastructure Projects","Together with LGUs, the national government will explore appropriate cost-sharing arrangements in the implementation of devolved infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"303","6","LGU PPP Capacity-Building Support","LGU capacity to prepare and structure PPPs will also be improved.",""],[1,"317","1","Priority Bills for Infrastructure Expansion and Upgrading","Table 12.2 presents priority bills of the 19th Congress during the Plan period to expand and upgrade infrastructure.",""],[1,"317","5","Build-Operate-Transfer Law Amendment for PPP Reform","This amends the Build-Operate-Transfer (BOT] Law to enhance the principal framework governing PPPs in the Philippines by fostering a more competitive and enabling environment for PPPs, addressing the ambiguities in the existing law, and addressing the bottlenecks and challenges affecting the PPP program.",""],[1,"317","8","Right-of-Way Acquisition Reform","This will address difficulties in complying with the law's strict requirements (such as valuation, compensation and expropriation problems) and further expedite the implementation of infrastructure projects; to provide clearer, fairer, and simpler terms for ROW acquisition for both property owners and the government.",""]],"149":[[1,"301","22","Equitable Health and Education Infrastructure Access Partnership","Ensure equitable access to health and education infrastructure, in partnership with the private sector",""],[1,"301","35","Social Infrastructure Financing","Invest in or provide financing for social infrastructure",""]],"150":[[1,"315","8","Local Site Identification for Resilient Public Facilities","LGUs will identify locations within their jurisdiction for health facilities, school buildings and evacuation centers taking into consideration not only accessibility and demand, but also long-term resilience to natural and anthropogenic hazards and risks, including those associated with climate change.",""],[1,"316","1","Disaster-Resilient Health and School Facility Upgrading","National and local government funding, coupled with multi-sectoral partnerships, will be pursued to adequately provide for the construction, retrofitting, and repair of health facilities and schools; to better withstand the impact of hazards and calamities; and to minimize disruption of services or classes.",""],[1,"316","1","Permanent Disaster-Resilient Evacuation Centers","In every LGU there will be permanent disaster-resilient evacuation centers, equipped with adequate Gender Equality, Disability and Social Inclusion (GEDSI)-responsive basic facilities constructed for families displaced during emergencies.",""]],"151":[[1,"152","4","Climate-Smart Irrigation Technology Investment","investing in climate-smart irrigation technologies (e.g., solar-powered irrigation systems, drip irrigation, and water-efficient varieties of crops);",""],[1,"153","1","Flexible and Durable Irrigation Systems Development","designing and managing flexible and durable irrigation systems for different farming systems",""],[1,"153","1","Rainwater Harvesting Incentive Scheme","incentivizing rainwater harvesting",""],[1,"153","1","Household and Community Wastewater Recycling for Irrigation","recycling domestic water for irrigation purposes at household and community levels",""],[1,"158","3","National Land Use Framework","This is to establish a national land use framework that will [a] define the indicative priorities for land utilization and allocation across residential, infrastructure, agricultural, and protective uses; [b] integrate efforts, monitor developments related to land use; and (c) evolve policies, regulations, and directions of land use planning processes.",""],[1,"158","11","Sustainable Land Management Promotion Programme","This aims to promote the adoption and implementation of Sustainable Land Management programs, projects, and activities for further prevention of land degradation through various soil and water conservation technologies and approaches, including rainwater harvesting.",""],[1,"309","8","Smart Irrigation Monitoring for Upland Rice","Inefficient irrigation water utilization especially for upland rice production may be addressed with \"smart monitoring\" of soil moisture conditions to optimize irrigation scheduling, and by timing the cropping season according to type of water calendar, which is location-specific in the country",""],[1,"310","2","Dam Safety Regulation and Monitoring Framework","Dam safety measures shall be prescribed and operations shall be stringently monitored.",""],[1,"310","2","Dam Safety Body Establishment","A dam safety body shall be created through executive action, with the goal of ensuring that all dams are safely operated, thereby protecting lives and property particularly in times of extreme weather events.",""]],"152":[[1,"311","8","Bureaucratic Process Rationalization and Local-Central Coordination Reform","The government will rationalize bureaucratic processes and removelocal-central government impasse when undertaking investments in",""],[1,"312","1","LGU Energy Code Convergent Framework for Energy Projects","The LGU Energy Code42 also espouses a convergent framework to facilitate putting-up energy projects.",""],[1,"312","1","Ease of Doing Business and Energy Virtual One-Stop Shop","The passage of the Ease of Doing Business and the Energy Virtual One-stop Shop43 are promising ways forward.",""],[1,"312","1","Review of Permit-Issuing Agency Practices","However, the implementation and practices of the various permit-issuing agencies will be reviewed to ensure the realization of the law's true intent.",""]],"153":[[1,"318","12","NEA Mandate Enhancement and Streamlining","This is to enhance and streamline the mandate of NEA to ensure quality, reliability, and security of electric power supply.",""],[1,"318","13","Energy Regulatory Commission Strengthening","Enhance Energy Regulatory Commission (ERC]",""]],"154":[[1,"312","3","Off-Grid Electrification and Grid Connection Programme","Energy will be delivered to consumers in off-grid or missionary areas.",""],[1,"312","3","Private Sector Participation in Off-Grid Energy Development","Enhancing private sector participation is a strategy that needs to be reinforced and strengthened.",""],[1,"324","7","Off-Grid Electrification and Regulatory Support","This includes off-grid electrification, Renewable Portfolio Standards for off-grid, and omnibus guidelines in enhancing off-grid power development.",""]],"155":[[1,"176","7","Industry 4.0 Roadmap Implementation","Implement Industry 4.0 roadmaps.","DTI | DOST"],[1,"177","1","AI Roadmap and Center for AI R&D","One example of such 4IR roadmaps that could be implemented is the AI Roadmap. It provides for the establishment of the Center for AI R&D.",""],[1,"177","2","Industry 4.0 Pilot Factory and Facilities","Build Industry 4.0 facilities.","DTI | DOST"],[1,"177","3","Smart Industry Readiness Index Project","Through the Smart Industry Readiness Index17 project, the government will support firms and industries that are shifting to new technologies by providing deeper awareness and understanding of digital transformation, assisting firms in their technology readiness assessment and guiding firms in crafting their firm-level Industry 4.0 roadmaps.",""],[1,"177","4","Soft Loans and Technical Assistance for Firm Resilience","Provide soft loans or technical assistance.",""],[1,"177","5","Industry 4.0 Sandbox","Create the Industry 4.0 Sandbox.",""],[1,"177","6","Skills Development Investment and Workforce Reskilling","Tapping these benefits will require increasing investments in skills development, along with greater efforts by companies to upskill or reskill",""],[1,"177","6","Company-Led Upskilling and Reskilling Initiative","greater efforts by companies to upskill or reskill",""],[1,"180","4","Industry Roadmap Updating for Innovation and 4IR Adoption","Thus, the updating of industry roadmaps, with focus on innovation measures, and skills & competencies critical to the industries for 4IR technology adoption and sustainable manufacturing, will be undertaken by DTI and DOST.","DTI | DOST"],[1,"417","16","AMERIAL Technology-Based Manufacturing Support Facility","AMERIAL serves as a complementary facility that makes enabling technology-based processes available to more industries to further support manufacturing resurgence efforts of the country.",""],[1,"428","3","Pilot Factory for Industry 4.0 Demonstration and Training","The Pilot Factory will serve as a demonstration and training hub for learning and pilot Industry 4.0 technologies and solutions to accelerate the digital transformation of Philippine enterprises (DTI website).",""]],"156":[[1,"419","8","Technology Acquisition Financial Assistance for Private Companies","This aims to provide financial assistance to Filipino private companies for the acquisition of strategic and relevant technologies so they can undertake their research and development (R&D).","DOST"],[1,"420","13","Science for Change Program","Through the program, the academe and/or RDI in partnership with a Filipino company, undertakes research and development to improve the company's products, processes, and services to become more competitive in their respective industries.",""],[1,"433","11","NICER Regional Research Grants Program","The NICER Program aims to address the disparity in access to R&D funding among the regions.",""],[1,"437","1","RDLead Program","The RDLead Program aims to help develop and strengthen further the research capabilities of the academe, research and development institutions (RDIs), and other government line agencies nationwide.","National Research Council of the Philippines (NRCP)"],[1,"437","6","Innovation Agent Network for Research Commercialization","A network of innovation agents that collaborate to commercialize market-oriented research toward the competitiveness of the region","Department of Trade and Industry"],[1,"438","13","Science for Change Program","Through the Science for Change Program (S4CP), the DOST can significantly accelerate STI in the country and create a massive increase in investment on S&T Human Resource Development and R&D","DOST"]],"157":[[1,"170","3","Regional Knowledge Hub Development","Develop knowledge hubs in each region.","Commission on Higher Education (CHED) | Department of Science and Technology (DOST) | DTI"],[1,"170","4","Expansion of Inclusive Innovation Centers","Inclusive innovation centers will be expanded to serve as platforms to promote an innovation culture, accelerate the commercialization of R&D outputs in the regions, equip universities to carry out research relevant to industries, and adopt technology solutions to create intellectual property.",""],[1,"170","5","Regional Inclusive Innovation Centers","These innovation centers will continue to provide design thinking workshops, and serve as venues for networking and engaging with the academe, industry, and other ecosystem players.",""],[1,"180","1","Industry-Academia Co-location and KIST Park Expansion","The skills and jobs needed by industries will be matched to those offered by the academic institutions by putting together in one location the industry, services, and academic institutions.",""],[1,"180","2","SUC and HEI Scientific Advancement Support Programme","The DTI and DOST will tap other SUCs and HEIs to host several programs, activities, and projects that help accelerate scientific advancements and technological developments in the form of technical services, industry assistance, collaborative research, and product design and development.","DTI | DOST"],[1,"181","23","National Science and Technology Parks Programme","This proposes the establishment of science and technology parks nationwide to largely promote the culture of competitiveness and innovation through the active promotion of investments from tech-based enterprises and knowledge-based institutions.",""]],"158":[[1,"57","24","Health Research and Health Technology Self-Sufficiency Strengthening","Strengthen health research for evidence-informed policy and self sufficiency in health technology",""],[1,"62","2","Health Research and Health Technology Self-Sufficiency Initiative","Strengthen health research for evidence-informed policy- making and self-sufficiency in health technology",""],[1,"62","3","Institutionalization of Health Research-Based Decision-Making","As such, promoting institutionalization of decision-making based on health research, development, and innovation (RDI) will be a priority.",""],[1,"62","3","Dedicated Funding for Health Research, Development, and Innovation","Increased, dedicated, and conditioned funding will focus on health RDI that: (a) translate basic health research into practical aspects; (b) promote low-cost and climate-resilient innovations for remote populations and vulnerable sectors based on projected health needs and service delivery gaps in the medium term; and (c) improve capacity for high quality local vaccine and medicine development and production (See Chapter 8).",""]],"159":[[1,"209","14","Education System Re-engineering","Re-engineer basic, technical-vocational and higher education",""],[1,"209","18","Integration of Creative Arts and Social Sciences with Science and Technology","Integrate creative arts and social sciences with science and technology",""],[1,"210","4","Education System Re-engineering","Re-engineer basic, technical-vocational, and higher education",""]],"160":[[1,"333","26","Local Government and Security Institution Compliance with Good Governance and Human Rights Standards","Sustain the compliance of LGUs to good governance principles and of security institutions on human rights and rule of law",""],[1,"333","27","Gender Mainstreaming and Vulnerable Group Protection in Conflict-Affected Communities","Ensure gender mainstreaming and protection of vulnerable groups in conflict-affected communities",""],[1,"335","3","Training for Social Workers and Relevant Agencies","Training and skills improvement will be initiated for social workers and other relevant government agencies to improve capacity in dealing with former combatants and child soldiers.",""],[1,"335","6","Strategic Communication Plan for Social Cohesion","developing a strategic communication plan aimed as social cohesion",""],[1,"338","12","Affirmative Action for Women and Gender Rights","Affirmative action will be done to protect and promote women and gender rights;",""],[1,"339","1","Protection of Vulnerable Groups in Conflict and Post-Conflict Settings","safeguard the welfare of vulnerable groups, including children, youth, elderly, persons with disability, and internally displaced persons, during conflict situations and post-conflict recovery.",""],[1,"339","2","Peace Education Integration and Culture of Peace Campaigns","Peace education will be integrated in formal and informal learning platforms, as well as a sustained culture of peace campaigns.",""],[1,"339","2","National Peace Institute Establishment","The establishment of a National Peace Institute",""],[1,"339","3","Strategic Peace Communications Plan","A strategic communication plan will be carried out to increase public awareness on peace and security strategies of the government, while an inclusive communication plan will be initiated to entice members of armed threat groups to abandon a life of violence and return to civilian life.","Office of the Presidential Adviser on Peace, Reconciliation and Unity (OPAPRU)"]],"161":[[1,"102","22","Anti-Competitive Practices and Price Manipulation Enforcement","Address anti-competitive practices and price manipulation",""],[1,"105","1","Consumer and Producer Rights Protection Against Fraud and Cybersecurity Risks","The government shall also promote consumer and producer rights' protection against fraud, cybercrime, and payment and website security issues (See Chapter 7).",""],[1,"105","9","Anti-Competitive Practices Monitoring and Enforcement","The Philippine Competition Commission shall be vigilant in monitoring anti-competitive",""]],"162":[[1,"43","6","Participatory Governance and Public Accountability Strengthening","Good governance entails bolstering public accountability and integrity and deepening participatory governance that ensures that marginalized sectors (e.g., women, children, indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities and in GIDAs) have concrete roles and significant influence in all stages of public decision-making",""],[1,"359","3","Freedom of Information Policy Implementation","This may be attributed to the implementation of the Freedom of Information (FOI) policy;",""],[1,"359","3","Electronic Procurement System Enhancement","enhancements in the Philippine Government Electronic Procurement System",""],[1,"359","3","Full Disclosure and Public Financial Management Reforms","At the same time, full disclosure and public financial management reforms",""],[1,"363","1","Freedom of Information Implementation Enhancement","the government will build on the gains of the FOI implementation in national agencies, improve on the e-FOI portal services, and intensify partnerships with LGUs for FOI policies.",""],[1,"364","2","Public Spending Transparency Enhancement","This will be achieved through the full implementation of the EODB and EGSD Act; better integration of government units and the observance of Open Contracting Data Standards in the modernized Philippine Government Electronic Procurement System; the timely publication of budget and financial accountability reports through the Transparency Seal among agencies; and the expansion of COA's CPA",""],[1,"364","3","Expanded Transparency Monitoring in Local Special Bodies","The DILG will intensify monitoring transparency practices in LSBs, extending these to the local Bids and Awards and Project Monitoring Committees.","DILG"],[1,"364","3","Joint Agency Transparency Initiatives on Data Privacy Policies","More joint agency initiatives will also help break down barriers to transparency in data privacy policies.",""],[1,"368","11","Freedom of Information Expansion to the Entire Bureaucracy","The bill will require government agencies to allow the public to review and copy all official information, and to promote meaningful and increased participation in government decision-making and public accountability.",""],[1,"370","25","Open Contracting Data Publication","Open Contracting Data Publication is a country commitment to the OGP.",""]],"163":[[1,"274","3","Debt Sustainability Management","To sustain sound fiscal management, the following outcomes will be pursued: (a) productive, equitable, and simple tax system; (b) efficient and inclusive budget system; (c) stronger local government finance; and (d) sustainable management of debt (see Figure 11.2.1).",""],[1,"274","26","Resilient and Strategic Debt Management","Maintain a resilient and strategic debt management",""],[1,"281","1","Debt Management Strategy","Debt management strategies will continue to ensure that the financing needs of the government and its payment obligations will be met at the lowest possible costs consistent with acceptable level of risks.",""],[1,"281","3","Fiscal Discipline and Prudent Debt Management","the government will maintain, if not improve, its high credit rating by adhering to fiscal discipline and prudent debt management.",""]],"164":[[1,"19","6","Macroeconomic Stability Strategy","ensuring macroeconomic stability (Chapter 11)",""],[1,"27","4","Macroeconomic Stability and Sound Fiscal Management Strategy","The Plan must therefore include strategies that would ensure macroeconomic stability and sound fiscal management to keep consumer and investor confidence in the economy high.",""],[1,"42","8","Sound Fiscal Management and Tax Regime Reform","Sound fiscal management, including a conducive tax regime, will be fostered (Subchapter 11.2).",""],[1,"42","8","Medium-Term Fiscal Framework","As it stands, a medium-term fiscal framework has been proposed and approved by President Marcos, Jr .; and endorsed by Congress.",""],[1,"44","8","Fiscal Discipline and Debt Reduction Policy","Ensure fiscal discipline.",""]],"165":[[1,"17","1","Government-Wide Plan Alignment Directive","I have issued an Executive Order to all government agencies and instrumentalities to align their programs and policies with the Plan.",""]],"169":[[1,"42","1","Local Firm Survival and Expansion Support","Renewed focus will be given to the survival, growth, and expansion of local firms in the export and domestic markets in order to drive productive employment, and increase incomes.",""]],"170":[[1,"19","5","Economic Sector Strengthening Agenda","The Plan shall strengthen the economic sectors, which are seen to create more and higher-quality jobs and produce globally competitive products.",""],[1,"19","5","Industrial Revitalization Programme","revitalize industries (Chapter 6),",""],[1,"19","5","Services Sector Reinvigoration Programme","and reinvigorate services (Chapter 7).",""],[1,"19","7","Industry Servicification Support","enabling the servicification of our industries",""],[1,"41","2","Domestic Production and Supplier Base Expansion","Domestic production and supplier base will be expanded, particularly corresponding to the value chains of the following industry clusters: (a) industrial, manufacturing, and transport (IMT); (b) technology, media, and telecommunication (TMT); (c) health and life",""],[1,"41","4","Services Sector Reinvigoration","Services sector will be reinvigorated (Chapter 7).",""],[1,"41","4","Tourism, Culture, Creative Sector, and IT-BPM Promotion","Demand for services will be expanded by actively promoting the country's tourism, culture, creative sector, and Information Technology-Business Process Management (IT-BPM).",""],[1,"41","4","Holiday Economics Initiative","Adoption of holiday economics will also be undertaken to boost domestic tourism, promote local products, and encourage inter-cultural exchanges.",""],[1,"42","2","Services Sector Training and Infrastructure Support","To this end, support will be provided to training and retraining programs for the sector and facilitate access to the necessary physical and digital infrastructure.",""]],"171":[[1,"44","1","Pandemic Recovery and Resilience Mainstreaming Agenda","the country will rebuild the losses from the pandemic and invest in improving areas where deep weaknesses were apparent in the pandemic response, for example: in health and responsiveness of social protection; and in mainstreaming resilience throughout the bureaucracy (e.g., local governments, finance, education, disaster risk reduction, and energy security) and communities.",""]],"172":[[1,"61","7","Regulatory Pathways and Sandbox Regulation Framework","Specific strategies include facilitating regulatory pathways and adopting sandbox approaches to regulation, especially for emerging developments, emergency medicines, technologies, business models, and innovations.",""],[1,"61","7","Public-Private Health Innovation Partnerships","Regulatory sandboxes and partnerships between publicly funded health care providers and private small and medium enterprises (SME) and startups make it easier to innovate and test new technologies and health delivery models for equity (See Chapter 8).",""],[1,"61","7","Periodic Horizon Scanning for Health System Foresight","Responsiveness can also be encouraged by institutionalizing periodic horizon scanning for new developments, to draw out their policy and long-run ethical implications among health system stakeholders.",""]],"173":[[1,"59","5","Hospital Network Expansion and Quality Improvement","Increasing the number, improving the distribution, and assuring the quality of hospitals, including establishing regional specialty centers, are ongoing priorities.",""],[1,"63","8","Specialty Centers for Specialized Healthcare Services","This bill seeks to establish specialty centers that will provide and improve access to specialized healthcare services.",""]],"174":[[1,"74","4","Harmonization of the Trifocalized Education System for Lifelong Learning","Harmonize the trifocalized system of education for lifelong learning",""],[1,"74","5","Rationalization of the Trifocalized Education System","the trifocalized education system shall be rationalized.","DepEd | Commission on Higher Education [CHED] | Technical Education and Skills Development Authority [TESDA]"],[1,"74","5","Coordination and Harmonization of the Human Capital Development Sector","Coordination and harmonization among the pillars of the human capital development sector (i.e., DepEd, CHED, TESDA, Department of Science and Technology, Professional Regulation Commission [PRC], Department of Information and Communications Technology, Department of Labor and Employment, Department of Trade and Industry, and Department of Migrant","DepEd | CHED | TESDA | Department of Science and Technology | Professional Regulation Commission [PRC] | Department of Information and Communications Technology | Department of Labor and Employment | Department of Trade and Industry | Department of Migrant"],[1,"74","6","Qualification Framework Cascading and Promotion","The Philippine Qualifications Framework, Philippine Skills Framework, and ASEAN Qualification Reference Framework will be cascaded and promoted by the concerned agencies, especially DepEd, CHED, and TESDA.","DepEd | CHED | TESDA"],[1,"74","6","International Qualification Framework Benchmarking","Qualification frameworks of other regions (e.g., European Qualifications Framework, Arab Qualifications Framework), especially regions with high job opportunities for Filipinos, will be given proper consideration.",""],[1,"74","6","Professional Mobility and Credit Transfer Partnerships","Partnerships with local and international institutions to enhance continuing professional development, career development support, credit transfer schemes and pathways, and equivalency systems will be initiated to facilitate standards comparability and professional mobility.",""]],"175":[[1,"86","3","Urban Greening and Green Space Expansion Programme","individual actions on urban greening will be encouraged.",""]],"176":[[1,"87","1","Balanced Housing Act Implementation Review","The implementation of the Balanced Housing Development Act ... shall be revisited.",""],[1,"87","1","Housing Escrow Fund Access and Monitoring Guidelines","This is to ensure that the guidelines for accessing the funds and monitoring the allocation and use of the Housing Escrow Fund will be in place to ensure that the funds will not be underutilized or misused.","DHSUD"],[1,"87","6","Informal Settler and Homeless Inventory and Database System","An inventory on the number of ISFs and the homeless will be undertaken, and an information database system shall be established.",""],[1,"87","6","Idle Government Land Inventory and Resettlement Site Database","Idle government lands will be completely inventoried and a database established to identify potential resettlement sites for informal settlers.",""],[1,"89","6","Local Government Housing Planning and Land Mobilization","Participation of LGUs in planning, financing, andimplementation ofhousing and community programs shall be accelerated.",""],[1,"90","8","Community Livability Monitoring and Incentive System","Sustained community livability planning shall be monitored and incentivized.","DHSUD"],[1,"90","8","Comprehensive Housing and Urban Development Monitoring Information System","DHSUD shall establish a comprehensive housing and urban development monitoring information system.","DHSUD"],[1,"90","8","Shelter and Urban Development Management Standards and Monitoring Information System","DHSUD is mandated to develop and maintain a shelter and urban development management, standards, and monitoring information system which shall include, but not limited to, the following data sets: inventory of idle lands, CLUP, inventory of housing stock, and list of beneficiaries.","DHSUD"],[1,"90","8","Housing and Urban Development Policy Integration","The passage of the DHSUD Act provided an impetus to integrate all housing and urban development policies, plans, programs, and projects.","DHSUD"],[1,"90","8","Housing Policy Effectiveness Data Collection and Analysis","DHSUD's role, as oversight to housing and urban development-related policies and programs, requires data collection, processing, and analysis to assess the effectiveness of policies and programs.","DHSUD"]],"177":[[1,"90","3","Climate and Disaster Risk Assessment Requirement for Housing and Community Development Approvals","Climate and disaster risk assessment shall be made a prerequisite in the approval of areas identified for housing and community development.",""],[1,"90","4","Carrying Capacity Assessment for Local Planning","carrying capacity assessments will be conducted in areas where population movement needs to be managed, such as ecotourism destination areas and urban areas.",""]],"178":[[1,"104","4","Food Banks and Community Pantries Establishment","The establishment of food banks and community pantries as food redistribution mechanisms shall be encouraged through the collaboration of the government and private sector.",""],[1,"104","4","Food Waste Reduction IEC Campaign","Moreover, the government shall intensify IEC activities on the practical benefits of and ways to cut down food waste.",""],[1,"104","4","Food Waste Management Policy Legislation","Such policies may include the legislation of a Food Waste Management Policy that will promote, facilitate, and ensure waste reduction in all sectors of society.",""],[1,"108","1","Local Procurement for Feeding and Relief Operations","food requirements of feeding programs and relief operations shall be sourced from farmers and fisherfolk groups and cooperatives, which will also provide farmers and fisherfolk with assured markets",""],[1,"108","11","Food Waste Reduction Mechanisms","This policy seeks to address the growing food waste problem in the country by adopting and institutionalizing mechanisms that will promote, facilitate, and ensure food waste reduction across different sectors of society (e.g., households, food establishments, food distributors, and supermarkets].",""],[1,"108","11","Food Donation and Distribution Platforms","This will include the establishment of [a] food donation and distribution platforms and networks such as food banks and community pantries;",""],[1,"108","11","Community Composting and Urban Green Space Linkages","and [b] community composting that may be linked with initiatives on developing green urban spaces, including urban agriculture sites.",""]],"179":[[1,"102","16","Food Technology Development and Adoption Initiative","Intensify the development and adoption of technologies that increase the nutritional content and prolong shelf-life of food products",""],[1,"107","1","Food Technology Development and Adoption Initiative","Intensify the development and adoption of technologies that increase the nutritional content and prolong the shelf-life of food products",""],[1,"107","2","Nutritious Food Product Development Initiative","The government, state universities and colleges, and private sector shall intensify the development of safe, affordable, nutritious, and energy-dense food products to address malnutrition",""],[1,"107","2","Food Processing and Packaging Technology Development","Development of processing and packaging technologies to prolong shelf life and improve the nutritional content of food products (including utilization of waste products and startups for processing and packaging) shall likewise be pursued",""],[1,"107","2","Food Fortification Research and Large-Scale Fortification Program","Moreover, the government shall (a) strengthen research and development efforts on food fortification (e.g., large-scale fortification of staple foods);",""],[1,"107","2","Iron-Fortified Rice Promotion and Utilization","promote and utilize iron-fortified rice and other products (e.g., NFA's Rice Fortification Project);",""],[1,"107","2","Advanced Food Preservation and Smart Packaging Technology Exploration","explore advanced and emerging technologies (e.g., food preservation, smart packaging, and targeted nutrition), including biotechnology (e.g., Golden Rice23 and orange-fleshed sweet potato).",""],[1,"107","2","Private Sector Food Technology Development Support","The private sector's role in the development of new technologies, both in processing and delivery of food, will also be enhanced especially since they have the financial resources, social capital, and expertise.",""],[1,"108","21","Mandatory Food Fortification Legislative Amendment","The proposed amendment aims to resolve gaps and inconsistencies of RA 8976 with RA 11037 (Child Nutrition Act), RA 10611 [Food Safety Act of 2013), and RA 8172 [Act for Salt Iodization Nationwide).",""],[1,"108","21","Salt Industry Support Amendment","This proposed legislative measure will also amend RA 8172 to enhance support for the local salt industry.",""]],"180":[[1,"113","40","Nutrition Integration in Social Protection Programs","Integrate the nutritional needs of vulnerable groups in SP program",""],[1,"116","6","Nutrition Integration in Social Protection Programs","Integrate the nutritional needs of vulnerable groups in social protection programs",""],[1,"116","7","Nutrition-Sensitive Social Protection Design","Nutritional concerns shall be considered in the design of social protection programs and policies.",""]],"181":[[1,"113","18","Strengthen Enforcement of Laws Protecting Women","Strengthen implementation of laws protecting women",""],[1,"116","10","Strengthen Enforcement of Laws Protecting Women","Strengthen implementation of laws protecting women",""],[1,"116","11","Women's Rights and Gender-Based Violence Awareness Campaigns","Wider and more effective dissemination in various media of women's rights, gender-based violence laws, and the available programs and facilities for women victims shall be undertaken.",""],[1,"116","11","National and Local Campaigns for Women Victims of Violence","Both national- and local-level campaigns shall be organized to encourage women victims of violence to seek help from appropriate authorities and private organizations.",""],[1,"117","1","Investigation and Prosecution Process Streamlining","Investigation and prosecutorial processes, prosecution, and case management processes, including those for heinous crimes against women, shall be streamlined.",""]],"182":[[1,"113","19","Rationalization of Livelihood and Public Works Cash-for-Work Programs","Rationalize existing livelihood and public works/cash for work programs implemented by various government agencies",""],[1,"118","2","Livelihood and Public Works Program Rationalization","Rationalize existing livelihood and public works/cash for work programs implemented by various government agencies",""],[1,"118","3","Livelihood and Public Works Program Coordination Committee","basic guidelines and standards shall be set by a committee to be composed of all agencies that have such programs.",""]],"183":[[1,"129","24","Employment Policy Collaboration Mechanism","Strengthen linkages and collaboration among government and industry associations, enterprises, and social partners to emphasize shared responsibility in promoting and implementing employment policies and strategies",""],[1,"129","25","Tripartite and Bipartite Social Dialogue Strengthening","Advocate and strengthen tripartite and bipartite social dialogue",""],[1,"129","27","Tripartite Wage and Productivity Mechanism Strengthening","Ensure effective and efficient use of existing tripartite wage and productivity mechanisms",""],[1,"129","33","Employment Access and Labour Market Governance Strengthening","to strengthen interventions that improve access to employment opportunities.",""],[1,"137","1","Employment Policy Collaboration Mechanism","Strengthen linkages and collaboration among government and industry associations, enterprises, and social partners to emphasize shared responsibility in promoting and implementing employment policies and strategies",""],[1,"137","3","Social Dialogue Plan Update on Megatrends","With its social partners, the government shall update the social dialogue plan to emphasize the role of megatrends such as digitalization, automation, and climate change, including how they affect the firm organization, skill composition, qualifications, working conditions, health, and safety.",""],[1,"137","6","Tripartite Wage and Productivity Mechanism Strengthening","Ensure effective and efficient use of existing tripartite wage and productivity mechanisms",""],[1,"137","7","Minimum Wage Protection and Adjustment Policy","The minimum wage shall be used to protect the lowest and most vulnerable wage earners from poverty.",""],[1,"138","1","Productivity-Based Incentive Scheme Technical Assistance","the government shall continue to provide technical assistance to workers and enterprises in designing and implementing productivity-based incentive schemes to increasingly link workers' compensation and labor productivity.",""],[1,"139","13","Productivity Incentives Committee and Incentive Program","Fortify the intentions of the \"Productivity Incentive Act of 1990\" by promoting inclusive and sustainable work productivity programs.",""],[1,"141","1","National Employment Action Plan Institutionalization","This Senate Bill institutionalizes the National 1 Employment Action Plan, which is an offshoot of the NERS.",""],[1,"181","21","Productivity Improvement and Gainsharing Initiative","This aims to strengthen the productivity improvement and gainsharing between workers and enterprises.",""]],"184":[[1,"129","26","Inclusive Participation and Equitable Access Mechanisms for Education and Skills Development","Design mechanisms to ensure inclusive participation and equitable access to education and skills development programs",""],[1,"136","1","Labor Market Anti-Discrimination Programs and Policies","Develop programs and policies that address all forms of labor market discrimination in work, education, and training",""],[1,"136","2","Equality Policy Impact Assessment Framework","The government shall conduct impact assessments of policies, laws, and institutions designed to promote equality.",""],[1,"136","2","Employment Facilitation and Labor Market Barrier Reduction Measures","Besides employment facilitation, policies shall be aimed at labor market issues such as gender, context-specific barriers, such as transportation constraints, security, technological capacities, and discrimination.",""],[1,"136","3","Framework to Eliminate Discrimination Between Full-Time and Part-Time Workers","The government shall explore the development of a framework that can progressively eliminate discrimination between full-time and part-time workers.",""],[1,"138","5","Women’s Economic Empowerment through Digital Technologies","promoting entrepreneurship, and advancing economic opportunities for women, through harnessing digital technologies.",""]],"185":[[1,"153","1","Farm and Non-farm Waste Utilization and Composting","there will be greater utilization and composting of farm and non-farm wastes and biological materials, such as palm sap, wood waste, and Napier grass, as energy and fertilizer sources",""]],"186":[[1,"156","4","Domestic Production of Agricultural and Food Inputs","Investments in the domestic production of AFF inputs will be intensified along with creating local business opportunities for the sector to lessen dependence on foreign sources and reduce supply chain disruptions.",""],[1,"156","4","Seed and Planting Material Buffer Stock System","The DA will also ensure sufficient buffer stocks of seeds and other planting materials to mitigate the impacts of global economic shocks.","DA"]],"187":[[1,"155","7","Research and Development on Indigenous Species and Traditional Food Culture Promotion","RDE on indigenous species and varieties of plants and breeds of animals and promoting traditional food culture through active advocacy and formal and informal education shall be prioritized.",""],[1,"155","7","Investment Promotion for Nutritious and Safe Local Food Value Chains","The government will also institute policies to encourage investments in growing, processing, marketing (domestic and international), and consuming nutritious and safe local dishes (See Subchapter 3.1).",""]],"188":[[1,"170","1","OTOP Upgrade Programme","These can be done by upgrading the OTOP, developing knowledge hubs in each region, and developing platforms that support an innovative culture.",""],[1,"170","1","Regional Knowledge Hub Development","These can be done by upgrading the OTOP, developing knowledge hubs in each region, and developing platforms that support an innovative culture.",""],[1,"170","1","Innovation Culture Support Platforms","These can be done by upgrading the OTOP, developing knowledge hubs in each region, and developing platforms that support an innovative culture.",""],[1,"170","2","One Town, One Product Upgrade","Upgrade the One Town, One Product.","DTI"],[1,"170","2","OTOP Technical Partnership for Improvement","The DTI will partner with the National Academy of Science and Technology and the Philippine American Academy of Science and Engineering to improve further the OTOP.","DTI"],[1,"170","2","Regional Production-Based Development Implementation","DTI regional offices will work with their respective Regional Development Councils (RDC) to advance the implementation of production-based regional development.","DTI regional offices"]],"189":[[1,"170","6","MSME Fablabs and Digital Fabrication Access","Another service facility that can be provided to MSMEs is the open-access do-it-yourself maker space called Fablabs, which will allow MSMEs to explore the use of digital fabrication.",""],[1,"170","6","Digital Training Centers for MSMEs","Meanwhile, digital training centers will provide support to MSMEs interested in exploring the use of digital technology.",""],[1,"172","5","Digital Platform for MSMEs and Startups","The DTI, in collaboration with the Department of Information and Communications Technology and private sector partners, will provide a digital platform for MSMEs and startups.","DTI | Department of Information and Communications Technology"],[1,"172","6","Startup Ecosystem Development Programs","craft and implement programs to build the startup ecosystem (with a common understanding of the startup journey and ecosystem development among government agencies toward the alignment and harmonization of startup",""],[1,"173","3","Innovation Pitching Support for MSMEs and Startups","Conduct extensive innovation pitching for MSMEs and startups.","DTI"],[1,"173","3","Industry Association Partnership for Startup Innovation","The DTI, through partnerships with industry associations, will create opportunities for MSMEs and startups to convert their ideas into breakthrough innovations.","DTI"],[1,"173","4","Regulatory Sandbox Institutionalization","The DTI will institutionalize a regulatory sandbox","DTI"],[1,"173","5","Blended Finance Support for Entrepreneurs and Startups","the government will provide a supportive policy environment for entrepreneurs and startups through the exploration of various modes of development finance or blended finance",""]],"190":[[1,"165","1","MSME Access to Science, Technology, and Innovation Ecosystem","to drive industrialization forward, accessibility, particularly of micro, small, and medium enterprises, to a dynamic science, technology, and innovation ecosystem will be ensured.",""],[1,"171","1","Industrial Research and Development Support for Technology Adoption","Support will be provided to the industries' R&D needs to enhance technology adoption and stimulate productivity growth.",""],[1,"171","2","Science for Change Program Expansion","The Science for Change Program (S4CP) of the DOST will be expanded to support the industries in their R&D needs.","DOST"],[1,"174","5","Harmonized National Research and Development Agenda Implementation","Execute the Harmonized National Research and Development Agenda (HNRDA) 2022-2028 with its Industry, Energy and Emerging Technologies roadmaps.","DOST | DTI"],[1,"174","6","Public-Private Collaboration for Emerging Knowledge- and Technology-Intensive Industries","The HNRDA 2022-2028 will also establish avenues for engagement between the public and private sector toward a strong collaboration in emerging knowledge- and technology-intensive industries (EKTI).",""],[1,"175","2","Science for Change Program Continuation","Sustain the Science for Change Program.","DOST"]],"191":[[1,"169","1","Construction Materials Demand Consolidation Arrangement","Demand consolidation will continue to be pursued by the Board of Investment, which has been active in arranging reverse trade agreements among buyers and sellers in the industry, wherein buyers present their needs for certain materials, and arrange for preferential pricing from interested suppliers.",""],[1,"169","2","Targeted Incentives for Labor-Intensive Industries and Businesses","Provide targeted, time-bound incentives to establish labor-intensive industries and businesses",""],[1,"169","8","Support for Competitive Regional and Urban Industrial Centers","The government will promote and support regional and urban centers specializing in industries where they are most competitive, recognizing the value of the industries in the",""],[1,"174","3","Strategic Investment Priority Plan Promotion","The BOI and other investment promotion agencies will continue aggressively promoting the SIPP.",""],[1,"180","5","Strategic Investment Priority Plan Fiscal Incentives","The implementation of the SIPP provided under the Corporate Recovery and Tax Incentives for Enterprises Act will provide targeted and time-bound fiscal incentives to activities that will enhance manufacturers' in-house servicification.",""]],"192":[[1,"169","4","Health and Life Science Manufacturing Support","Support for health and life science (HLS) will specifically target manufacturing of essential products like personal protective equipment",""],[1,"169","5","Support for Domestic PPE and Medical Supplies Manufacturing","This includes loans for equipment needed in manufacturing hospital-grade PPEs and medical supplies.",""],[1,"169","5","Technical Assistance for Hospital-Standard Compliance","Technical assistance will also be provided to companies to meet the standards of hospitals.",""],[1,"169","5","Regulatory Streamlining for HLS Manufacturers","Government support will also be provided for the streamlining of complex rules and regulations affecting business operations of HLS manufacturers.",""],[1,"176","4","Pharmaceutical Sector Investment Attraction and Domestic Supplier Network Promotion","the pharmaceutical sector will attract leading multinational companies while promoting the domestic suppliers' network.",""],[1,"180","4","Pharmaceutical Roadmap Upgrade to HLS Roadmap","One example of the roadmap that can be updated is the pharmaceutical roadmap, which can be elevated into an HLS roadmap by: (a) incorporating plans for the institution of a knowledge center of excellence in collaboration with HEIs; (b) mapping the innovation ecosystem available to the cluster; and (c) enabling a superior environment afforded by, for example, a dedicated technology park or campus and venture capital provision.",""]],"193":[[1,"169","6","Strategic Investment Priority Plan Support for Food Processors","Through the Strategic Investment Priority Plan (SIPP), fiscal and non-fiscal support will be provided to food processors to enable them to compete against imports from neighbors in the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN).",""],[1,"170","7","Agribusiness and Commodity Industry Roadmap Upgrade","The agribusiness and/or commodity industry roadmaps will be upgraded to consider the evolving domestic and international environment.",""]],"194":[[1,"169","7","Electric Vehicle Incentive Strategy Expansion","government support to programs and measures such as the Electric Vehicle Incentive Strategy, which is similar to the Comprehensive Automotive Resurgence Strategy program, will be expanded",""],[1,"171","5","Energy Crop Seedling Development and Feedstock Mapping for Biofuels","seedling development for high-yield coconuts and other energy crops will be pursued to increase feedstock. This includes the mapping of suitable areas for feedstock production for the biofuels industry.","DA | Department of Energy (DOE)"],[1,"172","1","Renewable Energy Act Implementing Rules Amendment","the implementing rules and regulations of the Renewable Energy Act of 2008 will be amended","DOE"],[1,"172","1","Preferential Power Cost Policy for Power-Generating Provinces","the DOE, in accordance with existing laws, will provide the legal and regulatory policy environment to ensure that power-generating provinces are given preferential treatment in availing lower power costs for its constituents, and a continuous 24/7 supply of power","DOE"],[1,"172","1","EPIRA Amendment Initiative","Likewise, the amendments to the Electric Power Industry Reform Act (EPIRA) will be pushed",""]],"195":[[1,"175","3","Ecozone Transformation Roadmap Implementation","Accelerate the implementation of the ecozone transformation roadmap.","Philippine Economic Zone Authority (PEZA)"],[1,"175","4","Ecozone Creation and Integration Reform","The creation of ecozones will be within the existing investment promotion agencies to maximize investments and promote industrial dispersion especially outside metropolitan areas.",""],[1,"175","4","Local Economic Integration of Ecozones","Further, the ecozones will be integrated into the local economy by relaxing the requirements, facilitating the free flow of parts, components, and other inputs, and increasing open trade between zone locators and firms outside the zones.",""],[1,"181","15","Update the PEZA Law for Digitalization","This entails updating of the 27-year-old PEZA law to adopt to the digitalization of the locators.",""]],"196":[[1,"189","1","Services Sector Market Expansion and Digital Transformation","Market expansion and digital transformation will create the pathways for services firms to enhance their strong presence in markets, reach new market segments and buyer geographies, and pursue diversification.",""],[1,"189","1","Technology, Talent, and Skills Development Ecosystem","The sector will gain strength, speed, and size from the dynamic ecosystem of technology, talent and skills development, intellectual property rights protection, and competition for creativity and innovation.",""],[1,"189","1","Public-Private-Social Partnership for Regional Investment and Value Chain Linkages","A strong public-private-social partnership will be nurtured to expand investments in the regions and enhance strategic inter-sectoral linkages for inclusive, resilient, and sustainable participation of the Philippines in global value chains that mark the Fourth Industrial Revolution.",""],[1,"191","1","Services Sector Upgrading and Market Expansion Initiative","During the Plan period, the government and private sector will strengthen their partnership to expand markets and achieve scale through aggressive marketing and promotions, trade, and global partnerships, and facilitate the use of digital technologies and processes to raise productivity in low-skills services.",""],[1,"191","1","Company Capability Upgrading for Higher-Value Services","Building the capabilities of more companies is important to shift to higher value and differentiated services and high-skills jobs.",""],[1,"191","1","Technology, Management, and Talent Support for Services Upgrading","To facilitate this upgrading, they need new technologies, skilled management and workforce, and a steady supply of talent.",""],[1,"191","11","Physical Connectivity Facilitation","Facilitate physical connectivity (aviation, shipping and maritime, and",""],[1,"191","19","Data Collection Ecosystem Strengthening","Strengthen data collection ecosystem",""],[1,"191","20","Trade Services Framework Development","Develop the services in trade framework to maximize trade",""],[1,"191","21","Research and Development Funding and Incentives Expansion","Increase access to funds and incentives for research and development (R&D)",""],[1,"191","34","Technology Parks and Centers Development","Develop technology parks, centers of",""]],"197":[[1,"190","5","Economic Reforms and Implementing Rules and Regulations","The economic reforms and their respective implementing rules and regulations will facilitate the flow of investments in the regions, modernize the services sector, accelerate the country's economic recovery from the coronavirus disease (COVID-19) pandemic, and promote inclusive growth.",""],[1,"243","11","Operationalization of Economic Liberalization Reforms","Expedite the operationalization of recent economic liberalization reforms (e.g., Public Service Act, Retail Trade Liberalization Act, and Foreign Investments Act)",""],[1,"246","5","Regulatory Enforcement of Public Service and Investment Laws","The government, through the appropriate agencies and sector regulators, will issue rules and regulations to enforce the recently enacted amendments to the Public Service Act, and fully implement the Foreign Investments Act and the Retail Trade Liberalization Act.",""]],"198":[[1,"191","10","MSME Access to Capital and Digital Technology Support","Increase access of MSMEs to capital, digital technologies, and startups",""],[1,"191","45","AI Applications Development and MSME Value Chain Linkage Initiative","government to develop AI applications and establish linkages between large companies and MSMEs for value chain upgrading",""],[1,"194","11","MSME E-Commerce Adoption Acceleration","Accelerate e-commerce adoption by micro, small, and medium enterprises",""],[1,"194","12","E-commerce Awareness and Advocacy Campaigns","Engage businesses in awareness and advocacy campaigns on the benefits of e-commerce in increasing their visibility and global reach.",""],[1,"194","12","MSME E-commerce Tool Adoption Partnership","Private technology and platform providers, industry associations, and conglomerates will be encouraged to scale up collaboration with the DTI and partner agencies to increase the adoption of e-commerce tools by MSMEs","DTI"],[1,"195","7","MSME Access to Capital and Digital Technology Support","Increase access of MSMEs to capital, digital technologies, and startups",""],[1,"195","8","STI-Driven MSME Upgrading Programme","Invest in STI-driven upgrading of MSMEs, including process, product, organization, and marketing.",""],[1,"195","8","Innovation Center Support for MSMEs","Through the Center for Artificial Intelligence Research (CAIR) and DTI's Regional Inclusive Innovation Centers, MSMEs will gain access to ideas, technology, and talents to improve firm performance.",""],[1,"195","8","Shared Service Facilities and R&D Support for Creative Industries","Under the Philippine Innovation Act, entities from the creative industries may avail of shared service facilities from the DTI, as well as the infrastructure and R&D support programs of the Department of Science and Technology.","DTI | Department of Science and Technology"],[1,"195","9","MSME Training and Capacity Building Programme","Increase access of MSME management and workforce to training and capacity building programs",""],[1,"195","10","MSME Digital Skills and Shared Service Facilities Program","Through the implementation of the Digital Workforce Competitiveness Act, the DTI, in coordination with relevant government agencies and the private sector, shall establish co-working or shared service facilities to support the development and enhancement of digital skills and competencies of entrepreneurs, especially women, and the current and future workforce.","DTI"],[1,"196","1","Business Development Training and Capacity Building Programme","The Philippine CIDC will undertake training and capacity building in business development to enhance financial literacy, ethics, digital skills, taxation, design thinking, contracts, negotiations, and entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"196","4","AI Applications Development and MSME Value Chain Linkage Partnership","Foster partnership with the government to develop AI applications and establish linkages between large companies and MSMEs for value chain upgrading",""],[1,"196","5","Private Sector Participation in CAIR","Private sector investors will be encouraged to take part in the CAIR.",""],[1,"243","27","Broadband and Digital Technology Expansion for MSMEs","Expand access to broadband internet and digital technologies to enhance consumer choice and facilitate digitalization and innovation among micro, small, and medium enterprises",""]],"199":[[1,"199","7","Local Investment Readiness and Advisory Services Ecosystem","Led by the DTI Board of Investments, in collaboration with sector- or area-focused investment promotion agencies, private sector, and academe, develop an ecosystem of advisory services to enable LGUs to acquire strategic skills tand capacitate them to match local service firms with investors, build the expertise of LGUs in risk management, and conduct due diligence.","DTI Board of Investments"],[1,"199","8","Data Collection Ecosystem Strengthening for Market Intelligence and Industry Studies","Strengthen data collection ecosystem for market intelligence, insights, and industry studies",""],[1,"199","9","University-Industry Services Data Collaboration","Promote the active participation of colleges and universities in collecting and analyzing data in the services sector.",""],[1,"199","9","Services Sector Satellite Accounts Development","The government shall invest in the development of satellite accounts for other services, such as transportation and logistics, including subnational satellite accounts (tourism, digital economy, creative industries, and logistics), on a phased priority basis.",""],[1,"199","11","Private Sector and Community Information-Sharing Mechanism","Strengthen regular and active participation of private sector and communities to promote free flow of information with the government.",""],[1,"199","11","Online Directories and Registries Development","Associations will share insights, market intelligence, and data on the sectors they represent and contribute to the development of online directories and registries.",""],[1,"209","15","Market and User Information System Integration Mechanism","Create mechanisms for integrating market/user information system",""],[1,"211","10","Market and User Information System Integration Mechanism","Create mechanisms for integrating a market/user information system",""],[1,"212","1","Common Market Intelligence Portal","the government will establish a common and accessible portal that provides market intelligence.",""],[1,"212","1","Primary Market Data Collection Support for Researchers","Social science researchers and student researchers in higher education institutions will be taught and provided support to conduct primary data collection that can capture relevant market data, such as customer needs and preferences, competitors, customer demographics, market trends, market price, and potential marketing processes.",""],[1,"227","3","Tradeline Philippines Platform Revamp and Expansion","The Tradeline Philippines will be revamped and given more resources to enable the platform to identify emerging products and market opportunities; better capture information on local suppliers and their capabilities; and create a dedicated space for",""],[1,"227","6","Merged Trade Transaction and Firm Survey Database Update","the Philippine Statistics Authority will ensure the updating of its merged Trade Transaction and Firm Survey database, which will be the basis for distinguishing more granular firm typologies and monitoring the health of local firms, particularly exporting firms.","Philippine Statistics Authority"],[1,"234","7","Firm-Level Export and Trade Impact Monitoring System","This includes monitoring of firm-level export growth, firm market shares, and market exits (e.g., product and country destinations); job creation impact of trade and investments; and monitoring of revealed comparative advantage.",""],[1,"234","7","Geographic Firm Mapping for Provincial and Municipal Support","Information on the geographic location of firms is essential to mobilize provincial and even municipal resources to assist ailing firms.",""]],"200":[[1,"216","9","Comprehensive Atomic Regulatory Framework","Providing for a Comprehensive Atomic Regulatory Framework, Creating for the Purpose the Philippine Atomic Regulatory Commission, and Appropriating Funds Therefor",""],[1,"216","10","Atomic Radiation Regulatory Framework and Commission Establishment","The bill aims to provide a legal framework that adequately protects public health and safety, and the environment against the harmful effects of ionizing radiation; and ensures the safety and security of radiation sources.",""]],"201":[[1,"216","14","Philippine Bamboo Industry Development Support Package","Promoting the Development of the Bamboo Industry by Strengthening the Philippine Bamboo Industry Development Council, Creating the Bamboo Industry Research and Development Center, Providing Incentives for Bamboo Plantation Development, and Appropriating Funds Therefor",""],[1,"216","15","Philippine Bamboo Industry Development Program","The bill seeks to promote the development of the Philippine bamboo industry through policies and programs that promote the planting of bamboo and accelerate the development of bamboo-based designs and products.",""],[1,"216","15","Bamboo Industry Research and Development Center","It proposes the creation of a Bamboo Industry Research and Development Center, which is tasked to ensure the effective implementation of the goals and objectives of the measure through research and development; and trade and propagation promotion, education, and capacity- building initiatives for farmers, processors, designers, and other stakeholders in the bamboo industry, among others.",""]],"202":[[1,"232","1","Innovative Payment for Environmental Services Pilot","The Innovative Payment for Environmental Services (PES) is already being piloted in the country, offering a more accessible alternative to the United Nations Programme on Reducing Emissions from Deforestation and Forest Degradation Warsaw Framework, or UN REDD+ schemes, among others.",""]],"203":[[1,"240","1","Integration of National Climate Policy Compliance into Performance Incentives and Local Governance Awards","compliance with the NCP be integrated in the criteria used in the grant of Performance-Based Bonus (PBB) for government personnel and in the conferment of the Seal of Good Local Governance (SGLG) on local government units (LGU).",""]],"204":[[1,"243","21","Separation of Regulatory and Proprietary Functions of Government-Owned and Controlled Corporations","Enforce the separation of regulatory and propriety activities of government-owned and controlled corporations",""],[1,"247","2","Revised Philippine Government Internal Audit Program","the implementation of the Revised Philippine Government Internal Audit Program.",""],[1,"248","6","Separation of Regulatory and Proprietary Functions of Government-Owned and Controlled Corporations","Enforce the separation of regulatory and proprietary activities of government-owned and controlled corporations",""],[1,"248","7","Separation of Regulatory and Proprietary Functions in GOCCs","The government will enforce the separation between the regulatory and proprietary activities of government-owned and controlled corporations (GOCCs) under the GOCC Governance Act of 2011 (RA 10149) to ensure that GOCCs are subject to the same regulatory framework as private companies.","Government Commission for GOCCs | PCC"]],"205":[[1,"262","7","Digital Bank Licensing and Regulatory Sandbox Framework","As part of the implementation of the DPTR, the BSP has approved six digital banks, the first of which was the Overseas Filipino (OF) Bank, a government-owned all-digital bank.",""],[1,"262","7","Financial Technology Regulatory Sandbox Framework","The BSP has likewise institutionalized a regulatory Sandbox Framework to evaluate financial technology (fintech) concepts and encourage innovation in the financial system.",""],[1,"264","12","Fintech Regulatory Sandbox","Adopt regulatory sandbox approach for fintech innovators",""],[1,"264","31","Enabling Fintech Regulatory Reform","Promote enabling regulations for fintech",""],[1,"264","33","Regtech Development Promotion","Promote regtech development",""],[1,"266","3","National Development Company Revitalization for Fintech Venture Capital","To provide venture capital funds to private sector fintech companies, the National Development Company will be revitalized to assist in the growth of fintech companies delivering digital financial services.",""],[1,"266","5","Fintech Regulatory Sandbox Promotion","The BSP will encourage fintech companies to capitalize on the regulatory sandbox of the BSP to ensure that innovation will benefit users while complying with regulations.",""],[1,"266","6","Regulatory Sandbox and Sandbox Lite Framework","the BSP will continue to maintain a test and learn environment to encourage responsible innovation.",""]],"206":[[1,"274","7","Tax Regime for Industries with Negative Externalities","An appropriate tax regime for industries generating negative externalities or those causing damages to society;",""],[1,"274","23","Tax Regime for Extractive Industries and Pollution","Implement appropriate tax regime for extractive industries and pollution",""],[1,"277","1","Tax Regime for Extractive Industries and Pollution","Implement appropriate tax regime for extractive industries and pollution",""],[1,"277","2","Special Fiscal Regime for Extractive Industries","A special fiscal regime will be designed to ensure that the state, as a resource owner, receives an appropriate share of the economic rent enjoyed by extractive industries, particularly mining.",""],[1,"277","3","Extractive Sector Monitoring and Governance Strengthening","The government will also strengthen the monitoring and governance of the extractive sector by enhancing civic space, people participation, and institutionalizing Extractive Industries Transparency Initiative (EITI) principles at the national and sub-national levels.",""],[1,"277","4","Carbon Tax Introduction","Another potential fiscal measure is a carbon tax that can encourage a shift to less-polluting fuel and reduce carbon dioxide emissions.",""],[1,"277","5","Fiscal Regime for Natural Gas and Oil Drilling","An appropriate fiscal regime for drilling natural gas and oil will be designed to compensate the state for the depletion of a finite resource.",""],[1,"281","9","Fiscal Regime Rationalization for Extractive Industries and Pollution","Rationalization of the fiscal regime for extractive industries and pollution",""],[1,"281","9","Tax Structure for Unhealthy Foods","developing an appropriate tax structure for unhealthy foods",""],[1,"281","10","Fiscal Regime for Extractive and Polluting Industries","Seeks to broaden the tax base by developing an appropriate fiscal regime for [a] both extractive and polluting industries to internalize the negative externalities they generate, protect patrimony and well- being, support green recovery, and strengthen monitoring and governance of the extractive sector through the institutionalization of Extractive Industries Transparency Initiative; and [b] unhealthy foods to discourage its consumption and encourage healthy alternatives.",""]],"207":[[1,"274","28","Military and Uniformed Personnel Pension Reform","Pursue the Military and Uniformed Personnel (MUP) pension reform",""],[1,"279","3","Military and Uniformed Personnel Pension Reform","reforms in the MUP pension system will be instituted to make the system financially sustainable.",""],[1,"281","13","MUP Pension Fund Establishment and Pension System Reform","Develop a sustainable pension system for MUPs by creating an MUP pension fund with mandatory contributions, adjustment of the indexation process, and identification of funding sources for the pension system.",""]],"208":[[1,"274","31","Government Asset Privatization Acceleration","Fast-track the privatization of government assets",""],[1,"278","4","Privatization Program","The privatization program will be continuously pursued to broaden ownership base and foster greater private sector participation.",""],[1,"278","4","Asset Verification and Disposition Process","The Privatization and Management Office has initiated the verification and disposition of about 27,000 assets that are still in the Asset Registry, including the claims of mining corporations and of the National Government Mining Assets.",""]],"209":[[1,"293","4","Foreign Ownership Liberalization for Renewable Energy Projects","Department Circular No. 2022-11-0034 was issued allowing 100 percent foreign ownership of RE projects where applicable.","Department of Justice"]],"210":[[1,"301","24","Asset Management and Preservation Implementation","Fully implement asset management and preservation",""],[1,"302","7","Infrastructure Asset Lifecycle and Utilization Analysis","the government will analyze the lifecycle, capacity, and utilization of infrastructure assets individually and collectively, with the view to optimizing government funds and targeting scarce resources to the most critical",""],[1,"303","1","Infrastructure Asset Maintenance and Rehabilitation","The government will ensure that infrastructure assets will be efficiently and effectively maintained and rehabilitated, as necessary, to maximize their economic life.",""]],"211":[[1,"301","20","Electricity Cost Reduction Reforms","Implement game-changing reforms to bring down the cost of electricity",""],[1,"301","21","Energy Delivery Coordination and Grid Investment","Enhance delivery of energy by coordinating investment in generation, transmission, and distribution",""],[1,"301","32","Fuel Mix Market Enabling Environment","Provide an enabling environment for the market to deliver an optimal fuel mix",""],[1,"301","36","Energy Innovation Investment for Clean Technology Markets","Invest energy innovation to respond to increasing demand and new markets for clean technology goods and services",""]],"212":[[1,"306","5","Underground Utility Corridor Development","Underground utility corridors for electricity and telecommunications cables, water supply, sewage, and other utilities will be established to secure public safety.",""]],"213":[[1,"312","8","Natural Gas Industry Development Acceleration","the government will expedite the development of the natural gas industry.",""],[1,"312","8","Liquefied Natural Gas Importation","Importing liquefied natural gas (LNG) is an immediate solution to this threat.",""],[1,"312","8","LNG Supply Security Investments","To secure LNG supply overtime, investments in the",""],[1,"313","1","Natural Gas Legal and Regulatory Framework Development","creating an enabling legal and regulatory framework for the natural gas industry should be prioritized.",""],[1,"313","1","New Oil and Gas Field Exploration","New oil and gas fields shall likewise be explored.",""],[1,"313","1","LNG Demand Diversification Assessment","potential demand outside of electricity generation will also be explored.",""],[1,"318","8","Natural Gas Regulatory Consolidation and Enhancement","This aims to consolidate and enhance various executive issuances and policies governing the natural gas transmission, distribution, and supply.",""]],"214":[[1,"313","4","Energy Storage and Smart Meter Deployment","Along with capacity markets are innovative game-changers in the sector for deployment such as energy storage systems and digitalization of energy systems through the use of ICT (network-connected devices) and smart meters (for real-time monitoring of energy consumption).",""],[1,"313","4","Wind-Solar Portfolio Diversification and Thermal Storage","Other ways to address intermittency such as diversification of the wind-solar portfolio by type and location and thermal storage (i.e., heat water when solar makes price low or make ice used later for air conditioning) will be pursued.",""],[1,"314","4","Private Sector Clean Energy Innovation Support","The government shall provide a conducive environment to encourage the private sector investments in game-changing innovations that will facilitate entry of cleaner energy in the market and respond to increasing demand.",""],[1,"314","4","Energy Storage and Digitalization Solutions Deployment","On the supply side, the innovative solutions include thermal storage, digitalization of energy systems through the use of ICT (network-connected devices), and development and deployment of energy storage systems.",""],[1,"314","4","Smart Meter and Energy-Efficient Appliance Rollout","On the demand side, innovative technologies include smart meters for real-time monitoring of energy consumption, and energy-efficient appliances, among others.",""]],"215":[[1,"313","5","Nuclear Energy Feasibility and Regulatory Framework Development","The government will explore the inclusion of nuclear energy in the mix.","DOE | Congress | Department of Science and Technology"],[1,"318","9","Comprehensive Atomic Energy Regulatory Framework","Drafting of the Comprehensive Atomic Energy Regulatory Framework",""],[1,"318","10","Nuclear Regulatory Body Establishment","This will create a nuclear regulatory body for the peaceful uses and application of nuclear energy",""]],"216":[[1,"337","3","Scenario-Based Disaster Preparedness and Response Mechanisms","Scenario-based planning, preparedness, and response mechanisms, as well as the protocols to protect critical infrastructure and assets, will be enhanced.",""],[1,"337","3","Marine Pollution Response Capacity Enhancement","Capacity to respond and manage maritime-based disasters like oil spills and hazardous and noxious substances spills will be improved by mobilizing coastal barangay information networks and Bantay-Dagat volunteer organizations, and by establishing marine pollution centers in strategic locations.",""],[1,"337","3","Critical Infrastructure Protection Coordination and Mapping","Meanwhile, existing mechanisms and procedures to protect critical infrastructure assets will be strengthened37 through improved coordination and capacity of various government agencies and LGUs in critical infrastructures mapping, vulnerability scanning, and threat assessment.",""]],"217":[[1,"333","13","Advocacy for a Rules-Based Regional and International Order","Strengthen advocacy on respect for the rules-based regime in the regional and international community",""],[1,"333","19","Regional and International Security Partnerships","Strengthen regional and international partnerships to counter and prevent threats from terrorism, violent extremism, radicalization, transnational crimes, and other non-traditional security threats",""],[1,"336","2","Regional and International Security Partnership Strengthening","Strengthen regional and international partnerships to counter and prevent threats from terrorism, violent extremism, radicalization, transnational crimes, and other non-traditional security threats",""],[1,"336","4","Cross-Border Law Enforcement Cooperation and Maritime Security Coordination","close partnerships with neighboring states will be sustained particularly on matters involving sea patrol, intelligence gathering, information exchange, rapid bilateral investigations, and apprehension of criminal elements in the porous borders of Southern Philippines and other critical areas.",""],[1,"337","7","Advocacy for a Rules-Based Regional and International Order","Strengthen advocacy on respect for rules-based regime in the regional and international community",""],[1,"337","8","Advocacy for the 2016 PCA Ruling","the government will advocate the 2016 PCA ruling favoring the Philippine position",""],[1,"337","9","Whole-of-Nation South China Sea Conduct Diplomacy","of conduct in the South China Sea will be pursued.",""],[1,"337","9","Whole-of-Nation Influence Strategy for Regional and International Bodies","A whole-of-nation approach will be adopted in influencing local, regional, and international bodies.",""],[1,"338","1","Regional Security Diplomacy and People-to-People Dialogue Expansion","Bilateral, minilateral, and multilateral diplomatic arrangements in promoting regional security will be strengthened and expanded, while greater people-to-people dialogue among allied states will be promoted.",""],[1,"338","2","Joint Military and Intelligence Exercises","Cooperative joint military and intelligence exercises with friends and allies will be strengthened, while defense cooperation arrangements, such as the Mutual Defense Treaty and Visiting Forces Agreements, will be maximized by involving other security institutions in the training exercises.",""]],"218":[[1,"336","4","Air Transportation Surveillance and Inspection Strengthening","surveillance and inspection in air transportation will be strengthened.",""],[1,"336","4","Coastal Management and Maritime Security Mandate Harmonization","mandates and functions of various agencies relative to coastal management and maritime security will be reviewed and harmonized to ensure efficiency and effectiveness in addressing maritime security threats",""],[1,"336","4","Philippine Coast Guard Modernization","the modernization of the Philippine Coast Guard and relevant maritime security institutions will be actively pursued.",""],[1,"338","4","Maritime Security Information Systems Harmonization","Monitoring and information systems and technical interoperability of maritime security agencies will be harmonized to ensure a holistic and integrated policy on maritime domain.",""],[1,"339","12","Maritime Zones and Sovereignty Jurisdictions Establishment","This aims to establish maritime zones and sovereignty jurisdictions where maritime rights can be exercised against unnecessary and dangerous maneuvers of foreign vessels traversing and entering the Philippine territory.",""],[1,"339","15","Designation of Sea Lanes and Air Routes","This aims to designate sea lanes and air routes for safe and innocent passage consistent with the provisions of the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea to prevent arbitrary international passage in the Philippine archipelago.",""]],"219":[[1,"343","22","Expansion of Non-Financial Bail and Preventive Detention Review","Expand access to non-financial bail and periodic review of preventive imprisonment",""],[1,"343","23","e-Dalaw System Expansion","Expand the e-Dalaw system, livelihood and entrepreneurial opportunities for PDL, and multi-disciplinary rehabilitation mechanisms",""],[1,"343","23","Livelihood and Entrepreneurial Support for PDL","Expand the e-Dalaw system, livelihood and entrepreneurial opportunities for PDL, and multi-disciplinary rehabilitation mechanisms",""],[1,"343","23","Multi-disciplinary Rehabilitation Mechanisms","Expand the e-Dalaw system, livelihood and entrepreneurial opportunities for PDL, and multi-disciplinary rehabilitation mechanisms",""],[1,"343","26","Early Release, Parole, and Probation Expansion","Identify classes of PDL, who may be qualified for early release, and expand access to parole and probation for certain classes of offenses",""],[1,"343","29","Unified Referral and Monitoring System for Former PDL","Operationalize the unified referral and monitoring system for former PDL",""],[1,"348","6","Recognizance Act Expansion and Automated Court Notification System","The Recognizance Act of 2012 (Republic Act 10389)55 will be revisited to expand the application of recognizance.",""],[1,"348","7","Periodic Judicial Review of Preventive Detention Cases","The courts will periodically review all criminal cases involving preventive imprisonment to safeguard the rights of preventively imprisoned persons against unreasonable prolonged detention.",""],[1,"348","7","eCourt Alert System for Preventive Detention Release Dates","The review will be reinforced by automating the computation of time served by the detainee, integrating an alert system in the eCourt system that will prompt the judge on the release date of the detainee.",""],[1,"349","7","e-Dalaw System Expansion","Expand the e-Dalaw system, livelihood, and entrepreneurial opportunities for PDL, and multi-disciplinary rehabilitation mechanisms",""],[1,"349","7","Livelihood and Entrepreneurial Support for PDL","Expand the e-Dalaw system, livelihood, and entrepreneurial opportunities for PDL, and multi-disciplinary rehabilitation mechanisms",""],[1,"349","7","Multi-disciplinary Rehabilitation Mechanisms","Expand the e-Dalaw system, livelihood, and entrepreneurial opportunities for PDL, and multi-disciplinary rehabilitation mechanisms",""],[1,"349","8","e-Dalaw System Expansion","The e-Dalaw system will be expanded to afford unhampered access to justice and enforce social reintegration.",""],[1,"349","8","Video Conferencing Infrastructure for Visitations and Hearings","Infrastructure to support video conferencing for visitations and hearings will be established to reduce possible risks associated with in-person contact, such as smuggling of prohibited items.",""],[1,"349","9","Product Development and Marketing Training for PDL","To provide livelihood opportunities for PDL, the DTI will continue its product development and marketing trainings for PDL who are skilled in handiwork.","DTI"],[1,"349","9","Employer Incentives for PDL Livelihood and Employment","The government will also provide tax incentives or other non-monetary incentives and recognition to employers and business establishments that will provide capacity-building, livelihood, or employment, as well as entrepreneurial opportunities to PDL.",""],[1,"349","9","Study on Expungement of Criminal Records","It will also conduct a study to determine whether expungement of criminal records adopted in other jurisdictions is viable to remove the stigma associated with incarceration.",""],[1,"350","1","Holistic Reintegration Law and Rehabilitation Program","A law that unifies the holistic reintegration strategy of formerly incarcerated offenders will be enacted, involving a multi-disciplinary program that ensures the successful rehabilitation of convicted offenders.",""],[1,"350","2","Early Release, Parole, and Probation Expansion","Identify classes of PDL who may be qualified for early release and expand access to parole and probation for certain classes of offenses",""],[1,"350","3","Review and Revision of Penal and Probation Laws","The Revised Penal Code, the Indeterminate Sentence Law, and the Probation Law will be reviewed and revised to allow convicted offenders to avail of the benefits provided by said laws.",""],[1,"350","4","Penal Law Classification Simplification and Reform","Distinctions in our penal laws with respect to heinous, violent, and non-violent offenders, rather than a simplistic penalty-based classification, will be considered.",""],[1,"350","5","Unified Referral and Monitoring System for Former PDLs","Operationalize the unified referral and monitoring system for former PDL",""],[1,"350","6","Post-Incarceration Rehabilitation and Reintegration Support","The government will assess post-incarceration outcomes in the form of facilities for psychiatric support and supportive residential housing, such as halfway houses.",""]],"220":[[1,"337","6","Space Science and Technology Applications Optimization","the country will optimize space science and technology applications through the Philippine Space Agency (PhilSA)",""]],"221":[[1,"347","1","Review of Indigenous Peoples Jurisdiction on Ancestral Domain Claims","The jurisdiction of the National Commission on Indigenous Peoples on claims of indigenous peoples and indigenous cultural communities on ancestral domains will also be considered.",""]],"222":[[1,"350","6","Drug Offender Rehabilitation Program","in drug cases, the rehabilitation program will be designed to address underlying problems of substance abuse that might lead to re-offending.",""],[1,"350","6","Barangay Anti-Drug Abuse Council Reintegration Monitoring Expansion","the functions of the Barangay Anti-Drug Abuse Council will be expanded to include monitoring of former PDL to assist in their complete rehabilitation and reintegration into communities.",""],[1,"351","5","Post-Incarceration Reintegration Program for Persons Deprived of Liberty","This creates a comprehensive and holistic program for the reintegration of persons deprived of liberty (PDL) post-incarceration, including employment opportunities in the public sector and providing incentives for the private sector that will accept PDL as employees.",""],[1,"353","29","Former Rebel Reintegration and Resilience Support Program","The Transformation Program will be implemented by the LGUs, in coordination with the Armed Forces of the Philippines, to help former rebels and their families to become productive and resilient members of society.","LGUs | Armed Forces of the Philippines"]],"223":[[1,"367","5","Legislation to Create LGU Human Resource Management Offices","Legislating the creation of HR management offices in LGUs will also be pursued.",""],[1,"367","6","Institutionalization of Alternative Working Arrangements in the Public Sector","the government will institutionalize alternative working arrangements in the public sector.",""],[1,"368","1","ICT Capability and Remote Work Support Initiative","capabilities for the effective use of information and communications technology (ICT) tools; providing support for remote work; and improving policies on authorizations, data management, and audit.",""],[1,"368","1","Occupational Health and Safety and Public Service Continuity Measures","Initiatives will also include advocating occupational health and safety, ensuring public service continuity, and",""],[1,"368","2","Mental Wellness Program Strengthening","strengthening mental wellness programs.",""],[1,"368","2","Bureaucracy-Wide HR Management Information System","The CSC will develop a bureaucracy-wide HR Management Information System, shifting HR management from transactional to the more proactive strategic through digital or web-based systems.","CSC"],[1,"368","12","Creation of Human Resource and Management Offices in Local Government Units","Creation of Human Resource and Management [HRM) Offices in local government units (LGUs)",""],[1,"368","13","Establishment of LGU Human Resource Management Offices","The bill seeks to establish HRM Offices and mandate regular [plantilla) HRM officers in LGUs to develop competent and credible employees at the local level.",""]],"224":[[1,"375","1","Green and Blue Economy Promotion Strategy","A green and blue economy will be promoted and developed to optimize their contribution to livelihood and employment generation while improving environmental and social well-being.",""],[1,"381","1","Green Goods and Jobs Promotion through Natural Assets","In addition, natural assets will be harnessed to stimulate demand for green goods, services, and technologies in order to support green jobs and generate income for resource-dependent communities.",""],[1,"382","2","Green and Blue Economy Enabling Policies","To promote the green and blue economy, the government will pursue enabling policies that will provide more livelihood and economic opportunities, particularly for the poor and vulnerable upland and coastal communities.",""],[1,"382","2","Natural Resource Management Investment Expansion","Investments in activities that foster the sustainable management of natural resources, such as on forest and coastal protection and rehabilitation, will be increased to generate more jobs and livelihoods.",""],[1,"382","2","Biodiversity-Friendly Enterprise and Ecotourism Promotion","The government and the private sector will also promote and develop more biodiversity-friendly enterprises and ecotourism sites within and outside protected areas.",""],[1,"382","2","Commercial Forest Plantation Revitalization","Likewise, forestry investments will be revitalized by establishing more commercial forest plantations for timber and non-timber forest products, fuelwood, and high-value crops (e.g., coffee, cacao, and rubber).",""],[1,"382","2","Marine-Based Livelihood Enterprise Scaling","Marine-based industries and enterprises, such as mudcrab fattening, blue swimming crab culture, seaweed farming, and salt production, will also be scaled up to provide employment opportunities and income for coastal communities.",""],[1,"382","3","Green Jobs Assessment and Certification System and Guidelines","The development and implementation of the Green Jobs Assessment and Certification System and Guidelines will be fast-tracked to facilitate the shift to cleaner production technologies and processes, while monitoring tools will be further harnessed to account for the contribution of green jobs to the economy.",""],[1,"382","3","Research and Development on Genetic Resources for Nature-Based Products","Also, government, academe, and the private sector will advance R&D on genetic resources for nature-based products, pharmaceuticals, and nutritional supplements.",""],[1,"382","3","Strengthening Intellectual Property Rights for Nature-Based Products","Intellectual property rights for such products will be strengthened to optimize their economic potential and ensure equitable sharing of revenues, especially for local and indigenous communities as stewards of our natural resources.",""]],"225":[[1,"375","1","Low-Carbon Development Policy Measures","Innovative policies and measures to advance low-carbon development will also be pursued while ensuring just transition and job creation.",""],[1,"379","8","Nationally Determined Contribution Policy and Measures Implementation","Implement the Nationally Determined Contribution (NDC) policies and measures",""],[1,"383","1","Private Sector Climate Mitigation Enablement","the government will strengthen the enabling environment for private sector engagement in mitigation, promote the development of green technologies, and implement transformative policies and actions to curb GHG emissions while ensuring just transition of the workforce.",""],[1,"383","1","Mitigation Hierarchy Implementation","The government will also prioritize actions based on the mitigation hierarchy that lead to the best outcomes for communities and the environment, wherein the following strategies are prioritized in order to: (a) avoid adverse impacts, (b) minimize impacts that cannot be avoided, (c) restore or rehabilitate damage or degradation, and (d) offset or compensate for unavoidable impacts.",""],[1,"383","1","Low-Carbon Transition and Ecosystem Restoration","transitioning to a low-carbon economy will involve strengthening adaptation actions with high mitigation potential, such as restoring and protecting terrestrial and blue carbon ecosystems (e.g., mangroves and seagrasses).",""],[1,"383","2","Low-Carbon Technology Adoption Initiative","Lead sectoral agencies,9 in collaboration with the private sector, will adopt innovative and transformative low-carbon emitting technologies in the energy, agriculture, waste, industry, and transport sectors.",""],[1,"383","2","Renewable Energy Expansion and Energy Efficiency Scaling","For the energy sector, the Department of Energy will reduce emissions in the supply side by expanding renewable energy systems and technologies and scaling-up energy efficiency and conservation measures (See Chapter 12).","Department of Energy"],[1,"383","2","Localization of NDC PAMs for LGUs","The government will also explore the localization of NDC PAMs to increase the capacity and contribution of LGUs to national mitigation actions.",""],[1,"383","3","Updated Nationally Determined Contribution with Adaptation and Loss-and-Damage Measures","updated NDC, to include PAMs for adaptation and loss and damage, through a multisectoral and consultative process.",""],[1,"383","3","Implementation and Financial Plan for NDC PAMs","The CCC will also develop an implementation and financial plan to guide the operationalization of NDC PAMs.",""],[1,"385","3","National Greenhouse Gas Inventory Capacity Strengthening","The capacity of lead sectoral agencies to conduct regular national GHG inventory will also be enhanced to enable the effective measurement and management of GHG emissions.",""],[1,"385","3","Regional Greenhouse Gas Inventory Exploration","The conduct of regional GHG inventory will also be explored to assess and determine the potential contribution of regions in attaining the NDC targets.",""]],"226":[[1,"383","4","Carbon Pricing Instrument Adoption Feasibility Study","This includes exploring the feasibility of adopting carbon pricing instruments (CPI) as a cost-effective means to encourage the transition to clean energy and improve energy efficiency in high-emitting sectors (i.e., energy and industry), raise state revenues, and address environmental concerns.",""],[1,"383","4","Local Carbon Market Development","Local carbon markets will also be established to tap private sector financing, including foreign investments, particularly for the agriculture and forestry sectors.",""],[1,"383","4","Carbon Offsetting and REDD+ Support Initiative","To this end, the DENR will identify and establish areas for carbon offsetting and encourage support for relevant initiatives such as efforts to advance the implementation of Reducing Emissions from Deforestation and Forest Degradation or REDD+ activities and rehabilitate and conserve blue carbon ecosystems.","DENR"],[1,"383","4","Sub-national Geospatial Carbon Accounting and National Carbon Registry","These measures will be complemented by intensified, granular geospatial carbon accounting at the sub-national level and in different property rights regimes, including ancestral domains, as well as developing a national carbon registry to monitor transactions.",""]],"227":[[1,"387","3","Legislative Measures for Natural Resource Protection and Management","Within the medium term, concerned national government agencies will collaborate with the legislative branch toward enacting legislative measures to strengthen the protection and management of natural resources toward a sustainable and climate-resilient development.",""],[1,"387","3","Priority Climate Action and Disaster Resilience Bills","Table 15.1 contains priority bills for the 19th Congress during the Plan period to accelerate climate action and strengthen disaster resilience.",""]],"228":[[1,"397","2","Peace and Security Strategy Implementation","the National Security Council will lead the implementation of strategies to ensure peace and security",""]],"229":[[1,"395","7","Income-Earning Ability Enhancement Measures","The Social Development Committee will also push for measures to increase the income-earning ability of Filipinos as identified in Chapter 4: Increase Income-Earning Ability.",""],[1,"396","32","Implementation of Measures to Reduce Vulnerabilities and Protect Purchasing Power","The Economic Development Cluster or the equivalent NEDA Board Committee will ensure that measures identified in Chapter 3: Reduce Vulnerabilities and Protect Purchasing Power are pursued.",""]],"230":[[1,"418","11","Accessible Tourism Establishments and Destinations Program","A program of the Department of Tourism to encourage DOT-accredited tourism related establishments as well as tourism destinations to become more user friendly for persons with disabilities.","Department of Tourism"],[1,"435","20","Philippine Tourism Human Resource Development Strategy and Action Plan Continuation","This plan is the continuation of the Philippine Tourism Human Resource Development Strategy and Action Plan (2015-2020).",""],[1,"436","7","Three-Level Recognition Scheme for Primary Tourism Enterprises","A three-level recognition scheme of the DOT for Primary Tourism Enterprises entailing progressive minimum standards and reflecting customers expectations.","DOT"]],"231":[[1,"421","2","Comprehensive Automotive Resurgence Strategy (CARS) Program","The Comprehensive Automotive Resurgence Strategy (CARS) program is intended to augment and enhance the policy directions of existing motor vehicle development programs toward ensuring a resurgent automotive industry","DTI"],[1,"421","6","National EV Industry Development Plan","The CREVI refers to a national development plan for the EV industry with an annual work plan to accelerate the development, commercialization, and utilization of EVs in the country comprised of the following four (4) components: 1) EVs and charging stations component; 2) Manufacturing component; 3) Research and development component; and 4) Human resource development component.",""]],"232":[[1,"426","14","Three-Year Planned Maintenance Outage Schedule","The GOMP of the National Grid Corporation of the Philippines (NGCP) contains the proposed three-year Planned/Maintenance Outages of grid and system operations- monitored power generation facilities (in consultation with the generating companies), information on the schedule of maintenance per unit/power plant as well as the overall weekly reserve profile per year per grid.",""],[1,"426","14","NGCP Transmission Facilities Maintenance Program","It also contains the three-year maintenance program of the Transmission facilities of NGCP aligned to the Planned Outage of the power generation facilities.",""]],"233":[[1,"434","10","Priority MSME Stimulus Program","A priority stimulus program for MSMEs as government's customized intervention to drive inclusive local economic growth.",""]],"234":[[1,"384","1","Carbon Capture and Storage Partnerships","local and global partnerships for carbon capture and storage from industries such as steel and cement production and power generation will also be explored.",""],[1,"384","3","Technology Development Partnership and Collaboration Initiative","Technology development will be promoted through partnership and collaboration among industries, civil society, and the academe.",""],[1,"384","4","Support for Green and Climate-Smart Technology Manufacturing","manufacturing and production of green and climate-smart technology products for global markets will also be provided.",""],[1,"384","4","Support for R&D and Commercialization of Sustainable Technologies","The government will also continue to support local industries for R&D and commercialization of sustainable and green technologies and products (e.g., through the Innovation Fund)",""],[1,"384","4","Market Access and Competitiveness Support for MSMEs and Export Producers","The government will assist micro, small, and medium enterprises and local export producers and suppliers to access international markets for these technologies and products by strengthening their compliance to sustainability standards and enhancing their competitiveness",""]],"235":[[1,"441","6","LGU Energy Code Implementation Guidelines","The LGU Energy Code provides the Guidelines for LGUs to facilitate the implementation of energy projects.",""]]}});